s Khuwaja, Kapal Dev, Weizheng Wang, and Lewis Nkenyereye. \u201cChatgpt needs spade (sustainability, privacy, digital divide, and ethics) evaluation: A review\u201d. In: Cognitive Computation (2024), pp. 1\u201323. DOI: 10.1007/s12559-024-10285-1.\n---\n# A PREPRINT - JANUARY 15, 2025\n\n1.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 58442, "end_char_idx": 59745, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "97ea82e6-b2d4-4efb-8b35-1952c06235e7", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_name": "ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 72913, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22", "document_title": "\"Navigating the Sustainable AI Trilemma: Balancing Energy Efficiency, Digital Equity, and Capability in Large Language Models and AI Agent Design\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the sustainable AI trilemma, focusing on the balance between energy efficiency, digital equity, and capability in the design of large language models (LLMs) and AI agents. It includes a list of relevant academic references that explore various aspects of AI sustainability, carbon footprint modeling, and the implications of AI on jobs and the environment. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Sustainable AI**: The challenges and strategies for making AI technologies environmentally friendly while maintaining their effectiveness.\n2. **Carbon Footprint**: Research on quantifying the carbon emissions associated with training and deploying large language models.\n3. **AI and Ethics**: The ethical considerations surrounding AI's impact on sustainability and job markets.\n4. **Emerging Trends**: A survey of current trends and challenges in AI sustainability, particularly in learning algorithms.\n5. **Green Algorithms**: The development of methodologies to measure and reduce the carbon footprint of computational processes.\n\nKey entities mentioned include authors and their works, such as Ahmad Faiz, Ekkehard Ernst, and Sophia Falk, along with their contributions to the discourse on AI sustainability. The section also references specific publications and DOI links for further reading."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "5bbe2f3b-a5cf-473e-9e50-1d182dcad9fb", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_name": "ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 72913, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "47c48bbdebdc34c45547d1ddc9efb86758d4c6bea59cc0a6ae9786ef666e699e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "a3adbf11-dc19-4dc5-a339-2344c4f20fe0", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_name": "ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 72913, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "2a84dd2d1774071f461d829763f2e6feb04bede6cbef181130e8c00b230e7151", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "ebe65192-4d8