harmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_name": "ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 72913, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22", "document_title": "\"Navigating the Sustainable AI Trilemma: Balancing Energy Efficiency, Digital Equity, and Capability in Large Language Models and AI Agent Design\"", "section_summary": "The section provides a list of academic references related to the design and implications of large language models (LLMs) and AI agents, focusing on themes such as energy efficiency, digital equity, and the challenges and opportunities in the field of machine learning operations (MLOps) and AI operations (AIOps). Key topics include:\n\n1. **Agent Design Patterns**: A reference to a catalogue of architectural patterns for foundation model-based agents, indicating a focus on structured approaches to AI agent design.\n   \n2. **Efficient Inference Serving**: Discussion on enabling efficient serverless inference for LLMs in cloud environments, highlighting the importance of optimizing resource usage.\n\n3. **MLOps and AIOps**: A systematic survey addressing the challenges and opportunities in integrating machine learning and AI operations, suggesting a roadmap for future developments.\n\n4. **Educational Inequalities**: An exploration of the real-world educational disparities exacerbated by the use of LLMs, raising concerns about equity in AI applications.\n\n5. **Potential Harms of LLMs**: Examination of the risks associated with LLMs in specific contexts, particularly in Africa, emphasizing the need for ethical considerations in AI deployment.\n\n6. **Intelligent Agents**: Insights into the definitions, methods, and future prospects of intelligent agents based on LLMs, indicating ongoing research in this area.\n\nEntities mentioned include various authors and their affiliations, as well as specific journals and conferences where the research is published. The references span a range of years, with a focus on recent studies from 2023 and 2024."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "5bbe2f3b-a5cf-473e-9e50-1d182dcad9fb", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_name": "ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 72913, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "47c48bbdebdc34c45547d1ddc9efb86758d4c6bea59cc0a6ae9786ef666e699e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "97ea82e6-b2d4-4efb-8b35-1952c06235e7", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_name": "ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 72913, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "9404ffc9374fd37eec5dbad39a279eab6b6de5aeb038500257a3d232ba58debe", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "7af13721-a355-4e40-b4da-758e2e500e6a", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "16c710aea27885197537194a0bd6ecc4f649f70e0376d882d79060f0fa8c9044", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "7. Yue Liu et al. \u201cAgent design pattern catalogue: A col