l Equity, and Capability in Large Language Models and AI Agent Design\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses various resources and references related to sustainable AI practices, particularly in the context of large language models (LLMs) and AI agent design. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Sustainable AI Trilemma**: The focus is on balancing energy efficiency, digital equity, and capability in AI systems.\n2. **Power Management**: References to the \"Powercap Linux Kernel Interface\" indicate a concern for energy efficiency in AI operations.\n3. **NVIDIA Management Library (NVML)**: This suggests a focus on monitoring and managing GPU resources, which is crucial for optimizing performance and energy use in AI applications.\n4. **LlamaIndex**: A tool developed by Jerry Liu, likely related to enhancing retrieval-augmented generation techniques in AI.\n5. **Best Practices in Retrieval-Augmented Generation**: A study by Xiaohua Wang et al. that explores effective methods in this area, indicating ongoing research and development in improving AI capabilities.\n\nOverall, the section highlights the intersection of technology, sustainability, and research in the field of AI, emphasizing the importance of efficient resource management and equitable access."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "5bbe2f3b-a5cf-473e-9e50-1d182dcad9fb", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_name": "ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 72913, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "47c48bbdebdc34c45547d1ddc9efb86758d4c6bea59cc0a6ae9786ef666e699e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "0057870d-d5ff-4748-b6c2-59173c49e796", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_name": "ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 72913, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "de48ae78426b61f08a180821a70ad94c51b3792c4da8f53e85f4c0801fd6c481", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "74\u201381. URL: https://aclanthology.org/W04-1013/.\n18. \"Powercap Linux Kernel Interface\". Accessed: 2025-01-10. 2024. URL: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/power/powercap/powercap.html.\n19. NVIDIA Corporation. \"NVIDIA Management Library (NVML) Python Bindings\". Accessed: 2025-01-10. 2024. URL: https://pypi.org/project/nvidia-ml-py/.\n20. Jerry Liu. \"LlamaIndex\". Nov. 2022. URL: https://github.com/jerryjliu/llama_index.\n21. Xiaohua Wang et al. \u201cSearching for best practices in retrieval-augmented generation\u201d. In: Proceedings of the 2024 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing. 2024, pp. 17716\u201317736.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 71898, "end_char_idx": 72527, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "71a1b50b-c278-49f6-85aa-a53af1c15b40", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses \"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation\" (Agentic RAG), a concept that enhances traditional Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems by incorporating autonomous AI agents. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Large Language Models (LLMs)**: The impact of LLMs on AI, particularly in text generation and natural language understanding, and their limitations due to reliance on static training data.\n\n2. **Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)**: An approach that integrates real-time data retrieval to improve the relevance and accuracy of responses generated by LLMs.\n\n3. **Agentic RAG**: A novel framework that incorporates autonomous agents into the RAG pipeline, allowing for dynamic management of retrieval strategies, iterative refinement of contextual understanding, and adaptable workflows.\n\n4. **Design Patterns**: The use of agentic design patterns such as reflection, planning, tool use, and multi-agent collaboration to enhance the capabilities of RAG systems.\n\n5. **Applications**: The potential applications of Agentic RAG in various industries, including healthcare, finance, and education.\n\n6. **Implementation Strategies**: Practical approaches for implementing Agentic RAG systems, emphasizing flexibility, scalability, and context-awareness.\n\nEntities mentioned include:\n- Authors: Aditi Singh, Abul Ehtesham, Saket Kumar, Tala Talaei Khoei.\n- Institutions: Cleveland State University, The Davey Tree Expert Company, The MathWorks Inc, Khoury College of Computer Science at Northeastern University. \n\nOverall, the survey aims to provide a comprehensive understanding of Agentic RAG, its principles, architectures, applications, and future directions."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "24165315-e7ed-4320-86dd-956c599ca07d", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "b499d1db52036cb05791d59303952aee44ec8b68989441db31c2eab533da2f5b", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "# AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION: A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG\n\nAditi Singh\n\nDepartment of Computer Science\n\nCleveland State University\n\nCleveland, OH, USA\n\na.singh22@csuohio.edu\n\nAbul Ehtesham\n\nThe Davey Tree Expert Company\n\nKent, OH, USA\n\nabul.ehtesham@davey.com\n\nSaket Kumar\n\nThe MathWorks Inc\n\nNatick, MA, USA\n\nsaketk@mathworks.com\n\nTala Talaei Khoei\n\nKhoury College of Computer Science\n\nRoux Institute at Northeastern University\n\nPortland, ME, USA\n\nt.talaeikhoei@northeastern.edu\n\n# ABSTRACT\n\nLarge Language Models (LLMs) have revolutionized artificial intelligence (AI) by enabling human-like text generation and natural language understanding. However, their reliance on static training data limits their ability to respond to dynamic, real-time queries, resulting in outdated or inaccurate outputs. Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) has emerged as a solution, enhancing LLMs by integrating real-time data retrieval to provide contextually relevant and up-to-date responses. Despite its promise, traditional RAG systems are constrained by static workflows and lack the adaptability required for multi-step reasoning and complex task management.\n\nAgentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (Agentic RAG) transcends these limitations by embedding autonomous AI agents into the RAG pipeline. These agents leverage agentic design patterns reflection, planning, tool use, and multi-agent collaboration to dynamically manage retrieval strategies, iteratively refine contextual understanding, and adapt workflows through clearly defined operational structures ranging from sequential steps to adaptive collaboration. This integration enables Agentic RAG systems to deliver unparalleled flexibility, scalability, and context-awareness across diverse applications.\n\nThis survey provides a comprehensive exploration of Agentic RAG, beginning with its foundational principles and the evolution of RAG paradigms. It presents a detailed taxonomy of Agentic RAG architectures, highlights key applications in industries such as healthcare, finance, and education, and examines practical implementation strategies.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 0, "end_char_idx": 2107, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "24165315-e7ed-4320-86dd-956c599ca07d", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the concept of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) and its significance in various industries, particularly healthcare, finance, and education. It outlines a detailed taxonomy of Agentic RAG architectures and highlights key applications, practical implementation strategies, and challenges such as scaling, ethical decision-making, and performance optimization. The excerpt emphasizes the importance of integrating real-time data to enhance the capabilities of Large Language Models (LLMs), which have transformed AI through their ability to generate human-like text and perform complex tasks. However, LLMs face limitations due to their reliance on static pre-training data, leading to issues like outdated information and hallucinated responses. The section also provides a GitHub link for further resources on Agentic RAG.\n\nKey topics include:\n- Agentic RAG architectures\n- Applications in healthcare, finance, and education\n- Implementation strategies and challenges\n- Limitations of LLMs\n- Importance of real-time data integration\n\nKey entities include:\n- Large Language Models (LLMs)\n- Artificial Intelligence (AI)\n- Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)\n- Ethical AI Decision-Making\n- Multi-Agent Collaboration"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "71a1b50b-c278-49f6-85aa-a53af1c15b40", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "de0ca16cfda453cb43a70d609cb02d8f49a9a05cb336dff5d568ec9b27d7b372", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "234f6c5b-b5f6-4188-8e38-9bb77854e3b2", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "288468f7af1a394009f1286903a8777bc67a24744c3f0cd9e153a630bf5f86ba", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "It presents a detailed taxonomy of Agentic RAG architectures, highlights key applications in industries such as healthcare, finance, and education, and examines practical implementation strategies. Additionally, it addresses challenges in scaling these systems, ensuring ethical decision-making, and optimizing performance for real-world applications, while providing detailed insights into frameworks and tools for implementing Agentic RAG1. The GitHub link for this survey is available at: https://github.com/asinghcsu/AgenticRAG-Survey.\n\n# Keywords\n\nLarge Language Models (LLMs) \u00b7 Artificial Intelligence (AI) \u00b7 Natural Language Understanding \u00b7 Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) \u00b7 Agentic RAG \u00b7 Autonomous AI Agents \u00b7 Reflection \u00b7 Planning \u00b7 Tool Use \u00b7 Multi-Agent Collaboration \u00b7 Agentic Patterns \u00b7 Contextual Understanding \u00b7 Dynamic Adaptability \u00b7 Scalability \u00b7 Real-Time Data Retrieval \u00b7 Taxonomy of Agentic RAG \u00b7 Healthcare Applications \u00b7 Finance Applications \u00b7 Educational Applications \u00b7 Ethical AI Decision-Making \u00b7 Performance Optimization \u00b7 Multi-Step Reasoning\n\n1GitHub link: https://github.com/asinghcsu/AgenticRAG-Survey\n---\n# 1 Introduction\n\nLarge Language Models (LLMs) [1, 2] [3], such as OpenAI\u2019s GPT-4, Google\u2019s PaLM, and Meta\u2019s LLaMA, have significantly transformed artificial intelligence (AI) with their ability to generate human-like text and perform complex natural language processing tasks. These models have driven innovation across diverse domains, including conversational agents [4], automated content creation, and real-time translation. Recent advancements have extended their capabilities to multimodal tasks, such as text-to-image and text-to-video generation [5], enabling the creation and editing of videos and images from detailed prompts [6], which broadens the potential applications of generative AI.\n\nDespite these advancements, LLMs face significant limitations due to their reliance on static pre-training data. This reliance often results in outdated information, hallucinated responses [7], and an inability to adapt to dynamic, real-world scenarios. These challenges emphasize the need for systems that can integrate real-time data and dynamically refine responses to maintain contextual relevance and accuracy.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 1910, "end_char_idx": 4170, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "234f6c5b-b5f6-4188-8e38-9bb77854e3b2", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the concept of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (Agentic RAG), highlighting its significance in addressing challenges faced by traditional Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Challenges in AI Systems**: Emphasizes the need for systems that can integrate real-time data and dynamically refine responses for contextual relevance and accuracy.\n\n2. **Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)**: Describes RAG as a solution that combines the generative capabilities of large language models (LLMs) with external retrieval mechanisms to enhance response relevance and timeliness.\n\n3. **Limitations of Traditional RAG**: Points out the linear and static design of traditional RAG workflows, which limits complex reasoning and contextual understanding.\n\n4. **Evolution of Agents**: Discusses modern agents, including LLM-powered and mobile agents, which enhance AI capabilities through perception, reasoning, and task execution.\n\n5. **Agentic Patterns and Workflows**: Introduces agentic patterns (reflection, planning, tool use, multi-agent collaboration) and workflows (prompt chaining, routing, parallelization, orchestrator-worker models, evaluator-optimizer) that optimize task execution.\n\n6. **Integration of Agents in RAG**: Explains how the convergence of RAG and agentic intelligence leads to Agentic RAG, which allows for dynamic retrieval strategies and iterative refinement.\n\n7. **Applications and Benefits of Agentic RAG**: Highlights the advantages of Agentic RAG in precision and adaptability, particularly in complex problem-solving scenarios.\n\nThe section serves as an overview of the foundational principles, taxonomy, and applications of Agentic RAG, indicating its potential impact across various domains."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "24165315-e7ed-4320-86dd-956c599ca07d", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "5b71f67910da967d9265827e50daaf67987fd88a8d6f3a964222c121924a86ae", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "34c35f9c-46c6-4c43-8bd0-c6793ea2ae85", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "9eeed31218fb03b818ee402185323b40dd841187af2108f5efd2faba7e0c4e89", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "These challenges emphasize the need for systems that can integrate real-time data and dynamically refine responses to maintain contextual relevance and accuracy.\n\nRetrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) [8, 9] emerged as a promising solution to these challenges. By combining the generative capabilities of LLMs with external retrieval mechanisms [10], RAG systems enhance the relevance and timeliness of responses. These systems retrieve real-time information from sources such as knowledge bases [11], APIs, or the web, effectively bridging the gap between static training data and the demands of dynamic applications. However, traditional RAG workflows remain limited by their linear and static design, which restricts their ability to perform complex multi-step reasoning, integrate deep contextual understanding, and iteratively refine responses.\n\nThe evolution of agents [12] has significantly enhanced the capabilities of AI systems. Modern agents, including LLM-powered and mobile agents [13], are intelligent entities capable of perceiving, reasoning, and autonomously executing tasks. These agents leverage agentic patterns, such as reflection [14], planning [15], tool use, and multi-agent collaboration [16], to enhance decision-making and adaptability.\n\nFurthermore, these agents employ agentic workflow patterns [12, 13], such as prompt chaining, routing, parallelization, orchestrator-worker models, and evaluator-optimizer, to structure and optimize task execution. By integrating these patterns, Agentic RAG systems can efficiently manage dynamic workflows and address complex problem-solving scenarios. The convergence of RAG and agentic intelligence has given rise to Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (Agentic RAG) [14], a paradigm that integrates agents into the RAG pipeline. Agentic RAG enables dynamic retrieval strategies, contextual understanding, and iterative refinement [15], allowing for adaptive and efficient information processing. Unlike traditional RAG, Agentic RAG employs autonomous agents to orchestrate retrieval, filter relevant information, and refine responses, excelling in scenarios requiring precision and adaptability. The overview of Agentic RAG is in figure 1.\n\nThis survey explores the foundational principles, taxonomy, and applications of Agentic RAG.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 4009, "end_char_idx": 6313, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "34c35f9c-46c6-4c43-8bd0-c6793ea2ae85", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section provides an overview of the document titled \"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education.\" It discusses the foundational principles, taxonomy, and applications of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), highlighting various paradigms such as Na\u00efve RAG, Modular RAG, and Graph RAG. \n\nKey topics include:\n- The evolution of RAG systems and their limitations.\n- Principles of agentic intelligence and agentic patterns.\n- A taxonomy of Agentic RAG frameworks, including single-agent, multi-agent, and graph-based systems.\n- Comparative analysis of these frameworks.\n- Applications of Agentic RAG in healthcare, finance, and education.\n- Implementation strategies, benchmarks, and ethical considerations.\n\nThe structure of the paper is outlined, detailing sections that cover the foundations of RAG, its overview, and the significance of combining generative capabilities with real-time data retrieval to enhance the accuracy and relevance of outputs."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "234f6c5b-b5f6-4188-8e38-9bb77854e3b2", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "b1109057bcb9aa410fdc46e4735a058319f0f943044ea48d089e4bec9cde3d20", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "77214e75-72b0-49e8-bf6a-efb07fd84bc6", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "367fb9de5dabea01ea938820462f73ccdb497863345837965ae491d93d6e030a", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "The overview of Agentic RAG is in figure 1.\n\nThis survey explores the foundational principles, taxonomy, and applications of Agentic RAG. It provides a comprehensive overview of RAG paradigms, such as Na\u00efve RAG, Modular RAG, and Graph RAG [16], alongside their evolution into Agentic RAG systems. Key contributions include a detailed taxonomy of Agentic RAG frameworks, applications across domains such as healthcare [17, 18], finance, and education [19], and insights into implementation strategies, benchmarks, and ethical considerations.\n\nThe structure of this paper is as follows: Section 2 introduces RAG and its evolution, highlighting the limitations of traditional approaches. Section 3 elaborates on the principles of agentic intelligence and agentic patterns. Section 4 elaborates agentic workflow patterns. Section 5 provides a taxonomy of Agentic RAG systems, including single-agent, multi-agent, and graph-based frameworks. Section 6 provides comparative analysis of Agentic RAG frameworks. Section 7 examines applications of Agentic RAG, while Section 8 discusses implementation tools and frameworks. Section 9 focuses on benchmarks and dataset, and Section 10 concludes with future directions for Agentic RAG systems.\n\n# 2 Foundations of Retrieval-Augmented Generation\n\n# 2.1 Overview of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)\n\nRetrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) represents a significant advancement in the field of artificial intelligence, combining the generative capabilities of Large Language Models (LLMs) with real-time data retrieval. While LLMs have demonstrated remarkable capabilities in natural language processing, their reliance on static pre-trained data often results in outdated or incomplete responses. RAG addresses this limitation by dynamically retrieving relevant information from external sources and incorporating it into the generative process, enabling contextually accurate and up-to-date outputs.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 6176, "end_char_idx": 8114, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "77214e75-72b0-49e8-bf6a-efb07fd84bc6", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the concept of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) and its evolution, particularly focusing on \"Agentic RAG.\" Key topics include:\n\n1. **RAG Overview**: RAG enhances generative processes by dynamically retrieving relevant information from external sources, leading to contextually accurate and up-to-date outputs.\n\n2. **Framework and Stack**: Tools and frameworks associated with RAG include Langraph, Llamalndex, AG2 (AutoGen), Semantic Kernel, Crew AI, Amazon Bedrock, and OpenAI Swarm.\n\n3. **Challenges and Limitations**: RAG faces issues such as hallucinations, inaccuracies, limited contextual integration, static workflows, and lack of adaptability.\n\n4. **Benefits of Agentic RAG**: Advantages include enhanced decision-making, multi-step reasoning, and iterative refinement.\n\n5. **Core Components of RAG**: The architecture consists of three main components:\n   - **Retrieval**: Queries external data sources for relevant information.\n   - **Augmentation**: Processes and summarizes retrieved data.\n   - **Generation**: Combines retrieved information with pre-trained knowledge to produce coherent responses.\n\n6. **Evolution of RAG Paradigms**: The development of RAG has been driven by the need for contextual accuracy, scalability, and multi-step reasoning in complex real-world applications.\n\n7. **RAG Paradigm Table**: A table outlines different task roles, memory types, and workflows associated with various RAG models, including Naive RAG, Modular RAG, and Graph RAG.\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the importance of RAG in dynamic AI systems across various sectors, including healthcare, finance, and education."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "34c35f9c-46c6-4c43-8bd0-c6793ea2ae85", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "5d00448445e99d1a2316149b3e3a21b7ca9719035ac35fcf61c57d79b80f7ed8", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "b04d578f-ad06-49fc-8dee-5f9e73ed50a3", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "5ab1409d266fe9363fd2e6095e9ec56c6ff4c5d1e5e5c06c1b8fa49e6219f376", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "RAG addresses this limitation by dynamically retrieving relevant information from external sources and incorporating it into the generative process, enabling contextually accurate and up-to-date outputs.\n---\n# Framework and Stack\n\nLangraph\nLlamalndex\nAG2 (AutoGen)\nSemantic Kernel\nCrew Al\nAmazon Bedrock\nOpen Al Swarm\n# RAG Challenges & Limitations\n\n# Agentic RAG\n\n# Agentic RAG Benefits & Advantages\n\n- Enhanced Decision-Making\n- Multi-Step Reasoning & Iterative Refinement\n\n# Hallucinations & Inaccuracies\n\n- Limited Contextual Integration\n- Static Workflow\n- Lack Adaptability\n\n# Tools\n\n- Planning\n- Real-Time Data Integration\n- Adaptive Learning & Context Awareness\n- Improved Accuracy\n- Reduced Hallucinations\n\n# RAG Paradigm\n\n|Task Role|Memory|Single Router|Multi-Agent|\n|---|---|---|---|\n|Reflection|Agentic Pattern|Planning|Hierarchical|\n|Naive RAG|Advanced RAG|Multi-Agents|Tools|\n|Modular RAG|Agentic Workflow Pattern|Prompt Chaining|Routing|\n|Graph RAG|Orchestrator-workers|Parallelization|Agentic Document Workflow|\n\nFigure 1: An Overview of Agentic RAG\n\n# Core Components of RAG\n\nThe architecture of RAG systems integrates three primary components (Figure 2):\n\n- Retrieval: Responsible for querying external data sources such as knowledge bases, APIs, or vector databases. Advanced retrievers leverage dense vector search and transformer-based models to improve retrieval precision and semantic relevance.\n- Augmentation: Processes retrieved data, extracting and summarizing the most relevant information to align with the query context.\n- Generation: Combines retrieved information with the LLM\u2019s pre-trained knowledge to generate coherent, contextually appropriate responses.\n\n# Evolution of RAG Paradigms\n\nThe field of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) has evolved significantly to address the increasing complexity of real-world applications, where contextual accuracy, scalability, and multi-step reasoning are critical.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 7911, "end_char_idx": 9852, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "b04d578f-ad06-49fc-8dee-5f9e73ed50a3", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the evolution of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, highlighting their transition from simple keyword-based retrieval to more sophisticated and adaptive systems. It outlines the progression of RAG paradigms, specifically focusing on Na\u00efve RAG and its characteristics, strengths, and limitations.\n\nKey Topics:\n1. **Evolution of RAG Systems**: The transition from basic keyword-based retrieval to advanced systems capable of integrating diverse data sources and autonomous decision-making.\n2. **RAG Paradigms**: The section introduces various stages of RAG development, including Na\u00efve RAG, Advanced RAG, Modular RAG, Graph RAG, and Agentic RAG.\n3. **Na\u00efve RAG**: Described as the foundational implementation of RAG, characterized by a simple retrieve-read workflow using keyword-based retrieval techniques (e.g., TF-IDF, BM25) and static datasets.\n\nKey Entities:\n- **Na\u00efve RAG**: The basic form of RAG that relies on keyword matching and has limitations in contextual awareness, output coherence, and scalability.\n- **Retrieval Techniques**: Methods like TF-IDF and BM25 used for document retrieval.\n- **Limitations of Na\u00efve RAG**: Issues such as lack of contextual awareness, fragmented outputs, and scalability challenges.\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the importance of Na\u00efve RAG as a proof-of-concept for integrating retrieval with generation, setting the stage for more advanced RAG systems."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "77214e75-72b0-49e8-bf6a-efb07fd84bc6", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "457816e758dffec97a72625e5f5c1c10e932cb1437aa025c4976c033c770870b", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "7c45a6f0-b83f-408d-bc76-471b0c426841", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "769e86f4e4e4392c26d4dc094b415622926fcb18e5dd92ed0c426be20198a334", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "What began as simple keyword-based retrieval has transitioned into sophisticated, modular, and adaptive systems capable of integrating diverse data sources and autonomous decision-making processes. This evolution underscores the growing need for RAG systems to handle complex queries efficiently and effectively.\n\nThis section examines the progression of RAG paradigms, presenting key stages of development\u2014Na\u00efve RAG, Advanced RAG, Modular RAG, Graph RAG, and Agentic RAG alongside their defining characteristics, strengths, and\n---\n# 2.3.1 Na\u00efve RAG\n\nNa\u00efve RAG [20] represents the foundational implementation of retrieval-augmented generation. Figure 3 illustrates the simple retrieve-read workflow of Naive RAG, focusing on keyword-based retrieval and static datasets. These systems rely on simple keyword-based retrieval techniques, such as TF-IDF and BM25, to fetch documents from static datasets. The retrieved documents are then used to augment the language model\u2019s generative capabilities.\n\n|Additional Documents|User Query|\n|---|---|\n|Encode|Encode|\n|Embedding Model|LLM|\n|Vector database|Similar Documents|\n|Similarity Search|Query|\n\nNa\u00efve RAG is characterized by its simplicity and ease of implementation, making it suitable for tasks involving fact-based queries with minimal contextual complexity. However, it suffers from several limitations:\n\n- Lack of Contextual Awareness: Retrieved documents often fail to capture the semantic nuances of the query due to reliance on lexical matching rather than semantic understanding.\n- Fragmented Outputs: The absence of advanced preprocessing or contextual integration often leads to disjointed or overly generic responses.\n- Scalability Issues: Keyword-based retrieval techniques struggle with large datasets, often failing to identify the most relevant information.\n\nDespite these limitations, Na\u00efve RAG systems provided a critical proof-of-concept for integrating retrieval with generation, laying the foundation for more sophisticated paradigms.\n\n# 2.3.2 Advanced RAG\n\nAdvanced RAG [20] systems build upon the limitations of Na\u00efve RAG by incorporating semantic understanding and enhanced retrieval techniques. Figure 4 highlights the semantic enhancements in retrieval and the iterative, context-aware pipeline of Advanced RAG.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 9853, "end_char_idx": 12138, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "7c45a6f0-b83f-408d-bc76-471b0c426841", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses advancements in Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, focusing on two specific paradigms: Modular RAG and Graph RAG.\n\n### Key Topics:\n\n1. **Advanced RAG**:\n   - Emphasizes semantic enhancements in retrieval.\n   - Utilizes dense retrieval models like Dense Passage Retrieval (DPR) and neural ranking algorithms for improved precision.\n\n2. **Modular RAG**:\n   - Represents a flexible and customizable evolution of RAG.\n   - Decomposes the retrieval and generation pipeline into independent, reusable components.\n   - Key innovations include:\n     - **Hybrid Retrieval Strategies**: Combines sparse and dense retrieval methods for improved accuracy.\n     - **Tool Integration**: Incorporates external APIs and databases for specialized tasks.\n     - **Composable Pipelines**: Allows independent replacement and enhancement of components for adaptability to specific use cases.\n\n   - Example: A Modular RAG system for financial analytics that retrieves live stock prices, analyzes trends, and generates investment insights.\n\n3. **Graph RAG**:\n   - Extends traditional RAG by integrating graph-based data structures.\n   - Enhances multi-hop reasoning and contextual enrichment through relationships and hierarchies in graph data.\n   - Characterized by its ability to capture and reason over relationships between entities.\n\n### Entities:\n- **Dense Passage Retrieval (DPR)**: A dense retrieval model used in Advanced RAG.\n- **BM25**: A sparse retrieval method mentioned in the context of hybrid strategies.\n- **APIs and Databases**: External tools integrated into Modular RAG for specialized tasks.\n- **Graph Data Structures**: Used in Graph RAG to enhance generative outputs through relational understanding.\n\nOverall, the section highlights the evolution of RAG systems towards greater flexibility, customization, and relational reasoning capabilities."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "b04d578f-ad06-49fc-8dee-5f9e73ed50a3", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "49d244eef7b724111227f6e73f18787630c008b25f928a0df1f870a65de72f1f", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "02350a13-aa26-4ca3-8509-4562c633ed34", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "438d9c57b6cc3a1b049da92a098e811c6a3fec6b76f5061bed4b087341b7019f", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Figure 4 highlights the semantic enhancements in retrieval and the iterative, context-aware pipeline of Advanced RAG. These systems leverage dense retrieval models, such as Dense Passage Retrieval (DPR), and neural ranking algorithms to improve retrieval precision.\n\nKey features of Advanced RAG include:\n---\n# 2.3.3 Modular RAG\n\nModular RAG [20] represents the latest evolution in RAG paradigms, emphasizing flexibility and customization. These systems decompose the retrieval and generation pipeline into independent, reusable components, enabling domain-specific optimization and task adaptability. Figure 5 demonstrates the modular architecture, showcasing hybrid retrieval strategies, composable pipelines, and external tool integration.\n\n# Key innovations in Modular RAG include:\n\n- Hybrid Retrieval Strategies: Combining sparse retrieval methods (e.g., a sparse encoder-BM25) with dense retrieval techniques [21] (e.g., DPR - Dense Passage Retrieval) to maximize accuracy across diverse query types.\n- Tool Integration: Incorporating external APIs, databases, or computational tools to handle specialized tasks, such as real-time data analysis or domain-specific computations.\n- Composable Pipelines: Modular RAG enables retrievers, generators, and other components to be replaced, enhanced, or reconfigured independently, allowing high adaptability to specific use cases.\n\nFor instance, a Modular RAG system designed for financial analytics might retrieve live stock prices via APIs, analyze historical trends using dense retrieval, and generate actionable investment insights through a tailored language model. This modularity and customization make Modular RAG ideal for complex, multi-domain tasks, offering both scalability and precision.\n---\n# 2.3.4 Graph RAG\n\nGraph RAG [16] extends traditional Retrieval-Augmented Generation systems by integrating graph-based data structures as illustrated in Figure 6. These systems leverage the relationships and hierarchies within graph data to enhance multi-hop reasoning and contextual enrichment. By incorporating graph-based retrieval, Graph RAG enables richer and more accurate generative outputs, particularly for tasks requiring relational understanding.\n\nGraph RAG is characterized by its ability to:\n\n- Node Connectivity: Captures and reasons over relationships between entities.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 12021, "end_char_idx": 14361, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "02350a13-aa26-4ca3-8509-4562c633ed34", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses two advanced paradigms within Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems: Graph RAG and Agentic RAG.\n\n### Key Topics:\n\n1. **Graph RAG**:\n   - **Characteristics**:\n     - Node Connectivity: Understanding relationships between entities.\n     - Hierarchical Knowledge Management: Managing both structured and unstructured data.\n     - Context Enrichment: Enhancing understanding through graph pathways.\n   - **Limitations**:\n     - Limited Scalability: Challenges with extensive data sources.\n     - Data Dependency: Requires high-quality graph data for effective outputs.\n     - Complexity of Integration: Difficulties in merging graph data with unstructured systems.\n   - **Applications**: Particularly useful in healthcare diagnostics, legal research, and areas requiring structured relationship reasoning.\n\n2. **Agentic RAG**:\n   - **Characteristics**:\n     - Autonomous Decision-Making: Agents manage retrieval strategies independently.\n     - Iterative Refinement: Feedback loops enhance retrieval accuracy.\n     - Workflow Optimization: Efficient task orchestration for real-time applications.\n   - **Challenges**:\n     - Coordination Complexity: Requires sophisticated management of agent interactions.\n     - Computational Overhead: Increased resource demands due to multiple agents.\n     - Scalability Limitations: Dynamic nature can strain resources under high query volumes.\n   - **Applications**: Effective in customer support, financial analytics, and adaptive learning platforms where adaptability and precision are critical.\n\n3. **Challenges of Traditional RAG Systems**: The section briefly mentions that traditional RAG systems have enhanced Large Language Models (LLMs) through real-time data retrieval but does not elaborate on specific challenges.\n\n### Entities:\n- **Graph RAG**: A type of RAG focused on graph structures.\n- **Agentic RAG**: A paradigm featuring autonomous agents for dynamic decision-making.\n- **Applications**: Healthcare, legal research, customer support, financial analytics, adaptive learning.\n\nOverall, the section highlights the advancements and challenges of these two RAG paradigms, emphasizing their potential applications across various domains."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "7c45a6f0-b83f-408d-bc76-471b0c426841", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "574306a28b10fb3a339f03f9870b283c097ebd9b38c72ec1f02fb6a4e69b0f19", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "9e01fbda-623e-4274-80fc-ceb6bc68b818", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "78a2f34ccf1c44c80f784e09c4c40c8c5248b852cc8f724c06b8672f926e0fea", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Graph RAG is characterized by its ability to:\n\n- Node Connectivity: Captures and reasons over relationships between entities.\n- Hierarchical Knowledge Management: Handles structured and unstructured data through graph-based hierarchies.\n- Context Enrichment: Adds relational understanding by leveraging graph-based pathways.\n\nHowever, Graph RAG has some limitations:\n\n- Limited Scalability: The reliance on graph structures can restrict scalability, especially with extensive data sources.\n- Data Dependency: High-quality graph data is essential for meaningful outputs, limiting its applicability in unstructured or poorly annotated datasets.\n- Complexity of Integration: Integrating graph data with unstructured retrieval systems increases design and implementation complexity.\n\nGraph RAG is well-suited for applications such as healthcare diagnostics, legal research, and other domains where reasoning over structured relationships is crucial.\n\n# 2.3.5 Agentic RAG\n\nAgentic RAG represents a paradigm shift by introducing autonomous agents capable of dynamic decision-making and workflow optimization. Unlike static systems, Agentic RAG employs iterative refinement and adaptive retrieval strategies to address complex, real-time, and multi-domain queries. This paradigm leverages the modularity of retrieval and generation processes while introducing agent-based autonomy.\n---\n# Key characteristics of Agentic RAG include:\n\n- Autonomous Decision-Making: Agents independently evaluate and manage retrieval strategies based on query complexity.\n- Iterative Refinement: Incorporates feedback loops to improve retrieval accuracy and response relevance.\n- Workflow Optimization: Dynamically orchestrates tasks, enabling efficiency in real-time applications.\n\nDespite its advancements, Agentic RAG faces some challenges:\n\n- Coordination Complexity: Managing interactions between agents requires sophisticated orchestration mechanisms.\n- Computational Overhead: The use of multiple agents increases resource requirements for complex workflows.\n- Scalability Limitations: While scalable, the dynamic nature of the system can strain computational resources for high query volumes.\n\nAgentic RAG excels in domains like customer support, financial analytics, and adaptive learning platforms, where dynamic adaptability and contextual precision are paramount.\n\n# 2.4 Challenges and Limitations of Traditional RAG Systems\n\nTraditional Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems have significantly expanded the capabilities of Large Language Models (LLMs) by integrating real-time data retrieval.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 14236, "end_char_idx": 16821, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "9e01fbda-623e-4274-80fc-ceb6bc68b818", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the challenges faced by Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems in real-world applications, particularly focusing on three main limitations: contextual integration, multi-step reasoning, and scalability and latency issues. \n\nKey Topics:\n1. **Contextual Integration**: RAG systems struggle to effectively incorporate retrieved information into generated responses, leading to fragmented or generic outputs.\n2. **Multi-step Reasoning**: The systems face difficulties in performing complex reasoning tasks that require multiple steps.\n3. **Scalability and Latency**: Issues related to the ability of RAG systems to scale effectively and respond in a timely manner.\n\nEntities:\n- **RAG Systems**: The primary subject of the discussion, referring to systems that combine retrieval and generation capabilities.\n- **Alzheimer\u2019s Research**: An example topic used to illustrate the limitations of RAG systems in synthesizing information.\n- **Sustainable Practices**: Another example topic highlighting the challenges in retrieving and contextualizing relevant information for specific scenarios in agriculture.\n\nOverall, the excerpt emphasizes the need for improvements in RAG systems to enhance their effectiveness in complex applications across various fields."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "02350a13-aa26-4ca3-8509-4562c633ed34", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "62e0ad7b14cd103e5fa5a1e12ca33e48c7538902ef724c2b1e6fc94e91a93419", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "7ec09d56-e4ac-40b6-9fda-b0e893413cfd", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "f69dd055d22d3b17929a04c1a14efcab701502fd2d0dc5ee06058d2480f8feef", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "However, these systems still face critical challenges that hinder their effectiveness in complex, real-world applications. The most notable limitations revolve around contextual integration, multi-step reasoning, and scalability and latency issues.\n\n# 2.4.1 Contextual Integration\n\nEven when RAG systems successfully retrieve relevant information, they often struggle to seamlessly incorporate it into generated responses. The static nature of retrieval pipelines and limited contextual awareness lead to fragmented, inconsistent, or overly generic outputs.\n\nExample: A query such as, \"What are the latest advancements in Alzheimer\u2019s research and their implications for early-stage treatment?\" might yield relevant research papers and medical guidelines. However, traditional RAG systems often fail to synthesize these findings into a coherent explanation that connects the new treatments to specific patient scenarios. Similarly, for a query like, \"What are the best sustainable practices for small-scale agriculture in arid regions?\", traditional systems might retrieve documents on general agricultural methods but overlook critical sustainability practices tailored to arid environments.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 16822, "end_char_idx": 18013, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "7ec09d56-e4ac-40b6-9fda-b0e893413cfd", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses various paradigms of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, highlighting their key features, strengths, and limitations. It emphasizes the challenges faced by traditional RAG systems in handling complex queries that require multi-step reasoning and the integration of diverse information sources. \n\nKey topics include:\n\n1. **Comparative Analysis of RAG Paradigms**:\n   - **Na\u00efve RAG**: Simple keyword-based retrieval methods suitable for fact-based queries.\n   - **Advanced RAG**: Utilizes dense retrieval models and hybrid approaches for improved precision and contextual relevance.\n   - **Modular RAG**: Focuses on tool integration and domain-specific pipelines, offering scalability and relational reasoning.\n   - **Graph RAG**: Employs multi-hop reasoning and contextual enrichment, effective for structured data tasks.\n   - **Agentic RAG**: Features autonomous agents and dynamic decision-making, adaptable for real-time changes and multi-domain tasks.\n\n2. **Multi-Step Reasoning**: Highlights the need for RAG systems to synthesize information across multiple steps for complex queries, which traditional systems often struggle to achieve.\n\n3. **Scalability and Latency Issues**: Discusses the computational challenges posed by increasing data volumes, leading to latency that affects the timeliness of responses in real-time applications.\n\nOverall, the section underscores the evolution of RAG systems towards more sophisticated and adaptable frameworks capable of addressing complex, real-world queries effectively."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "9e01fbda-623e-4274-80fc-ceb6bc68b818", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "4bbfffef462f3ba6bde16d7c50c7213e8b9905bd503e3d3bec87124392d0250d", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "c64169e7-2928-40f2-a60e-e26b97cd7832", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "d2616682adba5f0d8463dcad9fc64e2cf5f302bc01d8a801538736b1f6addfc0", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "\", traditional systems might retrieve documents on general agricultural methods but overlook critical sustainability practices tailored to arid environments.\n---\n# Table 1: Comparative Analysis of RAG Paradigms\n\n|Paradigm|Key Features|Strengths|\n|---|---|---|\n|Na\u00efve RAG|\u2022 Keyword-based retrieval (e.g., TF-IDF, BM25)|\u2022 Simple and easy to implement \u2022 Suitable for fact-based queries|\n|Advanced RAG|\u2022 Dense retrieval models (e.g., DPR) \u2022 Neural ranking and re-ranking \u2022 Multi-hop retrieval \u2022 Hybrid retrieval (sparse and dense)|\u2022 High precision retrieval \u2022 Improved contextual relevance \u2022 High flexibility and customization|\n|Modular RAG|\u2022 Tool and API integration \u2022 Composable, domain-specific pipelines \u2022 Integration of graph-based structures|\u2022 Suitable for diverse applications \u2022 Scalable \u2022 Relational reasoning capabilities|\n|Graph RAG|\u2022 Multi-hop reasoning \u2022 Contextual enrichment via nodes|\u2022 Mitigates hallucinations \u2022 Ideal for structured data tasks|\n|Agentic RAG|\u2022 Autonomous agents \u2022 Dynamic decision-making \u2022 Iterative refinement and workflow optimization|\u2022 Adaptable to real-time changes \u2022 Scalable for multi-domain tasks \u2022 High accuracy|\n\n# 2.4.2 Multi-Step Reasoning\n\nMany real-world queries require iterative or multi-hop reasoning\u2014retrieving and synthesizing information across multiple steps. Traditional RAG systems are often ill-equipped to refine retrieval based on intermediate insights or user feedback, resulting in incomplete or disjointed responses.\n\nExample: A complex query like, \"What lessons from renewable energy policies in Europe can be applied to developing nations, and what are the potential economic impacts?\" demands the orchestration of multiple types of information, including policy data, contextualization for developing regions, and economic analysis. Traditional RAG systems typically fail to connect these disparate elements into a cohesive response.\n\n# 2.4.3 Scalability and Latency Issues\n\nAs the volume of external data sources grows, querying and ranking large datasets becomes increasingly computationally intensive. This results in significant latency, which undermines the system\u2019s ability to provide timely responses in real-time applications.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 17856, "end_char_idx": 20049, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "c64169e7-2928-40f2-a60e-e26b97cd7832", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the concept of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), highlighting its significance in improving the performance of AI systems in dynamic environments such as healthcare, finance, and education. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Latency Issues**: Traditional RAG systems face significant latency, which affects their ability to provide timely responses in real-time applications, particularly in time-sensitive scenarios like financial analytics and customer support.\n\n2. **Agentic RAG**: This represents a paradigm shift from traditional RAG systems by integrating autonomous agents that enable dynamic decision-making, iterative reasoning, and adaptive retrieval strategies. Agentic RAG aims to overcome the limitations of static workflows and enhance the system's ability to handle complex, multi-domain tasks.\n\n3. **Core Principles of Agentic Intelligence**: The foundation of Agentic RAG is built on agentic intelligence, which allows for greater adaptability and precision through the use of autonomous agents.\n\n4. **Components of an AI Agent**: The section outlines the essential components of an AI agent, including:\n   - **Large Language Model (LLM)**: Acts as the reasoning engine and dialogue interface.\n   - **Memory**: Consists of short-term memory for immediate context and long-term memory for accumulated knowledge and experiences.\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the evolution of RAG systems towards more sophisticated, efficient, and context-aware AI applications through the implementation of agentic intelligence."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "7ec09d56-e4ac-40b6-9fda-b0e893413cfd", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "dd2a02a47f2464099df25d2eae28d3b31d056919f4fc1dfe5e769ed40fa2a6b5", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "b2c995a3-beb6-433f-ab15-34be5c151059", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "1e548b16c53f97cad0e5948d958a1093af584011b3d56dadbcd4996574621d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "This results in significant latency, which undermines the system\u2019s ability to provide timely responses in real-time applications.\n\nExample: In time-sensitive settings such as financial analytics or live customer support, delays caused by querying multiple databases or processing large document sets can hinder the system\u2019s overall utility. For example, a delay in retrieving market trends during high-frequency trading could result in missed opportunities.\n\n# 2.5 Agentic RAG: A Paradigm Shift\n\nTraditional RAG systems, with their static workflows and limited adaptability, often struggle to handle dynamic, multi-step reasoning and complex real-world tasks. These limitations have spurred the integration of agentic intelligence.\n---\nresulting in Agentic RAG. By incorporating autonomous agents capable of dynamic decision-making, iterative reasoning, and adaptive retrieval strategies, Agentic RAG builds on the modularity of earlier paradigms while overcoming their inherent constraints. This evolution enables more complex, multi-domain tasks to be addressed with enhanced precision and contextual understanding, positioning Agentic RAG as a cornerstone for next-generation AI applications. In particular, Agentic RAG systems reduce latency through optimized workflows and refine outputs iteratively, tackling the very challenges that have historically hindered traditional RAG\u2019s scalability and effectiveness.\n\n# 3 Core Principles and Background of Agentic Intelligence\n\nAgentic Intelligence forms the foundation of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, enabling them to transcend the static and reactive nature of traditional RAG. By integrating autonomous agents capable of dynamic decision-making, iterative reasoning, and collaborative workflows, Agentic RAG systems exhibit enhanced adaptability and precision. This section explores the core principles underpinning agentic intelligence.\n\n# Components of an AI Agent. In essence, an AI agent comprises (Figure. 7):\n\n- LLM (with defined Role and Task): Serves as the agent\u2019s primary reasoning engine and dialogue interface. It interprets user queries, generates responses, and maintains coherence.\n- Memory (Short-Term and Long-Term): Captures context and relevant data across interactions. Short-term memory [22] tracks immediate conversation state, while long-term memory [22] stores accumulated knowledge and agent experiences.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 19920, "end_char_idx": 22326, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "b2c995a3-beb6-433f-ab15-34be5c151059", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the principles and methodologies of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, focusing on the roles of memory, planning, and reflection in enhancing the capabilities of AI agents. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Memory Types**:\n   - **Short-term Memory**: Tracks immediate conversation states.\n   - **Long-term Memory**: Stores accumulated knowledge and agent experiences.\n\n2. **Planning**:\n   - Involves reflection and self-critique to guide the agent's reasoning process.\n   - Essential for breaking down complex tasks into manageable subtasks.\n   - Enables dynamic adaptation and flexibility in decision-making, particularly in uncertain scenarios.\n\n3. **Tools**:\n   - Includes vector search, web search, and APIs, which expand the agent's capabilities beyond mere text generation.\n\n4. **Agentic Patterns**:\n   - Provide structured methodologies for agent behavior in RAG systems, allowing for dynamic adaptation, planning, and collaboration.\n\n5. **Reflection**:\n   - A foundational design pattern that allows agents to evaluate and refine their outputs through self-feedback mechanisms.\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the importance of these components in enabling AI agents to perform complex, real-world tasks effectively and adaptively."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "c64169e7-2928-40f2-a60e-e26b97cd7832", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "0d365607c5e6f58478c737e9b426d2c484cd19fa6740dd1606cd2d2ae4ff3ece", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "967b07bc-2031-48b5-8cf6-3f14723a46a4", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "6b604bc892f1c778022dbbf65c88442a29a93bdff9672ac15a247e2866e9b187", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Short-term memory [22] tracks immediate conversation state, while long-term memory [22] stores accumulated knowledge and agent experiences.\n- Planning (Reflection & Self-Critique): Guides the agent\u2019s iterative reasoning process through reflection, query routing, or self-critique [23], ensuring that complex tasks are broken down effectively [24].\n- Tools (Vector Search, Web Search, APIs, etc.): Expands the agent\u2019s capabilities beyond text generation, enabling access to external resources, real-time data, or specialized computations.\n\n|Memory| |Short-term|Tools|Vector Search|Data Sources|\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n|Planning|Long-term|Agent|Web Search|API| |\n|Reflection|Self-critics| | | | |\n\nFigure 7: An Overview of AI Agents\n\nAgentic Patterns [25, 26] provide structured methodologies that guide the behavior of agents in Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems. These patterns enable agents to dynamically adapt, plan, and collaborate, ensuring that the system can handle complex, real-world tasks with precision and scalability. Four key patterns underpin agentic workflows:\n\n# 3.1 Reflection\n\nReflection is a foundational design pattern in agentic workflows, enabling agents to iteratively evaluate and refine their outputs. By incorporating self-feedback mechanisms, agents can identify and address errors, inconsistencies, and areas for improvement, enhancing performance across tasks like code generation, text production, and question answering.\n---\n# 3.2 Planning\n\nPlanning [24] is a key design pattern in agentic workflows that enables agents to autonomously decompose complex tasks into smaller, manageable subtasks. This capability is essential for multi-hop reasoning and iterative problem-solving in dynamic and uncertain scenarios as shown in Figure 9a.\n\nBy leveraging planning, agents can dynamically determine the sequence of steps needed to accomplish a larger objective. This adaptability allows agents to handle tasks that cannot be predefined, ensuring flexibility in decision-making. While powerful, Planning can produce less predictable outcomes compared to deterministic workflows like Reflection. Planning is particularly suited for tasks that require dynamic adaptation, where predefined workflows are insufficient.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 22187, "end_char_idx": 24449, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "967b07bc-2031-48b5-8cf6-3f14723a46a4", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses key concepts related to agentic workflows in AI systems, focusing on two main patterns: Planning and Tool Use, as well as the importance of Multi-Agent collaboration.\n\n1. **Planning**: \n   - Planning is highlighted as a powerful but less predictable approach compared to deterministic workflows like Reflection. \n   - It is particularly effective for tasks requiring dynamic adaptation, where predefined workflows may fall short.\n   - The potential for innovative applications across various domains, such as healthcare, finance, and education, is emphasized as the technology evolves.\n\n2. **Tool Use**:\n   - Tool Use allows agents to enhance their capabilities by interacting with external tools, APIs, and computational resources.\n   - This integration enables agents to gather information, perform computations, and manipulate data beyond their pre-trained knowledge.\n   - Modern workflows leverage advancements like GPT-4\u2019s function calling capabilities to create sophisticated systems where agents autonomously select and execute relevant tools.\n   - Challenges in optimizing tool selection, especially in contexts with many options, are noted, with techniques like heuristic-based selection proposed as solutions.\n\n3. **Multi-Agent Collaboration**:\n   - Multi-agent systems facilitate task specialization and parallel processing, improving efficiency and coherence in workflows.\n   - Agents communicate and share intermediate results, allowing for the distribution of subtasks among specialized agents, enhancing scalability and adaptability.\n\nOverall, the section underscores the significance of these patterns in developing dynamic and efficient AI systems capable of handling complex tasks."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "b2c995a3-beb6-433f-ab15-34be5c151059", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "10d1d6bacaf8bc7242c7054d7849664427d3aad5883b39105318426c1b92683f", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "ec660857-c5e5-41f8-a35f-da1566285f10", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "c6fbf02e32e9e2eb2038e187717ad1d8e4b3d7fceee94f6eabb53d413027adcc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "While powerful, Planning can produce less predictable outcomes compared to deterministic workflows like Reflection. Planning is particularly suited for tasks that require dynamic adaptation, where predefined workflows are insufficient. As the technology matures, its potential to drive innovative applications across domains will continue to grow.\n\n# 3.3 Tool Use\n\nTool Use enables agents to extend their capabilities by interacting with external tools, APIs, or computational resources as illustrated in 9b. This pattern allows agents to gather information, perform computations, and manipulate data beyond their pre-trained knowledge. By dynamically integrating tools into workflows, agents can adapt to complex tasks and provide more accurate and contextually relevant outputs.\n\nModern agentic workflows incorporate tool use for a variety of applications, including information retrieval, computational reasoning, and interfacing with external systems. The implementation of this pattern has evolved significantly with advancements like GPT-4\u2019s function calling capabilities and systems capable of managing access to numerous tools. These developments facilitate sophisticated workflows where agents autonomously select and execute the most relevant tools for a given task.\n\nWhile tool use significantly enhances agentic workflows, challenges remain in optimizing the selection of tools, particularly in contexts with a large number of available options. Techniques inspired by retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), such as heuristic-based selection, have been proposed to address this issue.\n\n# 3.4 Multi-Agent\n\nMulti-agent collaboration [29] is a key design pattern in agentic workflows that enables task specialization and parallel processing. Agents communicate and share intermediate results, ensuring the overall workflow remains efficient and coherent. By distributing subtasks among specialized agents, this pattern improves the scalability and adaptability.\n---\n# Response\n\n# User Input\n\n# Response\n\n# Memory Augmented Planning\n\n# Reflection & Refinement\n\n# Task Decomposition\n\n# External Planner\n\n# Plan Selection\n\n# Revised Response\n\n# Environment\n\n# (a) An Overview of Agentic Planning\n\n# (b) An Overview of Tool Use\n\nFigure 9: Overview of Agentic Planning and Tool Use of complex workflows. Multi-agent systems allow developers to decompose intricate tasks into smaller, manageable subtasks assigned to different agents.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 24214, "end_char_idx": 26650, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "ec660857-c5e5-41f8-a35f-da1566285f10", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the concept of multi-agent systems in the context of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG). Key topics include:\n\n1. **Multi-Agent Systems**: These systems allow for the decomposition of complex tasks into smaller subtasks assigned to different agents, enhancing performance and managing complex interactions.\n\n2. **Agent Functionality**: Each agent operates with its own memory and workflow, utilizing tools, reflection, or planning for dynamic problem-solving.\n\n3. **Emerging Frameworks**: New frameworks like AutoGen, Crew AI, and LangGraph are highlighted as innovative solutions for implementing multi-agent collaboration.\n\n4. **Agentic Workflow Patterns**: These patterns are essential for the success of Agentic RAG systems, enabling dynamic adaptation of retrieval and generative strategies to meet real-world demands.\n\n5. **Prompt Chaining**: A specific workflow pattern that enhances accuracy by breaking down complex tasks into sequential subtasks, although it may increase latency.\n\n6. **Use Cases**: The section emphasizes when to use prompt chaining, particularly in scenarios requiring step-by-step reasoning to improve accuracy.\n\nOverall, the excerpt outlines the principles, architectures, and applications of multi-agent systems and their workflows in dynamic AI environments across various fields such as healthcare, finance, and education."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "967b07bc-2031-48b5-8cf6-3f14723a46a4", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "198013a566da0d268723802a7b5b2ac7814a8fa7809b41522b405ff0d216cc8f", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "8e84f652-e1e4-494d-8c97-2a6ee16d2ee2", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "00642151404c29c90939c853cf539230e08370ad3443009d5e36c4f3ba01d174", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Multi-agent systems allow developers to decompose intricate tasks into smaller, manageable subtasks assigned to different agents. This approach not only enhances task performance but also provides a robust framework for managing complex interactions. Each agent operates with its own memory and workflow, which can include the use of tools, reflection, or planning, enabling dynamic and collaborative problem-solving (see Figure 10).\n\nWhile multi-agent collaboration offers significant potential, it is a less predictable design pattern compared to more mature workflows like Reflection and Tool Use. Nevertheless, emerging frameworks such as AutoGen, Crew AI, and LangGraph are providing new avenues for implementing effective multi-agent solutions.\n\n# Query\n\n|Agent 1|Response|\n|---|---|\n|Agent 2|Agent 3|\n\nFigure 10: An Overview of MultiAgent\n\nThese design patterns form the foundation for the success of Agentic RAG systems. By structuring workflows\u2014from simple, sequential steps to more adaptive, collaborative processes\u2014these patterns enable systems to dynamically adapt their retrieval and generative strategies to the diverse and ever-changing demands of real-world environments. Leveraging these patterns, agents are capable of handling iterative, context-aware tasks that significantly exceed the capabilities of traditional RAG systems.\n\n# 4 Agentic Workflow Patterns: Adaptive Strategies for Dynamic Collaboration\n\nAgentic workflow patterns, [12, 13] structure LLM-based applications to optimize performance, accuracy, and efficiency. Different approaches are suitable depending on task complexity and processing requirements.\n---\n# 4.1 Prompt Chaining: Enhancing Accuracy Through Sequential Processing\n\nPrompt chaining [12, 13] decomposes a complex task into multiple steps, where each step builds upon the previous one. This structured approach improves accuracy by simplifying each subtask before moving forward. However, it may increase latency due to sequential processing.\n\nQuery\nLLM\nGate\nLLM\nResponse\nFigure 11: Illustration of Prompt Chaining Workflow\n\nWhen to Use: This workflow is most effective when a task can be broken down into fixed subtasks, each contributing to the final output. It is particularly useful in scenarios where step-by-step reasoning enhances accuracy.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 26521, "end_char_idx": 28816, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "8e84f652-e1e4-494d-8c97-2a6ee16d2ee2", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses various methodologies and workflows in the context of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, emphasizing their applications and benefits in enhancing processing efficiency and accuracy. \n\nKey Topics:\n1. **Step-by-Step Reasoning**: Highlighted as beneficial for improving accuracy in various scenarios.\n2. **Routing**: Involves classifying inputs and directing them to specialized processes to enhance efficiency and response quality. Example applications include categorizing customer service queries.\n3. **Parallelization**: Focuses on dividing tasks into independent processes that run concurrently, thereby reducing latency and improving throughput. It includes two categories: sectioning (independent subtasks) and voting (multiple outputs for accuracy). Example applications include content moderation and code vulnerability analysis.\n4. **Orchestrator-Workers**: Describes a workflow where a central orchestrator model dynamically assigns subtasks to specialized worker models, adapting to varying input complexities. Example applications include modifying files in a codebase and conducting real-time research.\n\nEntities:\n- **Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)**\n- **Routing**\n- **Parallelization**\n- **Orchestrator-Workers**\n- **Applications in Healthcare, Finance, and Education** \n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the importance of these methodologies in optimizing task handling and improving the performance of AI systems across various domains."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "ec660857-c5e5-41f8-a35f-da1566285f10", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "23416590769243e991fba260209b82e9da50bebbad03fbfee5fa9aecef0f3f06", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "44acfe8d-ed52-457f-8cc1-d23232e7509f", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "80956f2c230aa0470b2798ddf99fb0ca65723848e54ff1f26cd8aba30080b627", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "It is particularly useful in scenarios where step-by-step reasoning enhances accuracy.\n\n# Example Applications:\n\n- Generating marketing content in one language and then translating it into another while preserving nuances.\n- Structuring document creation by first generating an outline, verifying its completeness, and then developing the full text.\n\n# 4.2 Routing: Directing Inputs to Specialized Processes\n\nRouting [12, 13] involves classifying an input and directing it to an appropriate specialized prompt or process. This method ensures distinct queries or tasks are handled separately, improving efficiency and response quality.\n\nQuery\nRouter\nLLM\nResponse\nFigure 12: Illustration Routing Workflow\n\nWhen to Use: Ideal for scenarios where different types of input require distinct handling strategies, ensuring optimized performance for each category.\n\n# Example Applications:\n\n- Directing customer service queries into categories such as technical support, refund requests, or general inquiries.\n---\n# 4.3   Parallelization: Speeding Up Processing Through Concurrent Execution\n\nParallelization [12, 13] divides a task into independent processes that run simultaneously, reducing latency and improving throughput. It can be categorized into sectioning (independent subtasks) and voting (multiple outputs for accuracy).\n\nWhen to Use: Useful when tasks can be executed independently to enhance speed or when multiple outputs improve confidence.\n\n# Example Applications:\n\n- Sectioning: Splitting tasks like content moderation, where one model screens input while another generates a response.\n- Voting: Using multiple models to cross-check code for vulnerabilities or analyze content moderation decisions.\n\n# 4.4   Orchestrator-Workers: Dynamic Task Delegation\n\nThis workflow [12, 13] features a central orchestrator model that dynamically breaks tasks into subtasks, assigns them to specialized worker models, and compiles the results. Unlike parallelization, it adapts to varying input complexity.\n\nWhen to Use: Best suited for tasks requiring dynamic decomposition and real-time adaptation, where subtasks are not predefined.\n---\n# Example Applications:\n\n- Automatically modifying multiple files in a codebase based on the nature of requested changes.\n- Conducting real-time research by gathering and synthesizing relevant information from multiple sources.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 28730, "end_char_idx": 31091, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "44acfe8d-ed52-457f-8cc1-d23232e7509f", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the principles and applications of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, focusing on their iterative refinement processes and architectural frameworks. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Example Applications**: \n   - Automating modifications in codebases.\n   - Conducting real-time research by synthesizing information from various sources.\n\n2. **Evaluator-Optimizer Workflow**: \n   - This process involves generating initial outputs and refining them based on feedback, enhancing response quality through iterative cycles.\n\n3. **When to Use**: \n   - The evaluator-optimizer approach is effective when clear evaluation criteria exist and iterative refinement can significantly improve results.\n\n4. **Taxonomy of Agentic RAG Systems**: \n   - RAG systems are categorized into different architectural frameworks, including single-agent architectures, multi-agent systems, and hierarchical agentic architectures, each designed to address specific challenges and optimize performance.\n\n5. **Single-Agent Agentic RAG**: \n   - This architecture features a centralized decision-making system where a single agent manages retrieval, routing, and integration of information, making it suitable for environments with limited tools or data sources.\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the importance of iterative refinement in enhancing output quality and categorizes RAG systems based on their design and complexity."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "8e84f652-e1e4-494d-8c97-2a6ee16d2ee2", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "2512fa4bdf670edf07990056b8241918eb98c2fc0af6b14f4022e2b7178e2262", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "1c8c54ad-874f-4696-a585-24b5211c7c2e", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "6279a5d90a1599a96450120ed0b4b045b6f2c3f6ef7a51b7464e8bd8d8e9acb7", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "---\n# Example Applications:\n\n- Automatically modifying multiple files in a codebase based on the nature of requested changes.\n- Conducting real-time research by gathering and synthesizing relevant information from multiple sources.\n\n# 4.5 Evaluator-Optimizer: Refining Output Through Iteration\n\nThe evaluator-optimizer [12, 13] workflow iteratively improves content by generating an initial output and refining it based on feedback from an evaluation model.\n\n|Query|LM|LLM|Accepted|Response|\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n|Rejected + Feedback|Rejected + Feedback|Rejected + Feedback|Rejected + Feedback|Rejected + Feedback|\n\nFigure 15: Illustration of Evaluator-Optimizer Workflow\n\n# When to Use:\n\nEffective when iterative refinement significantly enhances response quality, especially when clear evaluation criteria exist.\n\n# Example Applications:\n\n- Improving literary translations through multiple evaluation and refinement cycles.\n- Conducting multi-round research queries where additional iterations refine search results.\n\n# 5 Taxonomy of Agentic RAG Systems\n\nAgentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems can be categorized into distinct architectural frameworks based on their complexity and design principles. These include single-agent architectures, multi-agent systems, and hierarchical agentic architectures. Each framework is tailored to address specific challenges and optimize performance for diverse applications. This section provides a detailed taxonomy of these architectures, highlighting their characteristics, strengths, and limitations.\n\n# 5.1 Single-Agent Agentic RAG: Router\n\nA Single-Agent Agentic RAG: [30] serves as a centralized decision-making system where a single agent manages the retrieval, routing, and integration of information (as shown in Figure 16). This architecture simplifies the system by consolidating these tasks into one unified agent, making it particularly effective for setups with a limited number of tools or data sources.\n\n# Workflow\n\n1. Query Submission and Evaluation: The process begins when a user submits a query. A coordinating agent (or master retrieval agent) receives the query and analyzes it to determine the most suitable sources of information.\n2. Knowledge Source Selection: Based on the query\u2019s type, the coordinating agent chooses from a variety of retrieval options:\n---\n# 3.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 30860, "end_char_idx": 33205, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "1c8c54ad-874f-4696-a585-24b5211c7c2e", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the process of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) in dynamic AI systems, focusing on knowledge source selection, data integration, and output generation. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Knowledge Source Selection**: The coordinating agent selects appropriate retrieval options based on the query type.\n2. **Data Integration and LLM Synthesis**: Retrieved data is synthesized by a Large Language Model (LLM) to create a coherent response.\n3. **Output Generation**: The system delivers a concise, actionable answer, potentially including references to the sources used.\n\nKey features and advantages of this system include:\n- Centralized simplicity for easier design and maintenance.\n- Efficiency and resource optimization through fewer agents.\n- Dynamic routing for real-time query evaluation.\n- Versatility in supporting various data sources and APIs.\n- Suitability for simpler systems with defined tasks.\n\nA specific use case in customer support illustrates the workflow, detailing how the system processes a query about order delivery status through a single-agent workflow, including query evaluation, knowledge source selection, and information retrieval from databases and APIs."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "44acfe8d-ed52-457f-8cc1-d23232e7509f", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "5b2756d122904208e044faf31261d87ad1b57439b78b6507252cf880f92b99ba", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "aa78a764-13ef-42b0-a3bf-eddd5d890d8d", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "2c5ec9e6c1b67708bd908da7f5e703a66398c56d3367a3945c3548ea607dddf0", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "2. Knowledge Source Selection: Based on the query\u2019s type, the coordinating agent chooses from a variety of retrieval options:\n---\n# 3. Data Integration and LLM Synthesis\n\nOnce the relevant data is retrieved from the chosen sources, it is passed to a Large Language Model (LLM). The LLM synthesizes the gathered information, integrating insights from multiple sources into a coherent and contextually relevant response.\n\n# 4. Output Generation\n\nFinally, the system delivers a comprehensive, user-facing answer that addresses the original query. This response is presented in an actionable, concise format and may optionally include references or citations to the sources used.\n\n|Input|Query|Prompt|Tools|\n|---|---|---|---|\n|Vector Search X|Data Sources|Retrieval|Vector Search Y|\n|Response|Router|Web Search| |\n\n# Key Features and Advantages\n\n- Centralized Simplicity: A single agent handles all retrieval and routing tasks, making the architecture straightforward to design, implement, and maintain.\n- Efficiency & Resource Optimization: With fewer agents and simpler coordination, the system demands fewer computational resources and can handle queries more quickly.\n- Dynamic Routing: The agent evaluates each query in real-time, selecting the most appropriate knowledge source (e.g., structured DB, semantic search, web search).\n- Versatility Across Tools: Supports a variety of data sources and external APIs, enabling both structured and unstructured workflows.\n- Ideal for Simpler Systems: Suited for applications with well-defined tasks or limited integration requirements (e.g., document retrieval, SQL-based workflows).\n---\n# Use Case: Customer Support\n\nPrompt: Can you tell me the delivery status of my order?\n\n# System Process (Single-Agent Workflow):\n\n1. Query Submission and Evaluation:\n- The user submits the query, which is received by the coordinating agent.\n- The coordinating agent analyzes the query and determines the most appropriate sources of information.\n2. Knowledge Source Selection:\n- Retrieves tracking details from the order management database.\n- Fetches real-time updates from the shipping provider\u2019s API.\n- Optionally conducts a web search to identify local conditions affecting delivery, such as weather or logistical delays.\n3.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 33071, "end_char_idx": 35332, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "aa78a764-13ef-42b0-a3bf-eddd5d890d8d", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the concept of **Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)**, focusing on its principles, architectures, and applications in dynamic AI systems across various sectors such as healthcare, finance, and education. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Real-Time Data Integration**: The system fetches updates from APIs and may conduct web searches to gather relevant information affecting delivery, such as weather conditions.\n\n2. **LLM Synthesis**: The relevant data is synthesized by a Large Language Model (LLM) to generate coherent and actionable responses.\n\n3. **Multi-Agent RAG Systems**: This represents an evolution from single-agent architectures to a modular system that utilizes multiple specialized agents to handle complex workflows and diverse queries.\n\n4. **Workflow Process**:\n   - **Query Submission**: Initiated by a user query, managed by a coordinator or master retrieval agent.\n   - **Specialized Retrieval Agents**: Different agents are assigned based on the type of data or task, including:\n     - Agent 1: Structured queries (SQL databases).\n     - Agent 2: Semantic searches (unstructured data).\n     - Agent 3: Real-time public information (web searches/APIs).\n     - Agent 4: Recommendation systems (context-aware suggestions).\n   - **Tool Access and Data Retrieval**: Each agent accesses specific tools or data sources relevant to its specialization.\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the modularity and scalability of multi-agent systems in enhancing the efficiency and effectiveness of information retrieval and response generation."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "1c8c54ad-874f-4696-a585-24b5211c7c2e", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "1335d9eb215cf6e8f75212d3d32f41eb9ed428b3e682637f0a19367325e90fcf", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "f01ce033-bdf9-46ef-b242-bea4424431b0", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "5188de08994bc45332326c88646352285b17d4273384366fd3e11d53b98edb24", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "- Fetches real-time updates from the shipping provider\u2019s API.\n- Optionally conducts a web search to identify local conditions affecting delivery, such as weather or logistical delays.\n3. Data Integration and LLM Synthesis:\n- The relevant data is passed to the LLM, which synthesizes the information into a coherent response.\n4. Output Generation:\n- The system generates an actionable and concise response, providing live tracking updates and potential alternatives.\n\nResponse:\n\nIntegrated Response: \u201cYour package is currently in transit and expected to arrive tomorrow evening. The live tracking from UPS indicates it is at the regional distribution center.\u201d\n\n# 5.2 Multi-Agent Agentic RAG Systems:\n\nMulti-Agent RAG [30] represents a modular and scalable evolution of single-agent architectures, designed to handle complex workflows and diverse query types by leveraging multiple specialized agents (as shown in Figure 17). Instead of relying on a single agent to manage all tasks\u2014reasoning, retrieval, and response generation\u2014this system distributes responsibilities across multiple agents, each optimized for a specific role or data source.\n\n# Workflow\n\n1. Query Submission: The process begins with a user query, which is received by a coordinator agent or master retrieval agent. This agent acts as the central orchestrator, delegating the query to specialized retrieval agents based on the query\u2019s requirements.\n2. Specialized Retrieval Agents: The query is distributed among multiple retrieval agents, each focusing on a specific type of data source or task. Examples include:\n- Agent 1: Handles structured queries, such as interacting with SQL-based databases like PostgreSQL or MySQL.\n- Agent 2: Manages semantic searches for retrieving unstructured data from sources like PDFs, books, or internal records.\n- Agent 3: Focuses on retrieving real-time public information from web searches or APIs.\n- Agent 4: Specializes in recommendation systems, delivering context-aware suggestions based on user behavior or profiles.\n3. Tool Access and Data Retrieval: Each agent routes the query to the appropriate tools or data sources within its domain, such as:\n- Vector Search: For semantic relevance.\n- Text-to-SQL: For structured data.\n- Web Search: For real-time public information.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 35146, "end_char_idx": 37428, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "f01ce033-bdf9-46ef-b242-bea4424431b0", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the principles and functionalities of a Multi-Agent Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) system, focusing on its application in various domains such as healthcare, finance, and education. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Retrieval Methods**: The system employs different retrieval techniques, including:\n   - Text-to-SQL for structured data access.\n   - Web search for real-time public information.\n   - APIs for interfacing with external services.\n\n2. **Data Integration and LLM Synthesis**: After retrieval, the data is synthesized by a Large Language Model (LLM) to create coherent responses that integrate insights from multiple sources.\n\n3. **Output Generation**: The system produces actionable and concise responses for users.\n\n4. **Key Features**:\n   - **Modularity**: Independent operation of agents allows for flexible system adjustments.\n   - **Scalability**: Parallel processing enhances the ability to manage high query volumes.\n   - **Task Specialization**: Agents are optimized for specific queries, improving accuracy.\n   - **Efficiency**: Task distribution minimizes bottlenecks and enhances performance.\n   - **Versatility**: Applicable across various domains, including research and customer support.\n\n5. **Challenges**:\n   - **Coordination Complexity**: Requires sophisticated mechanisms for managing inter-agent communication.\n   - **Computational Overhead**: Increased resource usage due to parallel processing.\n   - **Data Integration**: Challenges in synthesizing diverse outputs into cohesive responses.\n\n6. **Use Case**: A Multi-Domain Research Assistant example illustrates the workflow, where multiple agents retrieve data from different sources to answer a prompt about the economic and environmental impacts of renewable energy adoption in Europe.\n\nOverall, the section highlights the architecture, advantages, and challenges of implementing a Multi-Agent RAG system in dynamic AI environments."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "aa78a764-13ef-42b0-a3bf-eddd5d890d8d", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "9efefb75f89f998e80b182c017840010624c9ac84c8881a02a7a68f327d588d5", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "5aab7aa8-53f7-4555-b56d-9be7687542eb", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "bbbfe2561533b238fce3de2172a0a1186bd967b79644cbfc8ec8e1da9b966d0b", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "- Text-to-SQL: For structured data.\n- Web Search: For real-time public information.\n- APIs: For accessing external services or proprietary systems.\n\nThe retrieval process is executed in parallel, allowing for efficient processing of diverse query types.\n---\n# 4. Data Integration and LLM Synthesis\n\nOnce retrieval is complete, the data from all agents is passed to a Large Language Model (LLM). The LLM synthesizes the retrieved information into a coherent and contextually relevant response, integrating insights from multiple sources seamlessly.\n\n# 5. Output Generation\n\nThe system generates a comprehensive response, which is delivered back to the user in an actionable and concise format.\n\n# Key Features and Advantages\n\n- Modularity: Each agent operates independently, allowing for seamless addition or removal of agents based on system requirements.\n- Scalability: Parallel processing by multiple agents enables the system to handle high query volumes efficiently.\n- Task Specialization: Each agent is optimized for a specific type of query or data source, improving accuracy and retrieval relevance.\n- Efficiency: By distributing tasks across specialized agents, the system minimizes bottlenecks and enhances performance for complex workflows.\n- Versatility: Suitable for applications spanning multiple domains, including research, analytics, decision-making, and customer support.\n\n# Challenges\n\n- Coordination Complexity: Managing inter-agent communication and task delegation requires sophisticated orchestration mechanisms.\n- Computational Overhead: Parallel processing of multiple agents can increase resource usage.\n- Data Integration: Synthesizing outputs from diverse sources into a cohesive response is non-trivial and requires advanced LLM capabilities.\n\nFigure 17: An Overview of Multi-Agent Agentic RAG Systems\n---\n# Use Case: Multi-Domain Research Assistant\n\nPrompt: What are the economic and environmental impacts of renewable energy adoption in Europe?\n\n# System Process (Multi-Agent Workflow):\n\n- Agent 1: Retrieves statistical data from economic databases using SQL-based queries.\n- Agent 2: Searches for relevant academic papers using semantic search tools.\n- Agent 3: Performs a web search for recent news and policy updates on renewable energy.\n- Agent 4: Consults a recommendation system to suggest related content, such as reports or expert commentary.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 37345, "end_char_idx": 39726, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "5aab7aa8-53f7-4555-b56d-9be7687542eb", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the concept of Hierarchical Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, which utilize a structured, multi-tiered approach to enhance information retrieval and decision-making. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Agentic RAG Systems**: These systems involve agents organized in a hierarchy, where higher-level agents oversee lower-level agents to improve efficiency and strategic decision-making.\n\n2. **Workflow Process**:\n   - **Query Reception**: A user query is received by a top-tier agent for initial assessment.\n   - **Strategic Decision-Making**: The top-tier agent evaluates the query's complexity and prioritizes subordinate agents or data sources.\n   - **Delegation**: Tasks are assigned to specialized lower-level agents for independent execution.\n\n3. **Aggregation and Synthesis**: Results from subordinate agents are collected and synthesized by the higher-level agent into a coherent response.\n\n4. **Response Delivery**: The final synthesized answer is provided to the user, ensuring comprehensiveness and contextual relevance.\n\n5. **Key Features and Advantages**: The hierarchical structure allows for multi-level decision-making and efficient handling of queries.\n\nEntities mentioned include:\n- **Agents**: Various levels of agents (master and subordinate) involved in the RAG process.\n- **Data Sources**: Different databases, APIs, and retrieval tools utilized by agents.\n- **Domains**: Areas of application such as healthcare, finance, and education, where these systems can be implemented. \n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the structured approach of Hierarchical Agentic RAG systems in improving information retrieval and decision-making processes."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "f01ce033-bdf9-46ef-b242-bea4424431b0", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "71607629e3bb15ecd43fc361f586f868f27d6508fb95dae3d5dfc89f81417375", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "6784f0aa-37c2-4231-9c1d-16d0ff332045", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "d61053327f0d489fd2dfc40298f734f60af0ff4f9e357490b315c8fc353d7772", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "- Agent 4: Consults a recommendation system to suggest related content, such as reports or expert commentary.\n\n# Response:\n\nIntegrated Response: \u201cAdopting renewable energy in Europe has led to a 20% reduction in greenhouse gas emissions over the past decade, according to EU policy reports. Economically, renewable energy investments have generated approximately 1.2 million jobs, with significant growth in solar and wind sectors. Recent academic studies also highlight potential trade-offs in grid stability and energy storage costs.\u201d\n\n# 5.3 Hierarchical Agentic RAG Systems\n\n# Hierarchical Agentic RAG:\n\n[14] systems employ a structured, multi-tiered approach to information retrieval and processing, enhancing both efficiency and strategic decision-making as shown in Figure 18. Agents are organized in a hierarchy, with higher-level agents overseeing and directing lower-level agents. This structure enables multi-level decision-making, ensuring that queries are handled by the most appropriate resources.\n\n|Query|Master Agent|Response|\n|---|---|---|\n|Sub-Agent X|Sub-Agent Y|Sub-Agent Z|\n\nFigure 18: An illustration of Hierarchical Agentic RAG\n\n# Workflow\n\n1. Query Reception: A user submits a query, received by a top-tier agent responsible for initial assessment and delegation.\n2. Strategic Decision-Making: The top-tier agent evaluates the query\u2019s complexity and decides which subordinate agents or data sources to prioritize. Certain databases, APIs, or retrieval tools may be deemed more reliable or relevant based on the query\u2019s domain.\n3. Delegation to Subordinate Agents: The top-tier agent assigns tasks to lower-level agents specialized in particular retrieval methods (e.g., SQL databases, web search, or proprietary systems). These agents execute their assigned tasks independently.\n---\n# 4. Aggregation and Synthesis:\n\nThe results from subordinate agents are collected and integrated by the higher-level agent, which synthesizes the information into a coherent response.\n\n# 5. Response Delivery:\n\nThe final, synthesized answer is returned to the user, ensuring that the response is both comprehensive and contextually relevant.\n\n# Key Features and Advantages.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 39617, "end_char_idx": 41796, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n