ons, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the concept of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) and its application in automating knowledge work through Agentic Document Workflows (ADW). Key topics include:\n\n1. **Agent-Based Retrieval**: This involves an autonomous agent selecting retrieval paths to gather information about a specific entity, such as a mentor in a literary context, and integrating unstructured data for a comprehensive understanding.\n\n2. **Response Synthesis**: The process of combining insights from graph and document retrieval to generate coherent responses that reflect complex relationships, exemplified by a response about J.K. Rowling's mentor and their literary influences.\n\n3. **Agentic Document Workflows (ADW)**: These workflows enhance traditional RAG by automating document-centric processes, including parsing, retrieval, reasoning, and output generation, while addressing limitations of Intelligent Document Processing (IDP).\n\n4. **Workflow Steps**:\n   - **Document Parsing**: Utilizing tools to extract structured data from documents.\n   - **State Maintenance**: Keeping track of document context and processing stages.\n   - **Knowledge Retrieval**: Accessing external knowledge bases for real-time, domain-specific information.\n\nEntities mentioned include J.K. Rowling, her mentor, and the use of tools like LlamaParse and LlamaCloud for document processing and knowledge retrieval."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "268ccbe5-4b42-4122-a72f-6aac836a0aa7", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "15f2e8ef7e1dac73bdbb515b3398bf368163fe49aa3663f73c591129ea31254c", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "7f5cf46e-d25e-4946-9776-58d03251787f", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "cdceaeebaaa1e5d3d08eeb781c23f2790693a9a968ac5cc027d47888bf1e698b", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Rowling\u2019s mentor is a key entity in the query.\n- Traces the literary influences on that mentor by exploring graph-structured data on literary relationships.\n3. Agent-Based Retrieval:\n- An agent autonomously selects the graph-expanded retrieval path to gather relevant information about the mentor\u2019s influences.\n- Integrates additional context by querying textual data sources for unstructured details about the mentor and their influences.\n4. Response Synthesis: Combines insights from the graph and document retrieval processes using the LLM to generate a response that accurately reflects the complex relationships in the query.\n\n# Response:\n\nIntegrated Response: \u201cJ.K. Rowling\u2019s mentor, [Mentor Name], was heavily influenced by [Author Name], known for their [notable works or genre]. This connection highlights the layered relationships in literary history, where influential ideas often pass through multiple generations of authors.\u201d\n\n# 5.7 Agentic Document Workflows in Agentic RAG\n\nAgentic Document Workflows (ADW) [36] extend traditional Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) paradigms by enabling end-to-end knowledge work automation. These workflows orchestrate complex document-centric processes, integrating document parsing, retrieval, reasoning, and structured outputs with intelligent agents (see Figure 23). ADW systems address limitations of Intelligent Document Processing (IDP) and RAG by maintaining state, coordinating multi-step workflows, and applying domain-specific logic to documents.\n\n# Workflow\n\n1. Document Parsing and Information Structuring:\n- Documents are parsed using enterprise-grade tools (e.g., LlamaParse) to extract relevant data fields such as invoice numbers, dates, vendor information, line items, and payment terms.\n- Structured data is organized for downstream processing.\n2. State Maintenance Across Processes:\n- The system maintains state about document context, ensuring consistency and relevance across multi-step workflows.\n- Tracks the progression of the document through various processing stages.\n3. Knowledge Retrieval:\n- Relevant references are retrieved from external knowledge bases (e.g., LlamaCloud) or vector indexes.\n- Retrieves real-time, domain-specific guidelines for enhanced decision-making.\n4.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 59350, "end_char_idx": 61608, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "7f5cf46e-d25e-4946-9776-58d03251787f", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the principles and workflows of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) in dynamic AI systems, particularly focusing on applications in healthcare, finance, and education. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Real-Time Retrieval**: The system retrieves domain-specific guidelines to enhance decision-making.\n2. **Agentic Orchestration**: Intelligent agents utilize business rules and multi-hop reasoning to generate actionable recommendations, integrating various components like parsers and external APIs.\n3. **Actionable Output Generation**: Outputs are structured and tailored for specific use cases, synthesizing recommendations and insights into concise reports.\n\nThe section also outlines an **Agentic Document Workflow (ADW)**, specifically detailing a use case for invoice payments. The workflow involves:\n\n- Parsing invoices to extract key details.\n- Retrieving vendor contracts to verify payment terms.\n- Generating a payment recommendation report that includes financial analysis and strategic actions.\n\nThe integrated response provides a specific example of an invoice processing outcome, highlighting potential discounts and recommendations for payment. Key features include state maintenance to track document context and workflow stages for consistency. \n\nEntities mentioned include:\n- Invoice\n- Vendor contract\n- Payment recommendation report\n- Discounts (early payment, bulk order)\n- Document context and workflow stages."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "cre