"node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "7f5cf46e-d25e-4946-9776-58d03251787f", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "2de0b77fb24401d97ae4ed7b50816c5ac2cbced990168b9633884d482b976387", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "b21bc08f-2be7-4148-a05d-62ccb21e153d", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "15724a53c64c1030d4add4c2f7c69075b419963532cf7835f4ac5bf7839dd35e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "# Key Features and Advantages\n\n- State Maintenance: Tracks document context and workflow stage, ensuring consistency across processes.\n- Multi-Step Orchestration: Handles complex workflows involving multiple components and external tools.\n- Domain-Specific Intelligence: Applies tailored business rules and guidelines for precise recommendations.\n- Scalability: Supports large-scale document processing with modular and dynamic agent integration.\n- Enhanced Productivity: Automates repetitive tasks while augmenting human expertise in decision-making.\n---\n# 6 Comparative Analysis of Agentic RAG Frameworks\n\nTable 2 provides a comprehensive comparative analysis of the three architectural frameworks: Traditional RAG, Agentic RAG, and Agentic Document Workflows (ADW). This analysis highlights their respective strengths, weaknesses, and best-fit scenarios, offering valuable insights into their applicability across diverse use cases.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 63401, "end_char_idx": 64336, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "b21bc08f-2be7-4148-a05d-62ccb21e153d", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section provides a comparative analysis of three frameworks: Traditional Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), Agentic RAG, and Agentic Document Workflows (ADW). Key topics include:\n\n1. **Framework Focus**:\n   - Traditional RAG: Isolated retrieval and generation tasks.\n   - Agentic RAG: Multi-agent collaboration and reasoning.\n   - ADW: Document-centric end-to-end workflows.\n\n2. **Context Maintenance**:\n   - Traditional RAG: Limited context maintenance.\n   - Agentic RAG: Enabled through memory modules.\n   - ADW: Maintains state across multi-step workflows.\n\n3. **Dynamic Adaptability**:\n   - Traditional RAG: Minimal adaptability.\n   - Agentic RAG: High adaptability.\n   - ADW: Tailored to document workflows.\n\n4. **Workflow Orchestration**:\n   - Traditional RAG: Absent orchestration.\n   - Agentic RAG: Orchestrates multi-agent tasks.\n   - ADW: Integrates multi-step document processing.\n\n5. **Integration with External Tools/APIs**:\n   - Traditional RAG: Basic integration.\n   - Agentic RAG: Extends via APIs and knowledge bases.\n   - ADW: Deep integration with business rules and domain-specific tools.\n\n6. **Scalability**:\n   - Traditional RAG: Limited scalability.\n   - Agentic RAG: Scalable for multi-agent systems.\n   - ADW: Scales for multi-domain enterprise workflows.\n\n7. **Complex Reasoning**:\n   - Traditional RAG: Basic reasoning capabilities.\n   - Agentic RAG: Supports multi-step reasoning.\n   - ADW: Enables structured reasoning across documents.\n\n8. **Primary Applications**:\n   - Traditional RAG: QA systems and knowledge retrieval.\n   - Agentic RAG: Multi-domain knowledge and reasoning.\n   - ADW: Contract review, invoice processing, and claims analysis.\n\n9. **Strengths and Challenges**:\n   - Traditional RAG: Simplicity and quick setup but poor contextual understanding.\n   - Agentic RAG: High accuracy and collaborative reasoning but faces coordination complexity.\n   - ADW: Offers end-to-end automation and domain-specific intelligence but has resource overhead and standardization challenges.\n\nThe analysis emphasizes the evolution from Traditional RAG to more advanced frameworks, highlighting the importance of understanding their strengths and limitations for selecting the appropriate architecture for specific applications."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "99da6ef5-9aea-464e-8a31-d336fdb3ac67", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "49cd5f7e7312a7f500d358d0280f3f2ea87584ed97ba37bff926cd32bc10c4df", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "af195478-b8aa-4cab-b3b3-049cf8f69edf", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "98887e3b25a3ad50ffbd9e9d9e911228f05e86e7ef67e95e5181933a87cdfe91", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "This analysis highlights their respective strengths, weaknesses, and best-fit scenarios, offering valuable insights into their applicability across diverse use cases.\n\n**Comparative Analysis: Traditional RAG vs Agentic RAG vs Agentic Document Workflows (ADW)**\n|Feature|Traditional RAG|Agentic RAG|Agentic Document Workflows (ADW)|\n|---|---|---|---|\n|Focus|Isolated retrieval and generation tasks|Multi-agent collaboration and reasoning|Document-centric end-to-end workflows|\n|Context Maintenance|Limited|Enabled through memory modules|Maintains state across multi-step workflows|\n|Dynamic Adaptability|Minimal|High|Tailored to document workflows|\n|Workflow Orchestration|Absent|Orchestrates multi-agent tasks|Integrates multi-step document processing|\n|Use of External Tools/APIs|Basic integration (e.g., retrieval tools)|Extends via tools like APIs and knowledge bases|Deeply integrates business rules and domain-specific tools|\n|Scalability|Limited to small datasets or queries|Scalable for multi-agent systems|Scales for multi-domain enterprise workflows|\n|Complex Reasoning|Basic (e.g., simple Q&amp;A)|Multi-step reasoning with agents|Structured reasoning across documents|\n|Primary Applications|QA systems, knowledge retrieval|Multi-domain knowledge and reasoning|Contract review, invoice processing, claims analysis|\n|Strengths|Simlicity, quick setup|High accuracy, collaborative reasoning|End-to-end automation, domain-specific intelligence|\n|Challenges|Poor contextual understanding|Coordination complexity|Resource overhead, domain standardization|\n\nThe comparative analysis underscores the evolutionary trajectory from Traditional RAG to Agentic RAG and further to Agentic Document Workflows (ADW). While Traditional RAG offers simplicity and ease of deployment for basic tasks, Agentic RAG introduces enhanced reasoning and scalability through multi-agent collaboration. ADW builds upon these advancements by providing robust, document-centric workflows that facilitate end-to-end automation and integration with domain-specific processes. Understanding the strengths and limitations of each framework is crucial for selecting the most appropriate architecture to meet specific application requirements and operational demands.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 64170, "end_char_idx": 66410, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "af195478-b8aa-4cab-b3b3-049cf8f69edf", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the applications of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems across various industries, highlighting their transformative potential in addressing complex challenges through real-time data retrieval and generative capabilities. \n\nKey Topics:\n1. **Understanding Frameworks**: Emphasizes the importance of selecting the appropriate architecture based on specific application requirements.\n2. **Applications of Agentic RAG**: Explores how these systems are shaping industries such as:\n   - Customer Support\n   - Healthcare\n   - Finance\n   - Education\n   - Legal Workflows\n   - Creative Industries\n\n3. **Customer Support and Virtual Assistants**: \n   - Highlights the shift from traditional chatbots to Agentic RAG systems that provide personalized, context-aware responses.\n   - **Use Case**: Twitch's ad sales enhancement through dynamic retrieval of advertiser data and audience demographics.\n\n4. **Healthcare and Personalized Medicine**: \n   - Discusses the integration of patient-specific data with medical research for informed decision-making.\n   - **Use Case**: Generation of patient case summaries by integrating electronic health records and current medical literature.\n\nKey Entities:\n- **Agentic RAG Systems**: The main technology discussed.\n- **Twitch**: Example of a company utilizing Agentic RAG for ad sales.\n- **Healthcare**: A sector benefiting from Agentic RAG through improved decision-making processes.\n\nOverall, the section underscores the advantages of Agentic RAG systems, including improved response quality, operational efficiency, and real-time adaptability."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "b21bc08f-2be7-4148-a05d-62ccb21e153d", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "02e9d56fab36d3d47744059323c9fb29a7328b243de80e1215248b00a8aad8f1", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "ec67c561-6dc2-4f9d-a748-866e3ac84aea", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "a623907d4ad48af668ab631559266cadc5d14fb2693508b045fce7166d302a18", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Understanding the strengths and limitations of each framework is crucial for selecting the most appropriate architecture to meet specific application requirements and operational demands.\n\n# 7 Applications of Agentic RAG\n\nAgentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems have demonstrated transformative potential across a variety of domains. By combining real-time data retrieval, generative capabilities, and autonomous decision-making, these systems address complex, dynamic, and multi-modal challenges. This section explores the key applications of Agentic RAG, providing detailed insights into how these systems are shaping industries such as customer support, healthcare, finance, education, legal workflows, and creative industries.\n\n# 7.1 Customer Support and Virtual Assistants\n\nAgentic RAG systems are revolutionizing customer support by enabling real-time, context-aware query resolution. Traditional chatbots and virtual assistants often rely on static knowledge bases, leading to generic or outdated responses.\n---\nBy contrast, Agentic RAG systems dynamically retrieve the most relevant information, adapt to the user\u2019s context, and generate personalized responses.\n\n# 7.1 Use Case: Twitch Ad Sales Enhancement [37]\n\nFor instance, Twitch leveraged an agentic workflow with RAG on Amazon Bedrock to streamline ad sales. The system dynamically retrieved advertiser data, historical campaign performance, and audience demographics to generate detailed ad proposals, significantly boosting operational efficiency.\n\n# Key Benefits:\n\n- Improved Response Quality: Personalized and context-aware replies enhance user engagement.\n- Operational Efficiency: Reduces the workload on human support agents by automating complex queries.\n- Real-Time Adaptability: Dynamically integrates evolving data, such as live service outages or pricing updates.\n\n# 7.2 Healthcare and Personalized Medicine\n\nIn healthcare, the integration of patient-specific data with the latest medical research is critical for informed decision-making. Agentic RAG systems enable this by retrieving real-time clinical guidelines, medical literature, and patient history to assist clinicians in diagnostics and treatment planning.\n\n# Use Case: Patient Case Summary [38]\n\nAgentic RAG systems have been applied in generating patient case summaries. For example, by integrating electronic health records (EHR) and up-to-date medical literature, the system generates comprehensive summaries for clinicians to make faster and more informed decisions.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 66223, "end_char_idx": 68743, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "ec67c561-6dc2-4f9d-a748-866e3ac84aea", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the applications and benefits of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems across various domains, including healthcare, legal, finance, and education. \n\n### Key Topics:\n1. **Healthcare**:\n   - Integration of electronic health records (EHR) and medical literature for generating summaries.\n   - Benefits include personalized care, time efficiency, and accuracy in recommendations.\n\n2. **Legal and Contract Analysis**:\n   - Redefining legal workflows with tools for rapid document analysis.\n   - Use case of contract review, where the system analyzes contracts, extracts clauses, and identifies risks.\n   - Benefits include risk identification, efficiency in review processes, and scalability.\n\n3. **Finance and Risk Analysis**:\n   - Transformation of the finance industry with real-time insights for investment and risk management.\n   - Use case of auto insurance claims processing, automating claim recommendations based on policy and accident data.\n   - Benefits include real-time analytics based on live market data.\n\n4. **Education and Personalized Learning**:\n   - Enabling adaptive learning through tailored explanations and study materials.\n   - Use case of research paper generation, assisting researchers by synthesizing findings from multiple sources.\n\n### Key Entities:\n- Agentic RAG systems\n- Electronic health records (EHR)\n- Legal knowledge graphs\n- Auto insurance claims\n- Adaptive learning\n- Research paper generation\n\nOverall, the section highlights the versatility and impact of Agentic RAG systems in enhancing efficiency, accuracy, and personalization across different sectors."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "af195478-b8aa-4cab-b3b3-049cf8f69edf", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "7da91bb3dc2dd16cf174ac4095caf9995eee6e664ab2929cc1e20a48de723ecb", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "e911e7c0-626b-4c48-b0f7-111716824f2d", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "4bff633750671eea2c882a1f2280c2d9f9936b83c5b14643dac707c1491c1dc0", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "For example, by integrating electronic health records (EHR) and up-to-date medical literature, the system generates comprehensive summaries for clinicians to make faster and more informed decisions.\n\n# Key Benefits:\n\n- Personalized Care: Tailors recommendations to individual patient needs.\n- Time Efficiency: Streamlines the retrieval of relevant research, saving valuable time for healthcare providers.\n- Accuracy: Ensures recommendations are based on the latest evidence and patient-specific parameters.\n\n# 7.3 Legal and Contract Analysis\n\nAgentic RAG systems are redefining how legal workflows are conducted, offering tools for rapid document analysis and decision-making.\n\n# Use Case: Contract Review [39]\n\nA legal agentic RAG system can analyze contracts, extract critical clauses, and identify potential risks. By combining semantic search capabilities with legal knowledge graphs, it automates the tedious process of contract review, ensuring compliance and mitigating risks.\n\n# Key Benefits:\n\n- Risk Identification: Automatically flags clauses that deviate from standard terms.\n- Efficiency: Reduces the time spent on contract review processes.\n- Scalability: Handles large volumes of contracts simultaneously.\n\n# 7.4 Finance and Risk Analysis\n\nAgentic RAG systems are transforming the finance industry by providing real-time insights for investment decisions, market analysis, and risk management. These systems integrate live data streams, historical trends, and predictive modeling to generate actionable outputs.\n\n# Use Case: Auto Insurance Claims Processing [40]\n\nIn auto insurance, Agentic RAG can automate claim processing. For example, by retrieving policy details and combining them with accident data, it generates claim recommendations while ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements.\n\n# Key Benefits:\n\n- Real-Time Analytics: Delivers insights based on live market data.\n---\n# 7.5 Education and Personalized Learning\n\nEducation is another domain where Agentic RAG systems are making significant strides. These systems enable adaptive learning by generating explanations, study materials, and feedback tailored to the learner\u2019s progress and preferences.\n\n# Use Case: Research Paper Generation [41]\n\nIn higher education, Agentic RAG has been used to assist researchers by synthesizing key findings from multiple sources.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 68545, "end_char_idx": 70890, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "e911e7c0-626b-4c48-b0f7-111716824f2d", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the concept of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) and its applications across various fields, particularly in higher education and marketing. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Use Case: Research Paper Generation** - Agentic RAG assists researchers by synthesizing findings from multiple sources, enhancing the quality and efficiency of academic work.\n\n2. **Key Benefits of Agentic RAG in Education**:\n   - Tailored Learning Paths: Customizes content based on individual student needs.\n   - Engaging Interactions: Offers interactive explanations and personalized feedback.\n   - Scalability: Facilitates large-scale deployment in diverse educational settings.\n\n3. **Graph-Enhanced Applications in Multimodal Workflows** - Graph-Enhanced Agentic RAG (GEAR) integrates graph structures with retrieval mechanisms, making it effective for workflows that require interconnected data.\n\n4. **Use Case: Market Survey Generation** - GEAR synthesizes text, images, and videos for marketing campaigns, providing detailed reports on trends and customer preferences.\n\n5. **Key Benefits of GEAR**:\n   - Multi-Modal Capabilities: Combines various data types for comprehensive outputs.\n   - Enhanced Creativity: Fosters innovative ideas for marketing and entertainment.\n   - Dynamic Adaptability: Adjusts to changing market trends and customer needs.\n\n6. **Overall Impact** - Agentic RAG systems are versatile and transformative, addressing complex challenges in various industries, including personalized customer support, adaptive education, and multimodal workflows.\n\n7. **Tools and Frameworks** - The section concludes by highlighting the evolution of Agentic RAG systems and the tools available for developing these systems to meet real-world application needs. \n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the potential of Agentic RAG and GEAR in enhancing research, education, and marketing through advanced AI capabilities."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "ec67c561-6dc2-4f9d-a748-866e3ac84aea", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "8295e5d1db318539e3967593f68573ca58198e8a92dac2f0bb818c11e1c0b2f4", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "a86f85e1-fda8-4291-84df-d179ac389f1b", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "7b7032197e8f84e437dd86ebd45f293e0d5b5992300eb30afd9e393e0e41236e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "# Use Case: Research Paper Generation [41]\n\nIn higher education, Agentic RAG has been used to assist researchers by synthesizing key findings from multiple sources. For instance, a researcher querying, \u201cWhat are the latest advancements in quantum computing?\u201d receives a concise summary enriched with references, enhancing the quality and efficiency of their work.\n\n# Key Benefits:\n\n- Tailored Learning Paths: Adapts content to individual student needs and performance levels.\n- Engaging Interactions: Provides interactive explanations and personalized feedback.\n- Scalability: Supports large-scale deployments for diverse educational environments.\n\n# 7.6 Graph-Enhanced Applications in Multimodal Workflows\n\nGraph-Enhanced Agentic RAG (GEAR) combines graph structures with retrieval mechanisms, making it particularly effective in multimodal workflows where interconnected data sources are essential.\n\n# Use Case: Market Survey Generation\n\nGEAR enables the synthesis of text, images, and videos for marketing campaigns. For example, querying, \u201cWhat are the emerging trends in eco-friendly products?\u201d generates a detailed report enriched with customer preferences, competitor analysis, and multimedia content.\n\n# Key Benefits:\n\n- Multi-Modal Capabilities: Integrates text, image, and video data for comprehensive outputs.\n- Enhanced Creativity: Generates innovative ideas and solutions for marketing and entertainment.\n- Dynamic Adaptability: Adapts to evolving market trends and customer needs.\n\nThe applications of Agentic RAG systems span a wide range of industries, showcasing their versatility and transformative potential. From personalized customer support to adaptive education and graph-enhanced multimodal workflows, these systems address complex, dynamic, and knowledge-intensive challenges. By integrating retrieval, generation, and agentic intelligence, Agentic RAG systems are paving the way for next-generation AI applications.\n\n# 8 Tools and Frameworks for Agentic RAG\n\nAgentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems represent a significant evolution in combining retrieval, generation, and agentic intelligence. These systems extend the capabilities of traditional RAG by integrating decision-making, query reformulation, and adaptive workflows. The following tools and frameworks provide robust support for developing Agentic RAG systems, addressing the complex requirements of real-world applications.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 70726, "end_char_idx": 73151, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "a86f85e1-fda8-4291-84df-d179ac389f1b", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses various tools and frameworks that support the development of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, which are designed to meet the complex needs of real-world applications across fields like healthcare, finance, and education. \n\n**Key Topics and Entities:**\n\n1. **Agentic RAG Systems**: Focus on the integration of retrieval and generation processes in AI applications.\n  \n2. **Tools and Frameworks**:\n   - **LangChain**: Provides modular components for RAG pipelines, integrating retrievers, generators, and external tools.\n   - **LangGraph**: Enhances LangChain with graph-based workflows for orchestration and self-correction.\n   - **LlamaIndex**: Offers Agentic Document Workflows (ADW) for automating document processing and reasoning through a meta-agent architecture.\n   - **Hugging Face Transformers**: Supplies pre-trained models for embedding and generation tasks.\n   - **Qdrant**: Improves retrieval workflows with adaptive vector search capabilities.\n\n3. **Current Frameworks**:\n   - **CrewAI**: Supports multi-agent architectures with memory systems and tool integrations.\n   - **AutoGen (AG2)**: Focuses on multi-agent collaboration, code generation, and decision-making.\n   - **OpenAI Swarm Framework**: A lightweight framework for multi-agent orchestration emphasizing autonomy and collaboration.\n   - **Vertex AI**: Developed by Google, it integrates with Agentic RAG for building and deploying machine learning models.\n   - **Semantic Kernel**: An open-source SDK by Microsoft that integrates large language models into applications.\n\nOverall, the section highlights the importance of these tools and frameworks in facilitating the development of sophisticated, context-aware AI systems."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "e911e7c0-626b-4c48-b0f7-111716824f2d", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "c3824f9ef22eeda68b0aaad66f0bf36b2a0b3a67c4efc7b881e956ad3205f584", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "6b19d4de-bed8-47ab-85e8-1f79c4d240d7", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "87edc3a91a6a74132ba47772ab04cbc8835d8902109b28fa2d1fe5ddfe6ec668", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "The following tools and frameworks provide robust support for developing Agentic RAG systems, addressing the complex requirements of real-world applications.\n\n# Key Tools and Frameworks:\n\n- LangChain and LangGraph: LangChain [42] provides modular components for building RAG pipelines, seamlessly integrating retrievers, generators, and external tools. LangGraph complements this by introducing graph-based workflows that support loops, state persistence, and human-in-the-loop interactions, enabling sophisticated orchestration and self-correction mechanisms in agentic systems.\n- LlamaIndex: LlamaIndex\u2019s [43] Agentic Document Workflows (ADW) enable end-to-end automation of document processing, retrieval, and structured reasoning. It introduces a meta-agent architecture where sub-agents manage smaller document sets, coordinating through a top-level agent for tasks such as compliance analysis and contextual understanding.\n- Hugging Face Transformers and Qdrant: Hugging Face [44] offers pre-trained models for embedding and generation tasks, while Qdrant [45] enhances retrieval workflows with adaptive vector search capabilities, allowing agents to optimize performance by dynamically switching between sparse and dense vector methods.\n---\n# Current Frameworks\n\n- CrewAI and AutoGen: These frameworks emphasize multi-agent architectures. CrewAI [46] supports hierarchical and sequential processes, robust memory systems, and tool integrations. AG2 [47] (formerly known as AutoGen [48, 49]) excels in multi-agent collaboration with advanced support for code generation, tool execution, and decision-making.\n- OpenAI Swarm Framework: An educational framework designed for ergonomic, lightweight multi-agent orchestration [50], emphasizing agent autonomy and structured collaboration.\n- Agentic RAG with Vertex AI: Developed by Google, Vertex AI [51] integrates seamlessly with Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), providing a platform to build, deploy, and scale machine learning models while leveraging advanced AI capabilities for robust, contextually aware retrieval and decision-making workflows.\n- Semantic Kernel: Semantic Kernel [52, 53] is an open-source SDK by Microsoft that integrates large language models (LLMs) into applications.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 72994, "end_char_idx": 75252, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "6b19d4de-bed8-47ab-85e8-1f79c4d240d7", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses various technologies and platforms related to Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, highlighting their applications and capabilities. Key topics and entities include:\n\n1. **Semantic Kernel**: An open-source SDK by Microsoft that integrates large language models (LLMs) into applications, facilitating the creation of autonomous AI agents for tasks such as natural language understanding and decision-making.\n\n2. **Amazon Bedrock**: A platform that supports the implementation of Agentic RAG workflows.\n\n3. **IBM Watson**: Specifically, the watsonx.ai platform, which aids in building Agentic RAG systems and enhances response accuracy by integrating external information.\n\n4. **Neo4j and Vector Databases**: Neo4j is an open-source graph database that manages complex relationships and semantic queries, while vector databases like Weaviate, Pinecone, Milvus, and Qdrant enhance similarity search and retrieval capabilities in RAG workflows.\n\n5. **Benchmarks and Datasets**: The section emphasizes the importance of benchmarks and datasets for evaluating RAG systems, mentioning the BEIR benchmark, which assesses embedding models across various information retrieval tasks.\n\nOverall, the content focuses on the integration of advanced technologies in RAG systems and the significance of structured evaluation methods."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "a86f85e1-fda8-4291-84df-d179ac389f1b", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "b3d8b2bbadeb418d528c1b1be71176b7711969b42c4578e53f5d60e61b1c3ea3", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "293f95af-bcf0-4b87-8c95-a8c1d9f7ca5a", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "7cf9022aa394fcfdf17efd0dfeb46e329c3e2883df03bc2a888a855e9067eee0", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "- Semantic Kernel: Semantic Kernel [52, 53] is an open-source SDK by Microsoft that integrates large language models (LLMs) into applications. It supports agentic patterns, enabling the creation of autonomous AI agents for natural language understanding, task automation, and decision-making. It has been used in scenarios like ServiceNow\u2019s P1 incident management to facilitate real-time collaboration, automate task execution, and retrieve contextual information seamlessly.\n- Amazon Bedrock for Agentic RAG: Amazon Bedrock [37] provides a robust platform for implementing Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) workflows.\n- IBM Watson and Agentic RAG: IBM\u2019s watsonx.ai [54] supports building Agentic RAG systems, exemplified by using the Granite-3-8B-Instruct model to answer complex queries by integrating external information and enhancing response accuracy.\n- Neo4j and Vector Databases: Neo4j, a prominent open-source graph database, excels in handling complex relationships and semantic queries. Alongside Neo4j, vector databases like Weaviate, Pinecone, Milvus, and Qdrant provide efficient similarity search and retrieval capabilities, forming the backbone of high-performance Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) workflows.\n\n# 9 Benchmarks and Datasets\n\nCurrent benchmarks and datasets provide valuable insights into evaluating Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, including those with agentic and graph-based enhancements. While some are explicitly designed for RAG, others are adapted to test retrieval, reasoning, and generation capabilities in diverse scenarios. Datasets are crucial for testing the retrieval, reasoning, and generation components of RAG systems. Table 3 discusses some key datasets based on the downstream task for RAG Evaluation.\n\nBenchmarks play a critical role in standardizing the evaluation of RAG systems by providing structured tasks and metrics. The following benchmarks are particularly relevant:\n\n- BEIR (Benchmarking Information Retrieval): A versatile benchmark designed for evaluating embedding models on a variety of information retrieval tasks, encompassing 17 datasets across diverse domains like bioinformatics, finance, and question answering [55].", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 75110, "end_char_idx": 77331, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "293f95af-bcf0-4b87-8c95-a8c1d9f7ca5a", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses various benchmarks and datasets used for evaluating Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems across different tasks, particularly in the context of question answering (QA). Key topics and entities include:\n\n1. **Benchmarks for RAG Systems**:\n   - **MS MARCO**: Focuses on passage ranking and question answering.\n   - **TREC**: Provides datasets for passage and document retrieval, emphasizing ranking model quality.\n   - **MuSiQue**: A benchmark for multihop reasoning across multiple documents.\n   - **2WikiMultihopQA**: Designed for multihop QA tasks over two Wikipedia articles.\n   - **AgentG**: Tailored for agentic RAG tasks, assessing dynamic information synthesis.\n   - **HotpotQA**: A multi-hop QA benchmark requiring interconnected context retrieval.\n   - **RAGBench**: A large-scale benchmark with 100,000 examples across various domains.\n\n2. **Tools and Libraries**:\n   - **BERGEN**: A library for systematic benchmarking of RAG systems.\n   - **FlashRAG Toolkit**: Implements multiple RAG methods and includes various benchmark datasets.\n   - **GNN-RAG**: Evaluates graph-based RAG systems focusing on retrieval quality and reasoning in Knowledge Graph Question Answering (KGQA).\n\n3. **Downstream Tasks and Datasets**:\n   - The section includes a table summarizing categories of tasks (single-hop and multi-hop QA) along with associated datasets such as Natural Questions, TriviaQA, SQuAD, and others.\n\nOverall, the excerpt highlights the importance of various benchmarks and tools in the evaluation and development of RAG systems, particularly in the context of QA tasks."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "6b19d4de-bed8-47ab-85e8-1f79c4d240d7", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "8e581b24a18c5dc5d6156d829f3a54c9cf1df4987059b5a9bb26bd7f279bfbf1", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "f36f9902-e875-44b3-baca-b51330b95f7f", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "4f51a5a9df81aa316107a9316b037a10ca384f67a8a9b7c2b621f34d962de377", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "- MS MARCO (Microsoft Machine Reading Comprehension): Focused on passage ranking and question answering, this benchmark is widely used for dense retrieval tasks in RAG systems [56].\n- TREC (Text REtrieval Conference, Deep Learning Track): Provides datasets for passage and document retrieval, emphasizing the quality of ranking models in retrieval pipelines [57].\n- MuSiQue (Multihop Sequential Questioning): A benchmark for multihop reasoning across multiple documents, emphasizing the importance of retrieving and synthesizing information from disconnected contexts [58].\n- 2WikiMultihopQA: A dataset designed for multihop QA tasks over two Wikipedia articles, focusing on the ability to connect knowledge across multiple sources [59].\n- AgentG (Agentic RAG for Knowledge Fusion): Tailored for agentic RAG tasks, this benchmark assesses dynamic information synthesis across multiple knowledge bases [8].\n- HotpotQA: A multi-hop QA benchmark requiring retrieval and reasoning over interconnected contexts, ideal for evaluating complex RAG workflows [60].\n- RAGBench: A large-scale, explainable benchmark featuring 100,000 examples across industry domains, with a TRACe evaluation framework for actionable RAG metrics [61].\n---\n- BERGEN (Benchmarking Retrieval-Augmented Generation): A library for systematically benchmarking RAG systems with standardized experiments [62].\n- FlashRAG Toolkit: Implements 12 RAG methods and includes 32 benchmark datasets to support efficient and standardized RAG evaluation [63].\n- GNN-RAG: This benchmark evaluates graph-based RAG systems on tasks like node-level and edge-level predictions, focusing on retrieval quality and reasoning performance in Knowledge Graph Question Answering (KGQA) [64].\n\n# Table 3: Downstream Tasks and Datasets for RAG Evaluation (Adapted from [20])\n\n|Category|Task Type|Datasets and References|\n|---|---|---|\n|QA|Single-hop QA|Natural Questions (NQ) [65], TriviaQA [66], SQuAD [67], Web Questions (WebQ) [68], PopQA [69], MS MARCO [56]|\n|Multi-hop QA|HotpotQA [60],", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 77332, "end_char_idx": 79363, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "f36f9902-e875-44b3-baca-b51330b95f7f", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The secti