ian-Yun Nie, and Ji-Rong Wen. A survey of large language models, 2024.\n4. Sumit Kumar Dam, Choong Seon Hong, Yu Qiao, and Chaoning Zhang. A complete survey on llm-based ai chatbots, 2024.\n5. Aditi Singh. A survey of ai text-to-image and ai text-to-video generators. In 2023 4th International Conference on Artificial Intelligence, Robotics and Control (AIRC), pages 32\u201336, 2023.\n6. Aditi Singh, Abul Ehtesham, Gaurav Kumar Gupta, Nikhil Kumar Chatta, Saket Kumar, and Tala Talaei Khoei. Exploring prompt engineering: A systematic review with swot analysis, 2024.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 82646, "end_char_idx": 84294, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "cedeb183-bca9-453e-a978-8e2d16508b25", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section provides a list of references related to the field of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) and its applications in various domains such as healthcare, finance, and education. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Prompt Engineering**: A systematic review that likely discusses techniques and strategies for optimizing prompts in AI systems.\n2. **Hallucination in Large Language Models**: A survey that addresses the principles, taxonomy, challenges, and open questions regarding inaccuracies or \"hallucinations\