Scientific Research in Computer Science, Engineering and Information Technology (IJSRCSEIT), 5(6).", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 43781, "end_char_idx": 45385, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "a39d814e-ca8b-4c82-894a-0e2e4920daaf", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AI-powered quality assurance Enhancing software infrastructure through intelligent.md", "file_name": "AI-powered quality assurance Enhancing software infrastructure through intelligent.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 46104, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Transforming Software Quality Assurance: Leveraging AI and Automation for Intelligent Fault Detection and Proactive Testing in Modern Development\"", "section_summary": "The section primarily discusses various research contributions in the field of computer science and artificial intelligence, particularly focusing on software quality assurance, load balancing algorithms in cloud environments, and machine learning applications. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Software Quality Assurance**: The document emphasizes the transformation of software quality assurance through the use of AI and automation for intelligent fault detection and proactive testing.\n\n2. **Load Balancing Algorithms**: A comparative analysis of load balancing algorithms in cloud environments is presented, highlighting efficiency in resource management.\n\n3. **Machine Learning Applications**: \n   - Brain tumor detection using transfer learning techniques is explored, showcasing advancements in medical imaging and diagnostics.\n   - A robust machine learning approach for identifying fraud in credit card transactions is discussed, indicating the application of AI in financial security.\n\nEntities mentioned include:\n- **Authors**: Nagelli, A., Yadav, N. K., Rele, M., Patil, D., Rathore, Himmat, and Renu Ratnawat.\n- **Conferences and Journals**: International Journal of Scientific Research in Computer Science, Engineering and Information Technology (IJSRCSEIT), International Journal of Information Technology and Management, and the International Conference on Artificial Intelligence Science and Applications in Industry and Society (CAISAIS).\n\nOverall, the section highlights the integration of AI in various domains, emphasizing its role in enhancing software quality, improving cloud computing efficiency, and advancing medical diagnostics and fraud detection."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "3cc7ef91-2447-4b5e-94de-b001d8d2b1ec", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AI-powered quality assurance Enhancing software infrastructure through intelligent.md", "file_name": "AI-powered quality assurance Enhancing software infrastructure through intelligent.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 46104, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "b9c245bd83c39565a3f052f4561a0cd6704ad175466c1279d0e5edaf5b5d5406", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "e7009acd-9866-4a14-b595-fb22f387a30a", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AI-powered quality assurance Enhancing software infrastructure through intelligent.md", "file_name": "AI-powered quality assurance Enhancing software infrastructure through intelligent.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 46104, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "687fa2dd3cf89a93aab1041bd7dc6de40e0d4dd75ffccb75315350df2932f96c", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "International Journal of Scientific Research in Computer Science, Engineering and Information Technology (IJSRCSEIT), 5(6).\n22. Nagelli, A., and Yadav, N. K. Efficiency Unveiled: Comparative Analysis of Load Balancing Algorithms in Cloud Environments. International Journal of Information Technology and Management, 18(2).\n23. Rele, M., and Patil, D. (2023, September). Machine Learning based Brain Tumor Detection using Transfer Learning. In 2023 International Conference on Artificial Intelligence Science and Applications in Industry and Society (CAISAIS) (pp. 1-6). IEEE.\n24. Rathore, Himmat, and Renu Ratnawat. \"A Robust and Efficient Machine Learning Approach for Identifying Fraud in Credit Card Transaction.\" 2024 5th International Conference on Smart Electronics and Communication (ICOSEC). IEEE, 2024", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 45262, "end_char_idx": 46072, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "557ca41a-08b4-44ed-8b5d-ad9af61a23de", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22", "document_title": "\"AIstorian: A Knowledge Graph-Driven Multi-Agent System for Accurate Biography Generation and Error Correction in Historical Research\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses \"AIstorian,\" a novel multi-agent system developed by researchers from Zhejiang University and Huawei, aimed at enhancing biography generation in historical research through the use of a knowledge graph (KG). Key topics include:\n\n1. **AI Application in Historical Research**: The focus is on utilizing AI for generating biographies, which is a specialized form of summarization in historical contexts.\n2. **Challenges in Biography Generation**: The system addresses issues such as maintaining historical writing styles, ensuring factual accuracy, and managing fragmented information from various sources.\n3. **System Features**:\n   - **Knowledge Graph (KG)**: Used for retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) to improve reference accuracy.\n   - **Chunking Strategy**: An in-context learning approach for efficient information processing.\n   - **Multi-Agent System**: Conducts real-time hallucination detection and error correction.\n   - **Fine-Tuning LLMs**: A two-step training process that combines data augmentation and stylistic optimization to teach language style.\n4. **Performance Improvements**: AIstorian shows significant enhancements in factual accuracy (3.8\u00d7 improvement) and a reduction in hallucination rates (47.6% decrease) compared to existing models.\n5. **Availability**: The data and code for AIstorian are accessible on GitHub.\n\nEntities involved include the authors Fengyu Li, Yilin Li, Junhao Zhu, Lu Chen, Yanfei Zhang, Jia Zhou, Hui Zu, Jingwen Zhao, and Yunjun Gao, affiliated with Zhejiang University and Huawei's Poisson Lab."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "86d6a30b-f854-412f-bc3d-7186c1cd0752", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "13c05f2b3c34a30ab2b06b824e9bb3dd58f7f63367e6cdae60eac9f97a72c8ac", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "7ca539f4-6e4a-4cda-a98f-b1f0a75cd382", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "dcc84ca18bf9892bf73787ef55fc0c1cf521280500409c048d6772454e50a626", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "# AIstorian lets AI be a historian: A KG-powered multi-agent system for accurate biography generation\n\n# Fengyu Li\u2020, Yilin Li\u2020, Junhao Zhu\u2020, Lu Chen\u2020, Yanfei Zhang\u2020, Jia Zhou\u2020, Hui Zu\u2020, Jingwen Zhao\u2021, Yunjun Gao\u2020\n\n# \u2020Zhejiang University, \u2021Poisson Lab, Huawei\n\n{fengyuli, zhujunhao, luchen, yanfei.zhang, 0012802, zdzh, gaoyj}@zju.edu.cn,\nyilin.23@intl.zju.edu.cn, jingwenzhao5@huawei.com\n\n# Abstract\n\nHuawei has always been committed to exploring the AI application in historical research. Biography generation, as a specialized form of abstractive summarization, plays a crucial role in historical research but faces unique challenges that existing large language models (LLMs) struggle to address. These challenges include maintaining stylistic adherence to historical writing conventions, ensuring factual fidelity, and handling fragmented information across multiple documents. We present AIstorian, a novel end-to-end agentic system featured with a knowledge graph (KG)-powered retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) and anti-hallucination multi-agents. Specifically, AIstorian introduces an in-context learning based chunking strategy and a KG-based index for accurate and efficient reference retrieval. Meanwhile, AIstorian orchestrates multi-agents to conduct on-the-fly hallucination detection and error-type-aware correction. Additionally, to teach LLMs a certain language style, we finetune LLMs based on a two-step training approach combining data augmentation-enhanced supervised fine-tuning with stylistic preference optimization. Extensive experiments on a real-life historical Jinshi dataset demonstrate that AIstorian achieves a 3.8\u00d7 improvement in factual accuracy and a 47.6% reduction in hallucination rate compared to existing baselines. The data and code are available at: https://github.com/ZJU-DAILY/AIstorian.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 0, "end_char_idx": 1832, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "7ca539f4-6e4a-4cda-a98f-b1f0a75cd382", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22", "document_title": "\"AIstorian: A Knowledge Graph-Driven Multi-Agent System for Accurate Biography Generation and Error Correction in Historical Research\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the development of \"AIstorian,\" a knowledge graph-driven multi-agent system designed for accurate biography generation and error correction in historical research. Key topics include:\n\n1. **AI and Historical Research**: The application of artificial intelligence in managing historical documents and generating biographies.\n2. **Biography Generation**: The process of automatically creating concise documents that summarize a person's life, including key facts and events.\n3. **Role of Large Language Models (LLMs)**: The potential of LLMs in abstractive summarization and biography generation, highlighting their superior performance in recent studies.\n4. **Unique Characteristics of Biography Generation**: The section emphasizes the distinct challenges of biography writing, particularly the need for stylistic adherence to specific language styles and professional terminology, which LLMs may struggle to maintain.\n\nEntities mentioned include:\n- **Authors**: Fengyu Li, Yilin Li, Junhao Zhu, Lu Chen, Yanfei Zhang, Jia Zhou, Hui Zu, Jingwen Zhao, Yunjun Gao.\n- **Institution**: Huawei, in partnership with museums.\n- **Publication**: Reference to a conference paper and a GitHub repository for data and code related to AIstorian."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "86d6a30b-f854-412f-bc3d-7186c1cd0752", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "13c05f2b3c34a30ab2b06b824e9bb3dd58f7f63367e6cdae60eac9f97a72c8ac", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "557ca41a-08b4-44ed-8b5d-ad9af61a23de", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "d7350158a47f0849446e6aeb2db0cb1b3b9f79439f25580474f7c501a463b94b", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "fad4bcb8-2a2a-4e4e-acf3-1ee34aaf632d", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "6f3cd21ed49f04fc9755f67c1867552ded4404e03f8898794995b5f3a060bd62", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "The data and code are available at: https://github.com/ZJU-DAILY/AIstorian.\n\n# ACM Reference Format:\n\nFengyu Li\u2020, Yilin Li\u2020, Junhao Zhu\u2020, Lu Chen\u2020, Yanfei Zhang\u2020, Jia Zhou\u2020, Hui Zu\u2020, Jingwen Zhao\u2021, Yunjun Gao\u2020. 2018. AIstorian lets AI be a historian: A KG-powered multi-agent system for accurate biography generation. In Proceedings of Make sure to enter the correct conference title from your rights confirmation email (Conference acronym \u2019XX). ACM, New York, NY, USA, 6 pages. https://doi.org/XXXXXXX.XXXXXXX\n\n# 1 Introduction\n\nHuawei has a commercial partnership with several museums, exploring the application of AI in the management of historical documents. Biography generation is an important intersection of AI and history. Typically, biography writing relies heavily on the domain expertise of historians who carefully gather and summarize diverse historical materials. The development of automatic biography generation can free historians from tedious tasks of reading and writing materials. Biography generation automatically writes a concise document comprising a series of facts and events (e.g., date and place of birth and death, career, etc.) that builds a professional image for a person\u2019s life, by extracting and rephrasing biographical events based on references (e.g., textbooks).\n\nBiography generation can be considered a special form of abstractive summarization [20]. Recent studies [18,20] have demonstrated the superior performance of LLMs for abstractive summarization, manifesting significant potential of LLMs in biography generation. However, distinct from general text summarization, the biography generation exhibits unique characteristics that neither existing LLM-based methods nor vertical pretrained models can accommodate:\n\n# Characteristic 1: Stylistic adherence.\n\nBiographies have to strictly follow specific language styles and use professional terminology, which LLMs can struggle with. For example, LLMs cannot keep consistency when required to write a biography in classical Chinese, especially following historical writing conventions.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 1757, "end_char_idx": 3835, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "fad4bcb8-2a2a-4e4e-acf3-1ee34aaf632d", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22", "document_title": "\"AIstorian: A Knowledge Graph-Driven Multi-Agent System for Accurate Biography Generation and Error Correction in Historical Research\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the challenges and solutions related to using Large Language Models (LLMs) for generating biographies, particularly in the context of historical research. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Consistency in Language Style**: LLMs struggle to maintain consistency when writing in specific styles, such as classical Chinese, due to limited training data. Fine-tuning with domain expertise has been attempted but remains insufficient.\n\n2. **Factual Fidelity**: The accuracy of biographies is critical, yet LLMs often produce content that contains factual errors, a phenomenon known as hallucination. The section outlines three approaches to mitigate this issue:\n   - **Training-based methods**: These involve training additional models to correct factual errors but require extensive datasets.\n   - **Decoding-based methods**: These constrain output to avoid hallucinations but may limit the model's creativity.\n   - **Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG)**: This method enhances biography generation by retrieving relevant information from external knowledge bases, emphasizing the importance of retrieval accuracy.\n\n3. **Information Fragmentation**: The section highlights the challenge of scattered information about historical figures across multiple documents. It mentions text chunking and chunk representation as key components in RAG workflows that are affected by this fragmentation.\n\nEntities mentioned include:\n- LLMs (Large Language Models)\n- RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)\n- Historical figures\n- External knowledge bases (e.g., history textbooks)\n\nOverall, the excerpt emphasizes the need for improved methods to ensure consistency, factual accuracy, and effective information retrieval in biography generation using AI."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "86d6a30b-f854-412f-bc3d-7186c1cd0752", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "13c05f2b3c34a30ab2b06b824e9bb3dd58f7f63367e6cdae60eac9f97a72c8ac", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "7ca539f4-6e4a-4cda-a98f-b1f0a75cd382", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "dd3f6a830ee17f3b11852dc26cc3a114625f7d5b037a9492a64d7e13508c754e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "12a93dee-28e0-4f6d-a5c1-004186e7e7a3", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "6507391c9e93277ec17a3dca5899af544a5b8b56cf1c75dcdfc69a25af6d3e11", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "For example, LLMs cannot keep consistency when required to write a biography in classical Chinese, especially following historical writing conventions. To address this, several work injected domain expertise into LLMs via fine-tuning [7, 27]. Due to the scarcity of training corpora that follow a particular style, however, fine-tuned LLMs still struggle to adhere to specific language styles and professional terminology.\n\n# Characteristic 2: Factual fidelity.\n\nBiographies have no tolerance for factual errors. However, since LLMs are notorious for the phenomenon of hallucination, they would generate plausible content that contradicts real facts, significantly undermining the usability of generated biographies [13, 16, 20, 21]. There are three kinds of work proposed to alleviate fabrications in text summarization: (1) Training-based methods [4, 7, 17] fix factual errors inherently by training additional reward models or classifiers. A key drawback is their reliance on tens of thousands of training samples. (2) Decoding-based methods [15] avoid hallucinations by constraining output tokens sampled from the given contexts. Though effective, such methods do harm to the model\u2019s creativity. (3) Retrieval-augmented-generation (RAG) based methods [5, 25] guide biography generation for LLMs by retrieving relevant information from an external knowledge base (e.g., history textbooks) as references. Apparently, the retrieval accuracy makes a pivotal difference in the quality of LLMs\u2019 generation.\n\n# Characteristic 3: Information fragmentation.\n\nDetailed information about a particular historical figure is scattered across multiple documents. Text chunking, which splits long documents into small text chunks, and chunk representation, which embeds text chunks into vectors, are two key components in a RAG workflow, suffering from the information fragmentation due to two-fold reasons: (1)\n---\n# Conference acronym \u2019XX, June 03\u201305, 2018, Woodstock, NY\n\nLi et al.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 3684, "end_char_idx": 5656, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "12a93dee-28e0-4f6d-a5c1-004186e7e7a3", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22", "document_title": "\"AIstorian: A Knowledge Graph-Driven Multi-Agent System for Accurate Biography Generation and Error Correction in Historical Research\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses \"AIstorian,\" a novel multi-agent system designed for accurate biography generation and error correction in historical research. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Architecture**: The system utilizes a knowledge graph (KG)-powered retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) mechanism, supported by anti-hallucination multi-agents.\n\n2. **Challenges**: The varied length of text describing individuals affects the quality of generated content, with specific metrics indicating a Rouge-L score of 80.54, a 47.6% reduction in hallucination rate, and a 3.8\u00d7 decrease in average atomic fact errors.\n\n3. **Methodology**: The system employs techniques such as chunking, regex for name extraction, and a two-step training process involving data synthesis and augmentation.\n\n4. **Performance Metrics**: The effectiveness of the system is highlighted through its ability to generate accurate biographies while minimizing errors.\n\n5. **Example**: The excerpt includes a specific example of generating a biography for \"Su Yi,\" detailing the process and the system's capabilities.\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the innovative approach of AIstorian in enhancing the accuracy and reliability of biographical data generation."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "86d6a30b-f854-412f-bc3d-7186c1cd0752", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "13c05f2b3c34a30ab2b06b824e9bb3dd58f7f63367e6cdae60eac9f97a72c8ac", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "fad4bcb8-2a2a-4e4e-acf3-1ee34aaf632d", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "8e0006ba3aebd720d646877450b783df149ea79a2e9d885c36e1b175355418ab", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "06a90c63-4a41-4a2c-9ec2-f104b518792e", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "ab283325f0a9bfd51b6421ae00eef9d07753369d08126ac258053f7a80647951", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "|Offline|KG-based Index|Style|Two-step Training| | | | | |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n|Su yi, styled Huiren, nicknamed Lushan,|name| | |Bio| | | | |\n|1 Chunking|Full|Teacher|Full| | | | | |\n| | | |Data Synthesis| |Data Augmentation|Fl|AI| |\n|2 Regex|name|name|2 Stylistic Preference| | | | | |\n|1 Supervised| | |Optimization|Fine-tune|Fine-tuned Model| | | |\n| | | | | |Base Model|Documents|Relation Extraction|Online|\n|Prompt|Retrieval|Reference #1|Biography:| | | | | |\n| | | | |\"Not Supported\"|56p|Su yi, styled Huiren,|&gt;0n| |\n|N&lt;]|G&gt;0|Reference #2|56p| | | | | |\n|&gt;n| | |In the 13th year of|N&lt;]|G&gt;u| | | |\n| | | |the Jiaqing reign|(1808), ... appointed|as a Hanlin Academy|Editor.| | |\n| | | | |\"Not Included\"|G&gt;0|Task instruction|Model| |\n|Queried name: Su Yi|Q: Generate the biography of \"Su Yi\"| |Error-aware Generation|Regenerate| | | | |\n\nFigure 1: The architecture of AIstorian\n\nThe varied length of text to describe a single person poses challenge generation quality (Rouge-L: 80.54) and factual accuracy, with a 47.6% reduction in hallucination rate and a 3.8\u00d7 decrease in average atomic fact error.\n\n# 2 AIstorian\n\n# 2.1 Overview\n\nTowards accurate biography generation, this work presents AIs-torian, a novel agentic system that consists of a knowledge graph (KG)-powered RAG mechanism and anti-hallucination multi-agents. Figure 1 illustrates the overall architecture.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 5658, "end_char_idx": 7072, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "06a90c63-4a41-4a2c-9ec2-f104b518792e", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22", "document_title": "\"AIstorian: A Knowledge Graph-Driven Multi-Agent System for Accurate Biography Generation and Error Correction in Historical Research\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the architecture and functionality of \"AIstorian,\" a knowledge graph-driven multi-agent system designed for generating accurate biographies and correcting errors in historical research. Key topics include:\n\n1. **System Architecture**: The system operates in two phases\u2014offline and online. The offline phase involves index building and model fine-tuning, while the online phase focuses on generating biographies based on user queries.\n\n2. **KG-based Index Construction**: The offline process includes constructing a knowledge graph (KG) to organize biographical facts and implementing a two-step training process for error correction and style adaptation.\n\n3. **Biography Generation Pipeline**: During the online phase, the system retrieves relevant information using a KG-powered retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) approach, which aids in generating biographies from user queries.\n\n4. **Error Validation and Correction**: A Verifier checks the accuracy of generated content in real time, and a Router categorizes any detected errors, invoking Solvers for corrections.\n\n5. **Pattern-Enhanced Text Chunking**: The section highlights a training-free method for splitting documents into smaller text chunks based on consistent structural patterns observed in historical documents.\n\nKey entities mentioned include:\n- **AIstorian**: The multi-agent system.\n- **Knowledge Graph (KG)**: The framework used for organizing biographical data.\n- **Verifier, Router, Solvers**: Components of the system responsible for validating and correcting generated content.\n- **Wang Runzhi**: An example of a historical figure mentioned in the context of the system's application. \n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the innovative use of knowledge graphs and structured patterns to enhance the accuracy and reliability of biography generation in historical research."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "86d6a30b-f854-412f-bc3d-7186c1cd0752", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "13c05f2b3c34a30ab2b06b824e9bb3dd58f7f63367e6cdae60eac9f97a72c8ac", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "12a93dee-28e0-4f6d-a5c1-004186e7e7a3", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "de7c60a40306f901f1451ef63341d709bff9a7b6f7418860940cfd7625b4ebc2", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "29d51caf-9676-445b-bc96-b9963cc9f147", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "2728585c64449a1482974cc5dac8a44c87d7d259608802f97fe0e411a536cf8c", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Figure 1 illustrates the overall architecture. The system operates in two modes, with upper half of the figure showing the offline process of index building and model fine-tuning, and the lower half showing the online biography generation pipeline. During the offline phase, AIstorian completes two preparations: (1) KG-based index construction, which reorganizes the biographical facts of historical figures into a knowledge graph, and (2) two-step training, detection and error-type-aware hallucination correction, ensuring that the generated biographies remain faithful to the source biographical data to teach LLMs a specific language style. During the online phase, AIstorian takes as an input a query of \u201cgenerating a biography of a historical figure\u201d, and then invokes the KG-powered RAG to retrieve relevant information (e.g., text chunks) with the assistance of KG-based index. Using the query and the retrieved relevant information, the aligned LLM starts biography generation.\n\nMeanwhile, a Verifier validates the correctness of the generated content in real time. Once an error is detected, a Router categorizes the error and invokes the Solvers to correct it.\n\n# 2.2 KG-based RAG\n\n# 2.2.1 Offline KG-based index construction.\n\nDocuments within the same book series reveal consistent structural patterns: the introduction of person entities follows a standardized format. As illustrated in Figure 2, the introduction of historical figures always begins with the name, followed by the alias and other details (e.g., hometown, career, etc.). Motivated by these, we propose a three-step index construction process to effectively reorganize biographical facts.\n\nTraining-free pattern-enhanced text chunking. Considering that most documents in the external knowledge base follow the same writing pattern, we can leverage the pattern to split long documents into smaller text chunks using in-context learning [24].\n---\n# AIstorian lets AI be a historian: A KG-powered multi-agent system for accurate biography generation\n\nConference acronym \u2019XX, June 03\u201305, 2018, Woodstock, NY\n\nWang Runzhi, styled Yuyuan, nicknamed Tingfang, from Qiantang, Zhejiang. <official career path>.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 7026, "end_char_idx": 9207, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "29d51caf-9676-445b-bc96-b9963cc9f147", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22", "document_title": "\"AIstorian: A Knowledge Graph-Driven Multi-Agent System for Accurate Biography Generation and Error Correction in Historical Research\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the development of \"AIstorian,\" a multi-agent system designed for generating accurate biographies and correcting errors in historical research using a knowledge graph. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Biographical Information**: The section provides examples of historical figures, including their names, styles, and official career paths, highlighting the importance of accurate biographical data.\n\n2. **Stylistic Preference Optimization (StylePO)**: The use of the SimPO algorithm for fine-tuning a language model (LLM) to enhance factual fidelity and align with a classical Chinese language style. This involves training the model with expert-written biographies as positive samples and modified translations as negative samples.\n\n3. **Online Biography Generation**: The challenges of generating biographies with LLMs, including the tendency for the model to produce plausible but inaccurate content (hallucinations) and the cascading effect of errors in auto-regressive outputs.\n\n4. **Error Correction Mechanism**: The AIstorian system employs seven agents, including a Verifier, Router, and five Solvers, to automatically identify and correct errors during the biography generation process.\n\n5. **Verifier Role**: The Verifier checks the accuracy of \"atomic facts\" (individual pieces of biographical information) against retrieved references to ensure the reliability of the generated content.\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the integration of advanced algorithms and multi-agent systems to enhance the accuracy and stylistic quality of biographical generation in historical research."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "86d6a30b-f854-412f-bc3d-7186c1cd0752", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "13c05f2b3c34a30ab2b06b824e9bb3dd58f7f63367e6cdae60eac9f97a72c8ac", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "06a90c63-4a41-4a2c-9ec2-f104b518792e", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "20c063bcd982042218ebd982c011d783d2347f70308c654c4573f74bf5e9eb45", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "60ec944f-82f4-4e81-a1cd-65955a4723d6", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "f9df911441d59914826b8ba52b9e304914d9801aed3d61700cb5536f19d0d358", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "<official career path>.\n\n\u6c6a\u6da6\u4e4b\uff0c \u5b57\u96e8\u5143\uff0c \u53f7\u542c\u822b\uff0c \u6d59\u6c5f\u94b1\u5858\u4eba\u3002 \u6563\u9986\u6388\u7f16\u4fee\uff0c\u5b98\u81f3\u5c11\u8a79\u4e8b\u3002\n\nHong Yao, styled Jingxin, nicknamed Shouyu, from Xin Cheng, Zhejiang. <official career path>.\n\n\u6d2a\u71ff\uff0c \u5b57\u955c\u5fc3\uff0c \u53f7\u5b88\u611a\uff0c \u6d59\u6c5f\u65b0\u57ce\u4eba\u3002 \u6563\u9986\u6539\u540f\u90e8\u4e3b\u4e8b,\u5b98\u81f3\u5e7f\u897f\u5de6\u6c5f\u9053\u3002\n\n# Stylistic preference optimization (StylePO)\n\nTo further align the LLM with preferences for high factual fidelity and a classical Chinese language style, we adopt the SimPO algorithm [14] to proceed fine-tuning the base model. The training set consists of pairs of positive and negative samples. In our setting, each positive sample is a golden biography written by experts in classical Chinese, while each negative sample is generated by translating the positive sample into modern Chinese and adding (or removing) additional details to (or from) the biography. SimPO steers the LLM to more likely generate biographies whose style resembles the expert-written ground truth.\n\n# 2.3.2 Online biography generation\n\nOffline model re-training improves generation quality, but it is inevitable that the LLM will output plausible content due to its inherent hallucination nature. Moreover, since LLMs output in an auto-regressive manner, errors in LLM outputs have a cascading effect, where one error results in further errors in LLM generation [4]. Therefore, error correction should be executed alongside biography generation. To this end, AIstorian orchestrates seven agents to automatically discover and fix errors during LLM generation. The multi-agents consist of a Verifier, a Router, and five Solvers.\n\n# Verifier\n\nFollowing prior work [16], we define the \u201catomic fact\u201d as a short sentence conveying one piece of biographical information. The core logic of the Verifier is to check whether each atomic fact in the generation can be supported by the retrieved references.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 9184, "end_char_idx": 10952, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "60ec944f-82f4-4e81-a1cd-65955a4723d6", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22", "document_title": "\"AIstorian: A Knowledge Graph-Driven Multi-Agent System for Accurate Biography Generation and Error Correction in Historical Research\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the functionality of the AIstorian system, which is a knowledge graph-driven multi-agent system designed for generating accurate biographies and correcting errors in historical research. \n\nKey topics include:\n\n1. **Verifier**: This component checks the validity of atomic facts generated by the system against retrieved references. It uses token-level Jaccard similarity to filter out irrelevant documents and instructs a language model (LLM) to extract supporting information for each atomic fact. The Verifier operates on a sentence-by-sentence basis to prevent cascading errors.\n\n2. **Router**: The Router classifies errors into two main categories:\n   - **Not-included errors**: Occur when an atomic fact is not found in the references.\n   - **Not-supported errors**: Occur when an atomic fact contradicts the references. The Router determines the appropriate corrective actions for each error type.\n\n3. **Solver**: A set of Solvers is employed to address various error types:\n   - **Era-conflict Solver**: Resolves timing-related errors by converting era names to the Gregorian calendar.\n   - **Ref-conflict Solver**: Involves expert intervention to resolve conflicts in references.\n   - **Knowledge-lack Solver**: Retrieves additional information online to address gaps in expertise.\n\nEntities mentioned include the AIstorian system, atomic facts, references, and various types of errors (not-included, not-supported). The section also references a conference and authors (Li et al.) related to the topic."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "86d6a30b-f854-412f-bc3d-7186c1cd0752", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "13c05f2b3c34a30ab2b06b824e9bb3dd58f7f63367e6cdae60eac9f97a72c8ac", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "29d51caf-9676-445b-bc96-b9963cc9f147", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "1d3116d816730ef05153b5842caf13d7a73ef96b50d4ae10d90a92d8e2adff10", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "9c24c511-1c6c-4778-9f42-e5067694452c", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "bf3b2d9447475c30c3fe3248c70713f669cc9cc378576e4e082367695bd7e6d4", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "The core logic of the Verifier is to check whether each atomic fact in the generation can be supported by the retrieved references. To achieve this, the Verifier first filters out the irrelevant documents from all retrieved references to reduce the number of references to be considered, based on the token-level Jaccard similarity between the atomic fact and each reference. In the following, the Verifier instructs the LLM to extract information related to the atomic fact from the remaining references and checks whether the atomic fact is supported. To avoid the cascading effect, the Verifier is executed for every single sentence generated. Once an error is found, AIstorian invokes the subsequent Router and Solvers.\n\n# Router\n\nBased on observations, the errors occurred in the generations are classified into two main categories:\n\n- \u201cNot-included\u201d error. A \u201cnot-included\u201d error occurs when the erroneous atomic fact is not founded in the given references.\n- \u201cNot-supported\u201d error. A \u201cnot-supported\u201d error occurs when the atomic fact in the generation contradicts the given references.\n\n\u201cNot-supported\u201d errors can be classified into finer-grained error types based on the content of the atomic fact. The Router determines the solutions to correct the detected errors based on their types. For \u201cnot-included\u201d errors, AIstorian fixes these errors by regeneration; for \u201cnot-supported\u201d errors, AIstorian invokes Solvers to provide more reliable solutions.\n\n# Solver\n\nTo fix various types of errors, a bunch of Solvers is used.\n\n1. Era-conflict Solver. For errors related to the timing of events, the Solver invokes the Python function to convert the era name into the Gregorian calendar and performs a double-check.\n2. Ref-conflict Solver. For conflicts that occur in the references, the Solver involves expert intervention to resolve the conflict.\n3. Knowledge-lack Solver. For errors caused by a lack of expertise, the Solver retrieves information (e.g., imperial competitive examination, ancient geography, etc.) online to prompt the LLM.\n---\n# Conference acronym \u2019XX, June 03\u201305, 2018, Woodstock, NY\n\n# Li et al.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 10821, "end_char_idx": 12940, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "9c24c511-1c6c-4778-9f42-e5067694452c", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22", "document_title": "\"AIstorian: A Knowledge Graph-Driven Multi-Agent System for Accurate Biography Generation and Error Correction in Historical Research\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the performance of various models in generating biographies and correcting errors in historical research, specifically within the context of a multi-agent system called AIstorian. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Model Performance Metrics**: The excerpt presents a table comparing different models based on several performance metrics, including ROUGE scores (ROUGE-1, ROUGE-2, ROUGE-L), Hallc-Rate, and Average Atomic Fact Error.\n\n2. **Models Compared**: The models evaluated include:\n   - mLongT5_large\n   - Qwen2.5-72B-Instruct-AWQ\n   - TongGu\n   - GraphRAG\n   - CL-KL (NER)\n   - BI-LSTM-CRF (NER)\n   - AIstorian\n   - A variant of AIstorian without multi-agents\n\n3. **Performance Highlights**: \n   - AIstorian achieved the highest scores in ROUGE-1, ROUGE-2, and ROUGE-L metrics, indicating superior performance in biography generation.\n   - The model also had the lowest Average Atomic Fact Error, suggesting it is more accurate in generating factual content compared to other models.\n\n4. **Conference Reference**: The excerpt references a conference where this research was presented, indicating its relevance in the academic community.\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the effectiveness of the AIstorian model in the context of biography generation and historical research, showcasing its advantages over other models."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creat