asizes the importance of accuracy in historical research and the potential of AI technologies like AIstorian to enhance this accuracy."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "86d6a30b-f854-412f-bc3d-7186c1cd0752", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "13c05f2b3c34a30ab2b06b824e9bb3dd58f7f63367e6cdae60eac9f97a72c8ac", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "79ff1081-561f-4a55-b857-73f177675dea", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "54c23aa03e6b49acc5d1883ca25b5c57f0723e13449c33c4271cdc8652a5c011", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "5b2103ef-dba1-4b22-b3e3-8b4cc83b5c59", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "f2c87ba933ad50c56a046ed4be790d4823a46ade66e4647e9bffbc66a9d5ea0a", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "2022. Teaching language models to support answers with verified quotes. arXiv:2203.11147 [cs.CL] https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.11147\n\n# A Appendix\n\n# A.1 Case study\n\nAs shown in Table. 3, AIstorian demonstrates a higher degree of fidelity to the source material, accurately capturing key historical details with remarkable stylistic consistency to golden ones. Additionally, through StylePO, it successfully captures contextual details occasionally overlooked by experts (marked in cyan). In contrast, while the biography produced by Qwen2.5-72B-Instruct appears more fluent and readable, it frequently introduces inaccuracies, such as unsupported factual errors (marked in red) and fabricated content (marked in blue), which compromise the reliability of its outputs.\n---\n# Conference acronym \u2019XX, June 03\u201305, 2018, Woodstock, NY\n\nLi et al.\n\n# Table 3: Qualitative analysis of Biographies\n\nBlue and red colors are used to indicate \"Not included\" errors and \"Not supported\" errors, respectively. Cyan is used to indicate the content that historians have overlooked.\n\n|Historian:|\u80e1\u9102\uff0c\u5b57\u5353\u5eb5\u3002\u660e\u5d07\u796f\u4e09\u5e74\uff081630\uff09\u4e8c\u6708\u5341\u4e09\u65e5\u751f\uff0c\u6d59\u6c5f\u7ecd\u5174\u5e9c\u4f59\u59da\u53bf\u4eba\u3002\u6cbb\u300a\u5c1a\u4e66\u300b\u3002|\n|---|---|\n| |Hu E, styled Zhuo\u2019an. Born on the thirteenth day of the second month in the third year of Chongzhen (1630) of the Ming dynasty, a native of Yuyao County in Shaoxing Prefecture, Zhejiang Province. Studied the Book of Documents.|\n| |He ranked seventy-ninth in the second class, in the palace examination, and was granted the title of Jinshi.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 22085, "end_char_idx": 23556, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "5b2103ef-dba1-4b22-b3e3-8b4cc83b5c59", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22", "document_title": "\"AIstorian: A Knowledge Graph-Driven Multi-Agent System for Accurate Biography Generation and Error Correction in Historical Research\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses Hu E, a historical figure from the Ming dynasty, highlighting his background, achievements, and contributions. Key topics and entities include:\n\n1. **Hu E**: The main subject, known by his courtesy name Zhuo'an, hailing from Yuyao County in Shaoxing Prefecture, Zhejiang Province.\n2. **Birth and Early Life**: Born on the thirteenth day of the second month in 1632, during the Chongzhen era of the Ming dynasty. He was noted for his passion for learning, particularly in the Book of Documents.\n3. **Academic Achievement**: Hu E ranked seventy-ninth in the second class during the palace examination and was awarded the title of Jinshi, a significant academic honor.\n4. **Political Career**: He began his career in the Tongzhengsi and was later appointed as the judicial officer of Songjiang Prefecture in Jiangnan in 1661.\n5. **Reputation**: Known for his integrity and diligence in governance, he earned a good reputation among the people during his tenure in Songjiang.\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes Hu E's scholarly pursuits, his accomplishments in examinations, and his contributions to governance and society."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "86d6a30b-f854-412f-bc3d-7186c1cd0752", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naiv