2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Transforming Software Quality Assurance: The Integration of Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, and Predictive Analytics for Enhanced Testing, Defect Detection, and User Experience\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses various scholarly articles related to the application of Artificial Intelligence (AI) in software quality assurance (QA) and automated testing. Key topics include:\n\n1. **AI in Software Quality Assurance**: The integration of AI, machine learning, and predictive analytics to enhance testing processes, defect detection, and overall user experience in software systems.\n\n2. **Test Case Generation**: The use of generative models for creating test cases, highlighting advancements in automated testing methodologies.\n\n3. **Collaborative Software Testing**: An empirical study focusing on interactions between developers and trackers during collaborative testing efforts.\n\n4. **Automation Tools and Techniques**: Exploration of modern tools and techniques in QA, emphasizing the role of automation in improving QA methodologies.\n\n5. **Digital Science in QA**: Leveraging digital science to enhance QA practices and methodologies.\n\n6. **Automated Testing Environments**: The role of AI in developing automated testing environments to streamline testing processes.\n\nThe section cites multiple authors and studies, with a notable focus on Mouna Mothey's contributions to the field, including articles published in various journals. The references include empirical studies, theoretical discussions, and practical applications of AI in QA."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "f30f272f-f44c-45fa-a7a9-1bbf727c984d", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path