nt]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "1d33b476-a23a-488f-9ac1-946d18adb868", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_name": "Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 52048, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22", "document_title": "\"Transforming Legal Research and Decision-Making: A Comprehensive Framework Integrating Retrieval-Augmented Generation, Knowledge Graphs, Semantic Understanding, and Advanced Machine Learning Techniques\"", "section_summary": "The section provides an overview of legal research and decision-making, highlighting the integration of various advanced techniques in the legal field. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Case Law Statistics**: \n   - Total cases from the Court of Appeals: 10,072\n   - Total cases from the Supreme Court: 5,727\n\n2. **Statutory H-Clusters**: \n   - A table listing various legal categories related to municipal court civil cases, public education, criminal codes, emergency health services, taxation, military regulations, insurance law, public financing, state investment grants, water rights, military honors, and corporate governance.\n\n3. **Appeals Court Case Law H-Clusters**: \n   - A table detailing legal issues such as real property rights, civil liability in healthcare, parental rights in custody disputes, motor vehicle insurance claims, mortgage foreclosure, and tribal jurisdiction.\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the structured categorization of legal topics and the depth of case law available in New Mexico, reflecting a comprehensive framework for legal research and decision-making."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_meta