s|\n|7|Public Obligations Financing and Project Bonds Issuance|\n|8|State Government Investment Grants for Education and Economic Development|\n|9|Irrigation and Water Rights Regulations|\n|10|Military Honors, Discrimination Penalties, and Trust Authority|\n|11|Corporation Governance Framework and Regulatory Compliance|\n\n**Table 3: NM Appeals Court Case Law Depth-0 H-Clusters**\n|#|Label|\n|---|---|\n|0|Real Property Rights and Interests|\n|1|Civil Liability and Injury Issues Arising from Healthcare Services|\n|2|Parental Rights and Custody Proceedings Involving Disputed Parental Fitness|\n|3|Motor Vehicle Insurance and Liability Claims Processing Procedures|\n|4|Mortgage Foreclosure and Secured Lending Frameworks|\n|5|Arraignments, Tribal Jurisdiction, Divorce, Bond Conditions,", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 23170, "end_char_idx": 24519, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "e07f7e78-9969-41a8-9713-909116ada3f0", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_name": "Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 52048, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22", "document_title": "\"Transforming Legal Research and Decision-Making: A Comprehensive Framework Integrating Retrieval-Augmented Generation, Knowledge Graphs, Semantic Understanding, and Advanced Machine Learning Techniques\"", "section_summary": "The section outlines various legal topics and concepts related to courtroom procedures, family law, criminal law, and administrative disputes. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Tribal Jurisdiction and Family Law**: Issues surrounding divorce, parental decision-making rights, and child protective services.\n2. **Criminal Law**: Topics such as Fourth Amendment protections, sentencing enhancements for repeat offenders, and procedures related to unlawful searches and seizures.\n3. **Legal Representation**: Strategies for courtroom advocacy and representation.\n4. **Financial and Business Law**: Taxation of gross receipts, business disputes, and financial disposition in marital property.\n5. **Workers' Rights**: Focus on work-related injury compensation and insurance benefits.\n6. **Governance and Legal Frameworks**: Public municipal legal structures and administrative disputes, including Native American legal considerations.\n\nAdditionally, the section discusses the hierarchical decomposition of legal data types using Non-negative Matrix Factorization (NMFk) to build a TF-IDF matrix, specifying parameters for vocabulary collection across different legal domains, including the Constitution, statutes, and Court of Appeals. The document highlights the importance of token document frequency in determining the vocabulary size for each legal category."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "1d3f5bd7-239e-43d2-ae7f-1e7cd01c88fb", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_name": "Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 52048, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "8b9a69e79061b64e3a9958d47ca5223db6e2ffd6fcab4d00822647d6e5777090", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "1d33b476-a23a-488f-9ac1-946d18adb868", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_name": "Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 52048, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "f6373c04db76ba35584fab678f86c1e19f31280a43927381b9950c339c7ac1a3", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "449bf1bb-ce0a-4f11-912e-274f80ab6890", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "ab04541ca32ba426b978e4e8a3b11c3d15c640053ff661a7618f052a7cb9f7a5", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Tribal Jurisdiction, Divorce, Bond Conditions, Motor Licensing|\n|6|Courtroom Advocacy and Representation Strategies|\n|7|Petitioner\u2019s Right to Parental Decision Making|\n|8|Fourth Amendment Protections Against Unlawful Searches and Seizures|\n|9|Taxation of Gross Receipts and Sales Transactions in a Business Context|\n|10|Key Legal Concepts Related to Sexual Offenses|\n|11|Child Protective Services Laws and Regulations|\n|12|Work-Related Injury and Disability Compensation Process|\n|13|Healthcare Contract Dispute Resolution Processes|\n|14|Marital Property and Financial Disposition|\n|15|Legal Proceedings Involving Jury Determination of Guilt|\n|16|Probation Supervision and Monitoring Oversight Process|\n|17|Juvenile Protection, Miranda Rights, Evidence Collection|\n|18|Firearms, Substances, DWI, and Sentencing|\n|19|Sentencing Enhancements for Serious Repeat Offenders|\n|20|Traffic Stop Under Suspicion with Mandatory Blood Alcohol Testing|\n|21|Criminal Proceedings Trial Litigation Documentation and Record-Keeping Procedures|\n|22|Workers\u2019 Rights and Insurance Benefits|\n|23|Children\u2019s Welfare and Family Reunification Efforts|\n|24|Public Municipal Legal Frameworks and Governance Structure|\n|25|Business Disputes, Wrongful Injury, Taxation Appeals, Workers\u2019 Compensation|\n|26|Administrative Disputes, Native American Legal Memorandums|\n\n# 4.2 Decomposition\n\nThe four component data types were decomposed hierarchically with NMFk. The vocabulary for building the TF-IDF matrix was collected using specific parameters for each part. For the Constitution vocabulary, the minimum token document frequency (DF) was set to 5 documents, with a maximum token DF of 80% of the corpus, resulting in a final size of 416 tokens. For the Statutes vocabulary, the minimum token DF was set to 30 documents, with a maximum token DF of 70% of the corpus, yielding 7,508 tokens. The Court of Appeals vocabulary used a minimum token DF of 50 documents (cases) and a maximum token DF of 70% of the corpus, resulting in 10,189 tokens.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 24473, "end_char_idx": 26488, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "449bf1bb-ce0a-4f11-912e-274f80ab6890", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_name": "Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 52048, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22", "document_title": "\"Transforming Legal Research and Decision-Making: A Comprehensive Framework Integrating Retrieval-Augmented Generation, Knowledge Graphs, Semantic Understanding, and Advanced Machine Learning Techniques\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the vocabulary and tokenization strategies used in legal research, specifically focusing on the Court of Appeals and Supreme Court. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Token Document Frequency (DF)**: Both the Court of Appeals and Supreme Court vocabularies utilized a minimum token DF of 50 documents (cases) and a maximum of 70% of the total corpus.\n2. **Token Counts**: The Court of Appeals vocabulary resulted in 10,189 tokens, while the Supreme Court vocabulary had 8,425 tokens.\n3. **Maximum Depth**: The maximum depth for analysis was set to 2, with the exception of constitutional sections, which did not reach this depth due to a limited number of sections.\n4. **Decomposition Limitation**: Further decomposition of clusters was limited by a threshold of 100 documents; if a cluster had 100 or more documents, it would decompose, otherwise, it would stop.\n\nEntities mentioned include the Court of Appeals and the Supreme Court, as well as concepts related to legal document analysis and tokenization."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "1d3f5bd7-239e-43d2-ae7f-1e7cd01c88fb", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_name": "Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 52048, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "8b9a69e79061b64e3a9958d47ca5223db6e2ffd6fcab4d00822647d6e5777090", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "e07f7e78-9969-41a8-9713-909116ada3f0", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_name": "Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 52048, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "bf48abece368b2eeb32b5cdd9d12d9c51b04e75b0624ab4ef29701136bfce084", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "62b965b7-27aa-49ce-b463-4573f7022841", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "7a90c934d195b5ede604e021ce17c5fb3b6db975c663ea048b17d6e97e4e89c8", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "The Court of Appeals vocabulary used a minimum token DF of 50 documents (cases) and a maximum token DF of 70% of the corpus, resulting in 10,189 tokens. Last, the Supreme vocabulary employed a minimum token DF of 50 papers and a maximum token DF of 70% of the corpus, with a final size of 8,425 tokens. The maximum depth was set to 2, of which only the constitution sections did not reach due to the limited number of sections. The limiting factor of further decompositions was 100 documents, so if the preceding cluster had \u2265 100, the cluster would decompose and stop otherwise.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 26336, "end_char_idx": 26915, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "62b965b7-27aa-49ce-b463-4573f7022841", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_name": "Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 52048, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22", "document_title": "\"Transforming Legal Research and Decision-Making: A Comprehensive Framework Integrating Retrieval-Augmented Generation, Knowledge Graphs, Semantic Understanding, and Advanced Machine Learning Techniques\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the organization and clustering of legal documents, specifically focusing on the NM Supreme Court case law. It highlights a method for clustering legal topics based on a limit of 100 documents per cluster. A table is provided that lists various legal topics, including:\n\n1. Arbitration of contract disputes\n2. Revenue and taxation frameworks\n3. Mineral rights leases\n4. Native American self-governance\n5. Municipal zoning ordinances\n6. Damages for wrongful conduct\n7. Jurisdictional appeals and sentencing\n8. Post-divorce asset distribution\n9. Constitutional challenges in education governance\n10. Secured financial instruments\n11. Water resource management\n12. Electric utility regulation\n13. Law enforcement procedures\n14. Legislative review processes\n15. Habeas corpus petitions\n16. Workers\u2019 compensation\n17. Real estate disputes\n18. Parental rights and guardianship\n19. Appellate arguments\n20. Business transaction terms\n21. Insurance policies\n22. Legal consequences of driver errors\n23. Civil litigation proceedings\n\nAdditionally, the section mentions the integration of various legal data types into a Neo4j knowledge graph, including constitutional provisions, statute sections, Supreme Court cases, and Court of Appeals cases. This integration aims to enhance legal research and decision-making through advanced data organization and semantic understanding."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "1d3f5bd7-239e-43d2-ae7f-1e7cd01c88fb", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_name": "Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 52048, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "8b9a69e79061b64e3a9958d47ca5223db6e2ffd6fcab4d00822647d6e5777090", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "449bf1bb-ce0a-4f11-912e-274f80ab6890", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\Br