.1038/s41598-021-92146-7\n13. Javaid M, Haleem A, Khan IH, Vaishya R, Vaish A. Extending capabilities of artificial intelligence for decision-making and healthcare education. Apollo Medicine. 2020;17(1):53. doi:10.4103/am.am_10_20\n14. Coraci D, Maccarone MC, Regazzo G, Accordi G, Papathanasiou JV, Masiero S. ChatGPT in the development of medical questionnaires. The example of the low back pain. Eur J Transl Myol. 2023;33(4):12114. doi:10.4081/ejtm.2023.12114\n15. Geoghegan L, Scarborough A, Wormald JCR, et al. Automated conversational agents for post-intervention follow-up: a systematic review. BJS Open. 2021;5(4):zrab070. doi:10.1093/bjsopen/zrab070\n16. Xu L, Sanders L, Li K, Chow JCL. Chatbot for Health Care and Oncology Applications using artificial intelligence and machine learning: systematic review. JMIR Cancer. 2021;7(4):e27850. doi:10.2196/27850\n17.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 24930, "end_char_idx": 26228, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "f6bb0c71-c6f5-42cd-b735-816762f3099b", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\Chatbots and Their Applications in Medical Fields Current Status.md", "file_name": "Chatbots and Their Applications in Medical Fields Current Status.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 28958, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-23", "document_title": "\"Advancing Healthcare: A Comprehensive Review of Chatbots and AI in Medical Applications, Trends, Challenges, and Future Opportunities\"", "section_summary": "The section provides a list of references related to the applications of chatbots and artificial intelligence (AI) in the medical field, particularly focusing on cancer care, psychiatry, and infectious diseases. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Large Language Models in Cancer Care**: The use of advanced AI models in improving cancer treatment and patient care, as discussed in the reference by Iannantuono et al. (2023).\n\n2. **AI-Enabled Chatbots in Medical Science**: An overview of chatbots, with a specific emphasis on ChatGPT and its implications in medical applications, highlighted by Chakraborty et al. (2023).\n\n3. **ChatGPT in Psychiatry**: The current and future roles of ChatGPT and similar AI technologies in psychiatric practice, as explored by Cheng et al. (2023).\n\n4. **AI and Chatbots in Psychiatry**: The integration of AI and chatbots in psychiatric care, discussed by Pham et al. (2022).\n\n5. **AI in Infectious Disease**: The potential applications of AI, using ChatGPT as a case study, in managing infectious diseases, as presented by Cheng et al. (2023).\n\n6. **Reflections on Mpox Outbreak**: Insights and suggestions from AI perspectives regarding the Mpox outbreak in 2022, also by Cheng et al. (2023).\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the growing significance of AI and chatbots in various medical domains, highlighting current research and future opportunities."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "dad35ff1-58aa-45cb-b326-0446ff627bda", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\Chatbots and Their Applications in Medical Fields Current Status.md", "file_name": "Chatbots and Their Applications in Medical Fields Current Status.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 28958, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-23"}, "hash": "4d0315e8f144da5f7f359eae5fa855cbb6e34f8f15c19f56fd0a30b52a22b7b2", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo