Their Applications in Medical Fields Current Status.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 28958, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-23", "document_title": "\"Advancing Healthcare: A Comprehensive Review of Chatbots and AI in Medical Applications, Trends, Challenges, and Future Opportunities\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the role of ChatGPT and its efficiency in providing accurate and quality health-related information, particularly in the context of orthopaedic residents. It references two specific studies: one published in \"Clinical Orthopaedics and Related Research\" that compares orthopaedic residents with ChatGPT, and another published in \"Cureus\" that evaluates ChatGPT's effectiveness in accessing health information. Additionally, it mentions an upcoming issue of \"Apollo Medicine\" scheduled for December 2024. The key topics include the application of AI in healthcare, the evaluation of chatbot efficiency, and the ongoing research in this field."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "dad35ff1-58aa-45cb-b326-0446ff627bda", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\Chatbots and Their Applications in Medical Fields Current Status.md", "file_name": "Chatbots and Their Applications in Medical Fields Current Status.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 28958, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-23"}, "hash": "4d0315e8f144da5f7f359eae5fa855cbb6e34f8f15c19f56fd0a30b52a22b7b2", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "f65beeb9-6ea3-42bd-836c-eae841c2441e", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\Chatbots and Their Applications in Medical Fields Current Status.md", "file_name": "Chatbots and Their Applications in Medical Fields Current Status.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 28958, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-23"}, "hash": "024a14cae8f05fe5e52524731859b87802b87f501477850cd08201c4516dfac1", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Orthopaedic residents versus ChatGPT. Clin Orthop Relat Res. 2023;481(8):1623\u201330. doi:10.1097/CORR.0000000000002704\n29. Ulusoy I, Y\u0131lmaz M, K\u0131vrak A. How efficient is ChatGPT in accessing accurate and quality health-related information? Cureus. 2023;15(10):e46662. doi:10.7759/cureus.46662\n\nApollo Medicine Volume 21 Issue 4 December 2024", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 28541, "end_char_idx": 28879, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "98e73893-d231-486b-95b0-c02c8b4b68dd", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the topic of Computer System Validation (CSV) within the context of Quality Management Systems (QMS) in the pharmaceutical industry. It highlights the importance of ensuring data integrity when using electronic records, emphasizing the need for compliance with regulatory requirements set by leading authorities such as the US Food and Drug Administration (FDA) and the European Medicines Agency (EMA). \n\nKey topics include:\n- The purpose of the paper, which is to present a practical example of QMS for computer systems validation.\n- The definition of QMS elements specific to computer system validation based on European and US legal requirements.\n- The validation process illustrated through a general V-model, detailing stages such as Planning, Specifying, Development/Building, Verification, and Reporting.\n- The use of process diagrams to demonstrate validation activities in a Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition (SCADA) manufacturing context.\n\nKey entities mentioned:\n- Borut Rusjan (author)\n- European Compliance Academy\n- US Food and Drug Administration (FDA)\n- European Medicines Agency (EMA)\n\nOverall, the excerpt emphasizes the critical role of structured validation processes in maintaining compliance and ensuring the integrity of electronic records in the pharmaceutical sector."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "9b1fe93f-84e8-4b53-8a9f-ae678f789f83", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "8f9409bbcb73a7e79b9d8baa633ad6ca585cf94bfbf2ebd37fa50e7e95238b06", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "# COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION: EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM DESIGN AND OF PROCESS IMPLEMENTATION\n\nBorut Rusjan*\n\nReceived: 26. 12. 2019\n\nOriginal scientific paper\n\nAccepted: 14. 11. 2020\n\nUDC 005.6:004\n\nDOI: https://doi.org/10.30924/mjcmi.25.2.1\n\n# Abstract\n\nThe purpose of this paper is to present a computer-aided system validation example. Quality Management System (QMS) for computer systems validation and to identify and demonstrate the validation process on a practical case of a pharmaceutical company. Based on the European and the US legal requirements, we define QMS for computer system validation elements. Validation process example based on the use of a general V-model provides a thorough understanding of the actual validation implementation in practice. Computer system validation in a concrete organization can be implemented, based on general and specific standard operating procedures which form the QMS. Planning, Specifying, Development/Building, Verification and Report validation activities are presented through process diagrams based on a practical Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition (SCADA) manufacturing.\n\n# Keywords\n\nQuality Management System, computer systems, validation, V-model, pharmaceutical industry\n\n# 1. INTRODUCTION\n\nIn today\u2019s world, when we operate with electronic records, the possibility of changing or copying the contents of electronic records, without leaving any visible trace of the change, is extremely high. According to the European Compliance Academy (2011a, p. 8), even in the case of the use of computer systems, regulatory authorities want to ensure data integrity through computer systems validation in accordance with their requirements. The world\u2019s leading regulatory bodies that set minimum conditions and limitations, both in general and in the field of computer-aided systems in the pharmaceutical industry, are the US Food and Drug Administration (FDA) and the European Medicines Agency (EMA).", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 0, "end_char_idx": 1968, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "9b1fe93f-84e8-4b53-8a9f-ae678f789f83", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The excerpt discusses the importance of quality management and computer system validation in the pharmaceutical industry, emphasizing regulatory frameworks and best practices. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Quality Management Systems**: Pharmaceutical companies are required to establish comprehensive quality systems to ensure traceability in production and supportive processes.\n\n2. **Computer System Validation**: The regulation surrounding computer system validation is described as both general and specific, mandating the validation of critical procedures and the education of personnel involved.\n\n3. **Regulatory Bodies and Guidelines**: The excerpt references various regulatory bodies, including the US FDA and EU legislation, which provide recommendations for implementing validation processes. The ISPE GAMP5 manual is highlighted as a significant resource for interpreting regulatory requirements and establishing quality systems for computer systems validation.\n\n4. **Quality Models**: The text mentions the development of quality models that transition from legal requirements to practical frameworks for computer systems in the pharmaceutical sector.\n\nEntities mentioned include:\n- **Borut Rusjan, PhD**: Author and professor at the University of Ljubljana.\n- **International Society for Pharmaceutical Engineering (ISPE)**: Organization that developed the GAMP5 manual.\n- **Regulatory Bodies**: US FDA and EU legislation.\n\nOverall, the excerpt underscores the critical role of computer system validation and quality management in ensuring data integrity and compliance within the pharmaceutical industry."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "98e73893-d231-486b-95b0-c02c8b4b68dd", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "d628131bb45ca7404bf48daba09826b3f507f517d8e6bf9914fa51ba5cbcf3b7", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "43795fb5-f355-4844-9443-1a78d5bff494", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "be7929bc45b56782206e827737be647ffef250fdd69ede7167a582783a79e9b1", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "* Borut Rusjan, PhD, Professor, University of Ljubljana, School of Economics and Business, Kardeljeva plo\u0161\u010dad 17, 1000 Ljubljana, Slovenia, Phone: +386 1 5892 553, E-mail: borut.rusjan@ef.uni-lj.si, ORCID: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7061-9242\n---\n# Journal of Contemporary Management Issues\n\nCommission, 2013a, 2013b; US FDA, 2013a, 2013b). Pharmaceutical companies are expected to establish a quality system at all levels of the organization and assure traceability of production and supportive processes (MetricStream, 2014). The paper deals with the computer system quality assurance in the pharmaceutical industry, where data integrity is crucial (Sai et al., 2019; Ranbaxy Laboratories Limited, 2014, pp. 1-20), since today there is virtually no production process that is not regulated and controlled by a single, or multiple computer systems.\n\nThe regulation of computer system validations is, on the one hand, very general, but on the other, it states quite clearly what is required from an organization. According to Velkovrh Remec (2007), both the US and the EU legislations require the validation of all critical procedures, processes and systems and the education of all individuals involved in the process. Regulatory bodies also give numerous recommendations for the implementation of specific systems validation. In the field of computer system validation in the pharmaceutical industry, the well-known professional manual of the International Society for Pharmaceutical Engineering Good Automated Manufacturing Practice- ISPE GAMP5 (2008) has been developed. ISPE GAMP5 interprets regulatory requirements for the computer systems validation and aids in setting up a quality system for validating computer systems.\n\nIn terms of quality of computer systems in the pharmaceutical industry, we distinguish between three concepts. The first is to create a quality model, where we move from legal requirements to the first drafts and frameworks, defining what we need to provide in the field of computer systems in the pharmaceutical industry. From these.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 1970, "end_char_idx": 4036, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "43795fb5-f355-4844-9443-1a78d5bff494", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the integration of Quality Management Systems (QMS) and Computer System Validation (CSV) within the pharmaceutical industry, focusing on regulatory frameworks and best practices. It addresses two primary research questions: \n\n1. The standard operating procedures that constitute a specific pharmaceutical company's QMS for computer system validation.\n2. The methodology for validating computer systems in compliance with pharmaceutical industry regulations.\n\nThe paper outlines the legal requirements in both the European and US contexts, comparing them to define essential QMS elements for CSV. It employs the V-model methodology, a prevalent approach in the industry, to illustrate the validation process of a computer-supported production system.\n\nThe research methods include descriptive and comparative analysis of legal requirements, as well as the design of a QMS for CSV using classification and compilation techniques. The effectiveness of the proposed QMS is evaluated through a case study and action research within a pharmaceutical company, specifically analyzing the validation of a Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition (SCADA) manufacturing system.\n\nKey topics include:\n- Quality Management Systems (QMS)\n- Computer System Validation (CSV)\n- Regulatory requirements (European and US)\n- V-model methodology\n- Research methods (case study, action research)\n\nEntities mentioned:\n- Pharmaceutical industry\n- Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition (SCADA) systems\n- Authors and references (B. Rusjan, Eisenhardt, Siggelkow, Yin)"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "9b1fe93f-84e8-4b53-8a9f-ae678f789f83", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "490eeb88849a74d02dab5b44c38938bd1289abe6a53c615fea94f03d5ec16fd2", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "1098590a-3366-48b9-9f10-10e7f92a6408", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "61324ce1097a0c5644d7541b29da6cbcb2500d95b506db42166d0ef988810315", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "From these.\n\n# Research Questions\n\nThe paper addresses two basic research questions:\n\n1. What are the standard operating procedures forming a specific pharmaceutical company QMS for computer system validation;\n2. How to perform the validation of the computer system, considering the pharmaceutical industry regulatory requirements.\n---\n# Management, Vol. 25, 2020, No. 2, pp. 1-23\n\n# B. Rusjan: COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION: EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT ...\n\nTo answer these questions, the paper first outlines the legal requirements governing the pharmaceutical industry and by comparing them defines the basic QMS elements for computer system validation. This is followed by an example of the process of validating a computer-supported production system in the pharmaceutical industry, which provides a thorough understanding of the actual validation implementation in practice and its connections with regulatory requirements. As a basic starting point for identifying the process of validating a computer system, we used the V-model methodology approach to validation, which is the most widespread within the area of computer-based system validation in the pharmaceutical industry.\n\n# 2. METHODS\n\nThe paper identifies the European and the US legal requirements governing the pharmaceutical industry by using descriptive and comparison methods. Then, we design a QMS for computer systems validation, by using classification and compilation methods.\n\nThe usefulness of the designed QMS was tested on a specific case within a pharmaceutical company. In this empirical part, we, therefore, employed two research strategies; a single case study and action research. We intended to analyse whether the general and specific standard operating procedures, which form the QMS, provide an appropriate framework for the validation of a concrete project of Supervisory control and data acquisition (SCADA) manufacturing computer system implementation. The validation example was based on the use of a general V-model for validation of computer systems. A single case study may be justifiable, when the research topic is in its early stages (Eisenhardt, 1989), when it is used to persuade (Siggelkow, 2007), and when used as a representative/typical, or a revelatory case (Yin, 2009).\n\n# 3.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 4025, "end_char_idx": 6305, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "1098590a-3366-48b9-9f10-10e7f92a6408", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses regulatory requirements in the pharmaceutical industry, specifically focusing on the European Union's EudraLex guidelines, which govern medicinal products. Key topics include:\n\n1. **EudraLex Overview**: EudraLex consists of 10 volumes, with Volume 4 addressing good manufacturing practices (GMP) and computer systems.\n2. **Relevant Chapters and Annexes**: \n   - Chapter 4 emphasizes good documentation practices as part of quality assurance.\n   - Annex 11 pertains to computer systems classified as GxP (Good Practices), which includes GMP and GLP (Good Laboratory Practices).\n   - Annex 15 outlines qualification and validation processes.\n3. **Key Principles from Annex 11**:\n   - The principles apply to all GxP systems, not just GMP.\n   - A risk-based approach is essential in all areas of validation.\n   - Acceptance of electronic records is acknowledged.\n   - Validation focuses on system design verification.\n   - Consideration of external suppliers of GxP-relevant IT systems is necessary.\n   - Clear milestones between validation and operational phases of IT systems are required.\n\nEntities mentioned include the European Commission and the European Compliance Academy, which provide guidance and standards for compliance in the pharmaceutical sector."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "43795fb5-f355-4844-9443-1a78d5bff494", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "ceb3e9a199a2a75f32afa4031603e345f0a085852dd4020f4efe06a003bf3d07", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "4def3c13-9e32-43ea-a772-4064cc8d559d", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "03af59ec4b6d625643483d3ac42965ce8efbcea89d5b3146f8363f47f411a1c8", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "# 3. REGULATORY REQUIREMENTS IN THE PHARMACEUTICAL INDUSTRY\n\nWhen considering current European regulatory requirements, we rely on the EU Legislation rules for governing medicinal products in the European Union, called EudraLex. EudraLex guidelines consist of 10 volumes and computer systems are described in Volume 4, which regulates good manufacturing practice (GMP). Although Volume 4 includes several chapters and annexes, only two of them are directly related to the validation of the computer systems: Chapter 4, which describes good documentation practices and Annex 11, which describes computer systems (European Commission, 2013a). Qualification and validation in general are described in Annex 15.\n---\n# Journal of Contemporary Management Issues\n\nAs stated in EudraLex, Volume 4, Chapter 4 (European Commission, 2011a, p. 2), document management is a key part of quality assurance and of operating in accordance with good manufacturing practice. Annex 11 relates to all types of computer systems, which are classified as GxP. GxP refers to systems used in good practices, where \"x\" represents a variable. So GxP can for example be GMP (Good Manufacturing Practices) or GLP (Good Laboratory Practices) etc. IT applications and IT infrastructure, which are subject to qualification activities, are also included into these guidelines. Regulation emphasise that using computer systems instead of manual operations shall not have negative impact on the product quality, process control or quality assurance and should not increase the process overall risks (European Commission, 2011b, p. 2).\n\nAccording to the European Compliance Academy (2011a, pg. 11) the following are the key points from Annex 11 that should be considered in computer system validation:\n\n- Described principles apply for GxP and not only for GMP.\n- Risk based approach should be considered in all areas.\n- Electronic records are acceptable.\n- During validation, the focus is on checking system design.\n- External suppliers of GxP relevant IT systems are taken into consideration.\n- Milestone between the validation phase and the operational phase of IT systems should be clear.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 6301, "end_char_idx": 8456, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "4def3c13-9e32-43ea-a772-4064cc8d559d", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the importance of computer system validation (CSV) within the context of quality management in the pharmaceutical industry, particularly focusing on regulatory frameworks established by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). Key topics include:\n\n1. **Regulatory Frameworks**: The section highlights the significance of 21 CFR Part 211 (current good manufacturing practices) and 21 CFR Part 11 (electronic records and electronic signatures) as critical regulations for validating computer systems.\n\n2. **Validation Phases**: It emphasizes the need for a clear distinction between the validation phase and the operational phase of IT systems, particularly for Good Manufacturing Practice (GxP) relevant IT systems supplied by external vendors.\n\n3. **Key Requirements of 21 CFR Part 11**:\n   - System controls, including validation, security of electronic records, unauthorized access controls, and change management.\n   - Controls for electronic signatures, including identification of the signee, timestamps, and responsibilities.\n   - The connection between electronic signatures and electronic data.\n   - User identification methods, such as biometrical identification and user administration.\n\n4. **Broader Considerations**: The section notes that effective computer system validation requires a comprehensive understanding of both technical and procedural controls, as well as adherence to additional regulatory requirements outlined in 21 CFR Part 211.\n\n5. **References**: The excerpt cites Lopez (2012) to support its claims regarding the technical and procedural controls necessary for electronic records and signatures.\n\nOverall, the section underscores the critical nature of adhering to regulatory requirements for ensuring the integrity and reliability of computer systems in the pharmaceutical industry."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "1098590a-3366-48b9-9f10-10e7f92a6408", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "a0f1887188213e9c0b5f9edc3ed0cbec31fc0a27085214e579117ae890c09707", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "c805d402-d81a-466c-9abd-3ad96b705d24", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "fe25fd63959be3ed4e3ce18c042c2a3feb66ed08c13dae3574bee85aedb5244b", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "- External suppliers of GxP relevant IT systems are taken into consideration.\n- Milestone between the validation phase and the operational phase of IT systems should be clear.\n\nUS regulatory agency FDA and its regulatory requirements can be found in the section Code of Federal Regulations (CFR).\n\nFor validation of computer systems, 21 CFR Part 211 and 21 CFR Part 11 are important. Number 21 represents the section of foods and medicines, Part 211 represents current good manufacturing practices (cGMP), and Part 11 represents electronic records and electronic signatures (U.S. Food and Drug Administration - FDA, 2013a, 2013b).\n\nCrucial for the computer system validation from FDA point of view is 21 CFR Part 11, which covers electronic records and electronic signatures and includes (U.S. Food and Drug Administration - FDA, 2013b):\n\n- System controls (closed and open type of computer system) \u2013 system validation, electronic records security, unauthorized access controls, system change management etc.\n- Controls for electronic signatures \u2013 signee identification, timestamp, responsibility (e.g. author, reviewer, approver).\n- Connection between electronic signature and electronic data.\n- Users identification \u2013 biometrical identification, username and password, user administration etc.\n\nLopez (2012) states that 21 CFR Part 11 requirements are considering more technical and procedural controls in case of electronic records (creation, modification, storage, archiving, copy, restoration) and electronic signatures. Annex 11, on the other hand, covers all activities, needed for computer system validation. To be able to validate computer systems, we, therefore, also need to consider a broader picture, which includes the regulatory requirements 21 CFR Part 211 (for computer systems subsections D (\u00a7211.68) and E (\u00a7211.80).\n---\n# Management, Vol. 25, 2020, No. 2, pp. 1-23\n\n# B. Rusjan: COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION: EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT ...\n\n# 4.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 8281, "end_char_idx": 10247, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "c805d402-d81a-466c-9abd-3ad96b705d24", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the establishment of a quality system for computer system validation within the pharmaceutical industry, emphasizing the importance of adhering to legal requirements. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Quality System Development**: The need for creating instructions and policies, known as standard operating procedures (SOPs), that encapsulate legal requirements for all employees.\n\n2. **Types of SOPs**:\n   - **General SOPs**: Applicable across various activities and business processes, including:\n     - Good documentation practices.\n     - Archiving procedures for electronic and paper records, crucial for accessibility during product recalls or investigations.\n     - Training procedures for users, particularly in relation to system functionality changes.\n   - **Specific SOPs**: Tailored for the implementation of computer system validation.\n\nThe excerpt highlights the significance of both general and specific SOPs in ensuring compliance and effective management of computer systems in the pharmaceutical sector."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "4def3c13-9e32-43ea-a772-4064cc8d559d", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "c87494622e4e148f10382b84134e5ba074e8fce652c855b4d25a6aa94df85b6c", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "4defe687-f292-4a8e-befb-664afd2c08ea", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "29e56ed7902721f77e75ed55a9f58f778ed2904e47beb544191abc9924c7eb3d", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "25, 2020, No. 2, pp. 1-23\n\n# B. Rusjan: COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION: EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT ...\n\n# 4. ESTABLISHING QUALITY SYSTEM FOR COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION\n\nTo develop a quality system for the computer systems validation, the legal requirements must be respected and fully implemented in the quality system. Establishing a successful quality system requires creating instructions and policies (which represent standard operating procedures - SOP), that summarize the parts of the legal requirements, which are then followed by all employees in the organization. We can distinguish between general and specific standard operating procedures (Sallubier and Rusjan, 2017).\n\nThe general SOP, developed in case of a pharmaceutical company, which are intended for use within most of the activities and business processes of the organization, are as follows:\n\n- Procedures for good documentation practice;\n- Procedures, which determine approaches and time periods of archiving for different records types in both, electronic and paper form. This is important for record accessibility and is needed, e.g. in cases of product recalls from the market, if investigations of deviations from good manufacturing practices need to be conducted, or in other cases when records are evidence of proper implementation of processes (e.g. manufacturing, laboratory);\n- Procedures which prescribe trainings for users, e.g. frequency and type of trainings. From the computer system point of view, this is very important, because when a system\u2019s functionality is developed or upgraded, consequentially, the work instructions or user manuals are changed accordingly.\n\nIn addition to the general SOP, which support multiple business processes in an organization, we also need specific SOP for the implementation of computer system validation.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 10140, "end_char_idx": 11967, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "4defe687-f292-4a8e-befb-664afd2c08ea", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the importance of Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) specific to computer system validation within the pharmaceutical industry. Key topics include:\n\n1. **General and Specific SOPs**: The need for both general SOPs that support various business processes and specific SOPs tailored for computer system validation.\n\n2. **Critical SOPs for Validation**:\n   - Overall procedure for computer systems validation.\n   - High-Level Risk Assessment execution.\n   - Assessment of computer system suppliers.\n   - Management of changes in computer systems.\n   - Access control and authorization management.\n   - Backup, archiving, and restoration of electronic records.\n   - Assurance of operational continuity.\n   - Configuration management.\n   - Incident management.\n   - Inventory management.\n   - Periodic reviews of computer systems.\n\n3. **Social Aspects**: Emphasizes the importance of addressing social issues related to governance, execution, training, and personnel in the effective use of SOPs.\n\n4. **Computer System Life Cycle**: Introduces the concept of the computer system life cycle, which includes systematic development activities, implementation, application, and retirement of computer systems. It references the GAMP5 framework and the V-model for minimizing quality risks and ensuring regulatory compliance.\n\n5. **Validation Phases**: Highlights the five fundamental activities in the computer system project phase/validation: planning, specifying, building/development, verification, and reporting.\n\nOverall, the section underscores the necessity of structured procedures and frameworks to ensure quality management and compliance in computer system validation within the pharmaceutical sector."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "c805d402-d81a-466c-9abd-3ad96b705d24", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "2459b852b5237b9538a67b258d4b5272585f0f04f10c6a3e50f21ed52a8040e3", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "d42bf0f1-a35e-41e6-9cf1-1ad44b14ee3e", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "1f17cecbad899dd47fcb920485e472ad9d5223b5314c676ff96e126cacb10c28", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "In addition to the general SOP, which support multiple business processes in an organization, we also need specific SOP for the implementation of computer system validation. These are procedures that are related to the specifics of validation, and the most important ones in the case of a pharmaceutical company are:\n\n- The overall general procedure that prescribes the computer systems validation;\n- Execution of High-Level Risk Assessment;\n- Assessment of computer system supplier;\n- Management of changes in computer systems;\n- Computer system access control and authorization management;\n---\n# Journal of Contemporary Management Issues\n\n- Performing backups, archiving electronic records, and restoring a computer system;\n- Computer system operational continuity assurance;\n- Computer system Configuration management;\n- Computer system Incident management;\n- Computer system inventory;\n- Computer system periodic reviews;\n\nTo assure appropriate use of the SOP social aspect is of critical importance. Sing et al. (2018) identify and explain common problems related to social issues challenges in organization and governance, execution, training, and personnel.\n\n# 5. COMPUTER SYSTEM LIFE CYCLE WITH VALIDATION CASE EXAMPLE\n\n# 5.1. Computer system life cycle\n\nTo ensure regulatory compliance, as well as that the computer system operates within the required specifications, we must consider the computer system life cycle (PIC/S, 2007, p. 7), which provides an understanding of the requirements that have to be met, regarding the computer system and systematic development activities, implementation, application and computer system retirement. Figure 1 shows the computer system life cycle concept as a whole, composed of four phases, as indicated in the GAMP5 (International Society for Pharmaceutical Engineering - ISPE, 2008, p. 26) and the five fundamental activities for the computer system project phase/validation - planning, specifying, building/development, verification and report.\n\nThe project phase is subject to the complete computer system validation, where we follow the V-model. In the computer system validation and IT applications, the V-model is primarily used for the purpose of minimizing the quality risks of the computer-aided system, or IT applications and for improving quality (International Society for Pharmaceutical Engineering - ISPE, 2008).", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 11794, "end_char_idx": 14169, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "d42bf0f1-a35e-41e6-9cf1-1ad44b14ee3e", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the life-cycle model of computer systems within the context of quality management and validation in the pharmaceutical industry. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Phases of Computer System Life-Cycle**:\n   - **Project Phase**: Involves the development and building of the computer system.\n   - **Operating Phase**: The system is in production use, where users can request upgrades or changes. Minor changes do not require full revalidation, only the affected parts.\n   - **Retirement Phase**: When a system is no longer usable, it must be retired following established procedures. Emphasis is placed on retaining Good Practice (GxP) relevant electronic records for a minimum of 10 years post-retirement. Data migration to new systems is also mentioned.\n\n2. **User Requirements**: The system can operate in both manual and automatic modes, with technologists monitoring the SCADA system and intervening as necessary.\n\n3. **Validation Importance**: The project phase is highlighted as crucial for successful validation of the computer system.\n\nEntities mentioned include:\n- **GxP**: Good Practice guidelines relevant to the retention of electronic records.\n- **SCADA**: Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition system used in production.\n\nOverall, the excerpt emphasizes the structured approach to managing computer systems in the pharmaceutical sector, focusing on validation, operational use, and retirement processes."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "4defe687-f292-4a8e-befb-664afd2c08ea", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "f894ba1ec323aee7873603253e2d4245281fc701d3875fcabac942fab2732da2", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "51781a66-e91c-4e09-8bf9-44a53e33af36", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "c4c3ac0e92ddbfcb30310e4bcd8d5b22be1f31b215dfdefbe96e0c5d05145b34", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Once the project phase is completed, the computer system enters the operating phase, which means the computer system production use. Once the system is in regular use, users can request the system upgrade and add new functionalities to the computer system, but there may also be a process change, or some other change to the computer system that needs to be implemented. In the case of changes that do not significantly affect the computer system operation, we do not need to revalidate the entire computer system, but only the part of the system that has changed. Therefore, the validation scope is smaller.\n\n|Conceptual phase|Plan|\n|---|---|\n|Project phase|Develop/Build|\n|Verification|Report|\n|Production phase (operating phase)|Retirement phase (out of use)|\n\nFigure 1. Computer system life-cycle model\n---\n# Management, Vol. 25, 2020, No. 2, pp. 1-23\n\n# B. Rusjan: COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION: EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT ...\n\nOver time, when a computer system can no longer be used to the full extent, or is removed from operational use for any other reason, we move into the retirement phase, where such a system needs to retire, according to the prescribed general procedures. Upon computer system retirement, the greatest attention should be given to the retention of GxP relevant electronic records (data) on a computer system, so that they remain accessible to authorized persons and fully readable for a number of years (usually 10 years) after the computer system retirement. In case when the retired computer system is replaced by a new computer system, we can perform data migration into a new system, thus ensuring the data availability. The project phase will be explained in more detail, since it is of key importance, if we want to successfully validate the computer system.\n\nAnother user requirement is that production can run in two modes; manual and automatic mode, where technologist only checks the SCADA system occasionally and intervenes only when corrections are necessary.\n\n# 5.2.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 14170, "end_char_idx": 16179, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "51781a66-e91c-4e09-8bf9-44a53e33af36", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the validation process for computer-based systems in the pharmaceutical industry, specifically focusing on the transition from manual to automated processes. It highlights the role of a technologist in overseeing critical process parameters during production and emphasizes the importance of computer system validation as a structured project phase that culminates when the system is operational.\n\nKey topics include:\n\n1. **Computer System Validation**: Defined as a project phase that ends when the system is in production.\n2. **Role of Technologist**: The technologist is crucial in managing and validating the automated production process.\n3. **SCADA System Validation**: The section outlines the validation process for a SCADA (Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition) system, detailing its components: planning, specification, building/development, verification, and reporting.\n4. **Planning Sub-process**: A detailed table illustrates the initial activities required when introducing a new computer system, including:\n   - Creating User Requirement Specifications (URS)\n   - Conducting High-Level Risk Assessments (HLRA)\n   - Assessing suppliers\n   - Developing a Validation Plan (VP)\n\nEntities mentioned include:\n- **User Requirements**\n- **High-Level Risk Assessment (HLRA)**\n- **Validation Plan (VP)**\n- **Supplier Assessment Report**\n\nOverall, the section provides a structured approach to ensuring that computer systems in pharmaceutical production meet regulatory and operational standards through a comprehensive validation process."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "d42bf0f1-a35e-41e6-9cf1-1ad44b14ee3e", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "228c9ce76e1185cd98a916e8dca500e80d07c9c4724b8614a83fd79b2958d1e9", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "177f729c-5487-41a4-92d2-e9bd7980b691", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "aa05581a263e8e27b8bee3315350c5de14d49102eaa0ea37899aeca14989aadb", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "# 5.2. Validation process example\n\nComputer-based systems validation is logically defined as a project (project phase), as illustrated in Figure 1, since the computer system validation ends, when the system enters the production phase (operational use). To facilitate illustration of the computer-based system validation through a concrete case, we provide key information about the selected computer system.\n\nA technologist in the production of a pharmaceutical company wants to replace a manually driven process with the automatic one, to be able to improve production process control and management. This individual must continuously review and adjust critical process parameters, such as temperature, speed, and time of mixing in the production process so that parameters do not exceed specified limits. Their activities also include sequencing of production steps, in accordance with the instructions of the batch record. In this case, the technologist is a key player in the computer system validation process model, described in the next section.\n\nThrough the process diagrams, we present an example of the SCADA computer production system validation process, composed of planning, specification, building/development, verification, and report sub-processes.\n---\n# Journal of Contemporary Management Issues\n\n# 5.3. Computer system project phase/ validation process\n\n# 5.3.1. Planning sub-process\n\nPlanning sub-process diagram (Figure 2) shows first activities that should be implemented in case when a new computer system is introduced.\n\n|INPUT|PROCESS|ACTIVITY|RESULT|\n|---|---|---|---|\n|User requirements|Create User Requirement Specification (URS)|[K1]|User Requirement spec. (URS)|\n|Security HSE|Create High Level Risk Assessment (HLRA)|[K2]|High Level Risk assessment (HLRA)|\n|GxP system categorization|Assessment|[R2]| |\n|G44P classification|Supplier assessment needed?|YES| |\n| |Conduct Supplier Assessment|[K4]|Supplier Assessment Report|\n|User Requirement spec. (URS)|Create Validation Plan|[K5]|Validation Plan (VP)|\n|High Level Risk Assessment (HLRA)| |[R2]| |\n\nFigure 2.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 16173, "end_char_idx": 18262, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "177f729c-5487-41a4-92d2-e9bd7980b691", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the process of creating a Validation Plan (VP) within the context of Computer System Validation (CSV) in the pharmaceutical industry, specifically focusing on the planning sub-process. Key topics include:\n\n1. **User Requirement Specification (URS)**: The initial step involves users in production identifying their needs for a new computer-based system, such as a SCADA system, which is intended to enhance the management and control of the production process.\n\n2. **Traceability**: Each requirement is assigned a unique identifier (e.g., URS-01) to ensure traceability throughout the validation process, helping to confirm that all functionalities are tested.\n\n3. **Collaboration**: The process involves collaboration between various stakeholders, including:\n   - Production users who provide insights on system requirements.\n   - Quality Assurance (QA) managers who contribute expertise in computer systems regulations and add requirements related to data integrity, alarm monitoring, and system access controls.\n   - Health, Safety, and Environment (HSE) personnel and information security officers who also contribute to identifying requirements.\n\n4. **Creation of URS Document**: The culmination of this collaborative effort results in the creation of a User Requirement Specification (URS) document, which outlines all identified requirements for the system.\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the importance of a structured approach to planning and validation in ensuring compliance and effective system functionality in the pharmaceutical industry."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "51781a66-e91c-4e09-8bf9-44a53e33af36", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "b30e3ed790839098b7a0f5dbf5f46950269184c89b0368a84d759bcc5a453d26", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "ab33f47e-cfb9-4bf3-87e5-440a61c1dda3", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "bfc11f7b517242370f51f70b82d0bdd98ffa7432d42a4e3c5f18ed2039914896", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "(URS)|Create Validation Plan|[K5]|Validation Plan (VP)|\n|High Level Risk Assessment (HLRA)| |[R2]| |\n\nFigure 2. Sub-process diagram - Planning\n\nA more detailed description of the specific steps within the planning sub-process is presented below.\n\n[K1] New system requirement\n\nThe user in the production is thinking about a new computer-based system that would give them useful information, regarding the production process and enable\n---\n# Management, Vol. 25, 2020, No. 2, pp. 1-23\n\n# B. Rusjan: COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION: EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT ...\n\nthe management and control of the produc-tion process. Specifically, the user is consid-ering the SCADA system.\n\nThe user writes down his ideas of the computer system, in our case - the SCADA system. Each requirement has its own unique identifier (e.g. URS-01 etc.), in order to assure traceability of the requirements in the next steps of validation and to help preventing omitting any of the desired system functionalities in the process of the computer system development. Unique identification facilitates control of whether all system functionalities were tested.\n\nThe technician, who is a SCADA system user and an expert in the production process management field, usually does not have sufficient knowledge of computer systems regulations, and therefore the quality assurance (QA) manager, an expert in the field of computer systems (eCompliance), gets involved in the process. In our case, the QA manager adds additional system requirements for data integrity management (e.g. data deletion prevention, user data access restrictions, system access levels etc.), requirements for alarm monitoring, and versioning of recipes stored in the SCADA system.\n\nAdditionally, the same person establishes the rules for controlling access to the SCADA system, periodic scans of the SCADA system, managing deviations from good manufacturing practice, managing changes on a computer system, etc. Other participants, contributing to identifying the requirements, are those responsible for health, safety, and environment (HSE) and information security officers. The result is creation of an URS [R1] document.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 18151, "end_char_idx": 20313, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "ab33f47e-cfb9-4bf3-87e5-440a61c1dda3", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the creation of a User Requirement Specification (URS) document in the context of quality management and computer system validation within the pharmaceutical industry. It includes a table that outlines example requirements for a computer-based system, highlighting their criticality levels (Essential, Important, Desired). \n\nKey topics include:\n\n1. **User Requirement Specification (URS)**: A document that outlines the necessary functionalities of a computer-based system.\n2. **Example Requirements**: Specific requirements for a control system, such as displaying the entire production process, user sign-in information, and real-time parameter recording.\n3. **High Level Risk Assessment (HLRA)**: A process for classifying computer-based systems based on Good Automated Manufacturing Practice (GAMP) categories, which helps in the validation process.\n4. **GAMP Categories**: Classification of computer systems in the pharmaceutical industry, with a specific mention of SCADA systems being categorized under GAMP4.\n5. **Regulatory Compliance**: Consideration of 21 CFR Part 11 relevance, which pertains to the storage of electronic records and the use of electronic signatures.\n\nEntities mentioned include:\n- URS (User Requirement Specification)\n- GxP (Good Practice)\n- GAMP (Good Automated Manufacturing Practice)\n- SCADA (Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition)\n- Proficy iFix (a specific SCADA platform)\n- 21 CFR Part 11 (regulatory standard for electronic records and signatures)."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "177f729c-5487-41a4-92d2-e9bd7980b691", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "67d26836149585cfacd33ac3a933eb92c5a23204bd60f63b9b11cd18f689f871", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "5a5bcc6b-d68d-403f-9c1f-9ffc3426b3c7", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "d7afbea2527f6a7c364364eb0b7dadd6f6d0ba80df99fc0115a94354e6558faf", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "The result is creation of an URS [R1] document.\n\n# Table 1 provides an example of an URS document with three very simple requirements for the computer-based system functionality:\n\n|URS ID|Requirement|Criticality|\n|---|---|---|\n|URS-x-01|\u2026|Essential/Important/Desired|\n|URS-F-49|Screen display of control system must show the entire production process on one screen with process values.|Essential|\n|URS-F-50|The control system must show on the screen display, who is signed in, and the date and time.|Essential|\n|URS-F-51|The control system must record all process parameters in graph with the time on the x-axis and parameter values on the y-axis and enable a real-time display of these parameters.|Essential|\n|\u2026|\u2026|\u2026|\n|URS-x-n|User requirement \u2013 n|Essential/Important/Desired|\n---\n# Journal of Contemporary Management Issues\n\n# Create High Level Risk Assessment (HLRA)\n\nWith HLRA, we perform the original computer-based system classification - GxP relevance of the computer-based system and the computer system/application categorization. With the purpose to ensure easier approach to validation, computer systems are classified into one of the GAMP categories that represent a standard for computer systems in the pharmaceutical industry (International Society for Pharmaceutical Engineering - ISPE, 2008, pp. 128-132; Tedstone, 2012; McDowall, 2010, pp. 22-31). As far as the SCADA system categorization, we determined it belongs to the GAMP4 category (for controlling and managing production), being a configurable computer system. In our case, platform (e.g. Proficy iFix) on the SCADA system will be modified and configured by an integrator (supplier), according to our business needs and the URS.\n\nIn HLRA, we also determine if the computer system is 21 CFR Part 11 relevant or not (we ask ourselves whether the system will store electronic records or use electronic signatures).", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 20266, "end_char_idx": 22151, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "5a5bcc6b-d68d-403f-9c1f-9ffc3426b3c7", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the process of computer system validation (CSV) within the pharmaceutical industry, focusing on regulatory compliance and best practices. Key topics include:\n\n1. **HLRA (High-Level Risk Assessment)**: \n   - Determines if a computer system is relevant to 21 CFR Part 11, which governs electronic records and signatures.\n   - Assesses the system's impact on information security, health, safety, and personal data.\n   - Guides the necessary validation activities based on the assessment results.\n\n2. **Supplier Assessment**:\n   - Involves evaluating suppliers of supervisory computer systems to ensure they meet industry and internal standards.\n   - Requires documentation in a Supplier Evaluation Report.\n   - Past assessments may be considered valid unless the supplier has undergone significant organizational changes.\n\n3. **Validation Plan (VP)**:\n   - A document outlining the validation method and principles for the computer system.\n   - Based on User Requirements Specification (URS), HLRA, and Supplier Evaluation Report.\n   - Details planned activities, necessary updates to internal procedures, training requirements, and documentation responsibilities.\n\nEntities mentioned include:\n- **Regulatory Framework**: 21 CFR Part 11\n- **Documents**: URS, HLRA, Supplier Evaluation Report, Validation Plan\n- **Assessment Types**: Supplier Assessment, High-Level Risk Assessment\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the importance of thorough assessment and planning in ensuring compliance and effective validation of computer systems in the pharmaceutical sector."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "ab33f47e-cfb9-4bf3-87e5-440a61c1dda3", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "c1e3fc6f1d4556611d305563e80225a2ee62d66ebe08ea13ab55982c382e08bc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "aa56a85f-5063-4081-8293-dc8e7947d2d3", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "e27a0ecca58d8cbd1613971f170e7d291531341eba14ee8c15cd2ca7355b8595", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "In HLRA, we also determine if the computer system is 21 CFR Part 11 relevant or not (we ask ourselves whether the system will store electronic records or use electronic signatures). In our case, the computer system will store process data that are classified as GxP relevant, therefore the system falls under 21 CFR Part 11 regulatory requirements. Electronic signatures will not be used. In addition, in HLRA, we determine information security (ISEC) impact, health, safety and environment (HSE) impact and impact on personal data. On the basis of the HLRA [R2] result, we decide which computer system validation activities are needed to properly validate the system.\n\n# Conduct Supplier Assessment\n\nSince in our case URS [R1] is sent to several integrators/suppliers of supervisory computer systems, it is necessary to carry out an assessment of suppliers before choosing the best one, in order to assess that the supplier is able to develop computer systems, in accordance with the pharmaceutical industry standards and company internal standards. The assessment shall be recorded in the Supplier Evaluation Report [R3] document. In case that we already conducted supplier assessment in the past (e.g. 5 years) and supplier obtained positive assessment results, the assessment implementation is not necessary, when validating a new computer system/application. Nevertheless, we conduct the supplier assessment once again, if the supplier has been gone through a major organizational change.\n\n# Create Validation Plan (VP)\n\nVP [R4] is a document describing the computer system validation method and principles for validating a computer system. The basis for producing VPs are URS [R1] and HLRA [R2]. We also consider the Supplier Evaluation Report [R3]. VP describes, on the aggregate level, which activities are planned and should be conducted for successful system validation, which internal SOP and general procedures should be updated, which trainings should be conducted and who needs to be trained, which documents will be created during the validation process, who will draw them up, who will review them and who will approve the validation documentation.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 21970, "end_char_idx": 24134, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "aa56a85f-5063-4081-8293-dc8e7947d2d3", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the process of specifying sub-processes in the context of computer system validation within the pharmaceutical industry. Key topics include:\n\n1. **User Requirements Specification (URS)**: The foundation for developing functional specifications and design documents.\n2. **Design Documents**: These include the Functional Specification (FS), Software Design Specification (SDS), and Hardware Design Specification (HDS), which are created based on the URS.\n3. **Design Qualification (DQ)**: A process that verifies the design meets the specified requirements.\n4. **Risk Assessment**: Conducting a functional risk assessment (FRA) based on user requirements.\n5. **Supplier Involvement**: The role of external suppliers in developing the SCADA monitoring/controlling system and creating design documents for review and approval.\n6. **Documentation and Compliance**: Emphasis on referencing URS IDs in design documents to ensure alignment with user requirements.\n\nEntities mentioned include:\n- **Computer System**: The subject of validation and specification.\n- **SCADA**: A specific type of monitoring/controlling system being developed.\n- **Design Qualification (DQ)** and **Functional Risk Assessment (FRA)**: Key processes in the validation framework.\n\nOverall, the section outlines the structured approach to ensuring that computer systems are developed in compliance with user requirements and regulatory standards."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "5a5bcc6b-d68d-403f-9c1f-9ffc3426b3c7", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "0dfb87f732de8f69b340b112809d5471a3133443cf3e2b2e0dfb6a52aa2e384e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "b9308984-90f2-45cb-9bbc-5029ed1ef231", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "99a24a734876c76918fef08059e7db7d47515f58004cbafa91fc0c5c1e734556", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "# Specifying sub-process\n\nWhen the new computer system basis is defined and HLRA and VP are developed, we begin to develop the computer system functionality and specifications, based on the approved URS. The sub-process diagram \u2013 Specifying (Figure 3) shows details of the key steps for conducting these activities.\n---\n# Management, Vol. 25, 2020, No. 2, pp. 1-23\n\n# B. Rusjan: COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION: EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT ...\n\n|INPUT|PROCESS / ACTIVITY|RESULT|\n|---|---|---|\n|User Requirements (URS)|Create Design Documents (HDS) Software Design Specification (SDS)| |\n|User Requirements|Conduct Design Qualification (DQ)|Design Qualification (DQ)|\n|Functional Specification (FS)|HW design (FDS) SW design Specification (SDS)| |\n|User Requirements (URS)|Conduct (functional) Risk Assessment (FRA)|(Functional) Risk Assessment (FRA)|\n\n# Figure 3. Sub-process diagram \u2013 Specifying\n\nA more detailed description of the specific steps within the sub-process Specifying is presented below.\n\nURS [R1] is the basis for creating the Functional Specification (FS), the Software Design Specification (SDS) and the Hardware Design Specification (HDS). The documentation is created by the computer system supplier, or, alternatively, produced by the company, when the computer system is internally developed. In our case, the monitoring/controlling system SCADA is developed by an external supplier, which creates the design documents and sends us the documents for review and approval.\n\nIn design documents, the suppliers describe how they see and understand the computer system, according to the given URS, while it is desirable to indicate the references to the URS ID, as shown in Table 2. Only in such a way, it can be ensured that the supplier will create a computer system in accordance with the URS. Table 2 presents an example of system functionalities described in FS.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 24136, "end_char_idx": 26016, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "b9308984-90f2-45cb-9bbc-5029ed1ef231", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the importance of ensuring that a supplier develops a computer system in alignment with the User Requirements Specification (URS) in the context of Quality Management and Computer System Validation within the pharmaceutical industry. Key topics include:\n\n1. **System Functionalities**: The excerpt presents a table (Table 2) that outlines various system functionalities as described in the Functional Specification (FS) document, including specific references to URS.\n\n2. **Design Qualification (DQ)**: The process of conducting Design Qualification is emphasized, highlighting the need for thorough documentation and review of design documents (FS, Software Design Specification (SDS), and Hardware Design Specification (HDS)) to ensure compliance with URS.\n\n3. **Documentation Review**: The importance of reviewing and approving design documentation from the supplier is stressed, ensuring that all URS requirements are met before the supplier begins building the computer system.\n\n4. **Approval Process**: The section mentions that appointed responsible persons must approve the documentation after comparing the URS with the FS, SDS, and HDS.\n\nEntities involved include:\n- **Supplier**: Responsible for creating the computer system.\n- **User Requirements Specification (URS)**: Defines the requirements that the system must meet.\n- **Functional Specification (FS)**: Describes the functionalities of the system.\n- **Software Design Specification (SDS)** and **Hardware Design Specification (HDS)**: Provide detailed design information.\n- **Responsible Persons**: Individuals tasked with reviewing and approving the documentation. \n\nOverall, the section underscores the critical role of documentation and validation processes in ensuring compliance and quality in computer system development for the pharmaceutical industry."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "aa56a85f-5063-4081-8293-dc8e7947d2d3", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "a007278d5f9a6c7d52001749cd62482cb0a412c2a2aacc7b916d1c6a15102192", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "cf49f1c3-a854-441f-8b0b-51d4f44ba67d", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "bc5804d8d1284fe5396aca1f83b7ea87a710010143a42ff3b03c058e51729b6b", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Only in such a way, it can be ensured that the supplier will create a computer system in accordance with the URS. Table 2 presents an example of system functionalities described in FS.\n---\n# Journal of Contemporary Management Issues\n\n# Table 2.FS example \u2013 System functionalities in FS document\n\n|FS ID|Function Description|URS reference|\n|---|---|---|\n|FS-xx-01|\u2026|URS-x-01|\n|FS-EP-01|Screen display of the control system contains all the standard elements, displays and interfaces for the review and control of the production process with the entire technological procedure, showing all the necessary parameters, including the time code and identification of the logged-in user.|URS-F-49|\n| |The display of the captured data in the form of a graph (histography) is part of the iFix application, which, in addition to other functionalities, enables real-time data display of all defined parameters.|URS-F-50|\n|FS-HI-01|\u2026|URS-F-51|\n|FS-xx-n|\u2026|URS-x-n|\n\nWhen reviewing the FS, we note all documentation to embrace all URSs, or disparities with the given URS and the user may limit its requirements for the whole process is formalized into Design Qualification (DQ). If no discrepancies are detected during the inspection, this should nevertheless be documented and formalized in the DQ.\n\n[K7] Conduct Design Qualification (DQ)\n\nIn our SCADA system case, at this point we receive the design documentation from the supplier for review and approval (FS, SDS and HDS [R5]). Since it is in our interest to obtain such a computer system, as defined in the URS [R1], at this stage, we need to review of whether the design documentation provided by the supplier actually covers all of our URS requirements. This is important, as the supplier will build the computer system exactly as it has been defined in FS, SDS and HDS. After completing the comparison between the URS and the FS, SDS and HDS, appointed responsible persons approve the record that was created, when review of the documents was conducted.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 25832, "end_char_idx": 27829, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "cf49f1c3-a854-441f-8b0b-51d4f44ba67d", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the process of design qualification (DQ) in the context of computer system validation within the pharmaceutical industry. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Design Qualification (DQ)**: The formal approval process involving the comparison of User Requirements Specification (URS) and Functional Specification (FS), along with Software Design Specification (SDS) and Hardware Design Specification (HDS). Responsible persons must approve the records created during this review.\n\n2. **Functional Risk Assessment (FRA)**: Following the confirmation of FS, SDS, and HDS, an FRA is conducted to evaluate the criticality of each URS based on Good Practice (GxP) standards. This assessment involves identifying potential risks associated with system failures, their frequency, impact on product quality, patient safety, and the ability to detect errors.\n\n3. **Testing Decisions**: The results of the FRA inform the selection of testing methods for each functionality, which can range from simple to complex. Each testing decision must be justified in relation to the specific functionality.\n\n4. **Risk Evaluation**: The section emphasizes the importance of evaluating risks associated with the computer system's performance against the functionalities outlined in the FS. High-risk scenarios necessitate thorough testing, including Installation Qualification (IQ), Operational Qualification (OQ), and Performance Qualification (PQ) during the verification phase.\n\nEntities mentioned include:\n- User Requirements Specification (URS)\n- Functional Specification (FS)\n- Software Design Specification (SDS)\n- Hardware Design Specification (HDS)\n- Good Practice (GxP)\n- Installation Qualification (IQ)\n- Operational Qualification (OQ)\n- Performance Qualification (PQ) \n\nOverall, the excerpt highlights the structured approach to ensuring that computer systems in the pharmaceutical industry meet regulatory standards and function as intended."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "b9308984-90f2-45cb-9bbc-5029ed1ef231", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "edde80599d3a71cc2d8f7bd11d9dbb31c62b45948f6766926e6c65d73fb95ec5", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "0991db5d-a1d2-42ca-9617-21728ec22b66", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "4cb3190b63280bda6157ef3336adffc6baf44d61176261e8a0d16c050dcbf8ad", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "After completing the comparison between the URS and the FS, SDS and HDS, appointed responsible persons approve the record that was created, when review of the documents was conducted. It is formally called the design qualification - DQ [R6]. In the event that deviations from the URS have been detected in the DQ, the supplier must update the design.\n\n[K8] Conduct (Functional) Risk Assessment (FRA)\n\nAfter confirming FS, SDS and HDS [R5] and considering this documentation together with URS [R1], we produce the FRA [R7], in which we evaluate each of the URSs, according to GxP computer system individual functionality criticality. We evaluate the possible risks we could encounter, in the event of a failure or non-performance of each functionality, assess the frequency at which these events can occur, the criticality of these events, in terms of impact on product quality, patient safety, safety at work, etc. and we evaluate the possibility of detecting an improper.\n---\n# Management, Vol. 25, 2020, No. 2, pp. 1-23\n\n# B. Rusjan: COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION: EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT ...\n\noperation or error. Based on the results of each computer system functionality criticality assessments, we decide what kind of testing will be selected for each functionality. The tests can be simple or complex, and each decision needs to be explained and commented on, in relation to each functionality, i.e. we need to explain why we have chosen a certain type of testing.\n\nTherefore, the evaluation and description of risks are implemented for the events where the computer system would not function in accordance with, in our case, the functionalities specified in FS. Where the risk of the system not operating as intended is high, the appropriate Installation Qualification (IQ), Operational Qualification (OQ) and Performance Qualification (PQ) testing of the computer system are performed at the verification phase.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 27646, "end_char_idx": 29568, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "0991db5d-a1d2-42ca-9617-21728ec22b66", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses quality management and computer system validation in the pharmaceutical industry, focusing on risk analysis and the development/building sub-process of computer systems. \n\nKey topics include:\n\n1. **Risk Analysis**: An example is provided in Table 3, which evaluates the GxP criticality of system functionalities, assessing the impact and possibility of errors or deviations. The table categorizes risks based on their criticality and outlines testing methods.\n\n2. **Development/Building Sub-process**: Figure 4 illustrates the inputs, processes, activities, and results involved in constructing a computer system. It highlights the importance of documentation, including the Validation Plan and Functional Specification.\n\n3. **Verification Sub-process**: This section emphasizes the need to ensure that the computer system meets user expectations during the verification phase.\n\nEntities mentioned include:\n- GxP (Good Practice) criticality\n- Functional Specification (FDS)\n- Validation Plan (VP)\n- Technical and User documentation\n- OQ (Operational Qualification) testing\n\nOverall, the excerpt emphasizes the structured approach to risk management and system development in compliance with regulatory standards in the pharmaceutical sector."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "cf49f1c3-a854-441f-8b0b-51d4f44ba67d", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "0c0a243036dd2a5cb91e717dfd00c1d2deb78aaa6110a60bf16b7189494098c4", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "04be796e-96fe-4078-8034-27ba28ceadcc", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "624b47b02cf46f178afeece0211fb077ae0b0159ac9ea18a8b1ea0162142185a", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "An example of risk analysis is shown in Table 3, where GxP criticality of the system functionalities is evaluated (YES/NO), the impact of errors/deviations, the possibility of an error/deviation, and the possibility of not detecting an error/deviation are determined (H - high impact/possibility; M - mean impact/possibility; L - low impact/possibility).\n\n**Table 3. FRA example**\n|Risk scenario/details of potential error or deviation|FS ID|Functionality GxP criticality|Impact/consequences of error/deviation|Possibility of occurrence of err. /dev.|Possibility of non-detection of err. /dev.|Remark|Way of testing|\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n|Un-sufficient production process management; inadequate product|FS-EP-01|YES|H|L|L|/|OQ test|\n|No process data for review; no possibility of process data review;|FS-HI-01|YES|H|L|L|/|OQ test|\n|regulatory inconsistency; GMP deviation investigation is not possible in full scale; product cannot be released on the market.| | | | | | | |\n---\n# Journal of Contemporary Management Issues\n\n# 5.3.3. Development/Building sub-process\n\nFigure 4 shows the inputs required for the construction of a computer system, as well as the result that follows - a developed computer system and the related technical and user documentation.\n\n|INPUT|PROCESS|ACTIVITY|RESULT|\n|---|---|---|---|\n|Validation Plan (VP)|System application Development and documentation|Functional Specification (FDS)|Technical and User documentation|\n|HW design spec|SW design Spec| | |\n\nFigure 4. Sub-process diagram \u2013 Development/Building\n\nA more detailed description of the specific steps within the sub-process of Development/building is presented below.\n\n# 5.3.4. Verification sub-process\n\nAs a part of the verification, we verify that the computer system works in accordance with the users\u2019 expectations.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 29570, "end_char_idx": 31388, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "04be796e-96fe-4078-8034-27ba28ceadcc", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the verification sub-process in the context of computer system validation within the pharmaceutical industry, emphasizing the importance of ensuring that computer systems meet user expectations. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Verification Process**: The verification process involves confirming that the computer system operates as intended, utilizing Installation Qualification (IQ), Operational Qualification (OQ), and Performance Qualification (PQ) tests.\n\n2. **Testing Framework**: The document outlines a structured approach to testing, including test planning, execution, and reporting. It highlights the roles of various documents such as the Test Plan and specifications for IQ, OQ, and PQ tests.\n\n3. **Sub-process Diagram**: A reference to a sub-process diagram (Figure 5) illustrates the verification steps and their interconnections.\n\n4. **Testing Methodology**: The methodology for validating computer systems is guided by a validation plan (VP) and includes detailed specifications for each type of qualification test.\n\n5. **Documentation**: The section mentions various reports and specifications that are crucial for documenting the testing process, including the Test and Certification Report and the Deviation Management report.\n\nOverall, the excerpt emphasizes the systematic approach to computer system validation, ensuring compliance with regulatory standards and user requirements through rigorous testing and documentation."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "0991db5d-a1d2-42ca-9617-21728ec22b66", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "2456117ec3ecc40485b83b7eacc28884a20a5478a5e26cfdb0fe204bb2797f90", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "3b771d6e-db4a-4632-8aab-135318dd9f6e", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "c2001c8c5ea485002db1de9c8ef61d310ed3f6158c21276e8270b67ed9e5a46a", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "# 5.3.4. Verification sub-process\n\nAs a part of the verification, we verify that the computer system works in accordance with the users\u2019 expectations. As shown in Figure 5, this is checked by IQ, OQ and PQ tests.\n---\n# Management, Vol. 25, 2020, No. 2, pp. 1-23\n\n# B. Rusjan: COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION: EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT ...\n\n|INPUT|PROCESS ACTIVITY|RESULT|\n|---|---|---|\n|Test Planning (according to VP)|[Reh]|[R1]|\n|[R1C]|Testing|OQ Test Report|\n|[Rt1]|Test and Certification Report|[R1]|\n|Deviation Management (URS)|[IK12]|[MII]|\n|Functional Specification|[Susi]|[R12]|\n|[R5]|Test and Definition Report|[R11]|\n\n# Figure 5. Sub-process diagram - Verification\n\nMore detailed description of specific steps, within the sub-process of Verification, is presented below.\n\nWhen a computer system is developed (a SCADA system, in this case), it must pass robust testing to prove that it works faultlessly and in accordance with the\n---\n# Journal of Contemporary Management Issues\n\nValidating a computer system scope and methodology is prescribed by the VP, and the Test plan [R10] further describes which IQ, OQ and PQ tests are required. When we have a developed and approved tests plan, we write the IQ [R10.1], OQ [R10.2] and PQ [R10.3] test specifications, where we define what we test, how to perform the test, and what is the expected result.\n\n# [K11] Testing\n\nWe test the system, in accordance with the test plan [R10] on pre-approved test specifications IQ [R10.1], OQ [R10.2] and PQ [R10.3], which are based on the results from the FRA.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 31238, "end_char_idx": 32790, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "3b771d6e-db4a-4632-8aab-135318dd9f6e", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the installation and testing of computer systems within the context of quality management in the pharmaceutical industry. It outlines three critical testing phases: \n\n1. **Installation Qualification (IQ)** - A documented verification that the computer system is installed according to pre-approved specifications.\n2. **Operational Qualification (OQ)** - A documented verification that the system performs as intended across all anticipated operating ranges.\n3. **Performance Qualification (PQ)** - A documented verification that the system can operate and control production processes in its specified environment.\n\nThe results of these tests are compiled into test reports, categorized as IQ test reports, OQ test reports, and PQ test reports. Any errors or deviations during testing are documented in a Test and Deviation Report.\n\nAdditionally, the section emphasizes the importance of having the test specifications approved prior to testing, and it mentions that the expected results and other relevant details are recorded manually during the testing process. An example of an OQ test specification is referenced, highlighting the manual entry of data.\n\nKey entities mentioned include:\n- International Society for Pharmaceutical Engineering (ISPE)\n- Test reports (IQ, OQ, PQ)\n- Test and Deviation Report\n\nOverall, the section underscores the structured approach to validating computer systems in compliance with regulatory standards in the pharmaceutical sector."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "04be796e-96fe-4078-8034-27ba28ceadcc", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "a99e0267b4dbcb1fed2d34dcc141bd150d2792a58cd2bd2d47f88cac05e0ef64", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "d961456e-07ed-49ce-9a10-18aafd1a686e", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "7272182b1c2160b077e28b7e61fec6847a87709b2c91602e98e33baefcd7a6df", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Installation of a computer system is tested with: an IQ test, which is a documented verification that the computer system is installed in accordance with the pre-approved specifications (International Society for Pharmaceutical Engineering, ISPE, 2008, p. 209, International Society for Pharmaceutical Engineering - ISPE, 2014); OQ test, which is a documented verification of pre-approved specifications that computer system performs as intended throughout all anticipated operating ranges (International Society for Pharmaceutical Engineering, ISPE, 2008, p. 334, International Society for Pharmaceutical Engineering - ISPE, 2014a) and PQ test, which is a documented verification that the system is capable of operating and/or controlling (in our case production) processes during operation in its specified production environment in accordance with the pre-approved specifications (International Society for Pharmaceutical Engineering - ISPE, 2008, p. 284, International Society for Pharmaceutical Engineering - ISPE, 2014b). The results of completed test specifications, obtained after the tests, are called test reports. This gives three sets of IQ test reports [R11.1], OQ test reports [R11.2], and PQ test reports [R11.3]. In cases where an error occurred in the course of testing and the testing was not successful or was only partially successful, this is documented as a test deviation. Both deviations as well as the relevant test reports are summarized in the Test and Deviation Report [R11] document.\n\nIf we look at the continuation of our case, it is clear from Table 4 that both functionalities of a computer system need to be tested with the OQ test. The test specification itself must be approved before the testing starts, as the test steps after the approval of the test specification are carried out on a copy of the approved test specification. The expected result, appropriateness, date, and signature are recorded manually in the fields provided for that purpose during the test implementation. In Table 4 we present an example of the OQ test specification, with the manually entered text being greyed out in the table.\n---\n# Management, Vol. 25, 2020, No. 2, pp.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 32791, "end_char_idx": 34976, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "d961456e-07ed-49ce-9a10-18aafd1a686e", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the topic of Computer System Validation (CSV) within the context of Quality Management Systems (QMS) in the pharmaceutical industry. It includes a specific example of an Operational Qualification (OQ) test, detailing a table that outlines various tests, their prerequisites, steps, references, descriptions, expected results, actual results, and documentation. \n\nKey topics include:\n- **Computer System Validation**: The process of ensuring that computer systems are compliant with regulatory standards and function as intended.\n- **Quality Management Systems**: Frameworks and practices that ensure consistent quality in products and services.\n- **Operational Qualification (OQ)**: A phase in the validation process that verifies that the system operates according to its specifications.\n- **Testing Procedures**: Specific tests (e.g., screen test, parameters and history test) are outlined with detailed descriptions and expected outcomes.\n\nKey entities mentioned:\n- **B. Rusjan**: The author of the document.\n- **iFix**: The application being tested.\n- **Janez Novak**: The individual who signed off on the test results.\n- **References**: Various documents such as URS (User Requirements Specification), FS (Functional Specification), and DQ (Design Qualification) are cited as part of the validation process.\n\nOverall, the excerpt emphasizes the importance of structured testing and documentation in ensuring compliance and quality in computer systems used in the pharmaceutical sector."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "3b771d6e-db4a-4632-8aab-135318dd9f6e", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "dadcb17e1ea94478e4ef4d29b74f175020bcaa28b5e10cf7f734986e48ceac15", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "373af4ec-28af-473f-87dd-09119e4c2270", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "5fccc2b887ce8ace651c3e02e26aa6a764f2807eba5f917c1814b1c8046260f9", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "---\n# Management, Vol. 25, 2020, No. 2, pp. 1-23\n\n# B. Rusjan: COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION: EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT ...\n\n# Table 4. OQ test example\n\n|Test name|Prerequisite|Step|Ref. URS|Ref. FS|Test description|Expected result|Actual result|As reference to the attachment|Date and signature|\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n|OQ-1_screen test|Approved FS and FRA|1|URS-F-49|FS-EP-01|Run and login into application iFix. Verify if on the control screen whole production process is shown, together with process values, time and date and logged-in user.|The screen shows the entire production process, including process values, date and time, and logged-in users.|Result as expected.|YES|30.04.2014 Janez Novak|\n|OQ-2_parameters and history test|Approved FS and FRA|1|URS-F-51|FS-HI-01|Open \u201ehistory\u201c in iFix. Verify that the control system records all process parameters in the graph in real time.|System is capturing defined process data real-time in the history graph.|Result as expected.|YES|30.04.2014 Janez Novak Attachment 1|\n| | |2|URS-F-51|FS-HI-01|Open \u00bbhistory\u00ab in iFix and verify that the graph shows time on X axis and parameters on Y axis.|Graph shows time values on X axis and parameter values on Y axis.|Result as expected.|YES|30.04.2014 Janez Novak Attachment 1|\n\n# [K12] Deviation management\n\nSDS and HDS [R5]. We have also examined the possible deviations, by comparing FS, SDS, HDS and URS and documented them in the DQ [R6].", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 34933, "end_char_idx": 36391, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "373af4ec-28af-473f-87dd-09119e4c2270", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the processes involved in ensuring quality management and computer system validation within the pharmaceutical industry. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Deviation Examination**: The comparison of Functional Specifications (FS), Software Design Specifications (SDS), Hardware Design Specifications (HDS), and User Requirements Specifications (URS) to identify and document deviations.\n\n2. **Traceability**: Emphasis on the importance of traceability in design documents, ensuring that all URS are accounted for and linked to the corresponding tests (Installation Qualification (IQ), Operational Qualification (OQ), and Performance Qualification (PQ)).\n\n3. **Test Management (TM)**: The creation of a Test Management document can begin during the Design Qualification (DQ) phase, facilitating early traceability between URS and other specifications.\n\n4. **Documentation and Reporting**: The necessity of connecting design documentation with test reports and maintaining unique identifiers for user requests to ensure traceability.\n\n5. **Testing Compliance**: The section highlights the importance of testing all functionalities of the computer system, particularly if any failures are identified based on Functional Risk Assessment (FRA) results.\n\n6. **Table of Traceability Matrix (TM)**: A table is provided that outlines the relationship between URS, FS, SDS, HDS, and the corresponding IQ, OQ, and PQ tests, indicating compliance for each requirement.\n\n7. **Final Activities Before Release**: Reference to a figure that illustrates the last activities required before the computer system is released for production and operational use.\n\nOverall, the section underscores the critical role of documentation, traceability, and compliance testing in the validation of computer systems in the pharmaceutical sector."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "d961456e-07ed-49ce-9a10-18aafd1a686e", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "5d5f9371019cbce2cb8cb0d75f71e7d3162faedf58a91bbe34f7f97f1c375053", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "6d247a1b-739b-444c-891f-02ae765b976f", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "21772175fc065b1cb5608ea17ac64bc5673d0f6c939a2ee768da5095f566b68a", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "We have also examined the possible deviations, by comparing FS, SDS, HDS and URS and documented them in the DQ [R6]. It is, also, necessary to provide traceability, where it is evident, in a transparent manner, whether all URS have been considered in the design documents (this is already checked in DQ) and which tests (IQ, OQ, PQ) were used to test these requirements. To start the creation of TM [R12], there is no need to wait for the computer system verification, as we can start to build it earlier (during the design qualification - DQ). This ensures the first part of the traceability between URS and FS, SDS and HDS.\n---\n# Journal of Contemporary Management Issues\n\nprovided by IQ, OQ and PQ tests, where we documented and, retrospectively, we must connect the design documentation with test reports. As already mentioned, each user\u2019s request is marked with a unique identifier (ID), so that we can guarantee the traceability of document designs and tests. If we find out that we have failed to test one of the computer system functionality, this must be tested, in accordance with the FRA results.\n\nTM for our example is shown in Table 5.\n\n|URS|FS|SDS|HDS|IQ|OQ|PQ|Comment|\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n|URS-F-49|FS-EP-01|/|/|/|OQ-1_screen test \u2013 step 1|/|Complies|\n|URS-F-50|FS-EP-01|/|/|/|OQ-1_screen test \u2013 step 1|/|Complies|\n|URS-F-51|FS-HI-01|/|/|/|OQ-2_parameters and history test \u2013 steps 1, 2|/|Complies|\n\n# 5.3.5. Report sub-process\n\nFigure 6 shows last activities needed before the release of the computer system into production and operational use.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 36275, "end_char_idx": 37848, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "6d247a1b-739b-444c-891f-02ae765b976f", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the sub-process involved in the report phase of computer system validation within the pharmaceutical industry, emphasizing the importance of quality management systems (QMS). Key topics include:\n\n1. **User Training**: Before a computer system is put into production, it is essential to conduct user training based on technical and user documentation. This training is documented in a Training Report.\n\n2. **Validation Report Creation**: After completing all activities outlined in the Validation Plan (VP), a Validation Report (VR) is created. This report confirms that the computer system, specifically a SCADA system in this context, has been successfully validated and is ready for routine operation.\n\n3. **Regulatory Compliance**: The paper highlights the need for adherence to standard operating procedures that align with European and US legislation governing the pharmaceutical industry, ensuring that computer systems validation meets regulatory requirements.\n\n4. **Sub-process Diagram**: A diagram (Figure 6) illustrates the inputs, processes, activities, and results involved in the report sub-process, detailing the steps leading to the system's operational phase.\n\nOverall, the section underscores the critical steps in ensuring that computer systems are validated and that users are adequately trained before deployment, all within the framework of regulatory compliance."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "373af4ec-28af-473f-87dd-09119e4c2270", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "2bc5ab08bfa35b87167a72ab8a4efa38631c1c811812c77da3104b0c019c2426", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "2b079a58-3bd9-48d8-9df5-e38b51f6e11d", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "80c3d11b9289b635c82177160538e10bfb17dd79c0f30228a559ef5ac156af7e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Report sub-process\n\nFigure 6 shows last activities needed before the release of the computer system into production and operational use.\n\n|INPUT|PROCESS|ACTIVITY|RESULT|\n|---|---|---|---|\n|Technical and User documentation|Conduct User Trainings|Training Report|[R13]|\n|Validation Plan (VP)|Create Validation Report (VR)|Validation Report|[R14]|\n|Test and Deviation Report| | |[R11]|\n|END|(production operating phase)| | |\n\n# Figure 6. Sub-process diagram \u2013 Report\n\nA more detailed description of the specific steps within the sub-process Report is presented below.\n\n[K14] Conduct User Training Before the system goes into production and operational use, it is necessary to ensure that all (prospective) users of the computer system are trained, by using the Technical and User documentation [R9].\n---\n# Management, Vol. 25, 2020, No. 2, pp. 1-23\n\n# B. Rusjan: COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION: EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT ...\n\nis also necessary to train users on instructions or company procedures that describe the process and workflow, controlled by the computer system. The training of users is documented in the Training report [R13].\n\n# [K15] Create Validation Report (VR)\n\nWhen all the activities envisaged in the VP [R4] are properly completed, this is listed in VR [R14]. A validated VR means that the computer system (in our case - the SCADA system) is successfully validated and can be routinely operated without any restrictions. The last approval date on VR means the computer system validation date (CSV date).\n\n# 6. DISCUSSION\n\nThe paper addresses two research questions. The first one is related to the standard operating procedures included in a specific pharmaceutical company QMS for computer systems validation.\n\nIn accordance with this question, the paper identified standard operating procedures, representing the elements of the quality system for the validation of computer systems in conformance with the requirements of the European and US legislation, governing the pharmaceutical industry.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 37712, "end_char_idx": 39724, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "2b079a58-3bd9-48d8-9df5-e38b51f6e11d", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the challenges and considerations in designing a Quality Management System (QMS) for computer systems within the pharmaceutical industry, particularly focusing on computer system validation (CSV). Key topics include:\n\n1. **Regulatory Requirements**: The importance of accurately interpreting regulatory requirements to avoid errors in content and ensure compliance.\n\n2. **Data Integrity**: Emphasizing that the primary goal of validating computer systems is to ensure data integrity and minimize quality risks, rather than merely passing inspections.\n\n3. **Supplier Compliance**: Highlighting the necessity for suppliers and integrators of computer systems to comply with both regulatory requirements and the internal standards of pharmaceutical companies.\n\n4. **Audits and Assessments**: The increasing rigor of audits conducted by pharmaceutical companies on their suppliers and integrators to ensure compliance.\n\n5. **QMS Structure**: The section presents a specific QMS structure designed for a pharmaceutical company, suggesting that it serves as a framework for operational CSV.\n\n6. **Future Research**: A call for further research to test the appropriateness of the proposed QMS structure across different pharmaceutical companies, acknowledging the limitations of using a single case study.\n\nEntities mentioned include:\n- Pharmaceutical Industry\n- Quality Management System (QMS)\n- Computer System Validation (CSV)\n- Good Practice (GxP) level regulations\n- Suppliers and Integrators of computer systems\n\nOverall, the excerpt emphasizes the critical role of understanding regulatory frameworks and the need for robust validation processes to ensure quality and compliance in the pharmaceutical sector."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "6d247a1b-739b-444c-891f-02ae765b976f", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "f481e647a72e5588354f1dbc0b118b6ec3cf02f8e453b6d40000a6da9c99c1fc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "47daf261-f552-4306-be84-c9eef4193a8e", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "cee7671f63e285ed47cfa21f852d2a681f2193f68e7b4b5c366f9ccdb59772f0", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Today, one of the major challenges in designing a QMS in the field of computer systems are either wrong, or simplified interpretations of regulatory requirements. Errors in content or non-conformance with regulatory requirements often occur, because of lack of understanding of computer usage and computer system definitions, and/or lack of understanding how computer systems work.\n\nAlthough the regulatory requirements are basically general, the key to defining and designing a proper QMS is understanding and correct interpretation in the computer system validation field.\n\nThe experience from this highly regulated industry, however, can be appropriately used in other, less regulated industries, to provide the basic purpose of validation, where ensuring data integrity is a key requirement for operation of the computer systems.\n\nThe paper contributes to understanding of interpretation of regulatory requirements in the computer system validation field.\n---\n# Journal of Contemporary Management Issues\n\nthe pharmaceutical industry. We do not vali- date computer systems to successfully un- dergo inspections, but rather to fully ensure the data integrity, to minimize quality risks of a computer system or IT applications and to improve the overall product quality. It is important for the pharmaceutical industry that all suppliers and integrators of comput- er-aided systems, working with pharmaceu- tical companies at the GxP level, be aware that the set of regulations, consequently, ap- plies to them, as well. They must be able to demonstrate compliance with the regulatory requirements and, in addition, the regula- tions and internal standards of the pharma- ceutical company, with which they cooper- ate. Pharmaceutical companies are obliged to carry out audits of the suppliers and in- tegrators with whom they cooperate, and these assessments are becoming increasing- ly rigorous in the computer systems field.\n\nThe presented structure of the QMS has been designed for a specific pharmaceutical company, operating in a highly regulated environment. The quality system elements shown also represent merely a framework for operational computer system valida- tion. Therefore, future work should be fo- cused on testing the appropriateness of the presented QMS structure within other phar- maceutical companies. Similar limitation is related to the use of a single case study for identification of process validation ele- ments.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 39725, "end_char_idx": 42167, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "47daf261-f552-4306-be84-c9eef4193a8e", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the importance of computer system validation (CSV) within the context of quality management systems (QMS) in the pharmaceutical industry. It highlights the limitations of relying on a single case study for identifying validation elements, suggesting that additional case studies are necessary to verify the validation process within the same regulatory framework. The paper outlines the need for a structured QMS that adheres to both European and US legal requirements, detailing standard operating procedures as essential components for effective CSV.\n\nKey topics include:\n- The significance of multiple case studies for comprehensive validation.\n- The applicability of QMS elements beyond the pharmaceutical industry.\n- The V-model methodology as a framework for CSV, encompassing planning, specification, development, verification, and reporting.\n- The use of process diagrams to illustrate the validation process, specifically in the context of a SCADA manufacturing system.\n\nEntities mentioned include:\n- Pharmaceutical industry\n- Regulatory frameworks (European and US legal requirements)\n- Quality Management System (QMS)\n- Computer System Validation (CSV)\n- V-model methodology\n- SCADA (Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition) systems."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "2b079a58-3bd9-48d8-9df5-e38b51f6e11d", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "9a948fc767ef0f2308b76589fc10eaae15e39cdf22008c64657c898fcf05eaa9", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "0ccca067-88aa-4019-a3a5-abd4b0da50ab", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "df8dc0a9ef60f655d615668bd03c3d6d781785e9d979bb09c8b499ff468beb14", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Similar limitation is related to the use of a single case study for identification of process validation ele- ments. Using a single case study enables the exploration of a particular field, problem, or situation in depth and in relation to a spe- cific context, in our case, as determined by the regulatory framework. In order to verify the presented validation process, it is neces- sary to add additional case studies, within the same context, i.e. the pharmaceutical industry. In addition, the appropriateness of presented QMS structure and valida- tion process, or respectively, the need for their adaptation and/or simplification, in another context, e.g. less regulated indus- tries, should also be investigated.\n\n# 7. CONCLUSION\n\nThis paper identifies elements of com- puter systems validation QMS and process, for a specific case of a pharmaceutical or- ganization. In the pharmaceutical industry, the computer system should be validated in accordance with the regulatory require- ments. Based on the European and US le- gal requirements, we defined general and specific standard operating procedures, which represent QMS elements for com- puter system validation in a pharmaceutical organization. The use of the QMS, which meets the strict pharmaceutical industry legal requirements, is not limited to it, but its elements are also applicable to other in- dustries. The presented QMS can provide guidelines for all companies that need to develop an appropriate framework for com- puter systems validation and implementa- tion of effective management of computer system validation processes.\n\nWith the production computer system validation process example in the pharma- ceutical industry, we assure a more pro- found understanding of computer system validation implementation in practice, with the emphasis on meeting pharmaceutical in- dustry regulatory requirements. As a basic premise, we use the V-model methodology to approach the validation. Planning, speci- fication, development/building, verification and reporting, as the key five activities of the project/validation of a computer system, are presented, by using process diagrams, based on a practical validation example of a SCADA manufacturing computer-aided system.\n---\n# Management, Vol. 25, 2020, No.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 42051, "end_char_idx": 44326, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "0ccca067-88aa-4019-a3a5-abd4b0da50ab", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the topic of computer system validation (CSV) within the context of quality management in the pharmaceutical industry. It highlights the regulatory frameworks, best practices, and case studies relevant to CSV. The document references various sources, including academic articles and guidelines from the European Commission, specifically focusing on Good Manufacturing Practices (GMP) and documentation standards. Key entities mentioned include:\n\n1. **B. Rusjan** - Author of the referenced work on computer system validation.\n2. **European Commission** - Pr