 scope.\n\nThe section then introduces the concept of memory-augmented agents, distinguishing between internal and external memory. Internal memory consists of historical interactions, while external memory includes data from various domain-specific sources. This enhancement aims to improve the agent's capabilities in knowledge-intensive and context-dependent applications.\n\nKey Topics:\n- LLM agents\n- Memory modules (internal and external)\n- Resource utilization inefficiencies\n- Limitations of LLMs without memory\n- Knowledge-intensive applications\n\nEntities:\n- LLM (Large Language Model)\n- User queries (Q)\n- Responses (A)\n- Internal memory (Minternal)\n- External memory (Mexternal)\n- Domain-specific repositories and databases (D)"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "5bbe2f3b-a5cf-473e-9e50-1d182dcad9fb", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_name": "ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 72913, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "47c48bbdebdc34c45547d1ddc9efb86758d4c6bea59cc0a6ae9786ef666e699e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "e9448068-1bb8-4a81-befb-4393cfd27d21", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_name": "ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 72913, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "bd6940fb17f03a1355b888e45df17b7283b681c29f5591ef9b732181eba3da92", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "7102bb57-2c7e-462e-a8a8-78678ac3394b", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "13793702682fe592ce8bd29bcfbcc9ef94fff15939474abedda03eeba32b468d", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "In this section, we take the memory module of LLM-based agents as an example to explore potential inefficiencies in resource utilization within their design and operations.\n\n# 3.1 Problem Definition\n\nTo understand its impact, we first define the simplest case of an LLM agent without memory before formalizing the enhanced capabilities of a memory-augmented agent.\n\nWithout Memory In its simplest configuration, an LLM agent operates as a standalone inference system. Given a user query Q, the LLM generates a response A:\n\nLLM(Q) = A (1)\n\nThis formulation assumes no access to external data or stored context. The model relies entirely on its pretrained knowledge and immediate input Q. While computationally efficient, this approach is limited by the LLM\u2019s inherent knowledge boundaries, which cannot be updated without retraining. When Q references information outside the model\u2019s scope, the output A is prone to inaccuracies or hallucination, failing to meet the requirements of knowledge-intensive or context-dependent applications.\n---\n# A PREPRINT - JANUARY 15, 2025\n\n# With Memory\n\nWhen a memory module is incorporated, the memory M is typically categorized into internal memory and external memory, i.e., M = {Minternal, Mexternal}. Internal memory comprises historical information collected during the agent\u2019s operation. For example, an agent solving iterative tasks may store user inputs i and its own responses o from prior interactions at time t: Minternal = {(i1, o1),(i2, o2), . . . , (it\u22121, ot\u22121)}. External memory refers to data retrieved from domain-specific repositories, databases, documents, or other external sources: Mexternal = {D1, D2, . . . , Dn}, where these external resources D are indexed and queried as needed.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 14152, "end_char_idx": 15892, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "7102bb57-2c7e-462e-a8a8-78678ac3394b", "embedding": [0.014444641768932343, 0.03850990906357765, 0.0575592927634716, -0.007105831988155842, 0.03127388283610344, 0.045088112354278564, 0.04385469853878021, 0.01878899708390236, -0.00032205795287154615, 0.04950099065899849, 0.031410928815603256, -0.05646292492747307, -0.02137916535139084, -0.010367524810135365, -0.04020927846431732, -0.03620753809809685, -0.003013297449797392, -0.03505634889006615, 0.015499895438551903, 0.020447254180908203, 0.047691985964775085, 0.025586476549506187, 0.017884494736790657, 0.05495541915297508, 0.023558195680379868, -0.0005023590056225657, 0.016020670533180237, 0.04221014678478241, -0.003189744194969535, -0.04188123717904091, 0.03615271672606468, -0.027834029868245125, -0.03620753809809685, -0.030122697353363037, -0.0052625639364123344, 0.071921706199646, -0.00022655406792182475, 0.01029215008020401, 0.011285732500255108, 0.014540573582053185, -0.01670590043067932, -0.03557712584733963, -0.04341615363955498, 0.05089886114001274, -0.021338053047657013, 0.036920174956321716, -0.004515663720667362, 0.016171419993042946, -0.027285845950245857, 0.051419634371995926, -0.02836850844323635, 0.026285409927368164, 0.023051125928759575, -0.01369088888168335, -0.004772624932229519, -0.014060912653803825, 0.018843816593289375, 0.012950841337442398, 0.04270351305603981, 0.009058736264705658, -0.011210357770323753, -0.03491930291056633, -0.0143487099558115, 0.019172726199030876, -