ity.\n\n2. **LLM Compression**: The basic structure of an LLM compressor is outlined, detailing the input (ranked memories), output (compressed memories), and energy consumption associated with different compression ratios (\u03b2).\n\n3. **Generation Process**: The final step involves synthesizing the input query and compressed memory to produce an answer, highlighting the computational costs involved and the importance of balancing compression ratio with answer quality.\n\n4. **Memory Management**: The section touches on advanced memory management strategies for LLM agents, emphasizing the importance of agent autonomy in managing memory over the long term.\n\nOverall, the excerpt emphasizes the need to balance computational efficiency with the quality of outputs in LLM applications, while also considering the implications for energy consumption and memory management."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "5bbe2f3b-a5cf-473e-9e50-1d182dcad9fb", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_name": "ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 72913, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "47c48bbdebdc34c45547d1ddc9efb86758d4c6bea59cc0a6ae9786ef666e699e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "64973664-4deb-47d9-b5e6-bd42eb46ea45", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_name": "ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 72913, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "2c4dc990a73f6fb4b87a2d234698368629637e7e76c599a222a877b318cee51c", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "c479f389-0256-4caf-b406-7d394b1123d3", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "3a1e2472e0e7566c0952d09e98c350bf10f4ed7c791038415cb187618ae3bf52", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Alternative entropy-based methods like Selective Context [59] and LLMLingua [60] reduce costs by avoiding full LLM inference, but may compromise compression quality [61]. The overall efficiency gains versus computational overhead remains a critical consideration, especially at scale.\n\nThe basic form of LLM compressor is as follows:\n\n- Input: Ranked memories, which has the same token as unranked just in a different order (token number = Tm).\n- Output: Compressed memories (token number = \u03b2 \u2217 Tm, 0 < \u03b2 < 1, where \u03b2 is the compression ratio).\n- Energy: E4 = eK(Tm, \u03b2 \u2217 Tm) = \u03b1K,0 \u2217 Tm + \u03b1K,1 \u2217 \u03b2 \u2217 Tm + \u03b1K,2 \u2217 \u03b2 \u2217 T2\n\n# Generation\n\nThe final step synthesizes the query and compressed memory to produce a coherent answer. The input query and output answer are unavoidable computational costs, making compressed memories the key variable factor. While a larger compression ratio (\u03b2) increases energy costs, it also preserves more information, potentially leading to more accurate and complete answers. The optimal compression ratio thus needs to balance the trade-off between computational efficiency and answer quality based on specific application requirements.\n\n- Input: Original query (token number = Tq), Compressed memories (token number = \u03b2 \u2217 Tm, 0 < \u03b2 < 1).\n---\n# A PREPRINT - JANUARY 15, 2025\n\n\u2022 Output: Answer (token number = Ta).\n\n\u2022 Energy: E5 = eK(Tq + \u03b2 \u2217 Tm, Ta) = \u03b1K,0 \u2217 (Tq + \u03b2 \u2217 Tm) + \u03b1K,1 \u2217 Ta + \u03b1K,2 \u2217 (Tq + \u03b2 \u2217 Tm) \u2217 Ta\n\n# 3.2.4 Memory Management\n\nBeyond basic memory read and write operations, some research focuses on the long-term maintenance and management of memory in LLM agents. These approaches often emphasize agent autonomy, delegating much of the memory management process to the LLM itself.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 25562, "end_char_idx": 27284, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "c479f389-0256-4caf-b406-7d394b1123d3", "embedding": [0.012423049658536911, 0.045888666063547134, 0.04337121918797493, 0.008099609054625034, 0.02862226776778698, 0.03352034091949463, 0.03108498640358448, 0.013688613660633564, 0.008879470638930798, 0.02272542379796505, 0.04115477204322815, -0.0627172440290451, -0.017156941816210747, -0.022465471178293228, -0.03009989857673645, -0.035326335579156876, -0.02667945623397827, -0.053495731204748154, -0.008557948283851147, 0.015692992135882378, 0.034478068351745605, 0.027815043926239014, 0.03034617193043232, 0.05538381636142731, 0.00016492948634549975, -0.010124512016773224, 0.045149847865104675, 0.042304039001464844, 0.0030339329969137907, -0.02606377564370632, 0.03149544075131416, -0.028074996545910835, -0.029142174869775772, -0.04703793302178383, 0.010439191944897175, 0.07048849016427994, -0.006556989625096321, -0.014653177931904793, 0.003353744512423873, 0.0017298890743404627, -0.02235601656138897, -0.027171999216079712, -0.02112465724349022, 0.055465906858444214, -0.005055414978414774, 0.01595294661819935, 0.00038501364178955555, -0.010589691810309887, -0.0014134980738162994, 0.03518952056765556, -0.05702562630176544, 0.02139829285442