he section discusses the evaluation of indexing strategies for large language models (LLMs) and AI agents, focusing on retrieval effectiveness and efficiency. Key metrics for effectiveness include Relevance, which measures how well retrieved memories match a query, and Accuracy, assessed through comparisons with a ground truth set using metrics like recall and F1 scores. For efficiency, the average retrieval time per memory token (Tretr) is considered, along with energy consumption (Etoken_m) and processing time (Tcost) per memory token during the memory formation process.\n\nTwo evaluation indicators are introduced: the Retrieval Energy-to-Relevance Ratio (RERR) and the Energy-to-Accuracy Ratio (EAR), both quantifying the energy cost for improvements in retrieval relevance and accuracy, respectively.\n\nAdditionally, the section outlines an ideal scenario for generating correct answers to queries, emphasizing minimal data usage and operations. In this optimal case, the system retrieves only relevant memories and generates answers without additional enhancements, focusing on the essential energy consumption from retrieval and response generation costs. \n\nKey topics include:\n- Indexing strategies for LLMs\n- Metrics for retrieval effectiveness (Relevance, Accuracy)\n- Metrics for retrieval efficiency (Tretr, Etoken_m, Tcost)\n- Evaluation indicators (RERR, EAR)\n- Optimal scenarios for query generation and energy consumption."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "5bbe2f3b-a5cf-473e-9e50-1d182dcad9fb", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_name": "ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 72913, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "47c48bbdebdc34c45547d1ddc9efb86758d4c6bea59cc0a6ae9786ef666e699e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "c479f389-0256-4caf-b406-7d394b1123d3", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_name": "ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 72913, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "95f4c1e0cb25c0933ded5ba4ee1e78950c9eac156265b8d61ab2f00093d54ca8", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "9e15e5de-c507-48a0-bc3f-e241cf83c94f", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "beeceba56dbc7a37630451648f97c11b156df22e11d003ac97df6715e76c881f", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "To comprehensively evaluate different indexing strategies, we propose a multi-dimensional evaluation. For retrieval effectiveness, we employ two key metrics: Relevance measures how well a retrieved memory matches a query and is typically calculated by having the LLM judge each entry\u2019s relevance, then dividing the number of relevant entries by the total retrieved. Accuracy is evaluated by comparing retrieved documents to a ground truth set and metrics such as recall and F1 scores can often be used. For retrieval efficiency, we use the average retrieval time per memory token Tretr. For the memory formation process, we focus on energy consumption Etoken_m and processing time Tcost per memory token.\n\nBased on these metrics, we design two comprehensive evaluation indicators that quantify the energy cost required to achieve a unit improvement in retrieval relevance and accuracy:\n---\n# A PREPRINT - JANUARY 15, 2025\n\n# Retrieval Energy-to-Relevance Ratio (RERR)\n\nRERR = Etoken_m\nRelevance\n\n# Energy-to-Accuracy Ratio (EAR)\n\nEAR = Etoken_m\nAccuracy\n\n# 3.3.2 Trade-offs between Memory Reading, Utilization and Generation\n\n# a. For Correct Generations\n\nFor correct generations of the query Q (token number = Tq), we propose an ideal case scenario that achieves accurate answers through minimal necessary data (as shown in Figure 2) and operations: in this optimal case, the system would use only the original query with vector embeddings, employing sparse or dense retrieval to extract precisely all relevant ground truth memories MG (token number = Tmg) and no irrelevant memories, which are then combined with the original query to directly generate the ground truth answer AG (token number = Tag) through the LLM, without requiring any additional enhancement operations (such as query optimization, reranking or compression).\n\nIn the optimal case, the essential energy consumption comprises two components: retrieval cost (Eretr) and response generation cost Eg = eK(Tq + Tmg, Tag).", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 29114, "end_char_idx": 31102, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "9e15e5de-c507-48a0-bc3f-e241cf83c94f", "embedding": [0.014374962076544762, 0.032643143087625504, 0.07584970444440842, 0.009031996130943298, 0.02225668914616108, 0.004641914740204811, 0.03789762780070305, 0.02496560662984848, 0.008269687183201313, 0.023277638480067253, 0.03953114524483681, -0.04326101392507553, -0.045439038425683975, -0.02997506409883499, -0.011584368534386158, -0.009324667975306511, -0.006537477020174265, -0.05967787280678749, -0.0013238305691629648, 0.022814808413386345, 0.04004842787981033, 0.0132655305787920