th": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_name": "ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 72913, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22", "document_title": "\"Navigating the Sustainable AI Trilemma: Balancing Energy Efficiency, Digital Equity, and Capability in Large Language Models and AI Agent Design\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the cost comparison of different indexing methods for large language models (LLMs) and AI agents, particularly focusing on the efficiency of these methods as the number of memory tokens increases. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Sustainable AI Trilemma**: The document addresses the balance between energy efficiency, digital equity, and capability in the design of LLMs and AI agents.\n\n2. **Cost Analysis**: It presents a detailed analysis of the costs associated with various indexing methods as the number of tokens increases, highlighting trends in efficiency scaling.\n\n3. **Vector-based vs. LLM-dependent Methods**: The section contrasts the cost patterns of vector-based methods, which show increasing costs across all metrics (energy per token, RERR, EAR) with the LLM-dependent methods, which maintain relatively stable costs despite increasing token volumes.\n\n4. **Energy Efficiency**: The analysis reveals a significant difference in energy costs between the two methods, indicating a need for further investigation into the energy efficiency of these approaches.\n\n5. **Table 3**: The section references a table (Table 3) that provides a cost comparison of memory formation for the same dataset with varying token numbers, emphasizing the implications of these findings for scalability and cost-effectiveness.\n\nOverall, the section highlights the importance of understanding cost dynamics in AI model design, particularly as they relate to sustainability and efficiency."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "5bbe2f3b-a5cf-473e-9e50-1d182dcad9fb", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_name": "ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 72913, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "47c48bbdebdc34c45547d1ddc9efb86758d4c6bea59cc0a6ae9786ef666e699e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "aacdae21-3de9-4a12-a688-2b99ea2cbe03", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_name": "ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 72913, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "8609975779520c5d7e029f53234e2de4b54d9943127a80cfa7f12b86a35785a6", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "7cea014e-89cd-430a-9519-93e39a6346b5", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "71cb6dd7e4b7d34382b485a8eff4b1e02b3946b2fdd368df65632f6fa0c874eb", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "02e-01|8.88e-05|3.27e+01|9.60e-01|5.15e-01|1.75e-01|2.01e-06|2.52e+01|\n|Summary|6.21e-01|12.67e-01|3.10e-01|4.14e-04|3.40e+01|9.19e-01|5.24e-01|1.71e-01|8.77e-05|2.50e+01|\n|Graph|7.17e-01|10.3