 self-controlled memory framework aimed at improving LLM capabilities.\n\n3. **LLMs as Operating Systems**: The concept of treating LLMs as operating systems is introduced in the work by Charles Packer et al., indicating a shift towards more complex and versatile AI systems.\n\n4. **Chatbot Modules for Open-Domain Conversations**: The use of prompted LLMs as modules for long, open-domain conversations is highlighted, showcasing their application in conversational AI.\n\n5. **General Read-Write Memory**: The paper by Ali Modarressi et al. discusses the development of a general read-write memory for LLMs, which could enhance their adaptability and learning.\n\n6. **Recent Publications**: The section lists several recent publications from 2023 and 2024, indicating ongoing research and advancements in the field of AI and LLMs.\n\nEntities mentioned include authors and their affiliations, specific research papers, and conferences such as the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence and the Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL). The section also references arXiv identifiers for accessing the papers."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "5bbe2f3b-a5cf-473e-9e50-1d182dcad9fb", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_name": "ADDRESSING THE SUSTAINABLE AI TRILEMMA A CASE STUDY ON LLM AGENTS AND RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 72913, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "47c48bbdebdc34c45547d1ddc9efb86758d4c6bea59cc0a6ae9786ef666e699e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"