48911, 0.0018221850041300058, 0.008946198038756847, -0.02094918303191662, -0.04991394281387329, -0.03616519272327423, -0.019427582621574402, 0.019128696992993355, -0.058092549443244934, -0.014862779527902603, -0.026057414710521698, -0.0031349053606390953, -0.018598852679133415, -0.009027712047100067, -0.011160670779645443, -0.006653607357293367, 0.0039058951660990715, 0.001995402853935957], "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses advancements in Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, focusing on two specific paradigms: Modular RAG and Graph RAG.\n\n### Key Topics:\n\n1. **Advanced RAG**:\n   - Emphasizes semantic enhancements in retrieval.\n   - Utilizes dense retrieval models like Dense Passage Retrieval (DPR) and neural ranking algorithms for improved precision.\n\n2. **Modular RAG**:\n   - Represents a flexible and customizable evolution of RAG.\n   - Decomposes the retrieval and generation pipeline into independent, reusable components.\n   - Key innovations include:\n     - **Hybrid Retrieval Strategies**: Combines sparse and dense retrieval methods for improved accuracy.\n     - **Tool Integration**: Incorporates external APIs and databases for specialized tasks.\n     - **Composable Pipelines**: Allows independent replacement and enhancement of components for adaptability to specific use cases.\n\n   - Example: A Modular RAG system for financial analytics that retrieves live stock prices, analyzes trends, and generates investment insights.\n\n3. **Graph RAG**:\n   - Extends traditional RAG by integrating graph-based data structures.\n   - Enhances multi-hop reasoning and contextual enrichment through relationships and hierarchies in graph data.\n   - Characterized by its ability to capture and reason over relationships between entities.\n\n### Entities:\n- **Dense Passage Retrieval (DPR)**: A dense retrieval model used in Advanced RAG.\n- **BM25**: A sparse retrieval method mentioned in the context of hybrid strategies.\n- **APIs and Databases**: External tools integrated into Modular RAG for specialized tasks.\n- **Graph Data Structures**: Used in Graph RAG to enhance generative outputs through relational understanding.\n\nOverall, the section highlights the evolution of RAG systems towards greater flexibility, customization, and relational reasoning capabilities."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "b04d578f-ad06-49fc-8dee-5f9e73ed50a3", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name