betes symptoms from medical literature.\n- **Critic Module**: Evaluating the quality and relevance of the retrieved data.\n- **Response Synthesis**: Integrating validated data into a coherent response.\n\nThe integrated response highlights the symptoms of Type 2 Diabetes and their correlation with heart disease, emphasizing shared risk factors like obesity and high blood pressure.\n\nAdditionally, the section introduces **GeAR (Graph-Enhanced Agent for Retrieval-Augmented Generation)**, which enhances traditional RAG systems by incorporating graph-based retrieval mechanisms to improve multi-hop retrieval capabilities for complex queries."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "2939ada4-3d75-459a-87dd-ef6d8bf3ba74", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "0e41bfc2e925d39b02c096e3a0765582920898d131fdcbb8e9b578a8b2c68a53", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "aecc53be-29dc-4c43-a3c3-9285fdbb3524", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "fe6317c010a63c8162faa8eb605309330adfedfecca0355d784ee5f417093f3f", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "- Dynamic Adaptability: Adjusts retrieval strategies dynamically based on query requirements.\n- Improved Accuracy: Critic module reduces the risk of irrelevant or low-quality data in responses.\n- Scalable Modularity: Supports the addition of new agents for specialized tasks, enhancing scalability.\n---\n# Use Case: Healthcare Diagnostics\n\nPrompt: What are the common symptoms of Type 2 Diabetes, and how are they related to heart disease?\n\n# System Process (Agent-G Workflow):\n\n1. Query Reception and Assignment: The system receives the query and identifies the need for both graph-structured and unstructured data to answer the question comprehensively.\n2. Graph Retriever:\n- Extracts relationships between Type 2 Diabetes and heart disease from a medical knowledge graph.\n- Identifies shared risk factors such as obesity and high blood pressure by exploring graph hierarchies and relationships.\n3. Document Retriever:\n- Retrieves descriptions of Type 2 Diabetes symptoms (e.g., increased thirst, frequent urination, fatigue) from medical literature.\n- Adds contextual information to complement the graph-based insights.\n4. Critic Module:\n- Evaluates the relevance and quality of the retrieved graph data and document data.\n- Flags low-confidence results for refinement or re-querying.\n5. Response Synthesis: The LLM integrates validated data from the Graph Retriever and Document Retriever into a coherent response, ensuring alignment with the query\u2019s intent.\n\n# Response:\n\nIntegrated Response: \u201cType 2 Diabetes symptoms include increased thirst, frequent urination, and fatigue. Studies show a 50% correlation between diabetes and heart disease, primarily through shared risk factors such as obesity and high blood pressure.\u201d\n\n# 5.6.2 GeAR: Graph-Enhanced Agent for Retrieval-Augmented Generation\n\nGeAR [35]: introduces an agentic framework that enhances traditional Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems by incorporating graph-based retrieval mechanisms. By leveraging graph expansion techniques and an agent-based architecture, GeAR addresses challenges in multi-hop retrieval scenarios, improving the system\u2019s ability to handle complex queries as shown in Figure 22.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 54041, "end_char_idx": 56220, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "aecc53be-29dc-4c43-a3c3-9285fdbb3524", "embedding": [-0.004521105904132128, 0.04476899653673172, 0.04313470050692558, 0.024554628878831863, 0.009236452169716358, 0.0023459517396986485, -0.0003309198364149779, 0.020924348384141922, -0.01827196590602398, 0.04206303134560585, 0.014253205619752407, -0.07287353277206421, -0.03440059348940849, -0.040723443031311035, 0.0018570023821666837, -0.009959829039871693, -0.01966513693332672, -0.05138655751943588, 0.00023066013818606734, -0.004604830406606197, 0.02984599769115448, 0.018124612048268318, 0.02731417864561081, 0.03504359349608421, -0.021781684830784798, -0.031507086008787155, 0.02080378495156765, 0.08648373186588287, -0.0068184975534677505, 0.005140664987266064, 0.012893524952232838, -0.025492340326309204, 0.007669135462492704, -0.01357671432197094, -0.01333558838814497, 0.041661154478788376, 0.011600823141634464, -0.05377102270722389, -0.0003204543318133801, 0.01919628120958805, 0.014065663330256939, -0.03525792807340622, 0.0003438970888964832, 0.032337628304958344, -0.03490963578224182, -0.014306789264082909, -0.014025475829839706, -0.0052310870960354805, 0.010267933830618858, 0.05224389210343361, -0.0