ting graph-structured data, allowing the system to understand complex relationships and dependencies between entities.\n2. **Agent Framework**: The system utilizes an agent-based architecture that dynamically manages retrieval tasks, enabling autonomous decision-making and the selection of retrieval strategies based on query complexity.\n3. **Workflow Components**:\n   - **Graph Expansion Module**: Integrates graph data into the retrieval process, enhancing the ability to handle multi-hop queries by considering relationships between entities.\n   - **Agent-Based Retrieval**: Employs agents to autonomously choose retrieval paths, improving the relevance and accuracy of the information retrieved.\n4. **LLM Integration**: Combines the enriched retrieved information with a Large Language Model (LLM) to generate coherent and contextually relevant responses, ensuring the generative process is informed by both unstructured documents and structured graph data.\n\n**Entities**:\n- GeAR (Graph-Enhanced Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation)\n- BM25 (a traditional retrieval method)\n- Large Language Model (LLM) \n\nOverall, the section highlights the advancements in retrieval techniques through the integration of graph data and agent-based decision-making, ultimately enhancing the generative capabilities of AI systems."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275