5", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems Across Healthcare, Finance, and Education\"", "section_summary": "The section provides an overview of various question-answering (QA) and related tasks in the field of artificial intelligence, specifically focusing on different types of datasets used for training and evaluation. Key topics and entities include:\n\n1. **Types of QA**:\n   - **Single-hop QA**: Datasets like SQuAD, Web Questions, and PopQA.\n   - **Multi-hop QA**: Datasets such as HotpotQA and MuSiQue.\n   - **Long-form QA**: Includes ELI5 and NarrativeQA.\n   - **Domain-specific QA**: Examples are Qasper and COVID-QA.\n   - **Multi-choice QA**: Datasets like QuALITY and CommonsenseQA.\n   - **Graph-based QA**: Mention of GraphQA.\n   - **Dialog**: Covers various dialog types including event argument extraction and open-domain dialog.\n\n2. **Dialog Types**:\n   - **Personalized Dialog**: Datasets like KBP and DuleMon.\n   - **Task-oriented Dialog**: Example includes CamRest.\n\n3. **Recommendation Systems**: Focus on personalized content using Amazon datasets.\n\n4. **Reasoning Tasks**:\n   - **Commonsense Reasoning**: Datasets like HellaSwag.\n   - **Chain of Thought (CoT) Reasoning**: Mention of CoT Reasoning dataset.\n   - **Complex Reasoning**: Example includes CSQA.\n\n5. **Language Understanding**: Datasets like MMLU and WikiText-103.\n\n6. **Other Tasks**:\n   - **Fact Checking/Verification**: Datasets such as FEVER and PubHealth.\n   - **Strategy QA**: Mention of StrategyQA.\n   - **Summarization**: Includes text summarization datasets like WikiASP and long-form summarization datasets like NarrativeQA.\n   - **Text Generation**: Biography dataset.\n   - **Text Classification**: Focus on sentiment analysis with SST-2.\n\nOverall, the section categorizes various AI tasks and their corresponding datasets, highlighting the diversity of applications in areas such as healthcare, finance, and education."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-3760-4de7-9cea-369ed82e58d6", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "293f95af-bcf0-4b87-8c95-a8c1d9f7ca5a", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "1054d0b83551ddd212f46f21efa439a3ffc63f4eb8a7474a188061e93a0d1d7b", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "94ed05bb-109c-4def-84ad-ac7cf0fc76ab", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "19cda73d9940dc7b794b3a772b02a7a4465325cbb69b89ff578d1fcea6af567d", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "SQuAD [67], Web Questions (WebQ) [68], PopQA [69], MS MARCO [56]|\n|Multi-hop QA|HotpotQA [60], 2WikiMultiHopQA [59], MuSiQue [58]| |\n|Long-form QA|ELI5 [70], NarrativeQA (NQA) [71], ASQA [72], QM-Sum [73]| |\n|Domain-spec