ion\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses various research contributions related to Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) and its applications in large language models (LLMs). Key topics include:\n\n1. **Retrieval-Augmented Generation**: The section highlights a survey on RAG for large language models, indicating its significance in enhancing AI systems.\n  \n2. **Dense Passage Retrieval**: A reference to a study on dense passage retrieval techniques for open-domain question answering, showcasing advancements in information retrieval methods.\n\n3. **Memory Mechanisms**: A survey focusing on the memory mechanisms utilized by large language model-based agents, emphasizing the importance of memory in AI performance.\n\n4. **Self-Correction in LLMs**: Discussion of a method where large language models can self-correct through tool-interactive critiquing, indicating a move towards more autonomous AI systems.\n\n5. **Planning in LLM Agents**: A survey that explores the planning capabilities of LLM agents, which is crucial for their functionality in dynamic environments.\n\n6. **Agentic Workflows**: Research on enhancing AI systems through agentic workflow patterns in large language models, presented at a notable AI conference.\n\n7. **Performance Improvement**: An article from DeepLearning.AI discussing how agents can enhance the performance of large language models, indicating ongoing research in optimizing AI capabilities.\n\nEntities mentioned include various authors and their contributions, as well as the IEEE World AI IoT Congress as a platform for presenting research. The section also includes a reference to an online resource for further reading."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "63cc26e7-37