fined as the overall correctness of the model in classifying instances as faulty or non-faulty. The formula for accuracy is provided, along with definitions for True Positives (TP), True Negatives (TN), False Positives (FP), and False Negatives (FN).\n\n2. **Precision**: This metric measures the proportion of true positives among all predicted positives, indicating the reliability of the system in predicting faults.\n\n3. **Recall**: Also known as sensitivity or the true positive rate, recall measures the proportion of actual faults that the model successfully detects.\n\n4. **F1-Score**: This is the harmonic mean of precision and recall, providing a balanced measure of model performance, especially when dealing with imbalanced classes (faults vs. non-faults).\n\nThe excerpt is sourced from an article titled \"Transforming Software Quality Assurance: Leveraging AI and Automation for Intelligent Fault Detection and Proactive Testing in Modern Development,\" published in the World Journal of Advanced Research and Reviews."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "3cc7ef91-2447-4b5e-94de-b001d8d2b1ec", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AI-powered quality assurance Enhancing software infrastructure through intelligent.md", "file_name": "AI-powered quality assurance Enhancing software infrastructure through intelligent.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 46104, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "b9c245bd83c39565a3f052f4561a0cd6704ad175466c1279d0e5edaf5b5d5406", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "b7ae88ca-de51-400c-b8ee-e4be3739cc1c", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AI-powered quality assurance Enhancing software infrastructure through intelligent.md", "file_name": "AI-powered quality assurance Enhancing software infrastructure through intelligent.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 46104, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "6eeed302da9c711f0aef4c1f00765c14a1035359c006c32ff351126bb334f06d", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "3518bbc0-8f27-45eb-be27-86540acd5cfc", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "8f9075955cf77a24f3b2ea44ba937ac16de49c03864d9f796bdb74318f8ffcd0", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Accuracy\n\nAccuracy denotes how well the model classifies both faulty and non faulty instances altogether.\n\nAccuracy = TP + TN / TP + TN + FP + FN\n\n- TP = True Positives (correctly predicted faults)\n- TN = True Negatives (correctly predicted non-faults)\n- FP = False Positives (incorrectly predicted faults)\n- FN = False Negatives (incorrectly predicted non-faults)\n\n# 4.1.2. Precision\n\nThe proportion of true positives in all predicted positives is called precision. These chances, in turn, reflect the reliability of the system to predict faults.\n---\n# World Journal of Advanced Research and Reviews, 2024, 23(03), 3199-3213\n\n# 4.1.3. Recall\n\nAlso recall, which equals sensitivity or true positive rate, that is, the proportion of actual faults detected by the model.\n\nRecall = TP / TP + FN\n\n# 4.1.4. F1-Score\n\nThe harmonic mean of precision and recall is the F1 score. It represents a balanced measure of the model\u2019s performance particularly when the classes (faults vs. non fault) are not in balance.\n\nF1-Score = 2 * Precision * Recall / Precision + Recall\n\n# 4.1.5.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 33457, "end_char_idx": 34526, "metadata_seperat