iting in specific styles, such as classical Chinese, due to limited training data. Fine-tuning with domain expertise has been attempted but remains insufficient.\n\n2. **Factual Fidelity**: The accuracy of biographies is critical, yet LLMs often produce content that contains factual errors, a phenomenon known as hallucination. The section outlines three approaches to mitigate this issue:\n   - **Training-based methods**: These involve training additional models to correct factual errors but require extensive datasets.\n   - **Decoding-based methods**: These constrain output to avoid hallucinations but may limit the model's creativity.\n   - **Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG)**: This method enhances biography generation by retrieving relevant information from external knowledge bases, emphasizing the importance of retrieval accuracy.\n\n3. **Information Fragmentation**: The section highlights the challenge of scattered information about historical figures across multiple documents. It mentions text chunking and chunk representation as key components in RAG workflows that are affected by this fragmentation.\n\nEntities mentioned include:\n- LLMs (Large Language Models)\n- RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)\n- Historical figures\n- External knowledge bases (e.g., history textbooks)\n\nOverall, the excerpt emphasizes the need for improved methods to ensure consistency, factual accuracy, and effective information retrieval in biography generation using AI."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "86d6a30b-f854-412f-bc3d-7186c1cd0752", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "13c05f2b3c34a30ab2b06b824e9bb3dd58f7f63367e6cdae60eac9f97a72c8ac", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "7ca539f4-6e4a-4cda-a98f-b1f0a75cd382", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "dd3f6a830ee17f3b11852dc26cc3a114625f7d5b037a9492a64d7e13508c754e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "12a93dee-28e0-4f6d-a5c1-004186e7e7a3", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "6507391c9e93277ec17a3dca5899af544a5b8b56cf1c75dcdfc69a25af6d3e11", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "For example, LLMs cannot keep consistency when required to write a biography in classical Chinese, especially following historical writing conventions. To address this, several work injected domain expertise into LLMs via fine-tuning [7, 27]. Due to the scarcity of training corpora that follow a particular style, however, fine-tuned LLMs still struggle to adhere to specific language styles and professional terminology.\n\n# Characteristic 2: Factual fidelity.\n\nBiographies have no tolerance for factual errors. However, since LLMs are notorious for the phenomenon of hallucination, they would generate plausible content that contradicts real facts, significantly undermining the usability of generated biographies [13, 16, 20, 21]. There are three kinds of work proposed to alleviate fabrications in text summarization: (1) Training-based methods [4, 7, 17] fix factual errors inherently by training additional reward models or classifiers. A key drawback is their reliance on tens of thousands of training samples. (2) Decoding-based methods [15] avoid hallucinations by constraining output tokens sampled from the given contexts. Though effective, such methods do harm to the model\u2019s creativity. (3) Retrieval-augmented-generation (RAG) based methods [5, 25] guide biography generation for LLMs by retrieving relevant information from an external knowledge base (e.g., history textbooks) as references. Apparently, the retrieval accuracy makes a pivotal difference in the quality of LLMs\u2019 generation.\n\n# Characteristic 3: Information fragmentation.\n\nDetailed information about a particular historical figure is scattered across multiple documents. Text chunking, which splits long documents into small text chunks, and chunk representation, which embeds text chunks into vectors, are two key components in a RAG workflow, suffering from the information fragmentation due to two-fold reasons: (1)\n---\n# Conference acronym \u2019XX, June 03\u201305, 2018, Woodstock, NY\n\nLi et al.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 3684, "end_char_idx": 5656, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "12a93dee-28e0-4f6d-a5c1-004186e7e7a3", "embedding": [-0.02343827486038208, 0.018870050087571144, -0.016138073056936264, 0.0022915764711797237, -0.005590849556028843, -0.02161695621907711, -0.02034800499677658, 0.023333773016929626, -0.033589884638786316, 0.05016089230775833, 0.02257240191102028, -0.06293997913599014, -0.02367713674902916, -0.015764852985739708, -0.02030321955680847, 0.01253275852650404, -0.04565238580107689, -0.023572634905576706, -0.021243736147880554, -0.019929997622966766, 0.028529008850455284, 0.004146484658122063, 0.03899412