*: The system operates in two phases\u2014offline and online. The offline phase involves index building and model fine-tuning, while the online phase focuses on generating biographies based on user queries.\n\n2. **KG-based Index Construction**: The offline process includes constructing a knowledge graph (KG) to organize biographical facts and implementing a two-step training process for error correction and style adaptation.\n\n3. **Biography Generation Pipeline**: During the online phase, the system retrieves relevant information using a KG-powered retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) approach, which aids in generating biographies from user queries.\n\n4. **Error Validation and Correction**: A Verifier checks the accuracy of generated content in real time, and a Router categorizes any detected errors, invoking Solvers for corrections.\n\n5. **Pattern-Enhanced Text Chunking**: The section highlights a training-free method for splitting documents into smaller text chunks based on consistent structural patterns observed in historical documents.\n\nKey entities mentioned include:\n- **AIstorian**: The multi-agent system.\n- **Knowledge Graph (KG)**: The framework used for organizing biographical data.\n- **Verifier, Router, Solvers**: Components of the system responsible for validating and correcting generated content.\n- **Wang Runzhi**: An example of a historical figure mentioned in the context of the system's application. \n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the innovative use of knowledge graphs and structured patterns to enhance the accuracy and reliability of biography generation in historical research."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "86d6a30b-f854-412f-bc3d-7186c1cd0752", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "13c05f2b3c34a30ab2b06b824e9bb3dd58f7f63367e6cdae60eac9f97a72c8ac", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "12a93dee-28e0-4f6d-a5c1-004186e7e7a3", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_name": "AIstorian lets AI be a historian A KG-powered multi-agent system.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 27860, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "de7c60a40306f901f1451ef63341d709bff9a7b6f7418860940cfd7625b4ebc2", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "29d51caf-9676-445b-bc96-b9963cc9f147", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "2728585c64449a1482974cc5dac8a44c87d7d259608802f97fe0e411a536cf8c", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Figure 1 illustrates the overall architecture. The system operates in two modes, with upper half of the figure showing the offline process of index building and model fine-tuning, and the lower half showing the online biography generation pipeline. During the offline phase, AIstorian completes two preparations: (1) KG-based index construction, which reorganizes the biographical facts of historical figures into a knowledge graph, and (2) two-step training, detection and error-type-aware hallucination correction, ensuring that the generated biographies remain faithful to the source biographical data to teach LLMs a specific language style. During the online phase, AIstorian takes as an input a query of \u201cgenerating a biography of a historical figure\u201d, and then invokes the KG-powered RAG to retrieve relevant information (e.g., text chunks) with the assistance of KG-based index. Using the query and the retrieved relevant information, the aligned LLM starts biography generation.\n\nMeanwhile, a Verifier validates the correctness of the generated content in real time. Once an error is detected, a Router categorizes the error and invokes the Solvers to correct it.\n\n# 2.2 KG-based RAG\n\n# 2.2.1 Offline KG-based index construction.\n\nDocuments within the same book series reveal consistent structural patterns: the introduction of person entities follows a standardized format. As illustrated in Figure 2, the introduction of historical figures always begins with the name, followed by the alias and other details (e.g., hometown, career, etc.). Motivated by these, we propose a three-step index construction process to effectively reorganize biographical facts.\n\nTraining-free pattern-enhanced text chunking. Considering that most documents in the external knowledge base follow the same writing pattern, we can leverage the pattern to split long documents into smaller text chunks using in-context learning [24].\n---\n# AIstorian lets AI be a historian: A KG-powered multi-agent system for accurate biography generation\n\nConference acronym \u2019XX, June 03\u201305, 2018, Woodstock, NY\n\nWang Runzhi, styled Yuyuan, nicknamed Tingfang, from Qiantang, Zhejiang. <official career path>.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 7026, "end_char_idx": 9207, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "29d51caf-9676-445b-bc96-b9963cc9f147", "embedding": [-0.020802484825253487, 0.022628827020525932, -0.010839266702532768, 0.003244356019422412, -0.00417608767747879, -0.013378328643739223,