ilize machine learning for this purpose.\n3. **Intelligent Test Maintenance**: AI enables self-healing capabilities in test scripts, allowing them to automatically adjust to changes in the application under test (AUT) without human intervention. Tools like Mabl and SmartBear's AI-driven platform exemplify this functionality.\n4. **Optimization Techniques**: AI also aids in managing large-scale test suites, reducing maintenance overhead.\n\nEntities:\n- **Tools**: Testim.io, Mabl, SmartBear\n- **Concepts**: Regression Testing, Predictive Algorithms, Intelligent Test Maintenance, Self-healing Test Scripts, Optimization Techniques\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the transformative role of AI in enhancing software testing processes, improving efficiency, and reducing manual effort."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "f30f272f-f44c-45fa-a7a9-1bbf727c984d", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\Artificial Intelligence in Quality Assurance for Software Systems.md", "file_name": "Artificial Intelligence in Quality Assurance for Software Systems.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 46770, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "5dbad9039ae67ed68798be7d57a52b3f05b9390adf56748e90646287c8345de5", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "914b4126-6000-43eb-a3cf-120d73ccd295", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\Artificial Intelligence in Quality Assurance for Software Systems.md", "file_name": "Artificial Intelligence in Quality Assurance for Software Systems.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 46770, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "ec1f0aaf0b2f4b7927256a3f137c83a5ca6f19f1289a4a0d92bb32e4dbbd5c9a", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "d3d6e9ad-c8c0-48cb-8a84-c2f841128f5d", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "5cb6b70e59a4b70f374eba601be520834596dde303f471ea6c1642d9527d885c", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "This reduces manual interference in test execution and optimizes resource use.\n\n# 4.2 Regression Testing Enhancements with AI\n\nIt helps ensure that new changes into software systems will not negatively impact existing functionalities. Traditional regression testing can be very resource consuming and time consuming as the same test suite has to be run repeatedly. AI improves this process by highlighting the most critical test cases to cover the impacted regions in the codebase.\n\nLeveraging predictive algorithms, AI can identify which modules are more likely to fail due to recent changes, code complexity, or historically observed defect patterns. The test case execution can be reduced with high fault detection rates due to such prioritization. Tools like Testim.io employ machine learning models to rank regression test cases in terms of risk, allowing faster and more efficient cycles of testing.\n\n# Evolution of Software Quality Assurance Techniques\n\n|Al-Driven Testing|25.09|\n|---|---|\n|Manual Testing|40.0%|\n|Scripted Automation|35.026|\n\nSource: Self-created\n\nAttribution\u2011NonCommercial\u2011NoDerivatives 4.0 International (CC BY\u2011NC\u2011ND 4.0)\n---\n# Stallion Journal for Multidisciplinary Associated Research Studies\n\nISSN (Online): 2583\u20113340\n\nVolume\u20112 Issue\u20112 || April 2023 || PP. 15\u201126\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.55544/sjmars.2.2.2\n\n# 4.3 Intelligent Test Maintenance and Optimization\n\nOne of the significant challenges in the automated testing of any software is maintaining test scripts when the software changes. AI provides the self\u2011healing capability of test cases, such that these systems can detect the change in the AUT - changed element locators or updated workflows, for example, and adjust the test scripts on their own without human intervention.\n\nFor example, Mabl or SmartBear's AI\u2011driven testing platform employs machine learning to watch for changes in the UI or backend systems. Once a change is detected, the tool automatically updates the affected test scripts, hence minimizing the maintenance overhead of a significant amount.\n\nAdditionally, optimization techniques powered by AI help in managing large\u2011scale test suites.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 12209, "end_char_idx": 14350, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "d3d6e9ad-c8c0-48cb-8a84-c2f841128f5d", "embedding": [-0.03513936698436737, 0.0058089387603104115, 0.05987067520618439, -0.031394410878419876, 0.032196901738643646, -0.04576629027724266, 0.0027783203404396772, 0.038884326815605164, -0.008304563350975513, 0.06312927603721619, 0.03582026809453964, -0.050435326993465424, -0.028257401660084724, -0.02609310857951641, 0.0073561654426157475, 0.004745030775666237, 0.009599491953849792, -0.0077148545533418655, -0.004462334793061018, 0.01344779971987009, 0.05053260177373886, 0.03684161975979805, 0.023029053583741188, 0.003462261287495494, -0.0013694018125534058, -0.03516368567943573, -0.013314051553606987, 0.053499385714530945, 0.005422892048954964, -0.010791068896651268, 0.024220630526542664, -0.013168144039809704, -0.011642195284366608, -0.010778909549117088, 0.0018557598814368248, 0.0058484552428126335, -0.02127816341817379, 0.010067611001431942, 0.0009704362601041794, 0.0036720032803714275, -0.0016156205674633384, -0.03951659053564072, -0.00330419489182