541305109858513, 0.006477189715951681, -0.009690679609775543, -0.021877551451325417, 0.004145975224673748, 0.028849676251411438, 0.0017295818543061614, -0.002248725388199091, -0.023269107565283775, -0.016426095739006996, -0.0022254132200032473, 0.004346818197518587, 0.020715530961751938, -0.0055375308729708195, 0.01335606537759304, -0.03351210430264473, -0.009633295238018036, 0.017129046842455864, -0.016268290579319, -0.0014059016248211265, 0.01743031106889248, -0.013721887022256851, 0.052075743675231934, -0.011892780661582947, 0.027572887018322945, 0.0060288794338703156, 0.0104940515011549, -0.0010678755352273583, 0.00606474420055747], "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\Automating FDA Compliance The Role of AI in Computer System Validation (CSV).md", "file_name": "Automating FDA Compliance The Role of AI in Computer System Validation (CSV).md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 28995, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Revolutionizing Compliance in FDA-Regulated Industries: The Role of AI in Automating Computer System Validation for Enhanced Safety and Efficiency\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the role of AI in automating Computer System Validation (CSV) within FDA-regulated industries, highlighting both ethical dilemmas and security gaps associated with AI implementation. \n\nKey Topics:\n1. **GDPR Violation**: Mention of a \u20ac500K fine due to a violation of GDPR\u2019s Article 4(5).\n2. **Ethical Dilemmas**:\n   - **Bias in AI Risk Scoring**: Example of an ML model that deprioritized validation for a diabetes management app in rural clinics, affecting underserved populations. \n   - **Mitigation Strategy**: Use of the Fairlearn toolkit to audit bias in risk scores.\n3. **Security Gaps**:\n   - **Adversarial Attacks**: Incident in 2022 where hackers manipulated training data for a CSV anomaly detection model, leading to ignored temperature excursions in a biologics warehouse.\n   - **Solution**: Implementation of Microsoft Azure Confidential Computing to encrypt CSV training data in use.\n4. **Case Studies**: \n   - **Company**: AstraZeneca\n   - **System**: Cloud-based ERP (SAP S/4HANA) for drug manufacturing.\n   - **Challenge**: Manual validation of over 1,200 test scripts across 15 global sites causing delays in FDA submission.\n   - **AI Solution**: Utilization of Testim.io for ML-driven test automation and AWS SageMaker for predictive analytics, resulting in auto-generated test scripts.\n   - **Key Metrics**: Reduction in validation time from 10 months to 6 months (40% decrease), cost savings of $2.1M, and increased test coverage from 95% to 99.5%.\n   - **Regulatory Outcome**: Zero 483 observations during FDA pre-approval inspection, compliant with FDA 21 CFR Part 11.\n   - **Lessons Learned**: Legacy data silos necessitated 3 months of preprocessing.\n\nEntities:\n- **Organizations**: AstraZeneca, Microsoft Azure\n- **Technologies**: Testim.io, AWS SageMaker, Fairlearn toolkit\n- **Regulatory Framework**: FDA regulations, GDPR\n- **Metrics**: Validation time, cost savings, test coverage, regulatory observations."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "809e2f15-9b79-4079-99f3-502b5a7460da", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\Automating FDA Compliance The Role of AI in Computer System Validation (CSV).md", "file_name": "Automating FDA Compliance The Role of AI in Computer System Validation (CSV).md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 28995, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "ha