 periods (Pre-1950, 1950-2000, 2001-Present) and highlighting the total of over 1,300 cases.\n\n4. **Model Performance**: It compares the capabilities of various models, including GPT-4 API, ChatGPT, Gemini, and nemotron:70b-instruct-q8_0, in retrieving and processing legal data. Notably, it points out the limitations of some models in accessing historical databases and the potential for hallucination in the outputs of offline models.\n\n5. **Legal Citations Inquiry**: A specific question regarding common citations in New Mexico Court of Appeals cases related to 'malpractice' is presented, showcasing the limitations of GPT-4 API in accessing specific databases.\n\nOverall, the section highlights the challenges and differences in the performance of LLMs in legal research and data retrieval."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "1d3f5bd7-239e-43d2-ae7f-1e7cd01c88fb", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_name": "Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 52048, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "8b9a69e79061b64e3a9958d47ca5223db6e2ffd6fcab4d00822647d6e5777090", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "a6d844fb-6559-452c-8226-a896caff5aa4", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_name": "Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 52048, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "f7229b17dc3801155ff1a387dce9dabf427877e447a16eee9e008ba80611b209", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "3fc79f36-7ae8-4a21-bbf9-6cf4f4ff4bcd", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "ae82f7373844403f96f57459da6c7856882de44b0760c466b531325519502f93", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "# 4.4 Query Cross Comparison\n\nQuestions were formulated to query information about legal concepts from LLM channels. There were five questions from each.\n---\n# Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI:\n\n# Retrieval-Augmented Generation with Vector Stores, Knowledge Graphs, and Hierarchical Non-negative Matrix Factorization\n\n# ICAIL 2025, June 16\u201320, 2024, Chicago, IL, USA\n\n100% Attempted Accuracy across the selected databases: Approximate Number of Cases Mentioning 'Habeas Corpus': Over 1,300 ... Breakdown ...:\n\n- Pre-1950: 450\n- 1950-2000: 550\n- 2001-Present: 300\n\nThe responses highlight significant differences in model abilities. GPT-4 API and ChatGPT provided an understanding of their limits to offer real-time or exact counts due to limitations such as access to historical databases or the complexity of case records. Gemini followed a similar pattern, explaining why determining a precise number is challenging. In contrast, our system directly reported a specific count, stating 215 cases mentioning 'Habeas Corpus,' showing its ability to process and retrieve meaningful data. Meanwhile, nemotron:70b-instruct-q8_0 provided a detailed method to find the correct answer in an open context. It even went into breaking the count into approximate ranges across different periods, suggesting over 1,300 cases in total. However, these counts from Nemotron are part of an extreme hallucination since it was an offline model without the ability to make any lookups.\n\n# (b) Comparison 2 - Legal Citations:\n\n\u2022 Question: \u201cWhat are common citations among New Mexico Court of Appeals cases that mention \u2