oject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_name": "Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 52048, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22", "document_title": "\"Transforming Legal Research and Decision-Making: A Comprehensive Framework Integrating Retrieval-Augmented Generation, Knowledge Graphs, Semantic Understanding, and Advanced Machine Learning Techniques\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the integration of advanced AI techniques in legal research and decision-making, specifically focusing on the QA Smart-Slic system. It highlights the strengths and weaknesses of various AI models, such as nemotron, GPT-4o, and Gemini, in summarizing legal principles and data retrieval. The excerpt includes two detailed case studies demonstrating the practical applications of the QA Smart-Slic system:\n\n1. **Case Study 1 - Constitutional Analysis**: Examines the process regarding what happens to a bill if the governor neither signs nor returns it within a specified timeframe, referencing Article IV, Section 22.\n\n2. **Case Study 2 - Statutory Analysis**: Discusses the accrual and utilization of earned sick leave under the Healthy Workplaces Act, detailing how employees earn sick leave, its usage, and provisions for carryover and reinstatement after employment separation.\n\nKey entities mentioned include:\n- Nemotron\n- GPT-4o\n- Gemini\n- NMSA 41-5-1 (statute)\n- Article IV, Section 22 (constitutional provision)\n- Healthy Workplaces Act (statutory provision)"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "1d3f5bd7-239e-43d2-ae7f-1e7cd01c88fb", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_name": "Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 52048, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "8b9a69e79061b64e3a9958d47ca5223db6e2ffd6fcab4d00822647d6e5777090", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "5f0fd656-5d5e-472d-9273-7ff312c19684", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_name": "Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 52048, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-22"}, "hash": "f03e4e6674a1ca12d3d395cf7f87d6e866237efa83a14dd5a5f913a37b3f5ee6", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "c57f0bbc-3cce-4c9e-8aaf-33ffe0f622cb", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "4f80c5ca412effddd0e0b787e3fba4131355909b01c345adf97c1dc043e0a853", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Additionally, nemotron\u2019s inclusion of actual statutes like NMSA 41-5-1 blurred the line between hypothetical examples and genuine analysis, leading to potential confusion. This comparison highlights the strengths and weaknesses of each system: some models are better at summarizing legal principles, such as GPT-4o and Gemini, while our System shows the capability for precise data retrieval and analysis. Nemotron, despite its detailed methodology, suffered most from hallucinations overall.\n\n# 4.5.1 Case Studies\n\nTo illustrate the practical applications and effectiveness of the QA Smart-Slic system, we present four detailed case studies:\n\n# (a) Case Study 1 - Constitutional Analysis:\n\n- Question Source: Article IV, Section 22 [1]\n- Question: \u201cWhat happens to a bill if the governor neither returns it within the specified three-day window (Sundays excepted) nor signs it?\u201d\n- Response: According to Article IV - Legislative Department \u2013 \u00a7 22 \"Governor\u2019s approval or veto of bills\" of the provided text, if a bill is presented to the governor and he neither returns it within the specified three-day window (Sundays excepted) nor signs it, then the bill becomes a law automatically, whether signed by him or not, unless the legislature by adjournment prevents such return.\n\n# (b) Case Study 2 - Statutory Analysis:\n\n- Question Source: Chapter 50, Article 17, Section 3 [4]\n- Question: \u201cUnder the Healthy Workplaces Act, how does an employee accrue and utilize earned sick leave, and what provisions exist for its carryover, use for family or personal health, and reinstatement after separation from employment?\u201d\n- Response: Accrue: Employees accrue a minimum of one hour of earned sick leave for every thirty hours worked. Employers may elect to provide the full sixty-four hours of earned sick leave for the year on January 1 or pro-rata for mid-year hires.\n- Use: Earned sick leave can be used for the employee\u2019s or their family members\u2019 illness, injury, health condition, medical care, or preventive medical care. It can also be used for issues related to domestic abuse, sexual assault, or stalking.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 34746, "end_char_idx": 36854, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "c57f0bbc-3cce-4c9e-8aaf-33ffe0f622cb", "embedding": [0.015510248951613903, 0.06945323199033737, 0.025213273242115974, 0.04575742408633232, 0.003483604872599244, 0.007313746493309736, 0.005785337649285793, -0.0006420046556740999, 0.019099637866020203, 0.04502787068486214, 0.06110716983675957, -0.04654533788561821, -0.03478498011827469, 0.01587502472102642, 0.027328971773386, 0.02757701836526394, 0.02