ity Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the integration of Quality Management Systems (QMS) and Computer System Validation (CSV) within the pharmaceutical industry, focusing on regulatory frameworks and best practices. It addresses two primary research questions: \n\n1. The standard operating procedures that constitute a specific pharmaceutical company's QMS for computer system validation.\n2. The methodology for validating computer systems in compliance with pharmaceutical industry regulations.\n\nThe paper outlines the legal requirements in both the European and US contexts, comparing them to define essential QMS elements for CSV. It employs the V-model methodology, a prevalent approach in the industry, to illustrate the validation process of a computer-supported production system.\n\nThe research methods include descriptive and comparative analysis of legal requirements, as well as the design of a QMS for CSV using classification and compilation techniques. The effectiveness of the proposed QMS is evaluated through a case study and action research within a pharmaceutical company, specifically analyzing the validation of a Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition (SCADA) manufacturing system.\n\nKey topics include:\n- Quality Management Systems (QMS)\n- Computer System Validation (CSV)\n- Regulatory requirements (European and US)\n- V-model methodology\n- Research methods (case study, action research)\n\nEntities mentioned:\n- Pharmaceutical industry\n- Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition (SCADA) systems\n- Authors and references (B. Rusjan, Eisenhardt, Siggelkow, Yin)"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "9b1fe93f-84e8-4b53-8a9f-ae678f789f83", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "490eeb88849a74d02dab5b44c38938bd1289abe6a53c615fea94f03d5ec16fd2", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "1098590a-3366-48b9-9f10-10e7f92a6408", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "61324ce1097a0c5644d7541b29da6cbcb2500d95b506db42166d0ef988810315", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "From these.\n\n# Research Questions\n\nThe paper addresses two basic research questions:\n\n1. What are the standard operating procedures forming a specific pharmaceutical company QMS for computer system validation;\n2. How to perform the validation of the computer system, considering the pharmaceutical industry regulatory requirements.\n---\n# Management, Vol. 25, 2020, No. 2, pp. 1-23\n\n# B. Rusjan: COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION: EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT ...\n\nTo answer these questions, the paper first outlines the legal requirements governing the pharmaceutical industry and by comparing them defines the basic QMS elements for computer system validation. This is followed by an example of the process of validating a computer-supported production system in the pharmaceutical industry, which provides a thorough understanding of the actual validation implementation in practice and its connections with regulatory requirements. As a basic starting point for identifying the process of validating a computer system, we used the V-model methodology approach to validation, which is the most widespread within the area of computer-based system validation in the pharmaceutical industry.\n\n# 2. METHODS\n\nThe paper identifies the European and the US legal requirements governing the pharmaceutical industry by using descriptive and comparison methods. Then, we design a QMS for computer systems validation, by using classification and compilation methods.\n\nThe usefulness of the designed QMS was tested on a specific case within a pharmaceutical company. In this empirical part, we, therefore, employed two research strategies; a single case study and action research. We intended to analyse whether the general and specific standard operating procedures, which form the QMS, provide an appropriate framework for the validation of a concrete project of Supervisory control and data acquisition (SCADA) manufacturing computer system implementation. The validation example was based on the use of a general V-model for validation of computer systems. A single case study may be justifiable, when the research topic is in its early stages (Eisenhardt, 1989), when it is used to persuade (Siggelkow, 2007), and when used as a representative/typical, or a revelatory case (Yin, 2009).\n\n# 3.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 4025, "end_char_idx": 6305, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_":