aceutical industry, emphasizing the importance of adhering to legal requirements. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Quality System Development**: The need for creating instructions and policies, known as standard operating procedures (SOPs), that encapsulate legal requirements for all employees.\n\n2. **Types of SOPs**:\n   - **General SOPs**: Applicable across various activities and business processes, including:\n     - Good documentation practices.\n     - Archiving procedures for electronic and paper records, crucial for accessibility during product recalls or investigations.\n     - Training procedures for users, particularly in relation to system functionality changes.\n   - **Specific SOPs**: Tailored for the implementation of computer system validation.\n\nThe excerpt highlights the significance of both general and specific SOPs in ensuring compliance and effective management of computer systems in the pharmaceutical sector."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "4def3c13-9e32-43ea-a772-4064cc8d559d", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "c87494622e4e148f10382b84134e5ba074e8fce652c855b4d25a6aa94df85b6c", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "4defe687-f292-4a8e-befb-664afd2c08ea", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "29e56ed7902721f77e75ed55a9f58f778ed2904e47beb544191abc9924c7eb3d", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "25, 2020, No. 2, pp. 1-23\n\n# B. Rusjan: COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION: EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT ...\n\n# 4. ESTABLISHING QUALITY SYSTEM FOR COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION\n\nTo develop a quality system for the computer systems validation, the legal requirements must be respected and fully implemented in the quality system. Establishing a successful quality system requires creating instructions and policies (which represent standard operating procedures - SOP), that summarize the parts of the legal requirements, which are then followed by all employees in the organization. We can distinguish between general and specific standard operating procedures (Sallubier and Rusjan, 2017).\n\nThe general SOP, developed in case of a pharmaceutical company, which are intended for use within most of the activities and business processes of the organization, are as follows:\n\n- Procedures for good documentation practice;\n- Procedures, which determine approaches and time periods of archiving for different records types in both, electronic and paper form. This is important for record accessibility and is needed, e.g. in cases of product recalls from the market, if investigations of deviations from good manufacturing practices need to be conducted, or in other cases when records are evidence of proper implementation of processes (e.g. manufacturing, laboratory);\n- Procedures which prescribe trainings for users, e.g. frequency and type of trainings. From the computer system point of view, this is very important, because when a system\u2019s functionality is developed or upgraded, consequentially, the work instructions or user manuals are changed accordingly.\n\nIn addition to the general SOP, which support multiple business processes in an organization, we also need specific SOP for the implementation of computer system validation.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 10140, "end_char_idx": 11967, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "4defe687-f292-4a8e-befb-664afd2c08ea", "embedding": [-0.025882449001073837, 0.05098280310630798, 0.050689518451690674, -0.009055190719664097, -0.02957295812666416, -0.040668927133083344, 0.034656573086977005, -0.001733745215460658, 0.03507206216454506, 0.03399668261408806, 0.056604109704494476, -0.02172756940126419, -0.062078770250082016, -0.017584912478923798, 0.019381286576390266, -0.02006561867892742, -0.0006763134151697159, 0.019100220873951912, 0.0035010960418730974, 0.00496141379699111, 0.059634726494550705, 0.0588037483394146, -0.013527795672416687, 0.040057916194200516, -0.02244856394827366, -0.0859326645731926, 0.004930863156914711, 0.05396454036235809, 0.003950189799070358, -0.03617188334465027, 0.029817363247275352, -0.029548518359661102, -0.02959739789366722, 0.013381152413785458, -0.017035001888871193, 0.011896394193172455, 0.016558412462472916, -0.024697085842490196, 0.023731688037514687, 0.015751877799630165, 0.015409710817039013, -0.022570766508579254, 0.027788804844021797, 0.026737865060567856, -0.0032872420269995928, 0.0016787542263045907, -0.0038890885189175606, -0.007545992266386747, -0.009892276488244534, 0.012043037451803684, -0.03714950010180473, 0.0020209206268191338, 0.04149990528821945, -0.02352394349873066,