ility throughout the validation process, helping to confirm that all functionalities are tested.\n\n3. **Collaboration**: The process involves collaboration between various stakeholders, including:\n   - Production users who provide insights on system requirements.\n   - Quality Assurance (QA) managers who contribute expertise in computer systems regulations and add requirements related to data integrity, alarm monitoring, and system access controls.\n   - Health, Safety, and Environment (HSE) personnel and information security officers who also contribute to identifying requirements.\n\n4. **Creation of URS Document**: The culmination of this collaborative effort results in the creation of a User Requirement Specification (URS) document, which outlines all identified requirements for the system.\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the importance of a structured approach to planning and validation in ensuring compliance and effective system functionality in the pharmaceutical industry."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "51781a66-e91c-4e09-8bf9-44a53e33af36", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "b30e3ed790839098b7a0f5dbf5f46950269184c89b0368a84d759bcc5a453d26", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "ab33f47e-cfb9-4bf3-87e5-440a61c1dda3", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "bfc11f7b517242370f51f70b82d0bdd98ffa7432d42a4e3c5f18ed2039914896", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "(URS)|Create Validation Plan|[K5]|Validation Plan (VP)|\n|High Level Risk Assessment (HLRA)| |[R2]| |\n\nFigure 2. Sub-process diagram - Planning\n\nA more detailed description of the specific steps within the planning sub-process is presented below.\n\n[K1] New system requirement\n\nThe user in the production is thinking about a new computer-based system that would give them useful information, regarding the production process and enable\n---\n# Management, Vol. 25, 2020, No. 2, pp. 1-23\n\n# B. Rusjan: COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION: EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT ...\n\nthe management and control of the produc-tion process. Specifically, the user is consid-ering the SCADA system.\n\nThe user writes down his ideas of the computer system, in our case - the SCADA system. Each requirement has its own unique identifier (e.g. URS-01 etc.), in order to assure traceability of the requirements in the next steps of validation and to help preventing omitting any of the desired system functionalities in the process of the computer system development. Unique identification facilitates control of whether all system functionalities were tested.\n\nThe technician, who is a SCADA system user and an expert in the production process management field, usually does not have sufficient knowledge of computer systems regulations, and therefore the quality assurance (QA) manager, an expert in the field of computer systems (eCompliance), gets involved in the process. In our case, the QA manager adds additional system requirements for data integrity management (e.g. data deletion prevention, user data access restrictions, system access levels etc.), requirements for alarm monitoring, and versioning of recipes stored in the SCADA system.\n\nAdditionally, the same person establishes the rules for controlling access to the SCADA system, periodic scans of the SCADA system, managing deviations from good manufacturing practice, managing changes on a computer system, etc. Other participants, contributing to identifying the requirements, are those responsible for health, safety, and environment (HSE) and information security officers. The result is creation of an URS [R1] document.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 18151, "end_char_idx": 20313, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "ab33f47e-cfb9-4bf3-87e5-440a61c1dda3", "embedding": [-0.049953605979681015, 0.054497286677360535, 0.04059738665819168, -0.01738159731030464, 0.008865555748343468, -0.03790881857275963, 0.00649289321154356, -0.01380580011755228, 0.03218216821551323, 0.044845327734947205, 0.039763931185007095, -0.04895883426070213, -0.052319545298814774, -0.0009603231446817517, 0.01920982263982296, -0.021669862791895866, 0.02023147977888584, -0.0012535451678559184, -0.01740848273038864, 0.016185183078050613, 0.06931129842996597, 0.06280496716499329, -0.00549812288954854, 0.011352481320500374, -0.03884981945157051, -0.05721274018287659, -0.0030817717779427767, 0.0337146520614624, -0.014437614008784294, -0.005598944146186113, 0.01864522323012352, -0.019505565986037254, -0.017663896083831787, 0.036349449306726456, -5.518917532754131e-05, 0.010841653682291508, 0.01680