nd computer system validation within the pharmaceutical industry. It includes a table that outlines example requirements for a computer-based system, highlighting their criticality levels (Essential, Important, Desired). \n\nKey topics include:\n\n1. **User Requirement Specification (URS)**: A document that outlines the necessary functionalities of a computer-based system.\n2. **Example Requirements**: Specific requirements for a control system, such as displaying the entire production process, user sign-in information, and real-time parameter recording.\n3. **High Level Risk Assessment (HLRA)**: A process for classifying computer-based systems based on Good Automated Manufacturing Practice (GAMP) categories, which helps in the validation process.\n4. **GAMP Categories**: Classification of computer systems in the pharmaceutical industry, with a specific mention of SCADA systems being categorized under GAMP4.\n5. **Regulatory Compliance**: Consideration of 21 CFR Part 11 relevance, which pertains to the storage of electronic records and the use of electronic signatures.\n\nEntities mentioned include:\n- URS (User Requirement Specification)\n- GxP (Good Practice)\n- GAMP (Good Automated Manufacturing Practice)\n- SCADA (Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition)\n- Proficy iFix (a specific SCADA platform)\n- 21 CFR Part 11 (regulatory standard for electronic records and signatures)."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "177f729c-5487-41a4-92d2-e9bd7980b691", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "67d26836149585cfacd33ac3a933eb92c5a23204bd60f63b9b11cd18f689f871", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "5a5bcc6b-d68d-403f-9c1f-9ffc3426b3c7", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "d7afbea2527f6a7c364364eb0b7dadd6f6d0ba80df99fc0115a94354e6558faf", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "The result is creation of an URS [R1] document.\n\n# Table 1 provides an example of an URS document with three very simple requirements for the computer-based system functionality:\n\n|URS ID|Requirement|Criticality|\n|---|---|---|\n|URS-x-01|\u2026|Essential/Important/Desired|\n|URS-F-49|Screen display of control system must show the entire production process on one screen with process values.|Essential|\n|URS-F-50|The control system must show on the screen display, who is signed in, and the date and time.|Essential|\n|URS-F-51|The control system must record all process parameters in graph with the time on the x-axis and parameter values on the y-axis and enable a real-time display of these parameters.|Essential|\n|\u2026|\u2026|\u2026|\n|URS-x-n|User requirement \u2013 n|Essential/Important/Desired|\n---\n# Journal of Contemporary Management Issues\n\n# Create High Level Risk Assessment (HLRA)\n\nWith HLRA, we perform the original computer-based system classification - GxP relevance of the computer-based system and the computer system/application categorization. With the purpose to ensure easier approach to validation, computer systems are classified into one of the GAMP categories that represent a standard for computer systems in the pharmaceutical industry (International Society for Pharmaceutical Engineering - ISPE, 2008, pp. 128-132; Tedstone, 2012; McDowall, 2010, pp. 22-31). As far as the SCADA system categorization, we determined it belongs to the GAMP4 category (for controlling and managing production), being a configurable computer system. In our case, platform (e.g. Proficy iFix) on the SCADA system will be modified and configured by an integrator (supplier), according to our business needs and the URS.\n\nIn HLRA, we also determine if the computer system is 21 CFR Part 11 relevant or not (we ask ourselves whether the system will store electronic records or use electronic signatures).", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 20266, "end_char_idx": 22151, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "5a5bcc6b-d68d-403f-9c1f-9ffc3426b3c7", "embedding": [-0.05374796316027641, 0.022788187488913536, 0.0619986318051815, -0.020653031766414642, -0.015091078355908394, -0.03716754913330078, 0.03447883203625679, -0.0007870920235291123, 0.022867267951369286, 0.057517439126968384, 0.04336214065551758, 0.000931659946218133, -0.050110287964344025, -0.010247435420751572, 0.0011516008526086807, -0.01651451736688614, -0.002273546764627099, 0.040831584483385086, -0.01737121492624283, -0.003983649425208569, 0.07254261523485184, 0.04312489926815033, -0.0013863693457096815, 0.033582594245672226, -0.03215915337204933, -0.08793683350086212, 0.012784581631422043, 0.04950401186943054, -0.01665949635207653, -0.0448646582