9651004076, -0.02757861092686653, -0.032658204436302185, 0.020459480583667755, 0.01985660009086132, -0.026937246322631836, 0.032991714775562286, -0.04045717790722847, 0.015508158132433891, 0.002267218194901943, 0.012718228623270988, -0.006830516271293163, -0.0011672807158902287], "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the importance of ensuring that a supplier develops a computer system in alignment with the User Requirements Specification (URS) in the context of Quality Management and Computer System Validation within the pharmaceutical industry. Key topics include:\n\n1. **System Functionalities**: The excerpt presents a table (Table 2) that outlines various system functionalities as described in the Functional Specification (FS) document, including specific references to URS.\n\n2. **Design Qualification (DQ)**: The process of conducting Design Qualification is emphasized, highlighting the need for thorough documentation and review of design documents (FS, Software Design Specification (SDS), and Hardware Design Specification (HDS)) to ensure compliance with URS.\n\n3. **Documentation Review**: The importance of reviewing and approving design documentation from the supplier is stressed, ensuring that all URS requirements are met before the supplier begins building the computer system.\n\n4. **Approval Process**: The section mentions that appointed responsible persons must approve the documentation after comparing the URS with the FS, SDS, and HDS.\n\nEntities involved include:\n- **Supplier**: Responsible for creating the computer system.\n- **User Requirements Specification (URS)**: Defines the requirements that the system must meet.\n- **Functional Specification (FS)**: Describes the functionalities of the system.\n- **Software Design Specification (SDS)** and **Hardware Design Specification (HDS)**: Provide detailed design information.\n- **Responsible Persons**: Individuals tasked with reviewing and approving the documentation. \n\nOverall, the section underscores the critical role of documentation and validation processes in ensuring compliance and quality in computer system development for the pharmaceutical industry."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "aa56a85f-5063-4081-8293-dc8e7947d2d3", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26"