data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21", "document_title": "\"Comprehensive Approaches to Quality Management and Computer System Validation in the Pharmaceutical Industry: Regulatory Frameworks, Best Practices, and Case Studies\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the processes involved in ensuring quality management and computer system validation within the pharmaceutical industry. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Deviation Examination**: The comparison of Functional Specifications (FS), Software Design Specifications (SDS), Hardware Design Specifications (HDS), and User Requirements Specifications (URS) to identify and document deviations.\n\n2. **Traceability**: Emphasis on the importance of traceability in design documents, ensuring that all URS are accounted for and linked to the corresponding tests (Installation Qualification (IQ), Operational Qualification (OQ), and Performance Qualification (PQ)).\n\n3. **Test Management (TM)**: The creation of a Test Management document can begin during the Design Qualification (DQ) phase, facilitating early traceability between URS and other specifications.\n\n4. **Documentation and Reporting**: The necessity of connecting design documentation with test reports and maintaining unique identifiers for user requests to ensure traceability.\n\n5. **Testing Compliance**: The section highlights the importance of testing all functionalities of the computer system, particularly if any failures are identified based on Functional Risk Assessment (FRA) results.\n\n6. **Table of Traceability Matrix (TM)**: A table is provided that outlines the relationship between URS, FS, SDS, HDS, and the corresponding IQ, OQ, and PQ tests, indicating compliance for each requirement.\n\n7. **Final Activities Before Release**: Reference to a figure that illustrates the last activities required before the computer system is released for production and operational use.\n\nOverall, the section underscores the critical role of documentation, traceability, and compliance testing in the validation of computer systems in the pharmaceutical sector."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "2f2b69d9-5dae-4221-9dcb-f2fbedd34145", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "1137d67616953033e3ad92507bb961ae6095138365fd269914446ae7383f7d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "d961456e-07ed-49ce-9a10-18aafd1a686e", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_name": "COMPUTER SYSTEM VALIDATION EXAMPLE OF QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 53509, "creation_date": "2025-03-26", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-21"}, "hash": "5d5f9371019cbce2cb8cb0d75f71e7d3162faedf58a91bbe34f7f97f1c375053", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "6d247a1b-739b-444c-891f-02ae765b976f", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "21772175fc065b1cb5608ea17ac64bc5673d0f6c939a2ee768da5095f566b68a", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "We have also examined the possible deviations, by comparing FS, SDS, HDS and URS and documented them in the DQ [R6]. It is, also, necessary to provide traceability, where it is evident, in a transparent manner, whether all URS have been considered in the design documents (this is already checked in DQ) and which tests (IQ, OQ, PQ) were used to test these requirements. To start the creation of TM [R12], there is no need to wait for the computer system verification, as we can start to build it earlier (during the design qualification - DQ). This ensures the first part of the traceability between URS and FS, SDS and HDS.\n---\n# Journal of Contemporary Management Issues\n\nprovided by IQ, OQ and PQ tests, where we documented and, retrospectively, we must connect the design documentation with test reports. As already mentioned, each user\u2019s request is marked with a unique identifier (ID), so that we can guarantee the traceability of document designs and tests. If we find out that we have failed to test one of the computer system functionality, this must be tested, in accordance with the FRA results.\n\nTM for our example is shown in Table 5.\n\n|URS|FS|SDS|HDS|IQ|OQ|PQ|Comment|\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n|URS-F-49|FS-EP-01|/|/|/|OQ-1_screen test \u2013 step 1|/|Complies|\n|URS-F-50|FS-EP-01|/|/|/|OQ-1_screen test \u2013 step 1|/|Complies|\n|URS-F-51|FS-HI-01|/|/|/|OQ-2_parameters and history test \u2013 steps 1, 2|/|Complies|\n\n# 5.3.5. Report sub-process\n\nFigure 6 shows last activities needed before the release of the computer system into production and operational use.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 36275, "end_char_idx": 37848, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "6d247a1b-739b-444c-891f-02ae765b976f", "embedding": [-0.006941495928913355, 0.075098119