ems, 2021.\n\n[101] Ralf Steinberger, Bruno Pouliquen, Anna Widiger, Camelia Ignat, Toma\u017e Erjavec, Dan Tufi\u00b8s, and D\u00e1niel Varga. The JRC-Acquis: A multilingual aligned parallel corpus with 20+ languages. In Nicoletta Calzolari, Khalid Choukri, Aldo Gangemi, Bente Maegaard, Joseph Mariani, Jan Odijk, and Daniel Tapias, editors, Proceedings of the Fifth International Conference on Language Resources and Evaluation (LREC\u201806), Genoa, Italy, May 2006. European Language Resources Association (ELRA).", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 103460, "end_char_idx": 103999, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}]}, "33feeb9da1f04d98ae88221b6097b5dfdb1313f5c68eef0b63b1e1f0d8e76c69": {"nodes": [{"__data__": {"id_": "3f326cbb-952c-497c-a542-d4a2cc488b78", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses \"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation\" (Agentic RAG), a novel approach that enhances traditional Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems by incorporating autonomous AI agents. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Introduction to Agentic RAG**: The paper introduces the concept of Agentic RAG, which aims to overcome the limitations of traditional RAG systems that rely on static workflows and struggle with dynamic, real-time queries.\n\n2. **Foundational Principles**: It outlines the foundational principles of Agentic RAG, emphasizing the integration of real-time data retrieval to improve the relevance and accuracy of responses generated by Large Language Models (LLMs).\n\n3. **Agentic Design Patterns**: The paper discusses various agentic design patterns such as reflection, planning, tool use, and multi-agent collaboration that enable dynamic management of retrieval strategies and adaptive workflows.\n\n4. **Taxonomy of Architectures**: A detailed taxonomy of Agentic RAG architectures is presented, categorizing different implementations and their functionalities.\n\n5. **Applications**: The survey highlights key applications of Agentic RAG in various industries, including healthcare, finance, and education, showcasing its versatility and potential impact.\n\n6. **Implementation Strategies**: It examines practical strategies for implementing Agentic RAG systems, focusing on their flexibility, scalability, and context-awareness.\n\nEntities mentioned include:\n- Authors: Aditi Singh, Abul Ehtesham, Saket Kumar, Tala Talaei Khoei\n- Institutions: Cleveland State University, The Davey Tree Expert Company, The MathWorks Inc, Khoury College of Computer Science at Northeastern University. \n\nOverall, the survey aims to provide a comprehensive understanding of Agentic RAG and its implications for dynamic AI systems."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "212c61a9-ccbe-409c-9c94-5eacecabc84e", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "b499d1db52036cb05791d59303952aee44ec8b68989441db31c2eab533da2f5b", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "# AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION: A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG\n\nAditi Singh\n\nDepartment of Computer Science\n\nCleveland State University\n\nCleveland, OH, USA\n\na.singh22@csuohio.edu\n\nAbul Ehtesham\n\nThe Davey Tree Expert Company\n\nKent, OH, USA\n\nabul.ehtesham@davey.com\n\nSaket Kumar\n\nThe MathWorks Inc\n\nNatick, MA, USA\n\nsaketk@mathworks.com\n\nTala Talaei Khoei\n\nKhoury College of Computer Science\n\nRoux Institute at Northeastern University\n\nPortland, ME, USA\n\nt.talaeikhoei@northeastern.edu\n\n# ABSTRACT\n\nLarge Language Models (LLMs) have revolutionized artificial intelligence (AI) by enabling human-like text generation and natural language understanding. However, their reliance on static training data limits their ability to respond to dynamic, real-time queries, resulting in outdated or inaccurate outputs. Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) has emerged as a solution, enhancing LLMs by integrating real-time data retrieval to provide contextually relevant and up-to-date responses. Despite its promise, traditional RAG systems are constrained by static workflows and lack the adaptability required for multi-step reasoning and complex task management.\n\nAgentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (Agentic RAG) transcends these limitations by embedding autonomous AI agents into the RAG pipeline. These agents leverage agentic design patterns reflection, planning, tool use, and multi-agent collaboration to dynamically manage retrieval strategies, iteratively refine contextual understanding, and adapt workflows through clearly defined operational structures ranging from sequential steps to adaptive collaboration. This integration enables Agentic RAG systems to deliver unparalleled flexibility, scalability, and context-awareness across diverse applications.\n\nThis survey provides a comprehensive exploration of Agentic RAG, beginning with its foundational principles and the evolution of RAG paradigms. It presents a detailed taxonomy of Agentic RAG architectures, highlights key applications in industries such as healthcare, finance, and education, and examines practical implementation strategies.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 0, "end_char_idx": 2107, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "212c61a9-ccbe-409c-9c94-5eacecabc84e", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the concept of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) and its significance in the field of artificial intelligence (AI). Key topics include:\n\n1. **Taxonomy of Agentic RAG Architectures**: The document presents a detailed classification of different Agentic RAG architectures.\n2. **Applications**: It highlights the use of Agentic RAG in various industries, specifically healthcare, finance, and education.\n3. **Implementation Strategies**: The section examines practical strategies for implementing Agentic RAG systems.\n4. **Challenges**: It addresses challenges related to scaling these systems, ensuring ethical decision-making, and optimizing performance for real-world applications.\n5. **Frameworks and Tools**: Insights into frameworks and tools for implementing Agentic RAG are provided.\n6. **Limitations of LLMs**: The introduction discusses the limitations of Large Language Models (LLMs), including reliance on static pre-training data, outdated information, and hallucinated responses.\n\nEntities mentioned include:\n- Large Language Models (LLMs) such as OpenAI\u2019s GPT-4, Google\u2019s PaLM, and Meta\u2019s LLaMA.\n- Key concepts like Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), ethical AI decision-making, and multi-agent collaboration.\n\nThe section also includes a GitHub link for further resources related to the survey on Agentic RAG."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "3f326cbb-952c-497c-a542-d4a2cc488b78", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "de0ca16cfda453cb43a70d609cb02d8f49a9a05cb336dff5d568ec9b27d7b372", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "944d7f01-b0db-409d-9a51-8c67f34072bc", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "288468f7af1a394009f1286903a8777bc67a24744c3f0cd9e153a630bf5f86ba", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "It presents a detailed taxonomy of Agentic RAG architectures, highlights key applications in industries such as healthcare, finance, and education, and examines practical implementation strategies. Additionally, it addresses challenges in scaling these systems, ensuring ethical decision-making, and optimizing performance for real-world applications, while providing detailed insights into frameworks and tools for implementing Agentic RAG1. The GitHub link for this survey is available at: https://github.com/asinghcsu/AgenticRAG-Survey.\n\n# Keywords\n\nLarge Language Models (LLMs) \u00b7 Artificial Intelligence (AI) \u00b7 Natural Language Understanding \u00b7 Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) \u00b7 Agentic RAG \u00b7 Autonomous AI Agents \u00b7 Reflection \u00b7 Planning \u00b7 Tool Use \u00b7 Multi-Agent Collaboration \u00b7 Agentic Patterns \u00b7 Contextual Understanding \u00b7 Dynamic Adaptability \u00b7 Scalability \u00b7 Real-Time Data Retrieval \u00b7 Taxonomy of Agentic RAG \u00b7 Healthcare Applications \u00b7 Finance Applications \u00b7 Educational Applications \u00b7 Ethical AI Decision-Making \u00b7 Performance Optimization \u00b7 Multi-Step Reasoning\n\n1GitHub link: https://github.com/asinghcsu/AgenticRAG-Survey\n---\n# 1 Introduction\n\nLarge Language Models (LLMs) [1, 2] [3], such as OpenAI\u2019s GPT-4, Google\u2019s PaLM, and Meta\u2019s LLaMA, have significantly transformed artificial intelligence (AI) with their ability to generate human-like text and perform complex natural language processing tasks. These models have driven innovation across diverse domains, including conversational agents [4], automated content creation, and real-time translation. Recent advancements have extended their capabilities to multimodal tasks, such as text-to-image and text-to-video generation [5], enabling the creation and editing of videos and images from detailed prompts [6], which broadens the potential applications of generative AI.\n\nDespite these advancements, LLMs face significant limitations due to their reliance on static pre-training data. This reliance often results in outdated information, hallucinated responses [7], and an inability to adapt to dynamic, real-world scenarios. These challenges emphasize the need for systems that can integrate real-time data and dynamically refine responses to maintain contextual relevance and accuracy.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 1910, "end_char_idx": 4170, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "944d7f01-b0db-409d-9a51-8c67f34072bc", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the concept of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) and its evolution into Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (Agentic RAG). Key topics include:\n\n1. **Challenges in AI Systems**: The need for systems that can integrate real-time data and dynamically refine responses for contextual relevance and accuracy.\n\n2. **Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)**: A solution that combines the generative capabilities of large language models (LLMs) with external retrieval mechanisms to enhance response relevance and timeliness. However, traditional RAG systems are limited by their linear and static design.\n\n3. **Evolution of Agents**: Modern AI agents, including LLM-powered and mobile agents, are capable of perception, reasoning, and autonomous task execution. They utilize agentic patterns such as reflection, planning, tool use, and multi-agent collaboration to improve decision-making.\n\n4. **Agentic Workflow Patterns**: These include prompt chaining, routing, parallelization, orchestrator-worker models, and evaluator-optimizer, which help structure and optimize task execution.\n\n5. **Agentic RAG**: A paradigm that integrates agents into the RAG pipeline, enabling dynamic retrieval strategies, contextual understanding, and iterative refinement. It allows for adaptive and efficient information processing, excelling in scenarios that require precision and adaptability.\n\nThe section concludes by indicating that the survey will explore the foundational principles, taxonomy, and applications of Agentic RAG."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "212c61a9-ccbe-409c-9c94-5eacecabc84e", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "5b71f67910da967d9265827e50daaf67987fd88a8d6f3a964222c121924a86ae", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "537faf4a-2890-4982-9493-4fdc24fa9ec6", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "9eeed31218fb03b818ee402185323b40dd841187af2108f5efd2faba7e0c4e89", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "These challenges emphasize the need for systems that can integrate real-time data and dynamically refine responses to maintain contextual relevance and accuracy.\n\nRetrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) [8, 9] emerged as a promising solution to these challenges. By combining the generative capabilities of LLMs with external retrieval mechanisms [10], RAG systems enhance the relevance and timeliness of responses. These systems retrieve real-time information from sources such as knowledge bases [11], APIs, or the web, effectively bridging the gap between static training data and the demands of dynamic applications. However, traditional RAG workflows remain limited by their linear and static design, which restricts their ability to perform complex multi-step reasoning, integrate deep contextual understanding, and iteratively refine responses.\n\nThe evolution of agents [12] has significantly enhanced the capabilities of AI systems. Modern agents, including LLM-powered and mobile agents [13], are intelligent entities capable of perceiving, reasoning, and autonomously executing tasks. These agents leverage agentic patterns, such as reflection [14], planning [15], tool use, and multi-agent collaboration [16], to enhance decision-making and adaptability.\n\nFurthermore, these agents employ agentic workflow patterns [12, 13], such as prompt chaining, routing, parallelization, orchestrator-worker models, and evaluator-optimizer, to structure and optimize task execution. By integrating these patterns, Agentic RAG systems can efficiently manage dynamic workflows and address complex problem-solving scenarios. The convergence of RAG and agentic intelligence has given rise to Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (Agentic RAG) [14], a paradigm that integrates agents into the RAG pipeline. Agentic RAG enables dynamic retrieval strategies, contextual understanding, and iterative refinement [15], allowing for adaptive and efficient information processing. Unlike traditional RAG, Agentic RAG employs autonomous agents to orchestrate retrieval, filter relevant information, and refine responses, excelling in scenarios requiring precision and adaptability. The overview of Agentic RAG is in figure 1.\n\nThis survey explores the foundational principles, taxonomy, and applications of Agentic RAG.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 4009, "end_char_idx": 6313, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "537faf4a-2890-4982-9493-4fdc24fa9ec6", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section provides an overview of the document titled \"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems.\" It discusses the foundational principles, taxonomy, and applications of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), highlighting various paradigms such as Na\u00efve RAG, Modular RAG, and Graph RAG. The document outlines the structure of the paper, which includes sections on the evolution of RAG, principles of agentic intelligence, agentic workflow patterns, a taxonomy of Agentic RAG systems, comparative analysis, applications, implementation tools, benchmarks, and future directions.\n\nKey topics include:\n- Overview of Agentic RAG and its frameworks\n- Applications in domains like healthcare, finance, and education\n- Implementation strategies and ethical considerations\n- Foundations of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)\n- Limitations of traditional approaches to AI\n- Dynamic data retrieval and its integration with generative models\n\nEntities mentioned include:\n- Agentic RAG\n- Large Language Models (LLMs)\n- Various application domains (healthcare, finance, education)\n- Frameworks (single-agent, multi-agent, graph-based)"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "944d7f01-b0db-409d-9a51-8c67f34072bc", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "b1109057bcb9aa410fdc46e4735a058319f0f943044ea48d089e4bec9cde3d20", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "47c68644-53e4-4433-baa9-9715df0b303e", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "367fb9de5dabea01ea938820462f73ccdb497863345837965ae491d93d6e030a", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "The overview of Agentic RAG is in figure 1.\n\nThis survey explores the foundational principles, taxonomy, and applications of Agentic RAG. It provides a comprehensive overview of RAG paradigms, such as Na\u00efve RAG, Modular RAG, and Graph RAG [16], alongside their evolution into Agentic RAG systems. Key contributions include a detailed taxonomy of Agentic RAG frameworks, applications across domains such as healthcare [17, 18], finance, and education [19], and insights into implementation strategies, benchmarks, and ethical considerations.\n\nThe structure of this paper is as follows: Section 2 introduces RAG and its evolution, highlighting the limitations of traditional approaches. Section 3 elaborates on the principles of agentic intelligence and agentic patterns. Section 4 elaborates agentic workflow patterns. Section 5 provides a taxonomy of Agentic RAG systems, including single-agent, multi-agent, and graph-based frameworks. Section 6 provides comparative analysis of Agentic RAG frameworks. Section 7 examines applications of Agentic RAG, while Section 8 discusses implementation tools and frameworks. Section 9 focuses on benchmarks and dataset, and Section 10 concludes with future directions for Agentic RAG systems.\n\n# 2 Foundations of Retrieval-Augmented Generation\n\n# 2.1 Overview of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)\n\nRetrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) represents a significant advancement in the field of artificial intelligence, combining the generative capabilities of Large Language Models (LLMs) with real-time data retrieval. While LLMs have demonstrated remarkable capabilities in natural language processing, their reliance on static pre-trained data often results in outdated or incomplete responses. RAG addresses this limitation by dynamically retrieving relevant information from external sources and incorporating it into the generative process, enabling contextually accurate and up-to-date outputs.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 6176, "end_char_idx": 8114, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "47c68644-53e4-4433-baa9-9715df0b303e", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the concept of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) and its evolution, focusing on the integration of external information to enhance generative processes in AI systems. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Framework and Stack**: Tools and frameworks used in RAG, such as Langraph, Llamalndex, AG2 (AutoGen), Semantic Kernel, Crew AI, Amazon Bedrock, and OpenAI Swarm.\n\n2. **Challenges and Limitations**: Issues faced by RAG, including hallucinations, inaccuracies, limited contextual integration, static workflows, and lack of adaptability.\n\n3. **Benefits and Advantages of Agentic RAG**: Enhanced decision-making, multi-step reasoning, and iterative refinement.\n\n4. **Core Components of RAG**: The architecture consists of three main components:\n   - **Retrieval**: Queries external data sources for relevant information.\n   - **Augmentation**: Processes and summarizes retrieved data.\n   - **Generation**: Combines retrieved information with pre-trained knowledge to produce coherent responses.\n\n5. **RAG Paradigm**: A table outlining different task roles, memory types, and workflows, including Naive RAG, Advanced RAG, Modular RAG, and Graph RAG.\n\n6. **Evolution of RAG Paradigms**: The development of RAG to meet the demands of complex real-world applications, emphasizing contextual accuracy, scalability, and multi-step reasoning.\n\nOverall, the section highlights the principles, architectures, applications, and future directions of Agentic RAG in dynamic AI systems."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "537faf4a-2890-4982-9493-4fdc24fa9ec6", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "5d00448445e99d1a2316149b3e3a21b7ca9719035ac35fcf61c57d79b80f7ed8", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "c3295406-e0a5-48b2-ae06-875d70ce1022", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "5ab1409d266fe9363fd2e6095e9ec56c6ff4c5d1e5e5c06c1b8fa49e6219f376", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "RAG addresses this limitation by dynamically retrieving relevant information from external sources and incorporating it into the generative process, enabling contextually accurate and up-to-date outputs.\n---\n# Framework and Stack\n\nLangraph\nLlamalndex\nAG2 (AutoGen)\nSemantic Kernel\nCrew Al\nAmazon Bedrock\nOpen Al Swarm\n# RAG Challenges & Limitations\n\n# Agentic RAG\n\n# Agentic RAG Benefits & Advantages\n\n- Enhanced Decision-Making\n- Multi-Step Reasoning & Iterative Refinement\n\n# Hallucinations & Inaccuracies\n\n- Limited Contextual Integration\n- Static Workflow\n- Lack Adaptability\n\n# Tools\n\n- Planning\n- Real-Time Data Integration\n- Adaptive Learning & Context Awareness\n- Improved Accuracy\n- Reduced Hallucinations\n\n# RAG Paradigm\n\n|Task Role|Memory|Single Router|Multi-Agent|\n|---|---|---|---|\n|Reflection|Agentic Pattern|Planning|Hierarchical|\n|Naive RAG|Advanced RAG|Multi-Agents|Tools|\n|Modular RAG|Agentic Workflow Pattern|Prompt Chaining|Routing|\n|Graph RAG|Orchestrator-workers|Parallelization|Agentic Document Workflow|\n\nFigure 1: An Overview of Agentic RAG\n\n# Core Components of RAG\n\nThe architecture of RAG systems integrates three primary components (Figure 2):\n\n- Retrieval: Responsible for querying external data sources such as knowledge bases, APIs, or vector databases. Advanced retrievers leverage dense vector search and transformer-based models to improve retrieval precision and semantic relevance.\n- Augmentation: Processes retrieved data, extracting and summarizing the most relevant information to align with the query context.\n- Generation: Combines retrieved information with the LLM\u2019s pre-trained knowledge to generate coherent, contextually appropriate responses.\n\n# Evolution of RAG Paradigms\n\nThe field of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) has evolved significantly to address the increasing complexity of real-world applications, where contextual accuracy, scalability, and multi-step reasoning are critical.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 7911, "end_char_idx": 9852, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "c3295406-e0a5-48b2-ae06-875d70ce1022", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the evolution of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, highlighting the transition from simple keyword-based retrieval to more sophisticated, adaptive systems capable of handling complex queries. It outlines the progression of RAG paradigms, specifically focusing on Na\u00efve RAG and its characteristics.\n\n**Key Topics:**\n1. **Evolution of RAG Systems**: The transition from basic keyword-based retrieval to advanced systems that integrate diverse data sources and autonomous decision-making.\n2. **Na\u00efve RAG**: The foundational implementation of RAG characterized by:\n   - Simple retrieve-read workflow.\n   - Use of keyword-based retrieval techniques (e.g., TF-IDF, BM25).\n   - Augmentation of language models with retrieved documents.\n3. **Limitations of Na\u00efve RAG**:\n   - Lack of contextual awareness.\n   - Fragmented outputs due to insufficient preprocessing.\n   - Scalability issues with large datasets.\n4. **Importance of Na\u00efve RAG**: Despite its limitations, it served as a proof-of-concept for integrating retrieval with generation, paving the way for more advanced paradigms.\n\n**Entities:**\n- **RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)**: A system that combines retrieval and generation processes.\n- **Na\u00efve RAG**: The initial stage of RAG systems.\n- **Techniques**: TF-IDF, BM25 (keyword-based retrieval methods).\n- **Key Characteristics**: Simplicity, ease of implementation, and foundational role in RAG development. \n\nThe section sets the stage for discussing more advanced RAG systems, such as Advanced RAG, which address the limitations of Na\u00efve RAG."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "47c68644-53e4-4433-baa9-9715df0b303e", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "457816e758dffec97a72625e5f5c1c10e932cb1437aa025c4976c033c770870b", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "f677dafe-f70d-4684-b485-29eef983d93a", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "769e86f4e4e4392c26d4dc094b415622926fcb18e5dd92ed0c426be20198a334", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "What began as simple keyword-based retrieval has transitioned into sophisticated, modular, and adaptive systems capable of integrating diverse data sources and autonomous decision-making processes. This evolution underscores the growing need for RAG systems to handle complex queries efficiently and effectively.\n\nThis section examines the progression of RAG paradigms, presenting key stages of development\u2014Na\u00efve RAG, Advanced RAG, Modular RAG, Graph RAG, and Agentic RAG alongside their defining characteristics, strengths, and\n---\n# 2.3.1 Na\u00efve RAG\n\nNa\u00efve RAG [20] represents the foundational implementation of retrieval-augmented generation. Figure 3 illustrates the simple retrieve-read workflow of Naive RAG, focusing on keyword-based retrieval and static datasets. These systems rely on simple keyword-based retrieval techniques, such as TF-IDF and BM25, to fetch documents from static datasets. The retrieved documents are then used to augment the language model\u2019s generative capabilities.\n\n|Additional Documents|User Query|\n|---|---|\n|Encode|Encode|\n|Embedding Model|LLM|\n|Vector database|Similar Documents|\n|Similarity Search|Query|\n\nNa\u00efve RAG is characterized by its simplicity and ease of implementation, making it suitable for tasks involving fact-based queries with minimal contextual complexity. However, it suffers from several limitations:\n\n- Lack of Contextual Awareness: Retrieved documents often fail to capture the semantic nuances of the query due to reliance on lexical matching rather than semantic understanding.\n- Fragmented Outputs: The absence of advanced preprocessing or contextual integration often leads to disjointed or overly generic responses.\n- Scalability Issues: Keyword-based retrieval techniques struggle with large datasets, often failing to identify the most relevant information.\n\nDespite these limitations, Na\u00efve RAG systems provided a critical proof-of-concept for integrating retrieval with generation, laying the foundation for more sophisticated paradigms.\n\n# 2.3.2 Advanced RAG\n\nAdvanced RAG [20] systems build upon the limitations of Na\u00efve RAG by incorporating semantic understanding and enhanced retrieval techniques. Figure 4 highlights the semantic enhancements in retrieval and the iterative, context-aware pipeline of Advanced RAG.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 9853, "end_char_idx": 12138, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "f677dafe-f70d-4684-b485-29eef983d93a", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses advancements in Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, focusing on two specific paradigms: Modular RAG and Graph RAG.\n\n### Key Topics:\n1. **Advanced RAG**: Highlights the use of dense retrieval models and neural ranking algorithms to enhance retrieval precision.\n2. **Modular RAG**: \n   - Emphasizes flexibility and customization by decomposing the retrieval and generation pipeline into independent components.\n   - Key innovations include:\n     - **Hybrid Retrieval Strategies**: Combining sparse and dense retrieval methods for improved accuracy.\n     - **Tool Integration**: Utilizing external APIs and databases for specialized tasks.\n     - **Composable Pipelines**: Allowing independent enhancement and reconfiguration of components for adaptability to specific use cases.\n   - Example: A Modular RAG system for financial analytics that retrieves live stock prices and generates investment insights.\n\n3. **Graph RAG**: \n   - Integrates graph-based data structures to enhance multi-hop reasoning and contextual enrichment.\n   - Characterized by its ability to capture relationships between entities through node connectivity.\n\n### Entities:\n- **Dense Passage Retrieval (DPR)**: A dense retrieval model used in Advanced RAG.\n- **BM25**: A sparse retrieval method mentioned in the context of hybrid strategies.\n- **APIs and Databases**: External tools integrated into Modular RAG for specialized tasks.\n- **Graph Data Structures**: Used in Graph RAG to improve relational understanding and generative outputs.\n\nOverall, the section outlines the evolution of RAG systems towards more modular and graph-integrated approaches, enhancing their adaptability and effectiveness in various applications."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "c3295406-e0a5-48b2-ae06-875d70ce1022", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "49d244eef7b724111227f6e73f18787630c008b25f928a0df1f870a65de72f1f", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "7d41fc1a-b325-4075-ba0d-fe449c82cb2f", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "438d9c57b6cc3a1b049da92a098e811c6a3fec6b76f5061bed4b087341b7019f", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Figure 4 highlights the semantic enhancements in retrieval and the iterative, context-aware pipeline of Advanced RAG. These systems leverage dense retrieval models, such as Dense Passage Retrieval (DPR), and neural ranking algorithms to improve retrieval precision.\n\nKey features of Advanced RAG include:\n---\n# 2.3.3 Modular RAG\n\nModular RAG [20] represents the latest evolution in RAG paradigms, emphasizing flexibility and customization. These systems decompose the retrieval and generation pipeline into independent, reusable components, enabling domain-specific optimization and task adaptability. Figure 5 demonstrates the modular architecture, showcasing hybrid retrieval strategies, composable pipelines, and external tool integration.\n\n# Key innovations in Modular RAG include:\n\n- Hybrid Retrieval Strategies: Combining sparse retrieval methods (e.g., a sparse encoder-BM25) with dense retrieval techniques [21] (e.g., DPR - Dense Passage Retrieval) to maximize accuracy across diverse query types.\n- Tool Integration: Incorporating external APIs, databases, or computational tools to handle specialized tasks, such as real-time data analysis or domain-specific computations.\n- Composable Pipelines: Modular RAG enables retrievers, generators, and other components to be replaced, enhanced, or reconfigured independently, allowing high adaptability to specific use cases.\n\nFor instance, a Modular RAG system designed for financial analytics might retrieve live stock prices via APIs, analyze historical trends using dense retrieval, and generate actionable investment insights through a tailored language model. This modularity and customization make Modular RAG ideal for complex, multi-domain tasks, offering both scalability and precision.\n---\n# 2.3.4 Graph RAG\n\nGraph RAG [16] extends traditional Retrieval-Augmented Generation systems by integrating graph-based data structures as illustrated in Figure 6. These systems leverage the relationships and hierarchies within graph data to enhance multi-hop reasoning and contextual enrichment. By incorporating graph-based retrieval, Graph RAG enables richer and more accurate generative outputs, particularly for tasks requiring relational understanding.\n\nGraph RAG is characterized by its ability to:\n\n- Node Connectivity: Captures and reasons over relationships between entities.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 12021, "end_char_idx": 14361, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "7d41fc1a-b325-4075-ba0d-fe449c82cb2f", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses two advanced paradigms within Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems: Graph RAG and Agentic RAG. \n\n**Key Topics:**\n\n1. **Graph RAG:**\n   - **Characteristics:**\n     - Node Connectivity: Understanding relationships between entities.\n     - Hierarchical Knowledge Management: Managing both structured and unstructured data.\n     - Context Enrichment: Enhancing understanding through graph pathways.\n   - **Limitations:**\n     - Limited Scalability: Challenges with extensive data sources.\n     - Data Dependency: Requires high-quality graph data for effective outputs.\n     - Complexity of Integration: Difficulties in merging graph data with unstructured systems.\n   - **Applications:** Suitable for fields like healthcare diagnostics and legal research.\n\n2. **Agentic RAG:**\n   - **Characteristics:**\n     - Autonomous Decision-Making: Agents manage retrieval strategies independently.\n     - Iterative Refinement: Uses feedback loops for improved accuracy.\n     - Workflow Optimization: Dynamically organizes tasks for efficiency.\n   - **Challenges:**\n     - Coordination Complexity: Requires sophisticated management of agent interactions.\n     - Computational Overhead: Increased resource demands due to multiple agents.\n     - Scalability Limitations: Dynamic nature can strain resources under high query volumes.\n   - **Applications:** Effective in customer support, financial analytics, and adaptive learning platforms.\n\n3. **Challenges of Traditional RAG Systems:** \n   - Traditional RAG systems enhance Large Language Models (LLMs) by integrating real-time data retrieval but face inherent challenges and limitations.\n\n**Entities:**\n- Graph RAG\n- Agentic RAG\n- Autonomous agents\n- Large Language Models (LLMs)\n- Applications in healthcare, legal research, customer support, financial analytics, and adaptive learning."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "f677dafe-f70d-4684-b485-29eef983d93a", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "574306a28b10fb3a339f03f9870b283c097ebd9b38c72ec1f02fb6a4e69b0f19", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "72802403-121c-4b98-9adc-75f90cb3fcc5", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "78a2f34ccf1c44c80f784e09c4c40c8c5248b852cc8f724c06b8672f926e0fea", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Graph RAG is characterized by its ability to:\n\n- Node Connectivity: Captures and reasons over relationships between entities.\n- Hierarchical Knowledge Management: Handles structured and unstructured data through graph-based hierarchies.\n- Context Enrichment: Adds relational understanding by leveraging graph-based pathways.\n\nHowever, Graph RAG has some limitations:\n\n- Limited Scalability: The reliance on graph structures can restrict scalability, especially with extensive data sources.\n- Data Dependency: High-quality graph data is essential for meaningful outputs, limiting its applicability in unstructured or poorly annotated datasets.\n- Complexity of Integration: Integrating graph data with unstructured retrieval systems increases design and implementation complexity.\n\nGraph RAG is well-suited for applications such as healthcare diagnostics, legal research, and other domains where reasoning over structured relationships is crucial.\n\n# 2.3.5 Agentic RAG\n\nAgentic RAG represents a paradigm shift by introducing autonomous agents capable of dynamic decision-making and workflow optimization. Unlike static systems, Agentic RAG employs iterative refinement and adaptive retrieval strategies to address complex, real-time, and multi-domain queries. This paradigm leverages the modularity of retrieval and generation processes while introducing agent-based autonomy.\n---\n# Key characteristics of Agentic RAG include:\n\n- Autonomous Decision-Making: Agents independently evaluate and manage retrieval strategies based on query complexity.\n- Iterative Refinement: Incorporates feedback loops to improve retrieval accuracy and response relevance.\n- Workflow Optimization: Dynamically orchestrates tasks, enabling efficiency in real-time applications.\n\nDespite its advancements, Agentic RAG faces some challenges:\n\n- Coordination Complexity: Managing interactions between agents requires sophisticated orchestration mechanisms.\n- Computational Overhead: The use of multiple agents increases resource requirements for complex workflows.\n- Scalability Limitations: While scalable, the dynamic nature of the system can strain computational resources for high query volumes.\n\nAgentic RAG excels in domains like customer support, financial analytics, and adaptive learning platforms, where dynamic adaptability and contextual precision are paramount.\n\n# 2.4 Challenges and Limitations of Traditional RAG Systems\n\nTraditional Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems have significantly expanded the capabilities of Large Language Models (LLMs) by integrating real-time data retrieval.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 14236, "end_char_idx": 16821, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "72802403-121c-4b98-9adc-75f90cb3fcc5", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the challenges faced by Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems in real-world applications, focusing on three main limitations: contextual integration, multi-step reasoning, and scalability and latency issues. \n\nKey Topics:\n1. **Contextual Integration**: RAG systems struggle to effectively incorporate retrieved information into generated responses, leading to fragmented or generic outputs.\n2. **Multi-step Reasoning**: The systems face difficulties in performing complex reasoning tasks that require multiple steps.\n3. **Scalability and Latency**: Issues related to the ability of RAG systems to scale and respond quickly in dynamic environments.\n\nEntities:\n- **RAG Systems**: The primary subject of the discussion, referring to systems that combine retrieval and generation of information.\n- **Alzheimer\u2019s Research**: An example topic used to illustrate the limitations of RAG systems in synthesizing relevant information.\n- **Sustainable Practices**: Another example topic highlighting the challenges in retrieving and contextualizing specific practices for small-scale agriculture in arid regions. \n\nOverall, the excerpt emphasizes the need for improvements in RAG systems to enhance their effectiveness in providing coherent and contextually relevant information."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "7d41fc1a-b325-4075-ba0d-fe449c82cb2f", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "62e0ad7b14cd103e5fa5a1e12ca33e48c7538902ef724c2b1e6fc94e91a93419", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "1d92370d-490b-4b33-93a7-accab10000a4", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "f69dd055d22d3b17929a04c1a14efcab701502fd2d0dc5ee06058d2480f8feef", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "However, these systems still face critical challenges that hinder their effectiveness in complex, real-world applications. The most notable limitations revolve around contextual integration, multi-step reasoning, and scalability and latency issues.\n\n# 2.4.1 Contextual Integration\n\nEven when RAG systems successfully retrieve relevant information, they often struggle to seamlessly incorporate it into generated responses. The static nature of retrieval pipelines and limited contextual awareness lead to fragmented, inconsistent, or overly generic outputs.\n\nExample: A query such as, \"What are the latest advancements in Alzheimer\u2019s research and their implications for early-stage treatment?\" might yield relevant research papers and medical guidelines. However, traditional RAG systems often fail to synthesize these findings into a coherent explanation that connects the new treatments to specific patient scenarios. Similarly, for a query like, \"What are the best sustainable practices for small-scale agriculture in arid regions?\", traditional systems might retrieve documents on general agricultural methods but overlook critical sustainability practices tailored to arid environments.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 16822, "end_char_idx": 18013, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "1d92370d-490b-4b33-93a7-accab10000a4", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses various paradigms of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, highlighting their key features, strengths, and limitations. It includes a comparative analysis of five RAG paradigms: \n\n1. **Na\u00efve RAG**: Utilizes keyword-based retrieval methods like TF-IDF and BM25, suitable for straightforward fact-based queries.\n2. **Advanced RAG**: Employs dense retrieval models and hybrid approaches, offering high precision and contextual relevance.\n3. **Modular RAG**: Focuses on tool integration and domain-specific pipelines, providing scalability and relational reasoning capabilities.\n4. **Graph RAG**: Features multi-hop reasoning and contextual enrichment, effective for structured data tasks and reducing hallucinations.\n5. **Agentic RAG**: Incorporates autonomous agents and dynamic decision-making, adaptable to real-time changes and scalable for multi-domain tasks.\n\nThe section also addresses challenges in multi-step reasoning, emphasizing that traditional RAG systems struggle with complex queries requiring iterative synthesis of information. Additionally, it highlights scalability and latency issues as external data sources increase, impacting the system's responsiveness in real-time applications."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "72802403-121c-4b98-9adc-75f90cb3fcc5", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "4bbfffef462f3ba6bde16d7c50c7213e8b9905bd503e3d3bec87124392d0250d", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "52fbc46b-858d-4757-8e58-8e2ec0aeb82a", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "d2616682adba5f0d8463dcad9fc64e2cf5f302bc01d8a801538736b1f6addfc0", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "\", traditional systems might retrieve documents on general agricultural methods but overlook critical sustainability practices tailored to arid environments.\n---\n# Table 1: Comparative Analysis of RAG Paradigms\n\n|Paradigm|Key Features|Strengths|\n|---|---|---|\n|Na\u00efve RAG|\u2022 Keyword-based retrieval (e.g., TF-IDF, BM25)|\u2022 Simple and easy to implement \u2022 Suitable for fact-based queries|\n|Advanced RAG|\u2022 Dense retrieval models (e.g., DPR) \u2022 Neural ranking and re-ranking \u2022 Multi-hop retrieval \u2022 Hybrid retrieval (sparse and dense)|\u2022 High precision retrieval \u2022 Improved contextual relevance \u2022 High flexibility and customization|\n|Modular RAG|\u2022 Tool and API integration \u2022 Composable, domain-specific pipelines \u2022 Integration of graph-based structures|\u2022 Suitable for diverse applications \u2022 Scalable \u2022 Relational reasoning capabilities|\n|Graph RAG|\u2022 Multi-hop reasoning \u2022 Contextual enrichment via nodes|\u2022 Mitigates hallucinations \u2022 Ideal for structured data tasks|\n|Agentic RAG|\u2022 Autonomous agents \u2022 Dynamic decision-making \u2022 Iterative refinement and workflow optimization|\u2022 Adaptable to real-time changes \u2022 Scalable for multi-domain tasks \u2022 High accuracy|\n\n# 2.4.2 Multi-Step Reasoning\n\nMany real-world queries require iterative or multi-hop reasoning\u2014retrieving and synthesizing information across multiple steps. Traditional RAG systems are often ill-equipped to refine retrieval based on intermediate insights or user feedback, resulting in incomplete or disjointed responses.\n\nExample: A complex query like, \"What lessons from renewable energy policies in Europe can be applied to developing nations, and what are the potential economic impacts?\" demands the orchestration of multiple types of information, including policy data, contextualization for developing regions, and economic analysis. Traditional RAG systems typically fail to connect these disparate elements into a cohesive response.\n\n# 2.4.3 Scalability and Latency Issues\n\nAs the volume of external data sources grows, querying and ranking large datasets becomes increasingly computationally intensive. This results in significant latency, which undermines the system\u2019s ability to provide timely responses in real-time applications.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 17856, "end_char_idx": 20049, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "52fbc46b-858d-4757-8e58-8e2ec0aeb82a", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the concept of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), highlighting its significance in improving the responsiveness and effectiveness of AI systems in dynamic environments. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Latency Issues**: Traditional RAG systems face significant delays due to querying multiple databases and processing large document sets, which can hinder performance in time-sensitive applications like financial analytics and customer support.\n\n2. **Agentic RAG**: This represents a paradigm shift from traditional RAG systems by incorporating autonomous agents that enable dynamic decision-making, iterative reasoning, and adaptive retrieval strategies. This evolution aims to enhance the system's ability to handle complex, multi-domain tasks with improved precision and contextual understanding.\n\n3. **Core Principles of Agentic Intelligence**: The foundation of Agentic RAG is built on agentic intelligence, which allows for greater adaptability and precision through the integration of autonomous agents.\n\n4. **Components of an AI Agent**: The section outlines the essential components of an AI agent, including:\n   - **Large Language Model (LLM)**: Acts as the reasoning engine and dialogue interface.\n   - **Memory**: Consists of short-term memory for immediate context and long-term memory for accumulated knowledge and experiences.\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the advancements brought by Agentic RAG in addressing the limitations of traditional RAG systems, particularly in terms of latency and adaptability."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "1d92370d-490b-4b33-93a7-accab10000a4", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "dd2a02a47f2464099df25d2eae28d3b31d056919f4fc1dfe5e769ed40fa2a6b5", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "ffd5ddaf-31ce-4fc5-a5d7-023d7616f1ad", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "1e548b16c53f97cad0e5948d958a1093af584011b3d56dadbcd4996574621d2e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "This results in significant latency, which undermines the system\u2019s ability to provide timely responses in real-time applications.\n\nExample: In time-sensitive settings such as financial analytics or live customer support, delays caused by querying multiple databases or processing large document sets can hinder the system\u2019s overall utility. For example, a delay in retrieving market trends during high-frequency trading could result in missed opportunities.\n\n# 2.5 Agentic RAG: A Paradigm Shift\n\nTraditional RAG systems, with their static workflows and limited adaptability, often struggle to handle dynamic, multi-step reasoning and complex real-world tasks. These limitations have spurred the integration of agentic intelligence.\n---\nresulting in Agentic RAG. By incorporating autonomous agents capable of dynamic decision-making, iterative reasoning, and adaptive retrieval strategies, Agentic RAG builds on the modularity of earlier paradigms while overcoming their inherent constraints. This evolution enables more complex, multi-domain tasks to be addressed with enhanced precision and contextual understanding, positioning Agentic RAG as a cornerstone for next-generation AI applications. In particular, Agentic RAG systems reduce latency through optimized workflows and refine outputs iteratively, tackling the very challenges that have historically hindered traditional RAG\u2019s scalability and effectiveness.\n\n# 3 Core Principles and Background of Agentic Intelligence\n\nAgentic Intelligence forms the foundation of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, enabling them to transcend the static and reactive nature of traditional RAG. By integrating autonomous agents capable of dynamic decision-making, iterative reasoning, and collaborative workflows, Agentic RAG systems exhibit enhanced adaptability and precision. This section explores the core principles underpinning agentic intelligence.\n\n# Components of an AI Agent. In essence, an AI agent comprises (Figure. 7):\n\n- LLM (with defined Role and Task): Serves as the agent\u2019s primary reasoning engine and dialogue interface. It interprets user queries, generates responses, and maintains coherence.\n- Memory (Short-Term and Long-Term): Captures context and relevant data across interactions. Short-term memory [22] tracks immediate conversation state, while long-term memory [22] stores accumulated knowledge and agent experiences.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 19920, "end_char_idx": 22326, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "ffd5ddaf-31ce-4fc5-a5d7-023d7616f1ad", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the principles and methodologies of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, focusing on the roles of memory, planning, and reflection in enhancing agent performance. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Memory Types**:\n   - **Short-term Memory**: Tracks immediate conversation states.\n   - **Long-term Memory**: Stores accumulated knowledge and agent experiences.\n\n2. **Planning**:\n   - Involves reflection and self-critique to guide the agent's reasoning process.\n   - Enables the decomposition of complex tasks into manageable subtasks, facilitating multi-hop reasoning and iterative problem-solving.\n\n3. **Tools**:\n   - Includes vector search, web search, and APIs, which expand the agent's capabilities beyond mere text generation.\n\n4. **Agentic Patterns**:\n   - Structured methodologies that guide agent behavior, allowing for dynamic adaptation, planning, and collaboration in real-world tasks.\n\n5. **Reflection**:\n   - A design pattern that allows agents to evaluate and refine their outputs through self-feedback, improving performance in various tasks.\n\n6. **Planning**:\n   - A design pattern that supports the autonomous breakdown of tasks and dynamic decision-making, though it may lead to less predictable outcomes compared to deterministic workflows.\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the importance of these components in creating effective AI agents capable of handling complex tasks with precision and scalability."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "52fbc46b-858d-4757-8e58-8e2ec0aeb82a", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "0d365607c5e6f58478c737e9b426d2c484cd19fa6740dd1606cd2d2ae4ff3ece", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "897380b9-bf32-4216-9589-e915a76bcb64", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "6b604bc892f1c778022dbbf65c88442a29a93bdff9672ac15a247e2866e9b187", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Short-term memory [22] tracks immediate conversation state, while long-term memory [22] stores accumulated knowledge and agent experiences.\n- Planning (Reflection & Self-Critique): Guides the agent\u2019s iterative reasoning process through reflection, query routing, or self-critique [23], ensuring that complex tasks are broken down effectively [24].\n- Tools (Vector Search, Web Search, APIs, etc.): Expands the agent\u2019s capabilities beyond text generation, enabling access to external resources, real-time data, or specialized computations.\n\n|Memory| |Short-term|Tools|Vector Search|Data Sources|\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n|Planning|Long-term|Agent|Web Search|API| |\n|Reflection|Self-critics| | | | |\n\nFigure 7: An Overview of AI Agents\n\nAgentic Patterns [25, 26] provide structured methodologies that guide the behavior of agents in Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems. These patterns enable agents to dynamically adapt, plan, and collaborate, ensuring that the system can handle complex, real-world tasks with precision and scalability. Four key patterns underpin agentic workflows:\n\n# 3.1 Reflection\n\nReflection is a foundational design pattern in agentic workflows, enabling agents to iteratively evaluate and refine their outputs. By incorporating self-feedback mechanisms, agents can identify and address errors, inconsistencies, and areas for improvement, enhancing performance across tasks like code generation, text production, and question answering.\n---\n# 3.2 Planning\n\nPlanning [24] is a key design pattern in agentic workflows that enables agents to autonomously decompose complex tasks into smaller, manageable subtasks. This capability is essential for multi-hop reasoning and iterative problem-solving in dynamic and uncertain scenarios as shown in Figure 9a.\n\nBy leveraging planning, agents can dynamically determine the sequence of steps needed to accomplish a larger objective. This adaptability allows agents to handle tasks that cannot be predefined, ensuring flexibility in decision-making. While powerful, Planning can produce less predictable outcomes compared to deterministic workflows like Reflection. Planning is particularly suited for tasks that require dynamic adaptation, where predefined workflows are insufficient.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 22187, "end_char_idx": 24449, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "897380b9-bf32-4216-9589-e915a76bcb64", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses key concepts related to agentic workflows in AI systems, focusing on two main patterns: Tool Use and Multi-Agent collaboration.\n\n1. **Planning vs. Reflection**: It highlights the unpredictability of Planning compared to deterministic workflows like Reflection. Planning is suited for dynamic tasks requiring adaptation, and its potential for innovative applications is expected to grow as technology advances.\n\n2. **Tool Use**: This pattern allows agents to enhance their capabilities by interacting with external tools, APIs, and computational resources. It enables agents to gather information, perform computations, and manipulate data beyond their pre-trained knowledge. The integration of tools into workflows is crucial for adapting to complex tasks and improving output relevance. Advances like GPT-4\u2019s function calling capabilities have significantly evolved this pattern, although challenges remain in optimizing tool selection, especially in contexts with many options.\n\n3. **Multi-Agent Collaboration**: This design pattern facilitates task specialization and parallel processing among agents. By enabling communication and sharing of intermediate results, it enhances workflow efficiency and coherence. Distributing subtasks among specialized agents improves scalability and adaptability.\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the importance of these patterns in developing sophisticated agentic workflows that can handle complex tasks effectively."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "ffd5ddaf-31ce-4fc5-a5d7-023d7616f1ad", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "10d1d6bacaf8bc7242c7054d7849664427d3aad5883b39105318426c1b92683f", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "4a626fc2-5836-40bb-b73a-9cedf711af87", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "c6fbf02e32e9e2eb2038e187717ad1d8e4b3d7fceee94f6eabb53d413027adcc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "While powerful, Planning can produce less predictable outcomes compared to deterministic workflows like Reflection. Planning is particularly suited for tasks that require dynamic adaptation, where predefined workflows are insufficient. As the technology matures, its potential to drive innovative applications across domains will continue to grow.\n\n# 3.3 Tool Use\n\nTool Use enables agents to extend their capabilities by interacting with external tools, APIs, or computational resources as illustrated in 9b. This pattern allows agents to gather information, perform computations, and manipulate data beyond their pre-trained knowledge. By dynamically integrating tools into workflows, agents can adapt to complex tasks and provide more accurate and contextually relevant outputs.\n\nModern agentic workflows incorporate tool use for a variety of applications, including information retrieval, computational reasoning, and interfacing with external systems. The implementation of this pattern has evolved significantly with advancements like GPT-4\u2019s function calling capabilities and systems capable of managing access to numerous tools. These developments facilitate sophisticated workflows where agents autonomously select and execute the most relevant tools for a given task.\n\nWhile tool use significantly enhances agentic workflows, challenges remain in optimizing the selection of tools, particularly in contexts with a large number of available options. Techniques inspired by retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), such as heuristic-based selection, have been proposed to address this issue.\n\n# 3.4 Multi-Agent\n\nMulti-agent collaboration [29] is a key design pattern in agentic workflows that enables task specialization and parallel processing. Agents communicate and share intermediate results, ensuring the overall workflow remains efficient and coherent. By distributing subtasks among specialized agents, this pattern improves the scalability and adaptability.\n---\n# Response\n\n# User Input\n\n# Response\n\n# Memory Augmented Planning\n\n# Reflection & Refinement\n\n# Task Decomposition\n\n# External Planner\n\n# Plan Selection\n\n# Revised Response\n\n# Environment\n\n# (a) An Overview of Agentic Planning\n\n# (b) An Overview of Tool Use\n\nFigure 9: Overview of Agentic Planning and Tool Use of complex workflows. Multi-agent systems allow developers to decompose intricate tasks into smaller, manageable subtasks assigned to different agents.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 24214, "end_char_idx": 26650, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "4a626fc2-5836-40bb-b73a-9cedf711af87", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the concept of multi-agent systems in the context of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG). Key topics include:\n\n1. **Multi-Agent Systems**: These systems allow for the decomposition of complex tasks into smaller subtasks assigned to different agents, enhancing performance and managing complex interactions. Each agent has its own memory and workflow, facilitating dynamic problem-solving.\n\n2. **Collaboration and Frameworks**: While multi-agent collaboration is less predictable than traditional workflows, emerging frameworks like AutoGen, Crew AI, and LangGraph are being developed to implement effective multi-agent solutions.\n\n3. **Agentic Workflow Patterns**: These patterns are crucial for the success of Agentic RAG systems, enabling dynamic adaptation of retrieval and generative strategies to meet real-world demands. They support iterative and context-aware tasks that surpass traditional RAG capabilities.\n\n4. **Prompt Chaining**: This specific workflow pattern enhances accuracy by breaking down complex tasks into sequential subtasks, although it may increase latency. It is most effective when tasks can be clearly defined into fixed subtasks that contribute to the final output.\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the importance of structured workflows and adaptive strategies in optimizing the performance of AI systems, particularly in dynamic and collaborative environments."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "897380b9-bf32-4216-9589-e915a76bcb64", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "198013a566da0d268723802a7b5b2ac7814a8fa7809b41522b405ff0d216cc8f", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "67ccf151-be45-4566-8a67-e8e8a7281b1b", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "00642151404c29c90939c853cf539230e08370ad3443009d5e36c4f3ba01d174", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Multi-agent systems allow developers to decompose intricate tasks into smaller, manageable subtasks assigned to different agents. This approach not only enhances task performance but also provides a robust framework for managing complex interactions. Each agent operates with its own memory and workflow, which can include the use of tools, reflection, or planning, enabling dynamic and collaborative problem-solving (see Figure 10).\n\nWhile multi-agent collaboration offers significant potential, it is a less predictable design pattern compared to more mature workflows like Reflection and Tool Use. Nevertheless, emerging frameworks such as AutoGen, Crew AI, and LangGraph are providing new avenues for implementing effective multi-agent solutions.\n\n# Query\n\n|Agent 1|Response|\n|---|---|\n|Agent 2|Agent 3|\n\nFigure 10: An Overview of MultiAgent\n\nThese design patterns form the foundation for the success of Agentic RAG systems. By structuring workflows\u2014from simple, sequential steps to more adaptive, collaborative processes\u2014these patterns enable systems to dynamically adapt their retrieval and generative strategies to the diverse and ever-changing demands of real-world environments. Leveraging these patterns, agents are capable of handling iterative, context-aware tasks that significantly exceed the capabilities of traditional RAG systems.\n\n# 4 Agentic Workflow Patterns: Adaptive Strategies for Dynamic Collaboration\n\nAgentic workflow patterns, [12, 13] structure LLM-based applications to optimize performance, accuracy, and efficiency. Different approaches are suitable depending on task complexity and processing requirements.\n---\n# 4.1 Prompt Chaining: Enhancing Accuracy Through Sequential Processing\n\nPrompt chaining [12, 13] decomposes a complex task into multiple steps, where each step builds upon the previous one. This structured approach improves accuracy by simplifying each subtask before moving forward. However, it may increase latency due to sequential processing.\n\nQuery\nLLM\nGate\nLLM\nResponse\nFigure 11: Illustration of Prompt Chaining Workflow\n\nWhen to Use: This workflow is most effective when a task can be broken down into fixed subtasks, each contributing to the final output. It is particularly useful in scenarios where step-by-step reasoning enhances accuracy.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 26521, "end_char_idx": 28816, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "67ccf151-be45-4566-8a67-e8e8a7281b1b", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses various methodologies in the context of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) and their applications in dynamic AI systems. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Step-by-Step Reasoning**: Emphasizes the importance of structured reasoning to enhance accuracy in AI-generated outputs.\n\n2. **Routing**: This process involves classifying inputs and directing them to specialized prompts or processes to improve efficiency and response quality. Example applications include categorizing customer service queries.\n\n3. **Parallelization**: This method divides tasks into independent processes that run concurrently, thereby reducing latency and improving throughput. It includes:\n   - **Sectioning**: Breaking tasks into independent subtasks.\n   - **Voting**: Utilizing multiple outputs to enhance accuracy. Example applications include content moderation and code vulnerability analysis.\n\n4. **Orchestrator-Workers**: A workflow where a central orchestrator model dynamically assigns subtasks to specialized worker models based on input complexity. This approach allows for real-time adaptation and is suitable for tasks that require dynamic decomposition. Example applications include modifying code files and conducting real-time research.\n\nOverall, the section highlights the principles, architectures, and applications of these methodologies in enhancing the performance of AI systems."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "4a626fc2-5836-40bb-b73a-9cedf711af87", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "23416590769243e991fba260209b82e9da50bebbad03fbfee5fa9aecef0f3f06", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "eb5b8516-3807-4c26-b6b0-9fcec881bbb8", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "80956f2c230aa0470b2798ddf99fb0ca65723848e54ff1f26cd8aba30080b627", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "It is particularly useful in scenarios where step-by-step reasoning enhances accuracy.\n\n# Example Applications:\n\n- Generating marketing content in one language and then translating it into another while preserving nuances.\n- Structuring document creation by first generating an outline, verifying its completeness, and then developing the full text.\n\n# 4.2 Routing: Directing Inputs to Specialized Processes\n\nRouting [12, 13] involves classifying an input and directing it to an appropriate specialized prompt or process. This method ensures distinct queries or tasks are handled separately, improving efficiency and response quality.\n\nQuery\nRouter\nLLM\nResponse\nFigure 12: Illustration Routing Workflow\n\nWhen to Use: Ideal for scenarios where different types of input require distinct handling strategies, ensuring optimized performance for each category.\n\n# Example Applications:\n\n- Directing customer service queries into categories such as technical support, refund requests, or general inquiries.\n---\n# 4.3   Parallelization: Speeding Up Processing Through Concurrent Execution\n\nParallelization [12, 13] divides a task into independent processes that run simultaneously, reducing latency and improving throughput. It can be categorized into sectioning (independent subtasks) and voting (multiple outputs for accuracy).\n\nWhen to Use: Useful when tasks can be executed independently to enhance speed or when multiple outputs improve confidence.\n\n# Example Applications:\n\n- Sectioning: Splitting tasks like content moderation, where one model screens input while another generates a response.\n- Voting: Using multiple models to cross-check code for vulnerabilities or analyze content moderation decisions.\n\n# 4.4   Orchestrator-Workers: Dynamic Task Delegation\n\nThis workflow [12, 13] features a central orchestrator model that dynamically breaks tasks into subtasks, assigns them to specialized worker models, and compiles the results. Unlike parallelization, it adapts to varying input complexity.\n\nWhen to Use: Best suited for tasks requiring dynamic decomposition and real-time adaptation, where subtasks are not predefined.\n---\n# Example Applications:\n\n- Automatically modifying multiple files in a codebase based on the nature of requested changes.\n- Conducting real-time research by gathering and synthesizing relevant information from multiple sources.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 28730, "end_char_idx": 31091, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "eb5b8516-3807-4c26-b6b0-9fcec881bbb8", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the principles and applications of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, focusing on their iterative refinement processes and architectural frameworks. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Example Applications**: \n   - Modifying codebases automatically based on requested changes.\n   - Conducting real-time research by synthesizing information from various sources.\n\n2. **Evaluator-Optimizer Workflow**: \n   - This process involves generating an initial output and refining it through feedback from an evaluation model, enhancing response quality through iterative cycles.\n\n3. **When to Use**: \n   - The evaluator-optimizer is particularly effective when clear evaluation criteria exist, improving outputs like literary translations and multi-round research queries.\n\n4. **Taxonomy of Agentic RAG Systems**: \n   - RAG systems are categorized into single-agent architectures, multi-agent systems, and hierarchical agentic architectures, each designed to address specific challenges and optimize performance.\n\n5. **Single-Agent Agentic RAG: Router**: \n   - This architecture centralizes decision-making, where a single agent manages retrieval, routing, and integration of information, making it effective for systems with limited tools or data sources.\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the iterative nature of refining outputs in RAG systems and provides a framework for understanding different architectural designs."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "67ccf151-be45-4566-8a67-e8e8a7281b1b", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "2512fa4bdf670edf07990056b8241918eb98c2fc0af6b14f4022e2b7178e2262", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "da2c2324-922e-4e22-8ee5-b30ec62fa013", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "6279a5d90a1599a96450120ed0b4b045b6f2c3f6ef7a51b7464e8bd8d8e9acb7", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "---\n# Example Applications:\n\n- Automatically modifying multiple files in a codebase based on the nature of requested changes.\n- Conducting real-time research by gathering and synthesizing relevant information from multiple sources.\n\n# 4.5 Evaluator-Optimizer: Refining Output Through Iteration\n\nThe evaluator-optimizer [12, 13] workflow iteratively improves content by generating an initial output and refining it based on feedback from an evaluation model.\n\n|Query|LM|LLM|Accepted|Response|\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n|Rejected + Feedback|Rejected + Feedback|Rejected + Feedback|Rejected + Feedback|Rejected + Feedback|\n\nFigure 15: Illustration of Evaluator-Optimizer Workflow\n\n# When to Use:\n\nEffective when iterative refinement significantly enhances response quality, especially when clear evaluation criteria exist.\n\n# Example Applications:\n\n- Improving literary translations through multiple evaluation and refinement cycles.\n- Conducting multi-round research queries where additional iterations refine search results.\n\n# 5 Taxonomy of Agentic RAG Systems\n\nAgentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems can be categorized into distinct architectural frameworks based on their complexity and design principles. These include single-agent architectures, multi-agent systems, and hierarchical agentic architectures. Each framework is tailored to address specific challenges and optimize performance for diverse applications. This section provides a detailed taxonomy of these architectures, highlighting their characteristics, strengths, and limitations.\n\n# 5.1 Single-Agent Agentic RAG: Router\n\nA Single-Agent Agentic RAG: [30] serves as a centralized decision-making system where a single agent manages the retrieval, routing, and integration of information (as shown in Figure 16). This architecture simplifies the system by consolidating these tasks into one unified agent, making it particularly effective for setups with a limited number of tools or data sources.\n\n# Workflow\n\n1. Query Submission and Evaluation: The process begins when a user submits a query. A coordinating agent (or master retrieval agent) receives the query and analyzes it to determine the most suitable sources of information.\n2. Knowledge Source Selection: Based on the query\u2019s type, the coordinating agent chooses from a variety of retrieval options:\n---\n# 3.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 30860, "end_char_idx": 33205, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "da2c2324-922e-4e22-8ee5-b30ec62fa013", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the process of data integration and output generation in a system utilizing Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) with a focus on a single-agent workflow. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Knowledge Source Selection**: The coordinating agent selects appropriate retrieval options based on the query type.\n2. **Data Integration and LLM Synthesis**: Retrieved data is synthesized by a Large Language Model (LLM) to create a coherent response.\n3. **Output Generation**: The system generates a user-facing answer that is actionable and may include references to the sources used.\n\n**Key Features and Advantages**:\n- Centralized simplicity in design and maintenance.\n- Efficiency and resource optimization through fewer agents.\n- Dynamic routing for real-time query evaluation.\n- Versatility in supporting various data sources and APIs.\n- Suitability for simpler systems with defined tasks.\n\n**Use Case**: The section provides an example of a customer support scenario where a user queries the delivery status of an order, illustrating the system's workflow from query submission to knowledge source selection and response generation."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "eb5b8516-3807-4c26-b6b0-9fcec881bbb8", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "5b2756d122904208e044faf31261d87ad1b57439b78b6507252cf880f92b99ba", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "d315b4b2-e9e6-43b1-bd81-a600a3d544e1", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "2c5ec9e6c1b67708bd908da7f5e703a66398c56d3367a3945c3548ea607dddf0", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "2. Knowledge Source Selection: Based on the query\u2019s type, the coordinating agent chooses from a variety of retrieval options:\n---\n# 3. Data Integration and LLM Synthesis\n\nOnce the relevant data is retrieved from the chosen sources, it is passed to a Large Language Model (LLM). The LLM synthesizes the gathered information, integrating insights from multiple sources into a coherent and contextually relevant response.\n\n# 4. Output Generation\n\nFinally, the system delivers a comprehensive, user-facing answer that addresses the original query. This response is presented in an actionable, concise format and may optionally include references or citations to the sources used.\n\n|Input|Query|Prompt|Tools|\n|---|---|---|---|\n|Vector Search X|Data Sources|Retrieval|Vector Search Y|\n|Response|Router|Web Search| |\n\n# Key Features and Advantages\n\n- Centralized Simplicity: A single agent handles all retrieval and routing tasks, making the architecture straightforward to design, implement, and maintain.\n- Efficiency & Resource Optimization: With fewer agents and simpler coordination, the system demands fewer computational resources and can handle queries more quickly.\n- Dynamic Routing: The agent evaluates each query in real-time, selecting the most appropriate knowledge source (e.g., structured DB, semantic search, web search).\n- Versatility Across Tools: Supports a variety of data sources and external APIs, enabling both structured and unstructured workflows.\n- Ideal for Simpler Systems: Suited for applications with well-defined tasks or limited integration requirements (e.g., document retrieval, SQL-based workflows).\n---\n# Use Case: Customer Support\n\nPrompt: Can you tell me the delivery status of my order?\n\n# System Process (Single-Agent Workflow):\n\n1. Query Submission and Evaluation:\n- The user submits the query, which is received by the coordinating agent.\n- The coordinating agent analyzes the query and determines the most appropriate sources of information.\n2. Knowledge Source Selection:\n- Retrieves tracking details from the order management database.\n- Fetches real-time updates from the shipping provider\u2019s API.\n- Optionally conducts a web search to identify local conditions affecting delivery, such as weather or logistical delays.\n3.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 33071, "end_char_idx": 35332, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "d315b4b2-e9e6-43b1-bd81-a600a3d544e1", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the concept of **Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)**, focusing on its principles, architectures, and applications in dynamic AI systems. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Real-Time Data Integration**: The system fetches updates from APIs (e.g., shipping providers) and may conduct web searches to gather relevant local conditions affecting delivery.\n\n2. **LLM Synthesis**: The relevant data is synthesized by a Large Language Model (LLM) to generate coherent responses.\n\n3. **Output Generation**: The system produces actionable responses, such as live tracking updates for packages.\n\n4. **Multi-Agent Systems**: The section introduces **Multi-Agent RAG**, which enhances single-agent architectures by distributing tasks among specialized agents. This modular approach allows for handling complex workflows and diverse queries.\n\n5. **Workflow Steps**:\n   - **Query Submission**: A coordinator agent receives user queries and delegates them to specialized retrieval agents.\n   - **Specialized Retrieval Agents**: Different agents are assigned specific tasks, such as handling structured queries, semantic searches, real-time information retrieval, and recommendation systems.\n   - **Tool Access and Data Retrieval**: Each agent accesses appropriate tools or data sources, including vector searches, text-to-SQL, and web searches.\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the efficiency and scalability of multi-agent systems in managing complex data retrieval and response generation tasks."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "da2c2324-922e-4e22-8ee5-b30ec62fa013", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "1335d9eb215cf6e8f75212d3d32f41eb9ed428b3e682637f0a19367325e90fcf", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "3a19f4d5-05d4-4986-bb80-28fee339277e", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "5188de08994bc45332326c88646352285b17d4273384366fd3e11d53b98edb24", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "- Fetches real-time updates from the shipping provider\u2019s API.\n- Optionally conducts a web search to identify local conditions affecting delivery, such as weather or logistical delays.\n3. Data Integration and LLM Synthesis:\n- The relevant data is passed to the LLM, which synthesizes the information into a coherent response.\n4. Output Generation:\n- The system generates an actionable and concise response, providing live tracking updates and potential alternatives.\n\nResponse:\n\nIntegrated Response: \u201cYour package is currently in transit and expected to arrive tomorrow evening. The live tracking from UPS indicates it is at the regional distribution center.\u201d\n\n# 5.2 Multi-Agent Agentic RAG Systems:\n\nMulti-Agent RAG [30] represents a modular and scalable evolution of single-agent architectures, designed to handle complex workflows and diverse query types by leveraging multiple specialized agents (as shown in Figure 17). Instead of relying on a single agent to manage all tasks\u2014reasoning, retrieval, and response generation\u2014this system distributes responsibilities across multiple agents, each optimized for a specific role or data source.\n\n# Workflow\n\n1. Query Submission: The process begins with a user query, which is received by a coordinator agent or master retrieval agent. This agent acts as the central orchestrator, delegating the query to specialized retrieval agents based on the query\u2019s requirements.\n2. Specialized Retrieval Agents: The query is distributed among multiple retrieval agents, each focusing on a specific type of data source or task. Examples include:\n- Agent 1: Handles structured queries, such as interacting with SQL-based databases like PostgreSQL or MySQL.\n- Agent 2: Manages semantic searches for retrieving unstructured data from sources like PDFs, books, or internal records.\n- Agent 3: Focuses on retrieving real-time public information from web searches or APIs.\n- Agent 4: Specializes in recommendation systems, delivering context-aware suggestions based on user behavior or profiles.\n3. Tool Access and Data Retrieval: Each agent routes the query to the appropriate tools or data sources within its domain, such as:\n- Vector Search: For semantic relevance.\n- Text-to-SQL: For structured data.\n- Web Search: For real-time public information.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 35146, "end_char_idx": 37428, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "3a19f4d5-05d4-4986-bb80-28fee339277e", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the principles and functionalities of a Multi-Agent Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) system, focusing on its data integration and output generation processes. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Retrieval Methods**: The system employs various retrieval techniques such as Text-to-SQL for structured data, web searches for real-time information, and APIs for accessing external services.\n\n2. **Data Integration and LLM Synthesis**: After retrieval, the data is synthesized by a Large Language Model (LLM) to create coherent responses that integrate insights from multiple sources.\n\n3. **Output Generation**: The system produces comprehensive and actionable responses for users.\n\n4. **Key Features**:\n   - **Modularity**: Independent operation of agents allows for flexible system adjustments.\n   - **Scalability**: Parallel processing enables efficient handling of high query volumes.\n   - **Task Specialization**: Agents are optimized for specific queries, enhancing accuracy.\n   - **Efficiency**: Task distribution minimizes bottlenecks and improves performance.\n   - **Versatility**: Applicable across various domains like research, analytics, and customer support.\n\n5. **Challenges**:\n   - **Coordination Complexity**: Requires sophisticated management of inter-agent communication.\n   - **Computational Overhead**: Increased resource usage due to parallel processing.\n   - **Data Integration**: Difficulty in synthesizing diverse outputs into a cohesive response.\n\n6. **Use Case**: A multi-domain research assistant that retrieves economic and environmental data on renewable energy adoption in Europe through a workflow involving multiple specialized agents.\n\nOverall, the section highlights the architecture, advantages, and challenges of implementing a multi-agent system for dynamic AI applications."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "d315b4b2-e9e6-43b1-bd81-a600a3d544e1", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "9efefb75f89f998e80b182c017840010624c9ac84c8881a02a7a68f327d588d5", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "4949350d-f521-458e-8b77-90ee3517561d", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "bbbfe2561533b238fce3de2172a0a1186bd967b79644cbfc8ec8e1da9b966d0b", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "- Text-to-SQL: For structured data.\n- Web Search: For real-time public information.\n- APIs: For accessing external services or proprietary systems.\n\nThe retrieval process is executed in parallel, allowing for efficient processing of diverse query types.\n---\n# 4. Data Integration and LLM Synthesis\n\nOnce retrieval is complete, the data from all agents is passed to a Large Language Model (LLM). The LLM synthesizes the retrieved information into a coherent and contextually relevant response, integrating insights from multiple sources seamlessly.\n\n# 5. Output Generation\n\nThe system generates a comprehensive response, which is delivered back to the user in an actionable and concise format.\n\n# Key Features and Advantages\n\n- Modularity: Each agent operates independently, allowing for seamless addition or removal of agents based on system requirements.\n- Scalability: Parallel processing by multiple agents enables the system to handle high query volumes efficiently.\n- Task Specialization: Each agent is optimized for a specific type of query or data source, improving accuracy and retrieval relevance.\n- Efficiency: By distributing tasks across specialized agents, the system minimizes bottlenecks and enhances performance for complex workflows.\n- Versatility: Suitable for applications spanning multiple domains, including research, analytics, decision-making, and customer support.\n\n# Challenges\n\n- Coordination Complexity: Managing inter-agent communication and task delegation requires sophisticated orchestration mechanisms.\n- Computational Overhead: Parallel processing of multiple agents can increase resource usage.\n- Data Integration: Synthesizing outputs from diverse sources into a cohesive response is non-trivial and requires advanced LLM capabilities.\n\nFigure 17: An Overview of Multi-Agent Agentic RAG Systems\n---\n# Use Case: Multi-Domain Research Assistant\n\nPrompt: What are the economic and environmental impacts of renewable energy adoption in Europe?\n\n# System Process (Multi-Agent Workflow):\n\n- Agent 1: Retrieves statistical data from economic databases using SQL-based queries.\n- Agent 2: Searches for relevant academic papers using semantic search tools.\n- Agent 3: Performs a web search for recent news and policy updates on renewable energy.\n- Agent 4: Consults a recommendation system to suggest related content, such as reports or expert commentary.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 37345, "end_char_idx": 39726, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "4949350d-f521-458e-8b77-90ee3517561d", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the concept of Hierarchical Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, which utilize a structured, multi-tiered approach to enhance information retrieval and processing. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Agentic Systems**: The role of agents in consulting recommendation systems to suggest related content.\n2. **Integrated Response**: An example response highlighting the impact of renewable energy in Europe, including reductions in greenhouse gas emissions and job creation.\n3. **Hierarchical Structure**: Agents are organized in a hierarchy, with higher-level agents overseeing lower-level agents to facilitate multi-level decision-making.\n4. **Workflow Process**:\n   - **Query Reception**: A top-tier agent receives and assesses user queries.\n   - **Strategic Decision-Making**: The top-tier agent evaluates query complexity and prioritizes resources.\n   - **Delegation**: Tasks are assigned to specialized subordinate agents for independent execution.\n5. **Aggregation and Synthesis**: Results from subordinate agents are collected and synthesized into a coherent response by the higher-level agent.\n6. **Response Delivery**: The final answer is delivered to the user, ensuring comprehensiveness and contextual relevance.\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the efficiency and strategic advantages of using hierarchical structures in agentic systems for information retrieval."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "3a19f4d5-05d4-4986-bb80-28fee339277e", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "71607629e3bb15ecd43fc361f586f868f27d6508fb95dae3d5dfc89f81417375", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "e5fe39cf-4dbe-4700-ab04-35c5d258f9f2", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "d61053327f0d489fd2dfc40298f734f60af0ff4f9e357490b315c8fc353d7772", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "- Agent 4: Consults a recommendation system to suggest related content, such as reports or expert commentary.\n\n# Response:\n\nIntegrated Response: \u201cAdopting renewable energy in Europe has led to a 20% reduction in greenhouse gas emissions over the past decade, according to EU policy reports. Economically, renewable energy investments have generated approximately 1.2 million jobs, with significant growth in solar and wind sectors. Recent academic studies also highlight potential trade-offs in grid stability and energy storage costs.\u201d\n\n# 5.3 Hierarchical Agentic RAG Systems\n\n# Hierarchical Agentic RAG:\n\n[14] systems employ a structured, multi-tiered approach to information retrieval and processing, enhancing both efficiency and strategic decision-making as shown in Figure 18. Agents are organized in a hierarchy, with higher-level agents overseeing and directing lower-level agents. This structure enables multi-level decision-making, ensuring that queries are handled by the most appropriate resources.\n\n|Query|Master Agent|Response|\n|---|---|---|\n|Sub-Agent X|Sub-Agent Y|Sub-Agent Z|\n\nFigure 18: An illustration of Hierarchical Agentic RAG\n\n# Workflow\n\n1. Query Reception: A user submits a query, received by a top-tier agent responsible for initial assessment and delegation.\n2. Strategic Decision-Making: The top-tier agent evaluates the query\u2019s complexity and decides which subordinate agents or data sources to prioritize. Certain databases, APIs, or retrieval tools may be deemed more reliable or relevant based on the query\u2019s domain.\n3. Delegation to Subordinate Agents: The top-tier agent assigns tasks to lower-level agents specialized in particular retrieval methods (e.g., SQL databases, web search, or proprietary systems). These agents execute their assigned tasks independently.\n---\n# 4. Aggregation and Synthesis:\n\nThe results from subordinate agents are collected and integrated by the higher-level agent, which synthesizes the information into a coherent response.\n\n# 5. Response Delivery:\n\nThe final, synthesized answer is returned to the user, ensuring that the response is both comprehensive and contextually relevant.\n\n# Key Features and Advantages.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 39617, "end_char_idx": 41796, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "e5fe39cf-4dbe-4700-ab04-35c5d258f9f2", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the process of response delivery in a hierarchical agentic system, focusing on the principles and advantages of using multiple tiers of agents for enhanced decision-making and scalability. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Response Delivery**: The final answer is synthesized to be comprehensive and contextually relevant.\n  \n2. **Key Features and Advantages**:\n   - **Strategic Prioritization**: Agents prioritize data sources based on query complexity and reliability.\n   - **Scalability**: Tasks are distributed across agent tiers to manage complex queries.\n   - **Enhanced Decision-Making**: Higher-level agents improve accuracy and coherence.\n\n3. **Challenges**:\n   - **Coordination Complexity**: Increased orchestration overhead due to inter-agent communication.\n   - **Resource Allocation**: Difficulty in efficiently distributing tasks to avoid bottlenecks.\n\n4. **Use Case**: A financial analysis system that evaluates investment options in renewable energy based on current market trends.\n\n5. **System Process**: Describes a hierarchical workflow involving top-tier, mid-level, and lower-level agents that gather and synthesize data.\n\n6. **Integrated Response**: Provides a synthesized answer regarding investment opportunities in renewable energy, highlighting market growth and sector performance.\n\n7. **Agentic Corrective RAG**: Introduces mechanisms for self-correction in retrieval results, enhancing document utilization and response quality through iterative refinement.\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the structured approach of agentic systems in delivering accurate and relevant responses while addressing potential challenges in coordination and resource management."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "4949350d-f521-458e-8b77-90ee3517561d", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "d2c7c664c7a24262871fa356ca17281d037f9c8ae0ffac3489e0d682448ce746", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "30c0485e-0957-4328-bcb0-70329897d0e2", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "fac7f25fe38fb79e71be58fdb0286d13e970cc42127c9dae552224db9fc5b68b", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "# 5. Response Delivery:\n\nThe final, synthesized answer is returned to the user, ensuring that the response is both comprehensive and contextually relevant.\n\n# Key Features and Advantages.\n\n- Strategic Prioritization: Top-tier agents can prioritize data sources or tasks based on query complexity, reliability, or context.\n- Scalability: Distributing tasks across multiple agent tiers enables handling of highly complex or multi-faceted queries.\n- Enhanced Decision-Making: Higher-level agents apply strategic oversight to improve overall accuracy and coherence of responses.\n\n# Challenges\n\n- Coordination Complexity: Maintaining robust inter-agent communication across multiple levels can increase orchestration overhead.\n- Resource Allocation: Efficiently distributing tasks among tiers to avoid bottlenecks is non-trivial.\n\n# Use Case: Financial Analysis System\n\nPrompt: What are the best investment options given the current market trends in renewable energy?\n\n# System Process (Hierarchical Agentic Workflow):\n\n1. Top-Tier Agent: Assesses the query\u2019s complexity and prioritizes reliable financial databases and economic indicators over less validated data sources.\n2. Mid-Level Agent: Retrieves real-time market data (e.g., stock prices, sector performance) from proprietary APIs and structured SQL databases.\n3. Lower-Level Agent(s): Conducts web searches for recent policy announcements and consults recommendation systems that track expert opinions and news analytics.\n4. Aggregation and Synthesis: The top-tier agent compiles the results, integrating quantitative data with policy insights.\n\n# Response:\n\nIntegrated Response: \u201cBased on current market data, renewable energy stocks have shown a 15% growth over the past quarter, driven by supportive government policies and heightened investor interest. Analysts suggest that wind and solar sectors, in particular, may experience continued momentum, while emerging technologies like green hydrogen present moderate risk but potentially high returns.\u201d\n\n# 5.4 Agentic Corrective RAG\n\nCorrective RAG: introduces mechanisms to self-correct retrieval results, enhancing document utilization and improving response generation quality as demonstrated in Figure 19. By embedding intelligent agents into the workflow, Corrective RAG ensures iterative refinement of context documents and responses, minimizing errors and maximizing relevance.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 41609, "end_char_idx": 43998, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "30c0485e-0957-4328-bcb0-70329897d0e2", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the concept of Corrective Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), which integrates intelligent agents to enhance the quality of generated responses in dynamic AI systems. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Core Principle of Corrective RAG**: The system evaluates retrieved documents dynamically, performs corrective actions, and refines queries to improve response quality.\n   - **Document Relevance Evaluation**: A Relevance Evaluation Agent assesses the relevance of retrieved documents, triggering corrective actions for those that fall below a certain threshold.\n   - **Query Refinement and Augmentation**: A Query Refinement Agent optimizes queries using semantic understanding to improve retrieval outcomes.\n\n2. **Overview of Agentic Corrective RAG**:\n   - **Dynamic Retrieval**: An External Knowledge Retrieval Agent supplements context by performing web searches or accessing alternative data sources when necessary.\n   - **Response Synthesis**: A Response Synthesis Agent compiles validated and refined information into a coherent final response.\n\n3. **Workflow**: The Corrective RAG system consists of five key agents:\n   - Context Retrieval Agent\n   - Relevance Evaluation Agent\n   - Query Refinement Agent\n   - External Knowledge Retrieval Agent\n   - Response Synthesis Agent\n\n4. **Key Features and Advantages**:\n   - Iterative Correction for high response accuracy.\n   - Dynamic Adaptability through real-time web searches and query refinement.\n   - Agentic Modularity for efficient and scalable operations.\n   - Factuality Assurance to minimize misinformation and hallucination risks.\n\n5. **Use Case**: The section includes a prompt for an academic research assistant, asking for the latest findings in generative AI research. \n\nOverall, the focus is on enhancing the accuracy and relevance of AI-generated responses through a structured agent-based approach."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "e5fe39cf-4dbe-4700-ab04-35c5d258f9f2", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "86f57b04f48b75578d3f3bc4fc8c4869f9538fe288222760f789b38dcf885036", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "55f0f141-fe0d-4ae3-8f9b-a07e5654a5e6", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "261bf849bb4bcf6c35fb34400dff648bb20ba7988341dc9d081df4ed97438866", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "By embedding intelligent agents into the workflow, Corrective RAG ensures iterative refinement of context documents and responses, minimizing errors and maximizing relevance.\n\n# Key Idea of Corrective RAG:\n\nThe core principle of Corrective RAG lies in its ability to evaluate retrieved documents dynamically, perform corrective actions, and refine queries to enhance the quality of generated responses. Corrective RAG adjusts its approach as follows:\n\n- Document Relevance Evaluation: Retrieved documents are assessed for relevance by the Relevance Evaluation Agent. Documents below the relevance threshold trigger corrective steps.\n- Query Refinement and Augmentation: Queries are refined by the Query Refinement Agent, which leverages semantic understanding to optimize retrieval for better results.\n---\n# Overview of Agentic Corrective RAG\n\n\u2022 Dynamic Retrieval from External Sources: When context is insufficient, the External Knowledge Retrieval Agent performs web searches or accesses alternative data sources to supplement the retrieved documents.\n\n\u2022 Response Synthesis: All validated and refined information is passed to the Response Synthesis Agent for final response generation.\n\n# Workflow\n\nThe Corrective RAG system is built on five key agents:\n\n1. Context Retrieval Agent: Responsible for retrieving initial context documents from a vector database.\n2. Relevance Evaluation Agent: Assesses the retrieved documents for relevance and flags any irrelevant or ambiguous documents for corrective actions.\n3. Query Refinement Agent: Rewrites queries to improve retrieval, leveraging semantic understanding to optimize results.\n4. External Knowledge Retrieval Agent: Performs web searches or accesses alternative data sources when the context documents are insufficient.\n5. Response Synthesis Agent: Synthesizes all validated information into a coherent and accurate response.\n\n# Key Features and Advantages\n\n\u2022 Iterative Correction: Ensures high response accuracy by dynamically identifying and correcting irrelevant or ambiguous retrieval results.\n\n\u2022 Dynamic Adaptability: Incorporates real-time web searches and query refinement for enhanced retrieval precision.\n\n\u2022 Agentic Modularity: Each agent performs specialized tasks, ensuring efficient and scalable operation.\n\n\u2022 Factuality Assurance: By validating all retrieved and generated content, Corrective RAG minimizes the risk of hallucination or misinformation.\n---\n# Use Case: Academic Research Assistant\n\n# Prompt: What are the latest findings in generative AI research?", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 43824, "end_char_idx": 46355, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "55f0f141-fe0d-4ae3-8f9b-a07e5654a5e6", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the use case of an Academic Research Assistant utilizing a Corrective Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) workflow to address queries related to the latest findings in generative AI research. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Workflow Steps**:\n   - **Query Submission**: User submits a query.\n   - **Context Retrieval**: Initial documents are retrieved from a database of published papers.\n   - **Relevance Evaluation**: Documents are assessed for relevance and categorized.\n   - **Corrective Actions**: If necessary, the query is refined, and additional external sources are searched.\n   - **Response Synthesis**: A coherent summary is created from validated documents.\n\n2. **Response Example**: A synthesized response highlights recent advancements in generative AI, including diffusion models and reinforcement learning, referencing studies from NeurIPS 2024 and AAAI 2025.\n\n3. **Adaptive Agentic RAG**: This concept enhances the efficiency of large language models by dynamically adjusting query handling strategies based on query complexity, allowing for various retrieval approaches.\n\nEntities mentioned include:\n- **Generative AI**: The primary subject of the research.\n- **NeurIPS 2024 and AAAI 2025**: Conferences where relevant studies are published.\n- **Adaptive RAG**: A method for improving query handling in AI systems."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "30c0485e-0957-4328-bcb0-70329897d0e2", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "60f9c06748c99c488a12016af110043de1e3575fd667335a0b7f09c57c33be6a", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "d4e5b647-1e3e-42cf-8944-630d71d16404", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "5203afc70c817808f1ba40bd2e7d22c134e06de27f8388695267e7ba218e03da", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "---\n# Use Case: Academic Research Assistant\n\n# Prompt: What are the latest findings in generative AI research?\n\n# System Process (Corrective RAG Workflow):\n\n1. Query Submission: A user submits the query to the system.\n2. Context Retrieval:\n- The Context Retrieval Agent retrieves initial documents from a database of published papers on generative AI.\n- The retrieved documents are passed to the next step for evaluation.\n3. Relevance Evaluation:\n- The Relevance Evaluation Agent assesses the documents for alignment with the query.\n- Documents are classified into relevant, ambiguous, or irrelevant categories. Irrelevant documents are flagged for corrective actions.\n4. Corrective Actions (if needed):\n- The Query Refinement Agent rewrites the query to improve specificity and relevance.\n- The External Knowledge Retrieval Agent performs web searches to fetch additional papers and reports from external sources.\n5. Response Synthesis:\n- The Response Synthesis Agent integrates validated documents into a coherent and comprehensive summary.\n\n# Response:\n\nIntegrated Response: \u201cRecent findings in generative AI highlight advancements in diffusion models, reinforcement learning for text-to-video tasks, and optimization techniques for large-scale model training. For more details, refer to studies published in NeurIPS 2024 and AAAI 2025.\u201d\n\n# 5.5 Adaptive Agentic RAG\n\nAdaptive Retrieval-Augmented Generation (Adaptive RAG) [33] enhances the flexibility and efficiency of large language models (LLMs) by dynamically adjusting query handling strategies based on the complexity of the incoming query. Unlike static retrieval workflows, Adaptive RAG [34] employs a classifier to assess query complexity and determine the most appropriate approach, ranging from single-step retrieval to multi-step reasoning, or even bypassing retrieval altogether for straightforward queries as illustrated in Figure 20.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 46245, "end_char_idx": 48146, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "d4e5b647-1e3e-42cf-8944-630d71d16404", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the concept of Adaptive Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) in dynamic AI systems, focusing on its principles, architecture, and workflow. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Core Principle**: Adaptive RAG dynamically tailors retrieval strategies based on the complexity of user queries.\n\n2. **Query Types**:\n   - **Straightforward Queries**: Fact-based questions answered directly using pre-existing knowledge.\n   - **Simple Queries**: Moderately complex tasks requiring minimal context, addressed through single-step retrieval.\n   - **Complex Queries**: Multi-layered questions needing iterative reasoning, handled via multi-step retrieval.\n\n3. **Workflow Components**:\n   - **Classifier Role**: A smaller language model predicts query complexity using automatically labeled datasets.\n   - **Dynamic Strategy Selection**: The system chooses retrieval strategies based on query type, optimizing efficiency and accuracy.\n   - **LLM Integration**: The language model synthesizes retrieved information into coherent responses, refining answers through iterative interactions.\n\n4. **Key Features and Advantages**:\n   - **Dynamic Adaptability**: Adjusts strategies based on query complexity.\n   - **Resource Efficiency**: Minimizes overhead for simple queries while ensuring thorough processing for complex ones.\n\nOverall, the section emphasizes the importance of adapting retrieval methods to enhance the performance of AI systems in responding to various types of queries."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "55f0f141-fe0d-4ae3-8f9b-a07e5654a5e6", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "e33045c200fba58e15f21051c1cbf9c0568b0e8299509dfa46aa9e6230e44311", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "67fb4226-b007-44de-881d-66c62fdbc03a", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "f859f56dbcf95ff344f67d99886439c5b04ec9266028d2d138df3ce188f81010", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "|Graph|Document|Questions|Answer|\n|---|---|---|---|\n|(Node)|relevant|Yes|Generate|\n|(Node)|Hallucination?|Yes|No|\n|Retrieve|(Node)|Query| |\n\n# Figure 20: An Overview of Adaptive Agentic RAG\n\n# Key Idea of Adaptive RAG\n\nThe core principle of Adaptive RAG lies in its ability to dynamically tailor retrieval strategies based on the complexity of the query. Adaptive RAG adjusts its approach as follows:\n---\n# Adaptive RAG System\n\n# Query Types\n\n- Straightforward Queries: For fact-based questions that require no additional retrieval (e.g., \"What is the boiling point of water?\"), the system directly generates an answer using pre-existing knowledge.\n- Simple Queries: For moderately complex tasks requiring minimal context (e.g., \"What is the status of my latest electricity bill?\"), the system performs a single-step retrieval to fetch the relevant details.\n- Complex Queries: For multi-layered queries requiring iterative reasoning (e.g., \"How has the population of City X changed over the past decade, and what are the contributing factors?\"), the system employs multi-step retrieval, progressively refining intermediate results to provide a comprehensive answer.\n\n# Workflow\n\nThe Adaptive RAG system is built on three primary components:\n\n1. Classifier Role:\n- A smaller language model analyzes the query to predict its complexity.\n- The classifier is trained using automatically labeled datasets, derived from past model outcomes and query patterns.\n2. Dynamic Strategy Selection:\n- For straightforward queries, the system avoids unnecessary retrieval, directly leveraging the LLM for response generation.\n- For simple queries, it employs a single-step retrieval process to fetch relevant context.\n- For complex queries, it activates multi-step retrieval to ensure iterative refinement and enhanced reasoning.\n3. LLM Integration:\n- The LLM synthesizes retrieved information into a coherent response.\n- Iterative interactions between the LLM and the classifier enable refinement for complex queries.\n\n# Key Features and Advantages\n\n- Dynamic Adaptability: Adjusts retrieval strategies based on query complexity, optimizing both computational efficiency and response accuracy.\n- Resource Efficiency: Minimizes unnecessary overhead for simple queries while ensuring thorough processing for complex ones.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 48148, "end_char_idx": 50452, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "67fb4226-b007-44de-881d-66c62fdbc03a", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the principles and applications of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) in dynamic AI systems, focusing on resource efficiency, enhanced accuracy, and flexibility. It presents a use case for a Customer Support Assistant, detailing a system process that includes query classification, dynamic strategy selection, multi-step retrieval, and response synthesis. The integrated response to a customer query about a delayed package illustrates the system's capabilities. Additionally, the section introduces Agent-G, an agentic framework that combines graph knowledge bases with unstructured document retrieval to improve reasoning and retrieval accuracy in RAG systems. Key entities include the concepts of resource efficiency, accuracy, flexibility, and the Agent-G framework."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "d4e5b647-1e3e-42cf-8944-630d71d16404", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "6c87f5ceddacf2f499dffcf73fe72d7e3c60f4d52bf92893421ba635248bbb84", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "ffed18b4-c6de-4198-80a8-6d7e5dbbbdcf", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "95976975012dc43ab6975b3d9d4914b04cb20acacf8eb970717a2bf3a11826c9", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "- Resource Efficiency: Minimizes unnecessary overhead for simple queries while ensuring thorough processing for complex ones.\n- Enhanced Accuracy: Iterative refinement ensures that complex queries are resolved with high precision.\n- Flexibility: Can be extended to incorporate additional pathways, such as domain-specific tools or external APIs.\n---\n# Use Case: Customer Support Assistant\n\nPrompt: Why is my package delayed, and what alternatives do I have?\n\n# System Process (Adaptive RAG Workflow):\n\n1. Query Classification:\n- The classifier analyzes the query and determines it to be complex, requiring multi-step reasoning.\n2. Dynamic Strategy Selection:\n- The system activates a multi-step retrieval process based on the complexity classification.\n3. Multi-Step Retrieval:\n- Retrieves tracking details from the order database.\n- Fetches real-time status updates from the shipping provider API.\n- Conducts a web search for external factors such as weather conditions or local disruptions.\n4. Response Synthesis:\n- The LLM integrates all retrieved information, synthesizing a comprehensive and actionable response.\n\n# Response:\n\nIntegrated Response: \u201cYour package is delayed due to severe weather conditions in your region. It is currently at the local distribution center and will be delivered in 2 days. Alternatively, you may opt for a local pickup from the facility.\u201d\n\n# 5.6 Graph-Based Agentic RAG\n\n# 5.6.1 Agent-G: Agentic Framework for Graph RAG\n\nAgent-G [8]: introduces a novel agentic architecture that integrates graph knowledge bases with unstructured document retrieval. By combining structured and unstructured data sources, this framework enhances retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) systems with improved reasoning and retrieval accuracy. It employs modular retriever banks, dynamic agent interaction, and feedback loops to ensure high-quality outputs as shown in Figure 21.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 50327, "end_char_idx": 52220, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "ffed18b4-c6de-4198-80a8-6d7e5dbbbdcf", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the \"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation\" (Agent-G) framework, which focuses on enhancing AI systems through dynamic retrieval strategies. Key topics and entities include:\n\n1. **Core Principle**: Agent-G dynamically assigns retrieval tasks to specialized agents, utilizing both graph knowledge bases and unstructured documents to improve information retrieval.\n\n2. **Components**:\n   - **Retriever Bank**: A modular set of agents that specialize in retrieving data from either graph-based or unstructured sources, selecting relevant information based on query requirements.\n   - **Critic Module**: Evaluates the relevance and quality of retrieved data, flagging low-confidence results for further refinement.\n   - **Dynamic Agent Interaction**: Collaboration among task-specific agents to integrate diverse data types, ensuring cohesive retrieval and synthesis.\n   - **LLM Integration**: Combines validated data into coherent responses, with iterative feedback from the critic to align with the query's intent.\n\n3. **Key Features**:\n   - **Enhanced Reasoning**: Merges structured graph relationships with contextual information from text.\n   - **Dynamic Adaptability**: Adjusts retrieval strategies based on specific query needs.\n   - **Improved Accuracy**: The critic module minimizes the inclusion of irrelevant or low-quality data in responses.\n\nOverall, the Agent-G framework aims to optimize information retrieval and synthesis in dynamic AI systems through a structured and iterative approach."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "67fb4226-b007-44de-881d-66c62fdbc03a", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "7e0c6b05996dd8aa1c204ddd9f1b3c789968528e6687196f77009391e2c18417", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "0cc175b6-0f3b-4da6-9550-605234530a0d", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "9222d9461936e2e64adc4e0c181cb7d6b5601612948894c3f256c8b9cd5b6d8f", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "It employs modular retriever banks, dynamic agent interaction, and feedback loops to ensure high-quality outputs as shown in Figure 21.\n\n|Database|Question|Answer|\n|---|---|---|\n|Retriever|Agent|NO|\n| |YESI| |\n|Graph|Text|C5|\n|Commentor|Critic|Validator|\n|Ranker|Generator| |\n\nFigure 21: An Overview of Agent-G: Agentic Framework for Graph RAG [8]\n---\n# Key Idea of Agent-G\n\nThe core principle of Agent-G lies in its ability to dynamically assign retrieval tasks to specialized agents, leveraging both graph knowledge bases and textual documents. Agent-G adjusts its retrieval strategy as follows:\n\n- Graph Knowledge Bases: Structured data is used to extract relationships, hierarchies, and connections (e.g., disease-to-symptom mappings in healthcare).\n- Unstructured Documents: Traditional text retrieval systems provide contextual information to complement graph data.\n- Critic Module: Evaluates the relevance and quality of retrieved information, ensuring alignment with the query.\n- Feedback Loops: Refines retrieval and synthesis through iterative validation and re-querying.\n\n# Workflow\n\nThe Agent-G system is built on four primary components:\n\n1. Retriever Bank:\n- A modular set of agents specializes in retrieving graph-based or unstructured data.\n- Agents dynamically select relevant sources based on the query\u2019s requirements.\n2. Critic Module:\n- Validates retrieved data for relevance and quality.\n- Flags low-confidence results for re-retrieval or refinement.\n3. Dynamic Agent Interaction:\n- Task-specific agents collaborate to integrate diverse data types.\n- Ensures cohesive retrieval and synthesis across graph and text sources.\n4. LLM Integration:\n- Synthesizes validated data into a coherent response.\n- Iterative feedback from the critic ensures alignment with the query\u2019s intent.\n\n# Key Features and Advantages\n\n- Enhanced Reasoning: Combines structured relationships from graphs with contextual information from unstructured documents.\n- Dynamic Adaptability: Adjusts retrieval strategies dynamically based on query requirements.\n- Improved Accuracy: Critic module reduces the risk of irrelevant or low-quality data in responses.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 52085, "end_char_idx": 54234, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "0cc175b6-0f3b-4da6-9550-605234530a0d", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the principles and applications of Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, particularly in the context of healthcare diagnostics. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Dynamic Adaptability**: The system adjusts its retrieval strategies based on the specific requirements of the query.\n2. **Improved Accuracy**: A critic module is employed to minimize the inclusion of irrelevant or low-quality data in responses.\n3. **Scalable Modularity**: The architecture allows for the integration of new agents to handle specialized tasks, enhancing scalability.\n\nThe use case presented focuses on healthcare diagnostics, specifically addressing the common symptoms of Type 2 Diabetes and their relationship to heart disease. The system's workflow includes:\n\n- **Query Reception and Assignment**: Identifying the need for both graph-structured and unstructured data.\n- **Graph Retriever**: Extracting relationships and shared risk factors from a medical knowledge graph.\n- **Document Retriever**: Gathering descriptions of Type 2 Diabetes symptoms from medical literature.\n- **Critic Module**: Evaluating the relevance and quality of the retrieved data.\n- **Response Synthesis**: Integrating validated data into a coherent response.\n\nThe integrated response highlights the symptoms of Type 2 Diabetes and their correlation with heart disease, emphasizing shared risk factors.\n\nAdditionally, the section introduces GeAR (Graph-Enhanced Agent for Retrieval-Augmented Generation), which enhances traditional RAG systems by incorporating graph-based retrieval mechanisms to improve multi-hop retrieval capabilities for complex queries."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "ffed18b4-c6de-4198-80a8-6d7e5dbbbdcf", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "0e41bfc2e925d39b02c096e3a0765582920898d131fdcbb8e9b578a8b2c68a53", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "8fd91fa5-32ee-4a8e-a239-ef653a801a15", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "fe6317c010a63c8162faa8eb605309330adfedfecca0355d784ee5f417093f3f", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "- Dynamic Adaptability: Adjusts retrieval strategies dynamically based on query requirements.\n- Improved Accuracy: Critic module reduces the risk of irrelevant or low-quality data in responses.\n- Scalable Modularity: Supports the addition of new agents for specialized tasks, enhancing scalability.\n---\n# Use Case: Healthcare Diagnostics\n\nPrompt: What are the common symptoms of Type 2 Diabetes, and how are they related to heart disease?\n\n# System Process (Agent-G Workflow):\n\n1. Query Reception and Assignment: The system receives the query and identifies the need for both graph-structured and unstructured data to answer the question comprehensively.\n2. Graph Retriever:\n- Extracts relationships between Type 2 Diabetes and heart disease from a medical knowledge graph.\n- Identifies shared risk factors such as obesity and high blood pressure by exploring graph hierarchies and relationships.\n3. Document Retriever:\n- Retrieves descriptions of Type 2 Diabetes symptoms (e.g., increased thirst, frequent urination, fatigue) from medical literature.\n- Adds contextual information to complement the graph-based insights.\n4. Critic Module:\n- Evaluates the relevance and quality of the retrieved graph data and document data.\n- Flags low-confidence results for refinement or re-querying.\n5. Response Synthesis: The LLM integrates validated data from the Graph Retriever and Document Retriever into a coherent response, ensuring alignment with the query\u2019s intent.\n\n# Response:\n\nIntegrated Response: \u201cType 2 Diabetes symptoms include increased thirst, frequent urination, and fatigue. Studies show a 50% correlation between diabetes and heart disease, primarily through shared risk factors such as obesity and high blood pressure.\u201d\n\n# 5.6.2 GeAR: Graph-Enhanced Agent for Retrieval-Augmented Generation\n\nGeAR [35]: introduces an agentic framework that enhances traditional Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems by incorporating graph-based retrieval mechanisms. By leveraging graph expansion techniques and an agent-based architecture, GeAR addresses challenges in multi-hop retrieval scenarios, improving the system\u2019s ability to handle complex queries as shown in Figure 22.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 54041, "end_char_idx": 56220, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "8fd91fa5-32ee-4a8e-a239-ef653a801a15", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the GeAR (Graph-Enhanced Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation) system, which improves retrieval performance in complex query scenarios through two main innovations: \n\n1. **Graph Expansion**: This technique enhances traditional retrieval methods (like BM25) by incorporating graph-structured data, allowing the system to understand and utilize complex relationships between entities.\n\n2. **Agent Framework**: An agent-based architecture is employed to manage the retrieval process dynamically, enabling autonomous decision-making and the selection of appropriate retrieval strategies based on the complexity of queries.\n\nThe workflow of the GeAR system includes:\n\n- **Graph Expansion Module**: Integrates graph data into the retrieval process, enhancing the ability to handle multi-hop queries by considering relationships between entities.\n  \n- **Agent-Based Retrieval**: Utilizes agents to dynamically select and combine retrieval strategies, improving the relevance and accuracy of the information retrieved.\n\nAdditionally, the section highlights the integration of retrieved information with a Large Language Model (LLM) to generate coherent and contextually relevant responses, ensuring that the generative process is informed by both unstructured documents and structured graph data. \n\nKey topics include graph expansion, agent-based architecture, multi-hop retrieval, and LLM integration."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "0cc175b6-0f3b-4da6-9550-605234530a0d", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "458090f520a9c4810940c57bdb92b0a7d8b36df5f50f0c4003f7977ca49dacc7", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "1432b431-cea3-405d-8229-2d41638ad101", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "7fba40f25d4497595da5cefb99e9bbac830cb82b620c11c5cf79bb2aca8b6d9e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "By leveraging graph expansion techniques and an agent-based architecture, GeAR addresses challenges in multi-hop retrieval scenarios, improving the system\u2019s ability to handle complex queries as shown in Figure 22.\n\n# Key Idea of GeAR\n\nGeAR advances RAG performance through two primary innovations:\n\n- Graph Expansion: Enhances conventional base retrievers (e.g., BM25) by expanding the retrieval process to include graph-structured data, enabling the system to capture complex relationships and dependencies between entities.\n- Agent Framework: Incorporates an agent-based architecture that utilizes graph expansion to manage retrieval tasks more effectively, allowing for dynamic and autonomous decision-making in the retrieval process.\n\n# Workflow:\n\nThe GeAR system operates through the following components:\n\n1. Graph Expansion Module:\n- Integrates graph-based data into the retrieval process, allowing the system to consider relationships between entities during retrieval.\n- Enhances the base retriever\u2019s ability to handle multi-hop queries by expanding the search space to include connected entities.\n2. Agent-Based Retrieval:\n- Employs an agent framework to manage the retrieval process, enabling dynamic selection and combination of retrieval strategies based on the query\u2019s complexity.\n- Agents can autonomously decide to utilize graph-expanded retrieval paths to improve the relevance and accuracy of retrieved information.\n---\n# 3. LLM Integration:\n\n- Combines the retrieved information, enriched by graph expansion, with the capabilities of a Large Language Model (LLM) to generate coherent and contextually relevant responses.\n- The integration ensures that the generative process is informed by both unstructured documents and structured graph data.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 56007, "end_char_idx": 57770, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "1432b431-cea3-405d-8229-2d41638ad101", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the principles and functionalities of a system called GeAR (Generative Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation), which integrates unstructured documents and structured graph data to enhance information retrieval and generation processes. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Integration of Data Types**: The system combines unstructured documents with structured graph data to inform the generative process.\n\n2. **Enhanced Multi-Hop Retrieval**: GeAR's graph expansion capability allows it to handle complex queries that require reasoning across multiple interconnected information pieces.\n\n3. **Agentic Decision-Making**: The framework enables dynamic and autonomous selection of retrieval strategies, improving efficiency and relevance in responses.\n\n4. **Improved Accuracy**: Incorporating structured graph data enhances the precision of retrieved information, leading to more accurate and contextually appropriate responses.\n\n5. **Scalability**: The modular design of the agent framework allows for the integration of additional retrieval strategies and data sources as needed.\n\n6. **Use Case - Multi-Hop Question Answering**: An example is provided where the system processes a query about the literary influences on J.K. Rowling's mentor, demonstrating the workflow of evaluating the query, identifying key entities, and utilizing graph-structured data.\n\nKey entities mentioned include J.K. Rowling and her mentor, as well as the concept of literary influences and relationships within a graph structure."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "8fd91fa5-32ee-4a8e-a239-ef653a801a15", "node_type":