pics:**\n1. **Evolution of RAG Systems**: The transition from basic keyword-based retrieval to advanced systems that integrate diverse data sources and autonomous decision-making.\n2. **Na\u00efve RAG**: The foundational implementation of RAG characterized by:\n   - Simple retrieve-read workflow.\n   - Use of keyword-based retrieval techniques (e.g., TF-IDF, BM25).\n   - Augmentation of language models with retrieved documents.\n3. **Limitations of Na\u00efve RAG**:\n   - Lack of contextual awareness.\n   - Fragmented outputs due to insufficient preprocessing.\n   - Scalability issues with large datasets.\n4. **Importance of Na\u00efve RAG**: Despite its limitations, it served as a proof-of-concept for integrating retrieval with generation, paving the way for more advanced paradigms.\n\n**Entities:**\n- **RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)**: A system that combines retrieval and generation processes.\n- **Na\u00efve RAG**: The initial stage of RAG systems.\n- **Techniques**: TF-IDF, BM25 (keyword-based retrieval methods).\n- **Key Characteristics**: Simplicity, ease of implementation, and foundational role in RAG development. \n\nThe section sets the stage for discussing more advanced RAG systems, such as Advanced RAG, which address the limitations of Na\u00efve RAG."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_mo