ON A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses advancements in Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, focusing on two specific paradigms: Modular RAG and Graph RAG.\n\n### Key Topics:\n1. **Advanced RAG**: Highlights the use of dense retrieval models and neural ranking algorithms to enhance retrieval precision.\n2. **Modular RAG**: \n   - Emphasizes flexibility and customization by decomposing the retrieval and generation pipeline into independent components.\n   - Key innovations include:\n     - **Hybrid Retrieval Strategies**: Combining sparse and dense retrieval methods for improved accuracy.\n     - **Tool Integration**: Utilizing external APIs and databases for specialized tasks.\n     - **Composable Pipelines**: Allowing independent enhancement and reconfiguration of components for adaptability to specific use cases.\n   - Example: A Modular RAG system for financial analytics that retrieves live stock prices and generates investment insights.\n\n3. **Graph RAG**: \n   - Integrates graph-based data structures to enhance multi-hop reasoning and contextual enrichment.\n   - Characterized by its ability to capture relationships between entities through node connectivity.\n\n### Entities:\n- **Dense Passage Retrieval (DPR)**: A dense retrieval model used in Advanced RAG.\n- **BM25**: A sparse retrieval method mentioned in the context of hybrid strategies.\n- **APIs and Databases**: External tools integrated into Modular RAG for specialized tasks.\n- **Graph Data Structures**: Used in Graph RAG to improve relational understanding and generative outputs.\n\nOverall, the section outlines th