66702941805124, -0.024693481624126434, 0.00302835158072412, -0.003196686040610075, -0.025853490456938744, 0.022213468328118324, -0.008193382993340492], "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20", "document_title": "\"Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Principles, Architectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the concept of Adaptive Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) in dynamic AI systems, focusing on its principles, architecture, and workflow. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Core Principle**: Adaptive RAG dynamically tailors retrieval strategies based on the complexity of user queries.\n\n2. **Query Types**:\n   - **Straightforward Queries**: Fact-based questions answered directly using pre-existing knowledge.\n   - **Simple Queries**: Moderately complex tasks requiring minimal context, addressed through single-step retrieval.\n   - **Complex Queries**: Multi-layered questions needing iterative reasoning, handled via multi-step retrieval.\n\n3. **Workflow Components**:\n   - **Classifier Role**: A smaller language model predicts query complexity using automatically labeled datasets.\n   - **Dynamic Strategy Selection**: The system chooses retrieval strategies based on query type, optimizing efficiency and accuracy.\n   - **LLM Integration**: The language model synthesizes retrieved information into coherent responses, refining answers through iterative interactions.\n\n4. **Key Features and Advantages**:\n   - **Dynamic Adaptability**: Adjusts strategies based on query complexity.\n   - **Resource Efficiency**: Minimizes overhead for simple queries while ensuring th