ity.\n\nThe use case presented focuses on healthcare diagnostics, specifically addressing the common symptoms of Type 2 Diabetes and their relationship to heart disease. The system's workflow includes:\n\n- **Query Reception and Assignment**: Identifying the need for both graph-structured and unstructured data.\n- **Graph Retriever**: Extracting relationships and shared risk factors from a medical knowledge graph.\n- **Document Retriever**: Gathering descriptions of Type 2 Diabetes symptoms from medical literature.\n- **Critic Module**: Evaluating the relevance and quality of the retrieved data.\n- **Response Synthesis**: Integrating validated data into a coherent response.\n\nThe integrated response highlights the symptoms of Type 2 Diabetes and their correlation with heart disease, emphasizing shared risk factors.\n\nAdditionally, the section introduces GeAR (Graph-Enhanced Agent for Retrieval-Augmented Generation), which enhances traditional RAG systems by incorporating graph-based retrieval mechanisms to improve multi-hop retrieval capabilities for complex queries."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "ffed18b4-c6de-4198-80a8-6d7e5dbbbdcf", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "0e41bfc2e925d39b02c096e3a0765582920898d131fdcbb8e9b578a8b2c68a53", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "8fd91fa5-32ee-4a8e-a239-ef653a801a15", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "fe6317c010a63c8162faa8eb605309330adfedfecca0355d784ee5f417093f3f", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "- Dynamic Adaptability: Adjusts retrieval strategies dynamically based on query requirements.\n- Improved Accuracy: Critic module reduces the risk of irrelevant or low-quality data in responses.\n- Scalable Modularity: Supports the addition of new agents for specialized tasks, enhancing scalability.\n---\n# Use Case: Healthcare Diagnostics\n\nPrompt: What are the common symptoms of Type 2 Diabetes, and how are they related to heart disease?\n\n# System Process (Agent-G Workflow):\n\n1. Query Reception and Assignment: The system receives the query and identifies the need for both graph-structured and unstructured data to answer the question comprehensively.\n2. Graph Retriever:\n- Extracts relationships between Type 2 Diabetes and heart disease from a medical knowledge graph.\n- Identifies shared risk factors such as obesity and high blood pressure by exploring graph hierarchies and relationships.\n3. Document Retriever:\n- Retrieves descriptions of Type 2 Diabetes symptoms (e.g., increased thirst, frequent urination, fatigue) from medical literature.\n- Adds contextual information to complement the graph-based insights.\n4. Critic Module:\n- Evaluates the relevance and quality of the retrieved graph data and document data.\n- Flags low-confidence results for refinement or re-querying.\n5. Response Synthesis: The LLM integrates validated data from the Graph Retriever and Document Retriever into a coherent response, ensuring alignment with the query\u2019s intent.\n\n# Response:\n\nIntegrated Response: \u201cType 2 Diabetes symptoms include increased thirst, frequent urination, and fatigue. Studies show a 50% correlation between diabetes and heart disease, primarily through shared risk factors such as obesity and high blood pressure.\u201d\n\n# 5.6.2 GeAR: Graph-Enhanced Agent for Retrieval-Augmented Generation\n\nGeAR [35]: introduces an agentic framework that enhances traditional Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems by incorporating graph-based retrieval mechanisms. By leveraging graph expansion techniques and an agent-based architecture, GeAR addresses challenges in multi-hop retrieval scenarios, improving the system\u2019s ability to handle complex queries as shown in Figure 22.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 54041, "end_char_idx": 56220, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "[Excerpt from document]\n{metadata_str}\nExcerpt:\n-----\n{content}\n-----\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "8fd91fa5-32ee-4a8e-a239-ef653a801a15", "embedding": [-0.009294206276535988, 0.051475606858730316, 0.04347888007760048, 0.019846176728606224, 0.009492800571024418, 0.001969392178580165, 0.00416385754942894, 0.02365918457508087, -0.017860235646367073, 0.04437917470932007, 0.0087977210059762, -0.06704539060592651, -0.03190746158361435, -0.037441618740558624, 6.20606733718887e-05, -0.016456836834549904, -0.020362520590424538, -0.04286985844373703, 0.003892445471137762, -0.002685985993593931, 0.023897496983408928, 0.015847813338041306, 0.0208391472697258, 0.031748585402965546, -0.018072068691253662, -0.03442298620939255, 0.015318229794502258, 0.08775214105844498, -0.008930117823183537, 0.00047662598080933094, 0.0086057465523