hitectures, Applications, and Future Directions in Dynamic AI Systems\"", "section_summary": "The section discusses the GeAR (Graph-Enhanced Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation) system, which improves retrieval performance in complex query scenarios through two main innovations: \n\n1. **Graph Expansion**: This technique enhances traditional retrieval methods (like BM25) by incorporating graph-structured data, allowing the system to understand and utilize complex relationships between entities.\n\n2. **Agent Framework**: An agent-based architecture is employed to manage the retrieval process dynamically, enabling autonomous decision-making and the selection of appropriate retrieval strategies based on the complexity of queries.\n\nThe workflow of the GeAR system includes:\n\n- **Graph Expansion Module**: Integrates graph data into the retrieval process, enhancing the ability to handle multi-hop queries by considering relationships between entities.\n  \n- **Agent-Based Retrieval**: Utilizes agents to dynamically select and combine retrieval strategies, improving the relevance and accuracy of the information retrieved.\n\nAdditionally, the section highlights the integration of retrieved information with a Large Language Model (LLM) to generate coherent and contextually relevant responses, ensuring that the generative process is informed by both unstructured documents and structured graph data. \n\nKey topics include graph expansion, agent-based architecture, multi-hop retrieval, and LLM integration."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "42831f3d26ca4cfa6d94fdd9504869cdd0ae1fd50debb205f921f3f248abd7cc", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "0cc175b6-0f3b-4da6-9550-605234530a0d", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_type": "text/markdown", "file_size": 104275, "creation_date": "2025-03-25", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-20"}, "hash": "458090f520a9c4810940c57bdb92b0a7d8b36df5f50f0c4003f7977ca49dacc7", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "1432b431-cea3-405d-8229-2d41638ad101", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "7fba40f25d4497595da5cefb99e9bbac830cb82b620c11c5cf79bb2aca8b6d9e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "By leveraging graph expansion techniques and an agent-based architecture, GeAR addresses challenges in multi-hop retrieval scenarios, improving the system\u2019s ability to handle complex queries as shown in Figure 22.\n\n# Key Idea of GeAR\n\nGeAR advances RAG performance through two primary innovations:\n\n- Graph Expansion: Enhances conventional base retrievers (e.g., BM25) by expanding the retrieval process to include graph-structured data, enabling the system to capture complex relationships and dependencies between entities.\n- Agent Framework: Incorporates an agent-based architecture that utilizes graph expansion to manage retrieval tasks more effectively, allowing for dynamic and autonomous decision-making in the retrieval process.\n\n# Workflow:\n\nThe GeAR system 