hmarks for RAG Systems**:\n   - **MS MARCO**: Focuses on passage ranking and question answering.\n   - **TREC**: Provides datasets for passage and document retrieval, emphasizing ranking model quality.\n   - **MuSiQue**: A benchmark for multihop reasoning across multiple documents.\n   - **2WikiMultihopQA**: Designed for multihop QA tasks over two Wikipedia articles.\n   - **AgentG**: Tailored for agentic RAG tasks, assessing dynamic information synthesis.\n   - **HotpotQA**: A multi-hop QA benchmark requiring interconnected context retrieval.\n   - **RAGBench**: A large-scale benchmark with 100,000 examples across various domains.\n\n2. **Tools and Libraries**:\n   - **BERGEN**: A library for systematic benchmarking of RAG systems.\n   - **FlashRAG Toolkit**: Implements multiple RAG methods and includes numerous benchmark datasets.\n   - **GNN-RAG**: Evaluates graph-based RAG systems focusing on retrieval quality and reasoning in Knowledge Graph Question Answering (KGQA).\n\n3. **Downstream Tasks and Datasets**:\n   - The section includes a table summarizing various task types (single-hop and multi-hop QA) along with associated datasets such as Natural Questions, TriviaQA, SQuAD, and others.\n\nOverall, the excerpt highlights the importance of diverse benchmarks and tools for evaluating the effectiveness and performance of RAG systems in dynamic AI applications."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "67f7d17c-65a8-47f0-8f2e-71490af5fab1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\ai_articles\\AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG.md", "file_name": "AGENTIC RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION A SURVEY ON AGENTIC RAG