ection provides a list of references related to the field of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) and its applications in AI systems. Key topics include:\n\n1. **Prompt Engineering**: A systematic review that includes a SWOT analysis, indicating a focus on the strengths, weaknesses, opportunities, and threats associated with prompt engineering in AI.\n\n2. **Hallucination in Large Language Models**: A survey discussing the principles, taxonomy, challenges, and open questions regarding the phenomenon of hallucination in AI-generated content.\n\n3. **Agentic Framework for Graph Retrieval**: Introduction of \"Agent-g,\" which presents a framework for enhancing graph retrieval through augmented generation techniques.\n\n4. **AI-Generated Content**: A survey on the use of retrieval-augmented generation specifically for content generated by AI.\n\n5. **Active Retrieval Augmented Generation**: A study focusing on the active aspects of retrieval-augmented generation, highlighting its practical applications.\n\n6. **Vector Databases**: A comprehensive survey addressing storage and retrieval techniques, as well as challenges associated with vector databases.\n\n7. **Effective Agents**: Research by Anthropic on building effective AI agents, indicating a focus on practical implementations in AI.\n\n8. **LangChain Workflows**: A tutorial on workflows related to LangChain, suggesting a practical guide for utilizing this framework in AI applications.\n\nEntities mentioned include various authors and their affiliations, as well as organizations like Anthropic and LangChain. The references span publications from 2023 to 2025, indicating ongoing research and development in the field."}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "